fix = "Bind the guard to a local and pass a reference to it; the production change (203 lines in human_runtime.rs, 235 in policy/approval.rs, 14 in outbox/recover.rs) is untested until the gates run."

[gotcha.3275]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 2: build and dependent-crate check pass; the first verify fails program_replay actual_module_start_refuses_unobservable_start_state with an EngineFault (preauthorized execution commitment accounting diverged from canonical state at step 5), which the repair cycle fixed (4 passed in the second verify); the second verify then fails the terminal decoder persistence case of repair_22_31_259 at line 957 with DigestMismatch from the settlement attach function, and the repair_22_31_564, repair_22_31_569 and repair_22_31_573 binaries never ran because cargo stops at the first failing test binary."
symptom = "22.31.488 (commit 87f25cefc8, 2026-11-05) made the settlement attach function of src/terminal (the storage-environment module, lines 296 to 318) take the canonical usage receipt bytes followed by their 32-byte sha256 digest and added append_receipt_digest (line 80), which the native host (host_ffi.rs line 853) and the 488 proof (tests/repair_22_31_488.rs lines 71 to 72) use; the 259 proof still passes the bare canonical_usage_receipt bytes (lines 945 and 957), so the reader takes the trailing transfer root as the digest. Only the 573 verify runs the 259 suite, the storage-environment module is identical to main on the attempt-2 tree, and the break has been on main since 488 landed."
fix = "Task 22.31.574 frames the receipt in the 259 proof (decision 2685); 573 requires it and continues with its own binaries run first."

[gotcha.3276]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 12: build and dependent-crate check pass after the compatibility include repair; the verify stops before any test runs because the Go test binary of rpc does not compile: rpc/repair_478_test.go line 382 calls balance.FillBytes on the value host.ReadBalance returns, which is the SDK Int of sdk/types/int.go and has no FillBytes method; the Rust market suite never ran."
symptom = "The SDK Int wraps a big.Int and exposes it through BigInt() (int.go line 84) and the arithmetic and comparison methods; FillBytes belongs to big.Int. The proof transports the observed balance to the Rust fixture as 16 big-endian bytes and must take the big integer first; line 418 of the same proof already uses the Int method Int64 correctly."
fix = "balance.BigInt().FillBytes(make([]byte, 16)) at line 382; no production change."

[gotcha.3277]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 16: the maintained batch shape of decision 2684 is accepted (the Sequence refusal is gone) and the funded path now stops at funded_scenario.rs line 900, PAY2 authenticated issue usage: Activity, from authenticate_cumulative_use on the entry that layerx_mcp::tools::wallet::cumulative_evidence builds from the verified first draw."
symptom = "The entry carries the exact submitted activity of the wallet execution (layerx-sdk rpc_verification.rs lines 73 to 84), which for a ledger operation is the signed EIP-1559 transaction the SDK sends under decision 2521; the daemon consumer (layerx-agentd protocol_evidence.rs lines 857 to 872 and the time-window twin at lines 1235 to 1262) only knows signed LayerX activity envelopes: peek_signed_activity_type refuses the 0x02 envelope and the refusal maps to CumulativeUseError::Activity before any receipt comparison. The node names such an activity by its transaction hash (node/sequencer/accept.go line 88, etx.Hash()) and its actor by the recovered sender; task 22.31.568 proved the node-receipt key path with a LayerX envelope only, so no production consumer ever accepted a real node activity."
fix = "Task 22.31.575 teaches both consumers the EVM transaction activity (transaction hash as the activity id, recovered sender as the actor bound to a caller-supplied account), decision 2687; 22.33.1569 requires it and continues on the attempt-16 tree."

[gotcha.3278]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 7: the instrumented trace of gotcha 3271 found the first silent refusal (the absent native session scope, human_runtime.rs line 7191, Session ScopeDenied) and the fixture now sends the signed local grant; the next run reached authenticated_native_policy_usage and px_getHistory was unserved, the peer now serves the authenticated ten-second history window; the third run passes session admission, the complete committed inventory and the history proof and the genuine first Prepare still answers 403 owner.refused with no diagnostic line, so the task ended its repair budget without the site."
symptom = "rpc_prepare_native_send (human_runtime.rs lines 7010 to 7461 of the attempt tree) maps about thirty distinct conditions to HumanOperationError::Refused without naming any of them: empty rate proofs, the budget source read, the fee policy bound, the owner purpose verification, the capability inspection, the durable preparation decode and its identity checks; the RPC surface collapses every one to the same owner.refused rejection. Each attempt can locate one site only by re-instrumenting the daemon, and the temporary prints are removed before qualification, so the next attempt starts blind again."
fix = "Decision 2688: the native send Prepare path reports the refusing site in the daemon diagnostic log as production behaviour, with the same private-log print that budget_read_parts already uses; the attempt-7 tree stands and the next attempt reads the site from the verify log and repairs the fixture for it."

[gotcha.3279]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 3: build and the dependent-crate check pass, program_replay and repair_22_31_259 pass (the 574 frame holds), then the verify stops in repair_22_31_564 at line 146: replay_capture_still_refuses_byte_and_boundary_profile_limits expects the reason deterministic execution observer refused: SupplementRejected and the runtime answers the same reason with the suffix at retain_boundary_capture.source; the 573 and 569 binaries never ran."
symptom = "Task 22.31.569 (landed as 9c0e7abe03) named the execution observer supplement refusal site in host/mod.rs line 603 and its own proof asserts the sited text (repair_22_31_569.rs line 206), but its verify ran only its binary, so the older 564 proof that asserts the unsited text has been red on main since that landing; the 573 verify lists 564 and stops there (decision 2685)."
fix = "Decision 2689: a producer that adds a site to a refusal reason runs every proof asserting that reason and amends them to the sited text; 573 amends tests/repair_22_31_564.rs within the task and continues."

[gotcha.3280]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 13: the Go proof compiles after the BigInt fix and runs: the baseline Fund exhausts the CPU allowance at 999975 fuel as recorded, the candidate Fund completes guest execution at 896330 CPU fuel under the 1000000 cap and then ends LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED (-736) in the occupancy settlement callback (stage 5) because the proof advances the host block from 1002 to 1003 (repair_478_test.go line 363) without the occupancy finalization of 1002 that the ledger requires; the Rust diagnostic example (examples/repair_478_fixture.rs line 17) panics on the kernel terminal wrapper, terminal-applied-legs/v1, instead of decoding it. The agent stopped and asked because the attempt-13 note limited Go proof edits to compiler fixes."
symptom = "The allowance goal of the task is reached in the candidate tree; both remaining failures are fixture setup the gate exposed, and the note scope was read as forbidding their repair."
fix = "Decision 2690: a fixture correction the gate exposes is within a continue note when it uses production paths and keeps every assertion; 478 continues with both corrections."

[gotcha.3281]
title = "22.31.571 attempt 3: the build and the dependent-crate check (15 crates) pass and the TRACK proof reaches PREPARE, which answers status 1 operation.refused with no diagnostic (tests/repair_22_31_571.rs line 1073); recovery admits writes. In its last cycle the agent found that the proof encoded the PREPARE and SUBMIT body-digest text lengths as 64-bit values where the daemon hashes 32-bit lengths (human_runtime.rs hash_text, line 20011), corrected both encoders, and could not re-run the verify because the repair budget was spent; the correction is in the tree unverified."
symptom = "The gated prepare path (human_runtime.rs prepare_gated, the body-digest check at line 15293 and 19 further Refused mappings behind it) answers every refusal as operation.refused, so a proof-frame digest mismatch is indistinguishable from an actor, authority, nonce or policy refusal; the proof encoder was written from the submit digest helper that uses 64-bit lengths (subscription_create_digest) instead of hash_text."
fix = "Continue at the same tree: run the gates first; if PREPARE still refuses, decision 2691 adds the sited diagnostic to the Human journey prepare path, as decision 2688 did for native send, and the site names the next repair."

[gotcha.3282]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 4: the build, the dependent-crate check (58 crates) and the four recorded suites pass, the 564 reason amendment is in, and two 573 cases fail: the eight-call case is refused by the legacy execution trace guard, execution trace peak retained bytes 333376350 exceed 67108864 (execute.rs line 893), after the observer admitted it; the 128-call case is refused SupplementRejected at retain_boundary_capture.source because every boundary witness carries the 4096-byte baseline storage value in both the host and the storage preimages, seven boundaries per read, so even 65 reads exceed the 1048576-byte witness bound. The agent stopped for direction because commit.rs is out of scope and no check may be disabled."
symptom = "The legacy ExecutionTrace materializes every full canonical state (17 pages each) beside the replay record and sums them in execute.rs and commit.rs, so a default-stack guest can never stay under its 64 MiB guard whatever the observer charges; and the proof baseline value is a fixture choice that scales the witness."
fix = "Decision 2692: under a replay profile the replay record is the commitment and the legacy trace is not materialized; the proof baseline storage value shrinks to 32 bytes so the 128 reads fit the witness bound."

[gotcha.3283]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 17: the account-bound evidence of 22.31.575 passes the cumulative-use checks; the funded MCP identity registration then fails BoundaryUnavailable at funded_scenario.rs line 138 after the loopback peer served eth_call to the address precompile, the identity sequence, eth_blockNumber, eth_getBlockByNumber 6 twice, px_getCommit 6 and px_getValidators 6; the agent added the missing peer responses in two cycles and ran out of budget."
symptom = "The qualification resolver (services/agent/qualification/pay2/sequence.rs, resolve from line 124) maps four distinct boundary reads to BoundaryUnavailable without naming which; the last of them, CommittedReads::open (layerx-agentd src/read/committed.rs line 719), authenticates the served checkpoint through the production verifier over the commit and the validator keys, so a served commit the keys did not sign is reported as an unavailable boundary."
fix = "Decision 2693: the resolver prints the failing read; the peer serves a checkpoint for the committed height that the production verifier authenticates."

[gotcha.3284]
title = "22.35.8 attempts 2 to 4: each run reached the result collection step and was ended by the qualification environment past its deadline grace; no result of those runs exists. The collection step added the changed explorer directories (thousands of files under apps/explorer/ui and apps/explorer/toolkit) to the candidate index one file at a time, rewriting the whole monorepo index per file, so every collection took 17 to 30 minutes."
symptom = "The per-file add was invisible on small tasks; the explorer restyle tasks change whole directories."
fix = "The collection step adds every file of a directory entry in one call and prints its timing; the collection step gets a grace of its own. Attempt 1 at 38bc60fa64 is the only tree and continues."

[gotcha.3285]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 8: the sited refusal helper prints native send prepare refused at budget source read; the first-Prepare case gets 403 owner.refused because budget/program_sources.rs lines 433 and 564 refuse caps.level() below STATE_PROVEN, and read/committed.rs CommittedCaps::level (lines 166 and 420) answers CHECKPOINT_FINALISED for every committed read."
symptom = "In layerx-types verify.rs the deprecated CheckpointFinalised rank orders below Unverified (the Ord keys CheckpointFinalised and SettlementAnchored to 0 and 1, the live ranks to wire rank plus 2), so a committed read never satisfies a STATE_PROVEN floor; the daemon-wide retirement of the label is 22.31.539, which waits on 560."
fix = "Decision 2694: the two level() sites answer COMMITTED now; 22.31.539 keeps the rest of its scope."

[gotcha.3286]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 18: the served checkpoint authenticates, the SDK Send verifies to Batched with pinned authority and coverage, the MCP grant issue executes and its executed receipt is served, then wait_batched (funded_scenario.rs line 598) fails InvalidRequest before any further peer request."
symptom = "Wallet::wait_for_submitted (layerx-sdk wallet.rs line 220) refuses a receipt without canonical activity (rpc_verification.rs submitted_activity line 80); the MCP wallet execute (layerx-mcp tools/wallet.rs lines 97 to 115) waits through Wallet::wait_for and never binds the signed bytes, unlike Wallet::send and Wallet::payment (wallet.rs lines 78 to 80 and 262 to 266); the MCP cumulative_evidence (line 312) refuses the same receipts."
fix = "Decision 2695 and task 22.31.576: the SDK exposes a wait that binds the signed bytes and the MCP execute uses it; 1569 continues after 576."

[gotcha.3287]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 14: the build and the dependent-crate check pass, every prior block and block 1002 finalize through the production host-module path, and the candidate Fund answers the canonical synthetic pre-runtime failure with code -3 (LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL), recorded CPU fuel 0 and no callback stage; the fixture binary panicked decoding that bare terminal as an applied-legs wrapper (examples/repair_478_fixture.rs line 17), the second repair selected the decoder by tag, and the budget ended before it ran under a gate."
symptom = "The -3 at pre-runtime with zero fuel is the native binding mapping of an executor error or a missing replay record of a profiled CALL (decision 2647, ffi_call.rs lines 2896 to 2902), not a fuel stop; the Go case reads only the terminal, so the cause is in the independent executor result the fixture now prints."
fix = "Attempt 15 runs the standing tree once, reads the executor result and repairs the cause it names."

[gotcha.3288]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 5: the build, the dependent-crate check (58 crates) and four recorded suites pass, the baseline value is 32 bytes and the proof searches for the largest admitted count; the 128-call case is refused SupplementRejected at retain_boundary_capture.source and the 65-call case is refused program replay record refused: Bounds, so no count above 64 fits the 1048576-byte witness."
symptom = "A portable boundary leaf carries the whole linear memory of the guest (portable_replay.rs line 128 reads it as one owned field up to MAX_STEP_STATE_BYTES; the proof asserts 17 pages, 1114112 bytes, in every leaf), so one leaf of a 17-page guest is larger than the kernel maximum of 1048576 witness bytes (programs.h line 677) and no profile the kernel accepts holds even one boundary of such a guest; the native CALL refusals of 22.99.77 under the 128-boundary 1 MiB profile are the same bound."
fix = "Decision 2696: a leaf carries the memory pages the boundary changed; 573 implements it and measures; 22.99.77 inherits it through 573."

[gotcha.3289]
title = "22.31.571 attempt 4: SUBMIT with the approval release reference now passes and the linked TRACK by reference equals the direct TRACK before the restart (byte 73 is 3, Submitted); after the Store is reopened and the runtime rebuilt the linked TRACK answers 5 (Unknown) at byte 73 and the proof stops at the assertion that the linked status survives restart (tests/repair_22_31_571.rs line 1199)."
symptom = "Production recovery restores a Submitted submission without a verified receipt as Unknown with the reason that the restart made the transport outcome indeterminate and lists it for receipt resolution (outbox/recover.rs restore_submissions, lines 233 to 243); the direct TRACK answers 5 after a restart as well, so the linked path mirrors the producer and the proof asserted a state recovery never keeps. The later assertion that the verified receipt survives restart (Executed, 6) is right because Executed restores unchanged in the same mapping."
fix = "The proof asserts the production recovery state after the first restart: byte 73 is 5 and the linked answer equals the direct TRACK taken after the same restart; decision 2697."

[gotcha.3290]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 6: the agent stopped at the reader condition of decision 2696 before changing the leaf encoding: the native market single-step adjudication opens one or two leaves by index against the trace root (execute.rs decode_market_step_evidence and open_market_boundary, lines 6258 to 6288 and 6020 to 6049), decodes the complete linear memory of the pre leaf (portable_replay.rs line 128) and replays that single boundary natively through the market step observer at line 5728, so a leaf that carries only the pages changed since the previous leaf leaves the adjudicator without the memory it replays; the build passed, no verify ran, the attempt-5 tree is preserved."
symptom = "Two consumers want two shapes of the same memory: the record witness needs small leaves (the whole record fits 1048576 bytes) and the single-step adjudicator needs the whole pre memory from one leaf. Decision 2696 served the first and broke the second. The kernel reader in src/modules/programs/call.c (lines 2968 to 3030) only hashes opaque leaves; the market program passes the evidence bytes through untouched (layerx-programs-market lib.rs lines 1298 and 1355), and the 259 and market proofs build their leaves at test time, so the encoding can change without recorded vectors."
fix = "Decision 2698: a leaf commits to its memory through a chunk root and carries the changed chunks; the adjudication evidence supplies the pre memory chunks that root authenticates. Task 22.31.577 implements it; 573 follows it and 22.99.77 inherits through 573."

[gotcha.3291]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 19: registration, the SDK Send, the SDK grant issue and draw and the MCP grant issue (batched wait) pass; the MCP grant draw is refused with WalletToolError::Arguments before submission (tests/support/funded_scenario.rs line 8 reports PAY2 MCP grant draw execution: Arguments)."
symptom = "policy_dimensions in services/agent/crates/layerx-mcp/src/tools/wallet.rs (line 256; the DrawGrant arm at lines 278 to 287) requires a Payment::Receive in the payment field of the disclosure, but bind_call for ConstructMethod::LedgerDraw (layerx-crypto disclosure/call.rs lines 968 to 981) sets only the counterparties, the Transfer amount and the idempotency key and never the payment field, since the draw calldata carries no payer and no asset; prepare_alias_call (wallet.rs lines 124 to 150) decodes the Receive with Payment::decode and discards it. The SDK draw path never consults policy_dimensions, so SDK draws pass."
fix = "Repair task 22.31.578 derives the DrawGrant policy dimensions from the decoded Receive cross-checked against the bound LedgerDraw (decision 2699); 22.33.1569 requalifies after it."

[gotcha.3292]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 9: after the denomination repair (reopen_daemon keeps the tenant-bound limit and attaches the protected denomination through attach_program_budget_denominations) the second verify run moves the refusal from the prepared cache lookup to native rate staging: services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs line 7374 answers owner.refused native rate staging and native_send_first_prepare_and_reopened_prepare_match_owner_preview fails (403 against 200 at tests/repair_22_31_560.rs line 622); the other 2 cases pass."
symptom = "StagedNativeRateUse::stage (layerx-agentd src/approval/native_program.rs lines 1333 to 1420) answers one CarrierError::Binding for every condition it checks: the disclosure binding, the canonical digest and the preparation id of the prepared bytes, the actor against the binding agent, an empty constraint chain or rate-obligation window set, an evidence count unequal to the window count, each window proof (actor, through_sequence equal to observed_head_sequence, observed_core_ms equal to the constraint observed_at_ms, window in the set, one observed batch id, no duplicate window) and the pending-use advance; the fixture evidence comes from operations.authenticated_native_policy_usage per window (human_runtime.rs near line 7224) and the test verifies history.time_window for a complete empty ten-second window (lines 876 to 890), so the refused equality is not visible from the log."
fix = "Attempt 10 adds a diagnostic inside stage naming the refused condition and repairs the fixture proof against the binding equalities; no production check is relaxed."

[gotcha.3293]
title = "22.33.1536 attempt 8: the gates passed at 34a1e6edcd856709cbac864b9843b542a03e018f but publication stopped on a three-way conflict in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/human_node_budgets.rs: the attempt changed lines 79, 92, 161 and 204 and added a 49-line case after line 503 while main (dbd4e68ed9, the part-2 task) changed the signed_receipt lines 204 (paymentDenom and feeDenom) and 208 (signingKey from the public key)."
symptom = "The attempt branched from 61612c2b19a7 before the part-2 landing and both sides edited the same signed_receipt literal; the merge cannot choose."
fix = "Attempt 9 replays the attempt-8 changes onto the main version keeping the main-side paymentDenom and signingKey lines, then reruns the gates."

[gotcha.3294]
title = "22.33.1135 attempt 1: the gates passed at 584642067465bfa30d22a870958c22b659179f38 but the qualified tree changed tests/codec/generate_nfc_tables.py, two codec tests, tests/vectors/codec/NormalizationTest-15.0.0.txt and UNICODE-LICENSE.txt, and wrote the task record at tests/repair_22_33_1135.kvx; the task touches only src/codec/lxp_codec.c with planned path tests/codec, so the publication was held."
symptom = "do_4 asks for pinned Unicode NFC checking against the published vectors, which the touches list did not foresee; tests/vectors/codec holds five files on main and is the right home for the vectors and the license; the record belongs under tests/codec."
fix = "The touches list is amended to tests/codec and tests/vectors/codec and attempt 2 moves the record to tests/codec/repair_22_33_1135.kvx."

[gotcha.3295]
title = "Audit of the carried native source-control specification (spec/layerx-merge/source-control): 7 of the 34 original tasks are done (0.2, 0.3 to 0.7, 3.1), 26 are partial and 0.14 is not done; no original receipt exists in the snapshot because every build directory is ignored, the drivers under tests/<project>/cases/source_control bind git rev-parse HEAD of the host repository (the monorepo commit and root tree, not the project subtree), and the live-provider, model and object-store parts (0.11 to 0.14, 1.1, 6.1) exit BLOCKED or LIVE_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED without credentials."
symptom = "The specification was written for a standalone checkout; vendored, its receipts, revisions and ancestry checks point at history that is not in this repository."
fix = "Tasks 22.37.1 to 22.37.27 complete the unfinished originals under the moved directory after 22.36.1, with component-mode gates and the live parts recorded UNRUN (decision 2700); audit.kvx records every verdict."

[gotcha.3296]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 15: the independent executor run answers Fund Ok at 896330 CPU fuel while the kernel candidate Fund still refuses at pre-runtime with LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL (-3), recorded CPU fuel 0 and the terminal wrapper LXP/programs/pre-runtime-failure/v1 behind a context-hash prefix; the agent found that the native balance sight requires the receipt of the immediately preceding sequence and the current state root while the fixture still passed the CREATE receipt after block 1002 was finalized, bound a fresh receipt obtained through the idempotent rewards-account registration after finalization, added a kernel gas counter reading and synchronized a C node layout declared in both modules/lxphost/ctx.go and simulate.go; the build passed at cc579828686b96262c97dc0fe3c6b9d72ff41486 but the repair budget was exhausted before a verify run."
symptom = "The pre-runtime refusal is a stale receipt binding, not an executor or replay refusal (the executor path of decision 2647 passes); the correction has not run under a gate."
fix = "Attempt 16 requalifies the attempt-15 tree as it stands; the touches list gains programs/Cargo.lock for the dependency the fixture example added."

[gotcha.3297]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 10: the fixture runs the real daemon library behind the recorded authority and the release reference resolves through TRACK (22.31.571), but both approval cases receive Corrupt from track_released at the first field of the answer. The daemon writes a TRACK observation as the 32-byte activity id, then the tracked submission of write_submission (services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs line 21778: the 32-byte submission id, the state code of state_code at line 18370, a 32-byte receipt digest for codes 6 and 9 or a 4-byte result code for code 7, the rung rank, the evidence count with text kind and 32-byte digest items, a zero transition count), then a zero receipt-presence byte. The Human decoder decode_tracked (services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/agent_runtime.rs line 4406) reads the submission reference as length-prefixed text, the code-6 receipt reference as text, and knows no code 9."
symptom = "The routing module of the daemon reads the same answer with 32-byte identifiers (lines 811 to 852) and the SDK contract names a 32-byte tx hash; the Human decoder was written against a text layout no producer serves, while the request side (hex text decoded by digest_from_hex) agrees on both sides, so only the answer layout diverges; the Human test agent_runtime_rungs.rs (lines 135 to 147) hand-encodes the same text layout and so never caught it."
fix = "Task 22.31.579 makes the Human decoder and that test follow the layout the daemon writes (decision 2701); 22.33.1510 requalifies after it."

[gotcha.3298]
title = "22.35.8 attempt 5: tsc passes and six of the seven vitest cases pass; pagesRenderInBothColourModes mounts Home, Transaction and Address in light and in dark mode under jsdom and took 66 seconds against the 60-second case timeout the spec sets (vi.setConfig at line 43), so the case failed as timed out and the production build was not reached."
symptom = "Six page mounts with the full provider tree, the mocked API and the token resolution cost about eleven seconds each in the qualification environment and one case carries all six."
fix = "Attempt 6 splits the case into one case per page with a 180-second timeout; the assertions stay."

[gotcha.3299]
title = "22.37.23 attempt 1 and 22.37.24 attempt 1: the build command (a pnpm filter on the control-services package) answered No projects matched the filters and exited zero without compiling anything; the vendored project directory excludes core/control-plane and core/kvx from its pnpm package set (pnpm-workspace.yaml) and builds that package standalone with npm --prefix core/control-plane ci --ignore-scripts and npm --prefix core/control-plane run build (Makefile lines 105 to 111), whose build script first copies the generated contracts module under src before tsc runs; without it dist/storage/runtime.js was missing, the standalone authority guard of 6_1.py failed before the component drill, and the recovery actor compile of 6_2.py stopped on the missing contracts module. The PostgreSQL 18 fixture server the drills need was present in the qualification environment."
symptom = "The series commands were derived from the package names, and the control-plane package is the one member of the vendored tree outside the pnpm package set."
fix = "Decision 2702 corrects the commands of 22.37.11, 22.37.12, 22.37.13, 22.37.22, 22.37.23 and 22.37.24 to the standalone npm build; 22.37.23 and 22.37.24 continue on their trees."

[gotcha.3300]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 20: the MCP draw is refused as WalletToolError::Policy before any receipt; the policy engine answers Deny InvalidContext because valid_context (layerx-agentd policy/eval.rs lines 831 to 878) requires the authenticated cumulative use to belong to the session agent, and the scenario authenticates the cumulative use of the treasury DID of the fixture with the payer wallet account (tests/support/funded_scenario.rs lines 1005 to 1030) while the session agent and the executing wallet are the recipient (line 1043); the issue step authenticates the treasury correctly for its own session."
symptom = "authenticate_account_cumulative_use (protocol_evidence.rs) counts the entries of the named actor and binds the actor into the AuthenticatedCumulativeUse; valid_context compares that actor with session.agent and refuses on mismatch; the MCP draw session is the recipient, so the usage must be authenticated for the recipient DID and the recipient wallet account."
fix = "The draw steps authenticate the cumulative use of the session agent; the policy engine, the MCP tool and the daemon are unchanged."

[gotcha.3301]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 10: the fixture proof fails at native rate staging with canonical_digest_matches_envelope=false and preparation_id_matches_envelope=false while the actor matches, and the pending-use advance answers Ok(0); the log also shows observed_core_ms=1789365544000 against constraint_time=1789365544."
symptom = "Two production consumer defects. StagedNativeRateUse::stage (approval/native_program.rs line 1332) compares the envelope digest (Sha256 of the prepared canonical bytes) with binding.canonical_digest() and binding.preparation_id(), which hold the call identifier under decision 2634; the binding carries the envelope digest in its envelope_digest field (capability/binding.rs lines 2276 to 2278 and 2415 to 2417) and the sibling checks at lines 2430, 2476 and 2647 already compare against it. The prepare snapshot stores the block timestamp in seconds into protocol_timestamp (prepare/mod.rs line 569 from head.timestamp, documented as seconds in layerx-client sequencer.rs) while every consumer reads it as milliseconds (CoreTimestampMs, expires_at_ms comparisons at lines 6159, 6434 and 9231, the Human preview and session_control)."
fix = "The staging compares the envelope digest with the envelope digest of the binding, and the producer stores the core timestamp in milliseconds (decision 2704)."

[gotcha.3302]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 16: the after-guest Fund completes its CPU work (fuel 896330 under the 1000000 cap) and is refused at ledger apply with LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED (-736) carrying callback stage 5 code -207, LXP_ERR_UNAUTHORIZED_DEBIT; the independent executor probe answers Ok because the executor applies no ledger leg."
symptom = "lxp_apply.c lines 103 to 116 admit a transfer leg only when exactly one transfer source authority of the call names authorized_from equal to the leg source account; the programs module builds those authorities from the declared transfer set of the call (src/modules/programs/call.c lines 2322 to 2412: one authority per declared leg with the kind of its declared source), and the Go fixture (rpc/repair_478_test.go) declares capabilities 3, 7 and 8 only, no transfer capability and no transfer leg for the Fund deposit, so the deposit leg finds no authority."
fix = "The fixture declares the transfer capability and the transfer leg of the Fund deposit as the production path does; a host-module omission in that path is a repair within the task touches."

[gotcha.3303]
title = "22.37.1 attempt 1: the layout driver test passes (6 cases) and the carried driver 0_8.py answers status BLOCKED with 3 assertions, 2 missing evidence kinds (the nonpublishing release startup and the prepared image) and no regression, exiting 2 (line 439 of the driver); the missing kinds are the live parts the series leaves UNRUN under decision 2700, so the verify failed on an outcome the series expects."
symptom = "The carried drivers distinguish BLOCKED (exit 2, missing live evidence) from FAIL (exit 1, a regression); the verify command treated both as failure."
fix = "A verify that runs a carried driver accepts exit 2 and refuses exit 1 (decision 2703); the task record names the missing evidence kinds."

[gotcha.3304]
title = "22.37.16, 22.37.19, 22.37.20 and 22.37.22 attempt 1: every pnpm typecheck or vitest run of the series stopped on modules the vendored tree generates or links at install time: the generated profile module of the process utilities library, the generated theme and export manifest of the plugin build package, the generated templates package, the domain package and the control-plane dependencies (Cannot find module pg, implicit any across src/agents and src/artifacts); 22.37.22 also lost the generated contracts module the control-plane build script copies under src because the build never ran before the native actor compile."
symptom = "The qualification environment installs the repository root node packages only; the vendored tree has two package managers (the control-plane package outside the pnpm package set with its own lock, gotcha 3299, and a pnpm workspace of 111 projects whose install runs the root prepare generation for the templates, plugin build and server packages in about 100 seconds) and the process utilities generate script sits outside that prepare filter."
fix = "Every series build command prepares the vendored tree explicitly (decision 2705): pnpm install with the frozen lockfile, the process utilities generate script, then the control-plane npm ci and build."

[gotcha.3305]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 1: the chunk-root boundary leaves build and the ten market tests pass, then the carried suite program_replay fails actual_module_start_refuses_unobservable_start_state (tests/program_replay.rs line 208): a module-start snapshot with capture enabled now answers Ok where the engine must map the observer refusal to UnreachableExecuted; the agent repaired it by refusing module-start snapshots before the profiled entry invocation, the repair compiled, and the gate ledger had no verify run left, so the 128-call proof never ran."
symptom = "The streamed capture replaced capture_program_record_from_store and started observing before the pre-start refusal the engine relies on; the final tree carries the repair unverified."
fix = "Requalify the final tree as it stands; the module-start assertion stays."

[gotcha.3306]
title = "22.31.217 attempt 8: 12 cases pass and 6 fail. Three Snapshot refusals (lines 1461, 1564 and 1629) come from read_native_effect_budget_sources (budget/program_sources.rs line 564) refusing caps.level() below STATE_PROVEN while CommittedCaps::level answers the retired CHECKPOINT_FINALISED (read/committed.rs lines 166 and 420), which the lattice orders below every current level (verify.rs compare): decision 2694 already assigns that repair to 22.31.560, so the three cases wait on it. Two MalformedPayload refusals (line 769) route the deploy and exitValue constructs through prepare_bound, which the binder table (layerx-crypto disclosure/call.rs lines 102 to 127) does not contain, as the attempt-7 ruling already said. One MalformedPayload refusal (line 549) is the create-source construct encoded by the production ABI encoder and refused by the production binder; the refusing word is not yet named."
symptom = "The level refusal is the producer defect of decision 2694, not a fixture matter; the two lifecycle constructs must never meet the binder; the create-source refusal needs the binder word index before any repair."
fix = "Continue after 22.31.560 with the three case classes separated; the create-source probe names the word or records a producer-to-consumer defect."

[gotcha.3307]
title = "22.37.21 attempt 1: the first control-plane build stopped on TS7034 and TS7005 (the validated legacy-map array at import.ts lines 1012 and 1042 without an element type) and the repaired build passed; the verify driver 5_2.py then reached the contribution checks and the strict deep-equality assertion at line 598 of the native source import actor failed although every field matched: the candidate scope read back through the source HTTP transport is a null-prototype object while the actor compares it with a plain object literal. The agent changed both sides of that comparison to canonical bytes, rebuilt (exit 0) and had no verify run left."
symptom = "The canonical JSON decoder of the source contracts module builds every object with Object.create(null) (contracts.ts line 113), so anything that crosses the transport comes back without a prototype; assert.deepEqual under node:assert/strict is deepStrictEqual and compares prototypes before fields. The decoder behaviour is deliberate (no prototype pollution) and is not a defect."
fix = "Proofs over transport-decoded source objects compare canonical content (decision 2706); the attempt tree requalifies as it stands."

[gotcha.3308]
title = "22.37.9 attempt 1: the control-plane build passed twice; the first verify stopped on a missing expected rejection at line 199 of the objects storage fixture (a test-input mistake the agent corrected); the second verify passed the 1_1.py component run (COMPONENT_PASS, 18 assertion groups, the 4096-entry patch metrics) and then the 0_1.py driver of the source-control cases raised FileNotFoundError for /root/.nvm/versions/node/v24.22.0/bin/node, the default it uses when its node override variable is unset; the qualification environment provides node 24.22.0 on the path under a different prefix."
symptom = "Six drivers of the source-control cases carry that home-directory path of the original author as a literal or as the default of an environment override (0_1.py line 119, 1_3.py line 125, 2_2.py line 191, 0_4.py line 96, 0_14_live.py line 23, 0_14_setup.py line 17); 0_8.py line 180 already resolves node through the override or shutil.which. The series gates of 22.37.8, 22.37.9, 22.37.11, 22.37.13 and 22.37.7 run the drivers with the literal path and would all stop the same way."
fix = "Drivers resolve node from the override variable they already read, else shutil.which on the path, and fail with a named message when neither resolves (decision 2707); the owners of the drivers make the change and 22.37.9 requalifies after 22.37.8."

[gotcha.3309]
title = "22.37.23 attempt 2 and 22.37.24 attempt 2: with the corrected build commands both builds passed and both verifies passed (the 6_1.py component drill with PROCESS_LOSS and PRIMARY_INSTANCE_LOSS PASS, FAILURE_DOMAIN_LOSS UNRUN; the 6_2.py workload checks), then the graph check refused the task because every entry of its symbols list is a file name (6_1.py, native_source_recovery_actor.mjs, routing.ts; campaign.mjs, native_source_external_workload.mjs, native_source_workload.mjs, storage_observer.mjs) and no such symbol exists in the graph; the agents correctly declined to edit the task record."
symptom = "All 27 symbols lists of the series 22.37.1 to 22.37.27 were written as file names when the series was authored; the graph check (spec.c line 4000) resolves each entry as a code symbol, and 3593 landed tasks carry an empty symbols list, which the check accepts. The live attempts 22.37.1 a2, 22.37.19 a2, 22.37.20 a2 and 22.37.22 a2 carry the old lists in their trees and will be refused the same way after a passing verify."
fix = "Every series symbols list becomes empty (decision 2708); the two attempts requalify on their trees and the live ones requalify as they report."

[gotcha.3310]
title = "22.37.16 attempt 2: the corrected build command passed (pnpm install, the profile module, the control-plane build) and the verify stopped at line 13 of the native source graph actor of the support directory: readFile of the vendored root path named like the project raised ENOENT; the graph actor, the signed transport, the qualification lanes and the roster graph scope of the support directory all execute that root binary, which the vendored tree ignores (.gitignore line 45) and the default make target builds from core/native with the tree-sitter runtime (Makefile lines 13 to 35: BIN and the cg compatibility alias, linked against sqlite3, curl and crypto)."
symptom = "The vendored project ships its CLI as a built artefact, never as a checked-in file; the series build commands prepared the packages (decision 2705) but not the native CLI, so the drivers of 22.37.16 (3_3.py), 22.37.18 (4_2.py), 22.37.19 (4_3.py) and 22.37.26 (7_1.py, which packages the root binary through release.sh) cannot run."
fix = "Those four build commands build the default make target of the vendored tree before the package steps that need it (decision 2709); the qualification environment provides the C headers the link needs; 22.37.16 attempt 2 requalifies on its tree."

[gotcha.3311]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 2: the build command passed the control-plane build and the host-daemon typecheck, then the source-control plugin typecheck reported 26 errors in app.tsx: TS2307 on the app entry of the plugin SDK package at line 6 and TS7006 implicit any on every parameter typed through it; the task record calls the declarations pre-existing and missing; no verify ran."
symptom = "The plugin SDK package (sdk/plugins of the vendored tree) exports its types from a bundled-types directory that Git ignores (.gitignore line 96) and that its build:types script produces with rollup over the sources; the plugin resolves the SDK through the package exports to that bundle, and a direct pnpm filter typecheck runs tsrs without the turbo dependency on the SDK type bundle that turbo.json declares for other consumers (lines 26, 32 and 554)."
fix = "The build command builds the SDK type bundle before the plugin typecheck (decision 2710)."

[gotcha.3312]
title = "22.37.22 attempt 2: the build passed twice; the first verify stopped on an authorization request that omitted the path its capability covered (corrected); the second reached the quiesce case and the isolation observer answered LEGACY_VISIBILITY_UNAVAILABLE, Cannot inspect every visible process storage handle and mapping; the final driver adjustment (no extra user namespace when the driver runs as root) is unverified."
symptom = "The observer in core/control-plane/src/migration/legacy.ts enumerates every pid of /proc and, for a pid that still exists, maps every error other than ENOENT on its stat, namespace link, mountinfo, descriptors or maps to that refusal without naming the pid, the file or the error code (line 187), so the record cannot say what was uninspectable; the 5_3.py driver re-executes itself as pid 1 of a private pid namespace with a private /proc and reaps no orphan, so a grandchild that outlives its parent stays listed as defunct, and a defunct process has no namespace link or mountinfo (ENOENT and EINVAL on a pid that still exists)."
fix = "The refusal detail names the pid, the file and the error code; a defunct process (state Z or X in its stat) is skipped since it holds no descriptor or mapping; the driver reaps orphans as pid 1 (decision 2711)."

[gotcha.3313]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 2 (the attempt-1 tree under the corrected environment): build, dependent-crate check and the earlier suites passed; two cases of repair_22_31_577.rs failed at lines 157 and 352 with EngineFault program replay record refused: Bounds while executing the 128-call guest under a profile of 4096 boundaries and 1048576 bytes; the task record is empty on the point."
symptom = "ReplayWitnessError::Bounds is raised at nine capture sites (the leaf count and byte appends of from_captured in replay_record.rs, the remaining-bytes, fuel-sum and step-index checks after captured_leaf in execute.rs around lines 1154 to 1196, the leaf decode) and the fault reason built at execute.rs line 1086 prints only the variant, so the record cannot say which bound a 128-boundary capture of a 17-page memory crossed."
fix = "The fault reason names the refusing check with its numbers; a boundary leaf carries the chunk root and the chunks the step changed, never the pre memory the previous leaf rebuilds (decision 2712)."

[gotcha.3314]
title = "22.37.20 attempt 2: the build passed twice after a PostgreSQL regex constraint repair; the second verify failed at native_source_git_actor.mjs line 1057 where assert.deepEqual compares the publication the SDK client decoded (a null-prototype object) with the service object the resume returned; the plugin tests were not reached."
symptom = "Decision 2706 applies: the canonical JSON decoder of the transport yields null-prototype objects (contracts.ts line 113) and strict deep equality distinguishes them from service objects."
fix = "The proof compares canonical bytes; the actor is audited for every other strict deep equality between a client result and a service object."

[gotcha.3315]
title = "22.37.11 attempt 2: the build command (install, the profile module, the control-plane npm ci) reached the control-plane build and tsc reported TS2305 in audit.ts line 4: the contracts module has no exported member PRIVATE_AGENT_GROUP_CONTEXT_FIELDS, then TS7006 at line 59; the task record says the build overwrites the control-plane contracts module from an SDK file outside its scope and that it removed the copy step; no verify ran."
symptom = "The control-plane build script (the contracts copy step under scripts, called first by its build) copies sdk/source-control/src/contracts.ts over src/source_control/contracts.ts before tsc; the two files are byte-identical on main, so the control-plane copy is a generated file, and the attempt authored about 1250 lines into the copy that the build replaces; the task touches only the copy."
fix = "The source-control contracts module is authored in the SDK package and the control-plane copy is generated (decision 2713); 22.37.11 touches the SDK source and keeps the copy step."

[gotcha.3316]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 11 (the attempt-10 tree over the landed 22.31.579): build and dependent-crate check passed; two cases of repair_22_33_1510 failed: the approvals case at line 240 with InboxError LifecycleMismatch while consuming the Rejected event of approval 2 after approval_decide(false) answered Rejected, and the decide case at line 504 with Refused on approval_get of approval 2 after the fixture reopened, the daemon logging approval_get lookup refused: Registry(NotFound) and its recovery reporting queued 0 and awaiting 0; the third case passed and the Corrupt reading of attempt 10 is gone."
symptom = "The inbox lifecycle check (approvals/mod.rs lines 388 to 410) compares the event kind with the state of the record the daemon serves at the event sequence, so the daemon served approval 2 in a state other than Rejected right after deciding it; after reopen (approval_owner.rs line 1002: a fresh store, a new owner from the recorded authority, a new server) the daemon registry has no approval 2 at all, so the decisions and records of the first session are not in the store the reopened owner reads, or the owner does not load them."
fix = "The attempt names the store path where the daemon library writes an approval decision and the reader that misses it after reopen, and repairs the one that is wrong; the inbox check and the recorded authority stand."

[gotcha.3317]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 11: build, dependent-crate check and the first verify ran at an earlier candidate; the verify failed three cases (the owner preview answered a refusal frame, tag byte 1 after the LXHAGT01 magic, at line 598 of the repair test twice, and the loopback peer bootstrap refused at line 918 of the EVM preview test); the attempt then converted the shared preview fixture authorization bounds and purpose expiry to milliseconds (decision 2704) and rebuilt at bb159a15db9db7911d63e604c6071688de760b29, and the engineering process refused a further verify because the repair budget was spent; the final tree has never been verified."
symptom = "The repair budget counts every gate invocation; the correction the attempt made after the failing verify is in the final tree but no gate ran over it."
fix = "Requalify the final tree once; a refusal frame that remains is decoded and named by the next attempt."

[gotcha.3318]
title = "22.37.16 attempt 3: the graph driver passed (component mode PASS) and the plugin test run failed three cases: the bundle test could not resolve the signed entry of the source-control SDK package because its dist/signed.js was never built (the build command builds the control plane and the native components, not the SDK package, and the plugin host imports the signed client on main), and two cases of the core server builtin-registry test that the plugin vitest config includes: the unprefixed bundled plugin id list of the test lacks the source-control plugin id that the registry lists at line 38, and the prepared-artifacts case expects packages/bundled-plugins/dist while the resolver (builtin-registry.ts lines 308 to 313) reads tools/bundled-plugins/dist, the directory that exists on main."
symptom = "The two registry cases are stale on main independent of the task: the test was not moved with the bundled plugins directory nor updated when the source-control plugin was bundled; the bundle case needs the SDK dist that only the SDK build produces."
fix = "A stale core server test is its own repair task (22.31.580) and the graph plugin verify names its own four test files; the build command builds the source-control SDK package before the control plane (decision 2714)."

[gotcha.3319]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 3: the 4_3.py driver failed in the unauthorized-read case at line 316 of the product actor: the read of main.txt with a capability whose path prefix list is [main.txt] and whose actions are the product actions was refused SCOPE_DENIED exactly like the read of private.txt; the refusal details carry only the operation id."
symptom = "The authorization loop (capabilities.ts line 67) matches a capability row by paths when the request carries paths and otherwise only when the row has the empty prefix or the action is metadata-only; the file read of the source API (api.ts line 130) authorizes without paths, so a path-prefixed row never matches and every read through it is refused, allowed path or not."
fix = "The source read actions pass the requested path as paths to the authorization so the prefix decides per path (decision 2715); 22.37.19 applies it to the file read."

[gotcha.3320]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 17: the Go production Fund proof passes with the transfer leg and capability declared (896330 CPU fuel, 635 kernel gas, the expected deposit and balance); the first verify did not compile (WRONG_EPOCH and WRONG_ROSTER not imported in the library test module), the attempt added the import and the second verify failed two Rust cases: the populated Fund test of the library test module (lib.rs line 492) refused with ApplicationError 12, WRONG_EPOCH, and the committed-receipt fixture case (repair_478_fixture.rs line 336) found storage_read_bytes 1114 in the receipt the Go gate wrote where the fixture asserts the program state length 1084."
symptom = "The populated test encodes an admission table opened at epoch 7 into the ReputationAdmission section and sends epoch 7 at the fixture height; WRONG_EPOCH is raised by admission.rs lines 494 (height before the market origin), 713 and 810 (effective epoch mismatch) and 851 (no opened epoch) and by aggregation.rs lines 460 to 467 and 870, and the test has never run before this attempt. With the transfer leg declared the host reads 30 bytes beyond the program state (the terminal usage is recorded at call.c line 1456), and the fixture assertion equates the reads with the state alone."
fix = "The attempt names the refusing epoch site and binds the test state to the epoch Fund reads, and names the 30 bytes the host reads and asserts their sum; no inequality, no library change for the test."

[gotcha.3321]
title = "9.98.4 attempt 5: the build and the dependent-crate check passed (15 crates) and the library verify failed six cases: policy_usage_sums_only_proven_receipts_in_the_window and native_policy_usage_refuses_a_page_without_a_proof stop on HistoryReadError ItemUnproven before any request reaches the history double (human_runtime.rs lines 22718 and 23229); the four retained settlement cases stop at line 23341, the first with the Snapshot refusal and the other three with PoisonError; the attempt diff only carries paymentDenom into the receipt fixtures of human_runtime.rs and the tests directory."
symptom = "read_policy_history (human_runtime.rs lines 22583 to 22597, landed by 22.31.219) requires the native results endpoint URL from the environment and maps its absence to ItemUnproven, while the HistoryRpc double (lines 22969 onward) neither publishes that variable nor answers the commit, validators and block_results queries NativeResultSource issues (read/result_source.rs lines 58, 75, 187 and 204); the 22.31.219 verify ran only its own integration test, so the two library cases have been red on main since then. The retained settlement path reaches the COMMITTED requirement 22.31.538 added (budget/budget_proof.rs line 22) with the CHECKPOINT_FINALISED level CommittedCaps::level still answers (read/committed.rs line 166), the exact defect decision 2694 assigns to 22.31.560; the first panic poisons the ENVIRONMENT lock of the retained settlement module (line 23334) so the three cases after it report PoisonError."
fix = "The history double publishes the results URL under an environment guard and answers the three native queries (decision 2716); the retained settlement cases wait for 22.31.560, which 9.98.4 now requires; CommittedCaps::level and the budget guard are not touched by 9.98.4."

[gotcha.3322]
title = "22.31.580 attempt 1: the two test edits are in place and the build passed; the verify stopped before any case ran with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, exit 1: the core server plugin service imports the process utilities performance diagnostics, which import the generated profile module of the process utilities library, and the install does not produce that module."
symptom = "The 22.31.580 build command ran only the install; the module is produced by the generate script of the process utilities library, which the 22.37.16 build command runs after its install."
fix = "The build command of 22.31.580 runs the generate step after the install (decision 2717); the attempt that follows runs the amended build."

[gotcha.3323]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 12: build and dependent-crate check passed; the approvals case and the snapshot recovery case pass (the inbox event ordering and the reservation expiry sharing the approval deadline); the decide case fails at decide.rs line 511: after the lost-reply reopen approval_get of approval 2 is refused with Registry(NotFound) while the recover path of the expiry record answers Rejected and the fixture reads the persisted decision record (the approval-v1 idempotency key, LocalOnly) from the same store root; the daemon diagnostic before the refusal is approval_get lookup refused: Registry(NotFound)."
symptom = "A rejection goes through finish_claim_releasing (policy/approval.rs line 635) and release_durable (line 1167), which persists the decision record and removes the durable hold in one batch (PreparedDecision::remove_hold, approval/expiry.rs line 316); replay_tenant (approval.rs lines 203 to 279) restores PreparedActivity holds, program terminals and released records (the Approved terminals 22.31.570 added for decision 2672), so a rejected approval leaves no record the registry can replay and ticket, get and list answer NotFound after a restart although decision 2672 promised every decided approval stays known."
fix = "The rejection path replaces the hold with a durable terminal record and replay_tenant restores it in the Rejected state (decision 2718); the repair is inside 22.33.1510, whose touches now include the daemon policy module."

[gotcha.3324]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 12 (requalify of the final tree): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101 with all three cases failed in 0.24 seconds: native_send_preview_is_an_unsigned_ledger_transfer_call panicked at native_send_preview_evm.rs line 171 with bootstrap peer: Os NotFound spawning the local EVM executable, and the two repair cases at repair_22_31_560.rs line 899 with PoisonError from the shared bootstrap; attempt 11 had started the same peer and reached the owner preview."
symptom = "The qualification environment provides the Foundry binaries when the command text names forge, cast or anvil (decision 2068) or when the test target the command names (tests/NAME.rs) carries the LAYERX_TEST_ANVIL marker; repair_22_31_560.rs carries only include!(native_send_preview_evm.rs), and the included file is the one that starts anvil (line 170), so the marker was not seen and no toolchain was provisioned; the attempt-11 run predated that rule of the environment."
fix = "The verify of 22.31.560 opens with anvil --version && (decision 2719, as 2068 did for 18.1233.1) and attempt 12 requalifies on its unchanged tree; the environment rule also follows include and path references of the named target."

[gotcha.3325]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 3 (continue): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0 (58 crates), verify exit 101: every carried suite passes and the two 128-call cases of repair_22_31_577.rs (lines 157 and 359) fail with the named check, capture witness bytes observed 1049624 permitted 1048576 (leaf length 1511) and observed 1048837 (leaf length 1368); the live-snapshot proof asserts exactly 128 changed chunks with at most one per boundary, so the chunk payload is 524288 bytes and the other half of the budget is per-leaf payload of about 2000 bytes over some 257 leaves."
symptom = "A boundary leaf (replay_record.rs captured_leaf_bytes) repeats in every leaf what the record already carries once and what the leaf carries twice: the arbitration identity (versions, trace policy, module code hash, input digest, execution parameters digest, host base state root, receipt oracle root, balance oracle root, about 230 bytes) and the three digests of the legacy execution state duplicate the record header of from_captured; the semantic bytes (host witness, storage witness, payment, composition witness, the shape the market semantic restore at replay.rs line 1977 reads) carry the storage pair and the host meter that the legacy state also carries as storage_overlay and metered usage and that host_state_root commits; the attempt then added an ad hoc LZ-style packing stage (portable_payload_bytes with a window, hash slots and the arbitration bytes as dictionary) to hide the duplication, and the record still crosses the bound by 1048 bytes."
fix = "Decision 2720: constants once in the record header, each datum once in a leaf, no packing stage; the attempt-3 tree continues with the per-leaf field breakdown recorded."

[gotcha.3326]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 13 (requalify with the local EVM provided): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101: native_send_preview_is_an_unsigned_ledger_transfer_call panicked at native_send_preview_evm.rs line 921 with bootstrap peer: Refused from the owner preview call before any assertion, and the two repair cases at repair_22_31_560.rs line 899 with PoisonError from the fixture lock the first case poisoned; the daemon log shows only the recovery lines and no refusing site."
symptom = "The attempt-11 correction (decision 2704) made the fixture authorization bounds milliseconds, so not_before_height and not_after_height of the HumanPrepare are 30000 apart (tests/native_send_preview_evm.rs lines 809 and 810) while the fixture still constructs the production Human operations with a timestamp span of 30 (line 632); native_send_preview_authorization (human_runtime.rs line 21725 of the attempt tree) refuses a bound wider than the span, the comparison the Prepare path makes at prepare/mod.rs line 875, and the preview path maps every refusal to HumanOperationError::Refused without the sited diagnostic decision 2688 gave the Prepare path. Attempt 10 passed the same case with the bounds 30 seconds apart. The span bounds the width of a protocol timestamp bound and the kernel batch timestamp is milliseconds (include/layerx/lxp_kernel.h line 398, batch_timestamp_ms), so the span is milliseconds; the hosted material still writes 60 (services/platform/hosted/human/material.py line 856)."
fix = "Decision 2721: the fixture span becomes 30000, the preview path names its refusing site as the Prepare path does, and 22.31.581 moves the hosted material span to 60000 and documents the unit."

[gotcha.3327]
title = "22.37.26 attempt 1: build exit 0, verify exit 1: the 7_1.py driver builds the native components, then the packaged native source component smoke reports FAIL with the single diagnostic Dependency resolves outside approved installed roots; the diagnostic names neither the file nor the roots, and the check has never passed in the qualification environment."
symptom = "The DEPENDENCIES resolver of the source-control package.py packager under the deploy directory of the vendored tree (resolve, line 82 of the attempt tree, line 80 on main) walks every directory that createRequire resolve.paths returns, which climbs above the vendored tree to the repository root node_modules of the qualification environment, and visit (line 83) follows dependencies, optionalDependencies and peerDependencies; @modelcontextprotocol/sdk in the control-plane lockfile declares an optional JSON schema peer at ^4.1.1, which is installed neither under core/control-plane/node_modules nor under the vendored tree node_modules but is installed at the repository root as 4.1.1, so the closure records a file outside the two approved roots and build (line 140 of the attempt tree, line 118 on main) refuses without naming it. An optional peer absent from the approved roots is rightly omitted; one present above them must not be found."
fix = "Decision 2722: the resolver searches only node_modules directories within the vendored tree, a missing optional dependency is omitted, a missing required one fails naming the package and the requiring file, and the refusal names the escaping file and the approved roots."

[gotcha.3328]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 4: build exit 0 at the final revision (the third build), verify exit 1 at the first revision of the attempt: the product actor unauthorized-read case still received SCOPE_DENIED on the allowed path main.txt; the two repair builds then went to a second denial and the verify never ran again at the final tree."
symptom = "The attempt-3 ruling (gotcha 3319, decision 2715) covered the first denial, the file read authorizing without paths; the attempt-4 tree passes the requested path (api.ts lines 187 and 188 of the attempt tree) and the capability loop then reaches the object check of capabilities.ts lines 69 and 70, which refuses a read carrying an object id under a path-prefixed capability unless an object-reachability authorizer is configured, and the service configures none. The attempt-4 tree adds a path-and-revision read to source.objects.read (api.ts from line 481) that authorizes the path with the revision and resolves the object from that revision; the second repair build passed and the engineering process allots two repair cycles, so no verify run remained."
fix = "Requalify at the final revision; the recorded verify belongs to an earlier tree."

[gotcha.3329]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 19: build exit 0 (two builds), dependent-crate check exit 0 (29 crates), verify exit 1 (two runs): at the final revision the Go proof passes (the FUND operation word at 896330 CPU fuel and 635 kernel gas), the crate library tests pass (10 cases) and two further test binaries pass (24 and 2 cases), then the artifact_binding integration binary fails 13 of 14 cases with ApplicationError(1), the BAD_VERSION code, in 0.01 s; the one passing case, a18_seal_region_codec_bounds, builds no World. The first verify run, at the first revision of the attempt, failed the library case repair478_fund_head_carries_populated_regions_and_epoch_binding and never reached the binary."
symptom = "The artifact_binding source is byte-identical to main, where the suite passes (22.99.77 attempts 16 and 18 ran it: 14 passed). No attempt of 22.31.478 ran it before: cargo test stops at the first failing binary and the library tests failed in every earlier attempt, so the regression travelled unseen through eighteen attempts. The attempt-18 to attempt-19 source difference is only the E0716 repair in lib.rs, so the regression lies in the library changes of this task since its merge-base be624853f195bc6710e07911f600277bcd6cfbf1: rewards.rs (the RecipientDictionary::validate rewrite, RewardState::init no longer decoding, RewardState::fund writing the ledger ahead of the dictionary offset, view splitting the joint section through reputation_transition::split_joint before AdmissionTable::decode, the FundingView and funding_epoch readers that refuse the joint section framing with BAD_VERSION at lines 2377 and 2403), registry.rs (derive_rewards_account through prepare_rewards_account), the routing module (the visible closure and 0x0601 added to the transition bypass list at line 945) and value_adapter.rs. The World of the suite runs production CREATE through registry_ops::apply, then enroll, evaluator, SCHEDULE_ACTIVATION, a direct decode_reward_state fund into a REWARD_STATE_BYTES buffer under FundingPhase::Accepting and FUNDING_POLICY_VERSION, open_epoch, ADMIT_TASK, seal, evidence, tasks and authority; the BAD_VERSION sites on that path are MarketHeader::validate (registry.rs line 104, called from registry_ops.rs line 211 and rewards.rs line 2421), AdmissionTable::decode (admission.rs line 660), the consent decoder (admission.rs line 1148), read_binding (aggregation_codec.rs line 198), the codec schema helper (codec.rs line 432) and funding_epoch (rewards.rs lines 2377 and 2403)."
fix = "Decision 2723: a crate verify runs every test binary with --no-fail-fast; the next attempt runs one World case alone, names the refusing site in the task record and repairs the library so the unchanged suite passes while the task tests stay green."

[gotcha.3330]
title = "22.35.10 attempt 1 and 22.31.577 attempt 4: each attempt built its final tree (the third build) after two repairs, and the single verify run of each attempt belongs to the first revision. 22.35.10 at 7e522f416fbc883cfb611923f21022e430c1ff60: the API spec passed 7 cases and the panel spec failed 4 of 7 (the ask row absent for a question with no matches, the no-results text absent when the assistant is disabled, an entity match answering null, the panel background resolving to transparent instead of the raised token). 22.31.577 at 6fb0b19d39df54c03aca69b0b4ee4b8a2bb0dc88: repair_22_31_577 2 passed and 2 failed, the two 128-call proofs refused with Bounds check=capture witness bytes observed=1050243 and 1052118 over the permitted 1048576."
symptom = "22.35.10: the search fixtures omitted the JSON content-type header the fetch hook requires before it parses a body, and the panel background shorthand did not resolve to the token; the repairs return the JSON header from every fixture and give the panel an explicit background-colour token; the final build (the type check) passed at d8e385529522b154a54743c4a998c803477b0fa9. 22.31.577: the capture witness repeated the immutable ABI authority, the meter parameters, the payment metadata and the metering schedule in every step record; the repair moves them into the record header, rebuilds the usage fields from the host meter and the current storage from baseline plus overlay, and keeps the per-record fields the replay needs; the final build passed at 92a3b8736a87423e7fd2db2494548cb6b477f30f. The engineering process allots two repair cycles, so no verify run remained in either attempt."
fix = "Requalify both at their final revisions; a failure the verify reports at the final tree is the tree and the next ruling starts from it."

[gotcha.3331]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 14: build exit 0 (two builds), dependent-crate check exit 0 (15 crates), verify exit 101 (two runs): at the first revision both native send cases refused at the preview with the print timestamp span exceeded; after the 30000 ms span repair the final revision passes 2 of 3 cases and native_send_first_prepare_and_reopened_prepare_match_owner_preview fails at line 622: the first Prepare after the owner preview answers 403 owner.refused with the print native send prepare refused at approval carrier binding (human_runtime.rs line 7470 of the attempt tree)."
symptom = "The site names only the call. NativeEffectApprovalCarrier::bind (approval/native_effect.rs from line 195) folds its refusals into three codes: Binding covers the disclosure binding, the origin tenant, generation and session, a zero capability or purpose commitment, a protocol version other than 3, the programs module, a reservation whose identity differs from the digest of the canonical bytes, a reservation expiry sequence at or below the observed head sequence, a reservation core deadline that differs from the envelope bound, a failed clock sample and a clock reading in milliseconds at or past the envelope not-after; Policy covers the intent construction and the local policy evaluation; Budget covers the reservation encoding. The attempt-14 tree makes the committed read produce the protocol timestamp in milliseconds (read/committed.rs, decision 2704) and the fixture builds the 30000 ms bound from that head time, while the presentation clock of the fixture is a clock peer sampling its own time; a reading at or past the bound refuses with the same code and the same print as a stale reservation, so the record cannot tell them apart."
fix = "Name every clause of the carrier bind as its own site through the Prepare helper, run the case, repair the input the print names (the fixture clock within the bound or the reservation expiry) and keep the production checks."

[gotcha.3332]
title = "22.37.26 attempt 2: build exit 0 (two builds), verify exit 1 (two runs): the first run at the first revision failed the confined dependency closure with Missing named package string_decoder required by the nested readable-stream of lazystream under the control-plane service node_modules; the repair resolved it and the final revision passes the closure (the repository-only optional peer omitted, string_decoder included), the native component assembly and the reproducibility check, then fails the new specification and claims consistency check with Full assertion inventory absent or reused: SCM-011 before the packaged component smoke."
symptom = "The consistency check the attempt wrote (7_1.py consistency, from line 106) refuses an assertion id that an earlier case already lists (the owners set at line 121) and adds a probe for it (cross-case assertion reuse refused, line 316). No clause of the carried source-control specification makes an assertion id the property of one case: the registry.json of the source-control test support directory lists for SCM-011 the 12 sparse assertions of SCM-010 and 12 virtual ones, the full-SCM-011-full and full-SCM-011-linux-fuse7-real-s3 registration records observe all 24, and workspace_cases.json defines SCM-011 with 24 assertions, because the virtual workspace case exercises sparse materialization before its own checks; 22.37.25 landed the inventory that way. The attempt refused the data it was given on a rule it invented."
fix = "Decision 2724: the consistency check compares each case inventory with its own registration and claim; an assertion id observed by more than one case is not a refusal and the cross-case probe is removed."

[gotcha.3333]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 5 (the requalify of the attempt-4 tree on current main): build exit 0 (two builds), verify exit 1 (two runs). The first run, at e6524bd65bfc5402d71832adfedb77abd6671136, stopped in the product actor at the VIRTUAL open of the product metrics and virtual refusal step: the host client answered INTERNAL_ERROR with the message Source operation failed, retry NEVER, outcome KNOWN. The attempt added the 0747 virtual-workspaces migration to the list the 4_3.py driver hands the fixture, and the final run at 24649c9cb9adfa6e84b08914b861a5c772d6c4a4 passed the open, the publish (QUEUED) and the service metrics, then stopped at the publication cancel (actor line 609) with the same INTERNAL_ERROR, the same message and no cause in the record."
symptom = "The driver hands the fixture a hand-picked migration list (0736 storage to 0743 assurance, 0747 virtual-workspaces, 0753 transfers; the fixture itself adds 0758 event-retention) while the service migration directory of the vendored tree carries the source-control series through 0765; 0746 retention, 0748 graph, 0750 import, 0751 cutover, 0752 recovery, 0754 epoch-adoption, 0755 final-delta, 0756 bootstrap-issuances, 0757 candidate-queue, 0759 recovery-effects, 0760 native-assurance-registration, 0764 publication-credentials, 0765 import-legacy-maps and three further files of the series never run under this driver. The publication cancel (the git export service, cancel from line 1048 of the attempt tree) settles the credential debt in its finally clause by selecting credential_state and cleanup_debt from the source_git_publications table; both columns are added by 0764, so the select refuses with an undefined column and the request handler catch of core/control-plane/src/source_control/http.ts (line 86) maps every error that is not a SourceControlError, a StorageError or a FoundationError to INTERNAL_ERROR with the fixed message Source operation failed and records nothing about the cause. The first-run failure was the same class: the VIRTUAL open read a schema that 0747 adds. The attempt repaired the one file the first failure named and never asked why the list exists."
fix = "Decision 2725: the fixture applies every migration of the source-control series whose keys resolve within the series, in name order, unless a driver names a subset with its reason, and the request handler catch records the underlying error with its name, message, code and stack and the action and operation id to the process standard error before mapping it; the next attempt repairs the driver and the catch, runs the actor alone and names the first refusing operation and its recorded cause in the task record."

[gotcha.3334]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 15: build exit 0 (two builds), dependent-crate check exit 0 (15 crates), verify exit 101: 2 of 3 cases pass and native_send_first_prepare_and_reopened_prepare_match_owner_preview fails at line 622 with 403 owner.refused; the helper the attempt added (human_runtime.rs lines 7467 to 7510 of the attempt tree) now prints the clause, native send prepare refused at approval carrier reservation identity. The agent record calls the carrier out of scope and stops."
symptom = "NativeEffectApprovalCarrier::bind (approval/native_effect.rs lines 212 and 220, unchanged from main) refuses a reservation whose id differs from the SHA-256 digest of the canonical bytes of the protocol envelope. Every caller of bind on main keys its reservation request by the preparation identifier (ProgramReservationRequest id at human_runtime.rs lines 5944, 6965 and 7438), and decision 2634 makes that identifier the digest of the unsigned EVM call the owner preview publishes as purpose.preparation_id, which verify_native_owner_send_purpose (capability/binding.rs from line 3922) recomputes from the transaction the Prepare built and compares before bind runs; the restore path (human_runtime.rs line 4005) compares the restored reservation witness with the same identifier. The envelope digest and the call digest are digests of different byte strings, so the clause refuses every genuine native send; it dates from issue 1199, before decision 2634 named the single identifier, and no earlier attempt reached it because an earlier clause or a transport refusal came first."
fix = "Decision 2726: bind takes the preparation identifier and binds the reservation id to it; the envelope digest no longer stands in for it; native_effect.rs joins the task touches."

[gotcha.3335]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 5 (the requalify of the attempt-4 tree): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 1: every carried suite passes (10, 4, 9, 4 and 2 cases) and the two 128-call proofs fail at the capture bound, profiled_executor_admits_128_distinct_chunk_writes_in_17_wasm_pages with capture witness bytes observed 1049962 permitted 1048576 at a 5061-byte leaf, and boundary_roots_rebuild_every_live_snapshot_and_authenticate_middle_step_memory with observed 1048801 at a 593-byte leaf. The verify log prints the measured middle boundary (step 456) in the final layout: prefix 31, header binding 32, arbitration 4320 (legacy 4216 of which memory 4140, engine 54, host commitment 40), semantic 216, frames 21, instruction 5, fuel expansion 16, supplement 48, trap 1, leaf total 4698, header total 1021."
symptom = "The 128 chunk leaves carry 4140 bytes of memory each (529920 bytes, half the budget) and every leaf, chunk or not, repeats two record constants: the 31-byte boundary domain prefix and the 32-byte binding of the record header digest, 63 bytes in each of roughly 930 leaves, about 58 kilobytes, against overages of 1386 and 225 bytes. The record already carries the header once and every leaf is decoded with it (from_captured decodes each leaf through decode_with_header; the task record states that individual boundary transport requires the record header), so the per-leaf copies bind nothing the record root does not bind. The profile maximum 1048576 is MAX_PROGRAM_REPLAY_BYTES, the kernel maximum, and does not move."
fix = "Decision 2727: the boundary domain and the header binding are record constants carried once in the record witness; a leaf carries neither; the two proofs then fit with margin."

[gotcha.3336]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 6: build exit 0, verify exit 1: the default migration set of the native source fixture helper now applies every source-control file numbered 0736 or higher whose foreign keys resolve within the series, the listener catch records a source_request_failed event with name, message, code, stack, action and operation id, and the publication cancel passes; the product actor then fails at line 615, where it asserts that the graphs family reports coverage UNAVAILABLE, against the actual COMPLETE. The agent record calls the assertion inherited and leaves it unchanged."
symptom = "The control-plane metrics sampler (core/control-plane/src/source_control/metrics.ts) answers coverage UNAVAILABLE with observed_rows 0 at line 115 only when the family table is absent, and PARTIAL or COMPLETE at line 202 by the per-family row budget once the table exists; the graphs family reads the table the 0748 migration creates. The assertion was written by an earlier attempt under the hand-picked driver list that omitted 0748, so it asserted the absence of a table the service always has; under decision 2725 the driver proves the schema the service runs, where the graphs family samples its table as the objects family at line 614 does."
fix = "Decision 2728: a consumer assertion on a metrics family takes the value of the schema the driver proves; the absent-table branch is proven, when a task needs it, by an explicit migration list that omits the family migration and states the reason."

[gotcha.3337]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 20: build exit 0 (two builds), dependent-crate check exit 0 (29 crates), verify exit 1 (two runs): the Go production Fund proof passes at 896330 CPU fuel and 635 kernel gas, the 10 library tests pass, and the crate-wide run reports 17 failing test binaries; 12 of them fail at AdmissionTable::decode (admission.rs line 660) with ApplicationError(1), BAD_VERSION, from the first enrol of their fixtures, and the agent record names the cause: the test loaders decode the ReputationAdmission section with AdmissionTable::decode while CREATE (registry_ops.rs line 601) writes it as the joint section of reputation_transition::encode_joint, and registry_ops.rs, admission.rs and tests/artifact_binding.rs are byte-identical to main. The other five are the native harness binaries (the manifest under build/paxai-host-boundary is absent because the task build does not run the make target that writes it), the chain-domain case (option_env PAXAI_CHAIN_DOMAIN unset in the qualification environment) and the routed fuel-cap case."
symptom = "Gotcha 3329 and the basis of decision 2723 were wrong: the artifact_binding suite does not pass on main. The runs cited (22.99.77 attempts 16 and 18) ran on trees that carry a different registry_ops.rs, admission.rs and tests/artifact_binding.rs; the 22.99.77 loader splits the joint section with split_joint before AdmissionTable::decode, and every 22.99.77 tree from attempt 10 on differs from main in those files. On main the consumer tests of the crate were never ported to the joint section the producer writes, so the 12 binaries are red on main, not on this task, and the port lives in the 22.99.77 tree. The native, chain-domain and routed fuel-cap cases are the subject of 22.99.77 as well: its attempts 16 and 18 fail exactly one f03 native case, nine host_boundary native cases, the routed fuel-cap case and two rewards_native cases."
fix = "Decision 2729: the 22.31.478 verify names the proof the task owns (the library tests and a Fund fuel case of its own); the crate-wide run stays the gate of 22.99.77, whose tree carries the consumer port."

[gotcha.3338]
title = "22.36.4 attempt 1: build exit 0, verify exit 1 after two repairs: five of the six audit tests pass (the nine files moved to docs/explorer, the links resolve, the validator and reporter sources name the new path, the pull request template heading); the tracked-references test fails on two files outside the task touches, services/explorer/deploy/env/frontend.example.env line 11 and the README.md of the service-definitions directory under services/explorer/deploy at line 214, both of which still name apps/explorer/docs/ENVS.md. The agent record calls them out of scope and stops."
symptom = "The touches list named the files the task record found; the two deployment files reference the moved catalogue and were not listed."
fix = "The two files join the touches; attempt 2 rewrites the remaining references to docs/explorer paths."

[gotcha.3339]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 16: build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0 (15 crates), verify exit 101: two of three cases pass; the first Prepare after the owner preview (request 80) answers 403 owner.refused, and the printed clauses are approval carrier validation envelope preparation identity, approval carrier error Corrupt and approval carrier binding. The agent record names the cause: NativeEffectApprovalCarrier::bind now stores the reservation identifier (the unsigned-call digest of the signed purpose) as the carrier preparation field, while validate (approval/native_effect.rs line 427) and the site mapping in bind (lines 346 to 350) still require that field to equal the SHA-256 digest of the authorization envelope canonical bytes; the two canonical objects are distinct real objects and cannot share a digest. The attempt also moved the fixture runtime clock to the authenticated checkpoint timestamp after the first verify refused at the clock bound."
symptom = "Decision 2726 moved the reservation identity clause of bind to the preparation identifier but left the validate self-check that derived the identifier from the envelope; the carrier binds the envelope through the decode of its canonical bytes, the authority and the expiry comparison at lines 439 to 445, so the digest equality is a leftover of the envelope-derived identifier and not an independent invariant."
fix = "Attempt 17 removes the digest equality clause and its site mapping, keeps every other predicate, and names the next printed clause if one refuses."

[gotcha.3340]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 7: build exit 0, verify exit 1: the product actor passes the corrected metrics check (graphs coverage and row budget, decision 2728) and the run reaches the browser journey, which stops with spawn ENOENT: the browser support module of the vendored product test support directory spawns the headless browser at the absolute path /opt/chromium/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell, a path of the vendored product own continuous-integration image, and the qualification environment has no browser there. The agent record calls it a pre-existing environment dependency and stops without a repair."
symptom = "The vendored tree assumes its own image layout; only 22.37.19 among the open tasks runs that browser support, and the earlier attempts never reached the journey because the actor failed first."
fix = "Decision 2730: the engineering process provides the headless browser at the path the browser support names before the gates run (the runtime libraries, the chrome-headless-shell build fetched with @puppeteer/browsers and linked at /opt/chromium/chrome-headless-shell-linux64), bounded, recorded and never fatal; attempt 8 requalifies the attempt-7 tree."

[gotcha.3341]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 6: build exit 0 (three builds), dependent-crate check exit 0 (58 crates), verify exit 101 after two repairs: every carried suite passes (program_replay, repair_22_31_259, repair_22_31_564, repair_22_31_569, the library market tests), the per-leaf prefix and header binding of decision 2727 are removed (middle step 456 measures 4635 bytes, header 1021 bytes, prefix 0, header_binding 0), and two cases of repair_22_31_577 fail: the profiled executor still refuses capture witness bytes observed 1049404 against permitted 1048576 at leaf length 4998 (execute.rs line 1104), and the live-snapshot proof faulted in its adjudicator guest because recompiling the validated module in the same engine shifted the compiled function identifiers that native execute_step compares with the captured legacy frame identifiers; the second repair shares the captured module through one Rc<ProgramCatalog> and built, but the repair budget was spent before a verify of that tree. The agent record names the remaining layout fact: the composed executor leaf carries the call graph in both the runtime semantic witness and the composition semantic witness, while the single-program capture carries an empty composition (2 bytes)."
symptom = "The semantic replay source (CapturedSemanticReplayV2 in replay.rs) already holds a CompositionReplayWitnessV1 (code hash, revision and graph replay state, optional failure graph) beside the host, storage and authority witnesses, and the leaf encodes a second composition semantic field with the same witness; for a composed execution each leaf therefore carries the graph replay state twice, which at 128 boundaries exceeds the unchanged 1048576-byte profile by 828 bytes."
fix = "Decision 2731: a leaf carries each semantic witness once; the second field binds the 32-byte digest of the witness it would repeat. Attempt 7 verifies the shared-catalog repair and applies the single-carry rule to the composition witness."

[gotcha.3342]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 8 (requalify under the corrected environment): the qualification environment now provides the headless browser (present after 52 s of provisioning) and the browser journey ran in a gate for the first time; it passed the checkpoint, diff pagination, merge conflict, qualification and acceptance steps and stopped after the acceptance at Timed out: button Refresh workspace, with the Workspace panel in the Open state and an empty Workspace field."
symptom = "The journey field helper picks the first label whose text starts with the requested name; on the Workspace panel the Workspace mode select label (workspace-detail.tsx line 256) precedes the Workspace input label (line 390), so filling Workspace wrote the workspace id into the mode select, the Workspace input stayed empty and the Refresh workspace button stays disabled while that field is empty (line 406). Two other calls rely on the same prefix rule because their labels carry a parenthetical suffix: Independent evidence IDs (one per line) and Expected remote Git identity (empty for new reference)."
fix = "The helper matches the label own text node exactly and the two suffixed calls name the full label text (decision 2732); the view labels stay."

[gotcha.3343]
title = "18.1562.1 attempt 16: build exit 0 (three builds, two repairs), verify exit 1: the authority receipt proof TestAiMarketTransferAuthorityReceipt passed the ordinary and account-bound decoder checks and stopped at sequencer_receipt_vectors_test.go line 1873: the source-built AI market guest measures 586929 bytes against the 524288-byte native deployment payload (104-byte envelope included) because the fixture built the guest with opt-level z alone. The final tree adds the production optimisation pass of the Makefile target paxai-host-boundary-build (wasm-opt -Oz --strip-debug --strip-producers, lines 2984 to 2987) to the fixture, but the repair budget was spent before a second verify, and the qualification environment did not provide wasm-opt for this task because its commands name neither the target nor the tool."
symptom = "The payload bound is the protocol maximum LXP_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES (lxp_protocol.h line 14) and is never raised (decision 2675); the production target enforces 524184 bytes after wasm-opt and passed that check in qualification at 22.99.77 attempt 19 (build exit 0), so the optimised guest fits and the fixture must deploy the same artifact it does."
fix = "The fixture mirrors the production recipe exactly and requires wasm-opt with the same named refusal as the Makefile; the qualification environment provides the tool for this proof (decision 2733)."

[gotcha.3344]
title = "22.33.223 attempt 9 (requalify after 22.31.478): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 1 after two repairs: 13 of 14 cases pass, FUND now measures 841651 fuel and the compiled close, restart and retry journey passes; every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap, which repair_22_33_223.rs includes from fuel_budget.rs by path, still fails because the maximum-state executions of twelve routed operations are refused over the 1000000 CPU cap (334 refusals, attempted values 1000001 to 1000234: CANCEL_TASK and ADMIT_TASK 64 each, SealEvidence, RevealScore and CommitScore 8 each, ProcessAggregation 4, BeginAggregation 3, OPEN_EPOCH and FinalizeAggregation 2 each, SEAL_TASK_SET, READ_STATE_CHUNK and READ_HEADER once)."
symptom = "Decision 2729 made the crate-wide fuel suite the gate of 22.99.77, whose tree brings the over-cap operations under the cap through the joint-section readers; both tasks sat in wave 1, so the dependency could not be expressed and 22.33.223 kept re-measuring a cap repair it does not own."
fix = "22.33.223 moves to wave 2 and requires 22.99.77; it requalifies on the attempt-9 tree once 22.99.77 lands and repairs only what its own coverage still shows."

[gotcha.3345]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 9: build exit 0, verify exit 1 after two repairs: the browser journey passes end to end (checkpoint, pagination, merge, acceptance, publication, exported state, transfers, metrics, the fifteen screenshots) and the product checks pass; the verify then runs the signed CLI journey, whose first command, open of the base revision with main.txt as read and write path and no dependency paths, exits 1 (native_source_product_signed_cli.mjs line 97: 1 is not 0)."
symptom = "The readiness function the task added to the runtime module of the source-control plugin (runtime.ts, sourceClosureReadiness) builds its required set from the read paths plus the dependency paths and refuses the open with DEPENDENCY_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE when any is absent from the revision tree; the signed CLI journey opens an empty base tree to create main.txt at its first checkpoint, a flow the product admitted before the task, so a read or write scope path a workspace is about to create cannot be a closure requirement."
fix = "The required set is the declared dependency paths alone; read paths define scope, and a dependency path outside that scope or absent from the tree makes the closure incomplete (decision 2734)."

[gotcha.3346]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 7: build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0 (58 crates), verify exit 101 after two repairs: every carried suite and the new composition digest case pass, the live-snapshot proof admits 128 calls at leaf total 1041745 and record total 1046552, and the executor proof is refused at step 734 with capture witness bytes 1048815 against 1048576 (239 over) at leaf length 853: arbitration 235 (legacy 131 with a 40-byte memory section and no changed chunk, engine 54, host commitment 40), frames 24, instruction 6, fuel expansion 16, supplement 48, semantic 515 (host source 382, storage 89, composition digest 32), header 988."
symptom = "Decision 2731 folded the composition witness into the host source, so the 382-byte host source is now the largest per-leaf semantic field; ReplayHostWitnessV1 (replay.rs line 351) still carries in every leaf the 32-byte program code hash, the optional ABI bytes, the meter state and the storage baseline, and the composition witness inside it repeats the code hash and the ABI revision, although the record header of decision 2720 binds the program identity, the ABI authority and the semantic storage baseline once per record; the agent stopped at the finding as its own attempt-7 plan required."
fix = "Decision 2735: a leaf host witness carries no field equal to a record constant; the decoder restores the header value; the executor proof is measured again under the unchanged profile."

[gotcha.3347]
title = "22.31.539 attempt 6 (requalify after 22.31.560): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101 with the same two failures as attempt 5: the library suite and five test targets pass; agent_register_prepares_bind_layerx is refused with PolicyRefusal owner.refused (403 against 200, bootstrap_bind_layerx.rs line 704) and session_open_prepares_grant_session_for_the_session_address falls to the poisoned fixture lock at line 880."
symptom = "The attempt-5 ruling assumed the refusal was the native send purpose digest 22.31.560 repairs; 22.31.560 is on main and the refusal is unchanged, so that assumption was wrong. Every refusal on the bootstrap path collapses into owner.refused through owner_error: bootstrap_authority (the routing module, line 299) refuses on a principal tenant or agent mismatch, on native_purpose_owner (human_runtime.rs line 5097: the permit boundary, a peer without subject or uid 0, a peer tenant or origin session mismatch, a subject identity that is frozen, below COMMITTED, whose head differs from the chain head the owner reads through operations.chain.head().number, whose revocation sequence is 0 or above the head, or whose authorities lack the primary key), on a missing or closed session record, a generation, authority_ref, client or policy mismatch, and the operation refuses when the node chain id differs from the configured 125; the fixture serves identity head 50 and the retired label checkpoint_finalised, which the tree maps to COMMITTED."
fix = "The next attempt names the refusing condition before repairing anything: instrument each refusal site on that path for one diagnostic run, record the condition, remove the instrumentation, then repair the production fact or the fixture it names."

[gotcha.3348]
title = "18.1562.1 attempt 17 (continue after decision 2733): the qualification environment installed binaryen (wasm-opt version 120) in 13 seconds; build exit 0; two verify runs, both exit 1 in TestAiMarketTransferAuthorityReceipt: the production-optimised guest now fits the 524288-byte payload and the first run reached FUND, which the producer refused as LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL because the fixture paid fees from the reward asset and ran CREATE and FUND in one block; after that repair the second run reached the post-finalisation balance anchor at line 811 (called from line 1923), where the ABI5 account re-registration with profile 2 is refused as LXP_ERR_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED; the agent corrected the re-registration to profile 1 in the final commit 0ffe1e9e3315f83c8147f3e901364b11216d79f7 but the repair budget was spent, so that tree has no verify run."
symptom = "Profile 2 is the ABI2 opt-in profile; an ABI5 re-registration of an existing binding carries profile 1 and preserves the opt-in, as repair_478_test.go line 322 registers the rewards binding; the fixture had copied the opt-in profile into the re-registration."
fix = "Decision 2736 records the profile rule; the attempt requalifies on its final tree, which already carries the correction."

[gotcha.3349]
title = "18.1562.1 attempt 18 (requalify at bf312fc2181bb527cab3d5cc8602bfa30d55e2a0): build exit 0, verify exit 1 after one run: the profile-1 re-registration of decision 2736 passes and TestAiMarketTransferAuthorityReceipt now refuses the FUND call at rpc/sequencer_receipt_vectors_test.go line 839 (reached from line 1925) with execution reverted, call committed runtime fixture LXP_ERR_FEE_UNPAYABLE, kernel gas allowance 10000000, EVM gas used 88480."
symptom = "The kernel refuses FEE_UNPAYABLE before it computes any fee whenever the actor spendable fee balance is below the fee limit of the call (src/protocol/lxp_fee.c lines 231 to 236 and lxp_fee_policy.c lines 22 to 25). The fixture gives the main account 100000000 in the fee asset (lines 598 and 614; in the reward case the fee asset is the occupancy asset, line 603) and every program call carries a fee limit of 100000000 (lines 683, 782 and 831): CREATE at line 782 passed the same check, then its own fee, the occupancy settlement at line 800 and the account read activity at line 811 charged the account below the limit, so FUND cannot clear it whatever its computed fee. The production occupancy proof rpc/repair_478_test.go gives the actor 1000000000 (lines 217 and 227) under the same 100000000 fee limit (line 235)."
fix = "Carry the production balance 1000000000 at lines 598 and 614 (decision 2737); the fee limits stay."

[gotcha.3350]
title = "22.31.217 attempt 9 at 9303d75302808e2710a4d0b3a72aa09a880866cd: build 1 exit 101, build 2 exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0 over 15 crates, verify exit 1 at the verified tree: 12 passed, 6 failed; four cases refuse SourceOwnership from read_native_effect_budget_sources after the fee snapshot passed at the Committed level (the reservation, sources, settlement and checkpoint cases) and the deploy and wind_down_exit lifecycle cases stop where read_signed_native_execution_observation answers Receipt; the final repair corrected the corpus burn account to the authenticated one and produced reservations through the real allocator, but its build (build 3, exit 101) fails because the reservation case calls BudgetLimiter::bind_program_denominations from the integration test (test line 933), a pub(super) method of src/budget/reserve.rs line 1209."
symptom = "read_signed_native_execution_observation (src/budget/program_settlement.rs lines 413 to 445) decodes the signed call, asks the case endpoint for the receipt of its transaction hash and answers Receipt when the endpoint serves none, serves a Submitted observation, or serves a receipt whose from, to or nonce differ from the call; the corpus serves the checkpoint answers only (checkpoint-answers.json), no receipt for any lifecycle transaction, and the native-program-*-v4.json captures are codec conformance captures without execution evidence. The private binder is reached in production only through install_program_enrolment_denominations and install_enrolment_renewals (src/budget/mod.rs lines 885 and 460), which bind from a VerifiedProgramBudgetDenominations of the enrolment module."
fix = "Serve a Receipted observation per lifecycle case in the node layout of decision 2648 with the from, to and nonce of the signed call, produce any account-status proof or retained approval entry the later verifications read through the production encoders, and bind the reservation denominations through install_program_enrolment_denominations."

[gotcha.3351]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 8 (continue, decision 2735) at 8b8f7f4246c2a20e64ed8dc46263ad1d19dd8a41: build exit 0, 58 dependent-crate checks exit 0, verify exit 1 after one run: every carried suite passes and the live-snapshot proof admits 128 calls with leaf_total 1027329 and record_total 1032152 under the 4096 by 1048576 profile, while the executor proof refuses the capture at step 743 with witness bytes observed 1052740 against 1048576 (4164 over) and a leaf of 4918 bytes; the task record now carries both leaf breakdowns."
symptom = "The two breakdowns are for the same calls and the same profile. The live-snapshot leaf at step 456 measures 4649 bytes: arbitration 4320 plus 4 (memory 4140 with one changed chunk, engine 54, host commitment 40), frames 21, instruction 5, fuel expansion 16, supplement 48, semantic 230 plus 4 (host 97, storage 89, composition digest 32, framing 12), trap 1; its compact host split is code hash flag 1, ABI flag 1, runtime 16, meter 70, storage baseline flag 1, framing 8, and its embedded composition is revision 0 with graph flags 2. The executor leaf at step 743 measures 4918 bytes with every one of those fields identical except the host runtime field: 285 instead of 16, because the composed runtime of the executor proof embeds the CompositionReplayWitnessV1 graph (252 bytes including its framing) in every leaf while the record header already carries that graph (header_total 1004 with runtime_composition_graph 252). ReplayHostWitnessV1::record_fields (src/replay.rs line 2286) writes the runtime source with a plain field call, not through record_field against the header, so decision 2735 left the graph per leaf. Removing 252 bytes from each of the 221 leaves the live-snapshot record counts (1027329 divided by 4649) projects an executor leaf of 4666 bytes and a leaf total near 1031200, under the bound by about 17000 bytes."
fix = "The composition graph of a composed runtime is a record constant: encode it per leaf as a presence flag against the header graph and restore it in the decoders (decision 2738); then the executor proof admits the 128 calls."

[gotcha.3352]
title = "18.1562.1 attempt 19 (continue, decision 2737) at 8a2efbc6c3fee2ec60a65571ba09db081831ddd7: build exit 0, verify exit 1 after one run: the fee balance of 1000000000 cleared FEE_UNPAYABLE and TestAiMarketTransferAuthorityReceipt now fails at rpc/sequencer_receipt_vectors_test.go line 839 with LXP_NON_CANONICAL on the FUND call (kernel gas allowance 10000000, EVM gas used 88480)."
symptom = "The FUND needs the balance-sight receipt as a receipt authority: the production proof (rpc/repair_478_test.go line 409) passes ReceiptAuthorities with the canonical sight receipt and the height before the call through the direct host path, while the fixture runs the sight through ExecuteActivity (line 811), puts the sight digest in the capabilities bytes (lines 822 to 830) and then sends the FUND through the call method of the programs precompile (line 831), whose handler (precompiles/layerxprograms/method_call.go line 37) submits with no authorities although submit (submit.go line 57) accepts them; the ABI call method has no authorities input, so no EVM transaction can cite a receipt."
fix = "The precompile gains callWithReceipts (task 22.31.582, decision 2739) and the fixture sends the FUND through it once that task lands."

[gotcha.3353]
title = "22.31.539 attempt 7 (continue, gotcha 3347) at 3c6a1baf032ad489aae2b83554d4b36e901640a0: build exit 0, verify exit 1: the COMMITTED decoding of the finalised checkpoint and the fixture that mines 50 real Anvil blocks cleared owner.refused; agent_register_prepares_bind_layerx now fails at tests/bootstrap_bind_layerx.rs line 709 with status 400 ProtocolIncompatibility envelope.malformed, and the session case at line 885 falls to the poisoned fixture lock."
symptom = "The daemon prepares the bootstrap bindLayerX call through bind_call of the call disclosure (the routing module line 187, every error mapped to malformed), and decode_method in services/agent/crates/layerx-crypto/src/disclosure/call.rs (line 544) has branches for the targets 0x101d, 0x101a, 0x101b, 0x101c and 0x1001 and for pointer transfers only; a call to the addr precompile 0x1004 with the bindLayerX selector (binding.rs line 10) falls to the final MalformedPayload at line 835. The signer verifies a construct call through the same disclosure, so no signer could sign the bootstrap call either; the gap is in the crypto crate, outside the task touches."
fix = "Task 22.31.583 (decision 2740) discloses the bindLayerX call; 22.31.539 continues after it on the attempt-7 tree."

[gotcha.3354]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 9 (continue, decision 2738) at a097f1b2762bbc7e1bf584114f5c71309f277c5c: build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101: the composition graph presence flag landed (the header carries the graph once, both decoders restore it, the graph-disagreement Binding case passes) and every carried suite passes; the live-snapshot proof admits 128 calls with leaf total 1027329 and record total 1032153; the executor proof is refused at step 900 on the capture witness bound, observed 1048953 against the permitted 1048576, 377 bytes over, on a 518-byte leaf with no changed chunk; the executor step-900 runtime source is 36 bytes where the live-snapshot runtime source of the same step shape is 16."
symptom = "Two of the twenty bytes are the composition revision and graph presence flags; the other eighteen are the response outcome region that write_v2_runtime_state (host/mod.rs lines 425 to 441) writes verbatim into the runtime tail of every leaf: the tag byte, an eight-byte length word and the ResponseRegion state of abi/response.rs canonical_state_write (an eight-byte capacity word, a published marker, a refusal marker), nineteen bytes for the empty region the composed runtime holds from construction (composed_with_response, host/mod.rs line 901) against the one-byte None tag of the live-snapshot runtime. The capacity is the response_capacity of the execution request (execute.rs lines 4872 and 4956), constant for the whole execution, so the record repeats a record constant in about 900 leaves; the guest runs 128 times five constants, a call and a drop, so the record ends near step 900 and the overrun is the last few leaves."
fix = "Decision 2741: the response capacity of the runtime response region is a record constant bound in the record header; the leaf encodes the region as the tag, a presence flag against the header capacity and the two markers with their payloads, about fifteen bytes less per leaf, which brings the executor record about 13500 bytes under the bound."

[gotcha.3355]
title = "22.31.582 attempt 1: the build passes and the verify fails only in the gas table test at the lease execution method row, where the shared lease request helper asserts byte equality between the request it encodes and the committed lease request vector; the program, asset, limits and receipt words differ because the gas fixture deploys a program keyed by the test name while the vector was recorded by the usage test; the task record calls the failure unrelated."
symptom = "Commit f3402ae5ff (task 22.33.213, verified only by its own repair tests) embedded the recorded lease request vector and made the shared helper of the lease execution method test file take the lease id from the vector and assert the recorded bytes for every caller (line 119); the gas table test has been red on main since 2026-11-05, and no attempt of 22.31.582 can pass its verify until the helper binds the vector to the fixture that recorded it."
fix = "Repair task 22.31.584 (decision 2742); 22.31.582 continues after it."

[gotcha.3356]
title = "22.31.583 attempt 1: the first build stopped with E0277 because the repair test applied the question-mark operator to a PayloadError inside a function returning a DisclosureError result; the second build passed; the dependent-crate check then stopped at the agent creation path of the human service (create.rs line 650), whose match over construct_method is exhaustive and lacks an arm for the new BindLayerX variant; the verify never ran."
symptom = "The ConstructMethod enum is matched exhaustively in exactly one consumer on main, the lifecycle transaction classifier of agent creation; every other consumer matches with if-let or a wildcard arm. A task that adds a variant adds an arm there, and the dependent-crate check is the gate that proves it."
fix = "22.31.583 continues with create.rs in its touches: a Refused arm for the bind registration beside the pointer-transfer arm, and the repair test maps the payload error explicitly."

[gotcha.3357]
title = "22.31.217 attempt 10: build and dependent-crate check pass (15 crates) and the verify fails 3 of 18 cases twice: the deploy and upgrade lifecycle cases and the wind-down cases refuse at prepare with Disclosure(MalformedPayload) from finish_call through the call disclosure binder, and the native effect settlement case panics because the corpus entry carries no capture for the burn construct, which the recording peer refused."
symptom = "decode_method of the call disclosure decodes a Programs precompile call (0x101D) only through decode_program_call, whose single selector is the nine-argument call signature; deploy, upgrade, setExitRoute, deprecate, tombstone, exitValue and exitValueBounded are refused as MalformedPayload although the disclosure crate already carries DisclosedProgramDeploy, DisclosedProgramUpgrade and DisclosedProgramWindDown with native encoders and the lifecycle settlement binder of this attempt already names every lifecycle signature; the same defect class as decision 2740. The missing burn capture is a separate corpus gap."
fix = "Repair task 22.31.585 (decision 2743) discloses the lifecycle calls; 22.31.217 continues after it and records the burn capture through the loopback peer."

[gotcha.3358]
title = "22.31.547 attempt 5 (requalify after 22.31.560): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101: the daemon crossing case fails at line 307 because the first native send Prepare answers 503 owner.unavailable after the daemon printed preparation receipt key read failed with the JSON-RPC refusal -32601 Method not found; the preview case then fell to the poisoned fixture lock as a cascade."
symptom = "Since 22.31.560 landed, genuine Prepare reads the head receipt key through budget_read_parts (human_runtime.rs line 12509, receipt_key_at_head of human_node.rs line 45, the px_getReceiptKeys read of the node client) before the chain id; the chain peer of the shared fixture (native_send_preview_evm.rs chain_peer, line 233) serves only the send refusal, the binding, fee and balance eth_call reads and the nonce, and answers every other method with Method not found, so the daemon reports Unavailable. The repair peer of 22.31.560 (repair_22_31_560.rs lines 358 to 367) serves px_getReceiptKeys, px_getCommit and px_getValidators for the same read; the shared fixture was never extended."
fix = "Serve the receipt key read in the shared chain peer (decision 2744); 22.31.547 continues."

[gotcha.3359]
title = "22.31.547 attempt 6: build and dependent-crate check pass twice; the first verify reached the daemon with the receipt keys served and the first Prepare answered 403 owner.refused under the partial preview fixture; the second cycle included the repair harness of 22.31.560 (fixture_with_receipt_keys, the authenticated committed reads, the policy window, the native effect policy) and the first Prepare answered 200, after which the SDK verdict at line 313 was Unknown with operation Prepare and no field named."
symptom = "prepare_native_send_surface of the SDK (agent_envelope.rs lines 881 to 917) collapses every disagreement into EnvelopeError::Unknown: a body decode_native_preparation refuses, an unsigned call validate_unsigned_preparation refuses, and each of the preparation id, canonical digest, activity, raw call fields (sender, activity, actor, sequence, window, idempotency key, fee limit, payload), signing preimage, chain id, transaction type and approval id checks; the test asserts only the status and then unwraps the verdict, so the private verify log cannot say which bound field the daemon body and the SDK purpose disagree on."
fix = "The crossing test decodes the accepted body and asserts each bound field before the SDK verdict (decision 2745); 22.31.547 continues."

[gotcha.3360]
title = "22.31.547 attempt 7: build and dependent-crate check pass twice; the field-by-field assertions of decision 2745 run and the first disagreeing field is not_before: the disclosure bound from the accepted canonical bytes carries not_before 0 while the request carries 1789365544000 (the not_after assertion would fail the same way against u64::MAX); the version, preparation identifier, canonical digest and re-encoding, activity, sender, actor payer account and account sequence assertions pass before it; the two included native send cases then fail with PoisonError on the shared fixture lock because the crossing case holds the lock guard directly and the assertion panic poisons it."
symptom = "A ledger send call (send(bytes) to 0x101A) carries the client send envelope and no activity window: SendDebit (send.rs lines 41 to 53) has from, to, asset, amount, source sequence, idempotency key, expires_at, context hash, conditions, authorization kind, network id and protocol version; bind_call discloses not_before 0 and not_after u64::MAX for every call and the LedgerSend arm sets only payload_expires_at from the envelope (call.rs lines 891 to 893 and 945 to 960); the daemon wraps the client payload unchanged (build_call, prepare/mod.rs lines 375 to 423) and binds the request window in the preparation digest (human_runtime.rs legacy_prepare_digest lines 18668 to 18681) and the human request record. The SDK matcher raw_call_matches_request (agent_envelope.rs lines 1592 to 1593) compares the request window to the disclosed bounds for every module, a consumer check the ledger send call cannot satisfy; the fixture send envelope itself expires at now plus 20000 while the request window ends at now plus 30000 (native_send_preview_evm.rs lines 736 and 817), so the window and the envelope expiry are distinct facts."
fix = "The SDK matcher compares the window only for calls that carry it (decision 2746); the crossing case asserts the absent window and the envelope expiry and runs under the catch-unwind lock helper; 22.31.547 continues."

[gotcha.3361]
title = "9.98.4 attempt 6: no gate ran; the attempt reached its 90-minute working-time limit after 44 read commands and two edits of human_runtime.rs. The carried tree already holds the linked-block history fixture the attempt-5 ruling asked for: history_result builds a per-height EVM transaction result, history_checkpoints builds blocks 6 to 9 parent-linked by block hash with last_results_hash equal to the Merkle root of the prior height results and two signed votes, an environment guard publishes the results endpoint URL under a module lock and restores it on drop, and the listener answers commit, validators, block_results, px_getHistory and pax_sequencerReceipt from those blocks; the refusal case takes the guard."
symptom = "The history reader on main (policy_history.rs read_policy_history_from_sources, lines 49 to 282) authenticates each ascending history page and its results against the signed root of the next block (abci_result.rs line 105), so the double needs one more signed block than history heights and a results root per height; reading that chain of readers through the daemon source consumed the working time before a single build."
fix = "The attempt-7 ruling carries the tree, names the remaining wiring only, and raises the task time limit to 150 minutes (decision 2747)."

[gotcha.3362]
title = "18.1562.1 attempt 20: build 0, verify 1 at two revisions; the Go vector case now produces the ABI5 reward Fund receipt through the committed runtime with the receipt authority of the balance sight, the ABI5 result decodes, the journal resolves and survives reopen, and every refusal subcase passes; the run then stops on the last assertion of the SDK case, which demands that the wrapper authority root differ from the applied-legs root, while the produced receipt carries one applied leg and the same root in both places."
symptom = "The runtime publishes the authorization and the transfer root of one transfer set (ffi_call.rs lines 2949 to 2952); the response contract says the wrapper carries a 32-byte transfer root equal to the verified root (precompiles/layerxprograms/response.md), and the Go binding refuses a wrapper whose bound root differs from the applied-legs root (response.go lines 54 to 65); occupancy is settled in its own activity and never adds a leg to the frame. The SDK decoder of the attempt reconstructs the root from the authorization legs and walks them as a subset of the applied legs (ai_market.ts line 3697 onward) but never binds the wrapper root to the applied-legs root, so it accepts a wrapper the node binding refuses."
fix = "Decision 2748: the test asserts equality and the SDK refuses inequality like the Go binding; the fixture stays as produced."

[gotcha.3363]
title = "9.98.4 attempt 7: the first build failed on a borrow of block.commit while it was mutably borrowed in the history checkpoint builder (E0502), the repaired build and the dependent-crate check passed, and the verify ended 6 passed, 6 failed: the first retained settlement case panics in the submission fixture transaction_submission of human_runtime.rs (line 20584) with unsupported submission fixture activity ActivityType(589825), which is module 9 ordinal 1, and the other three retained cases then fail on PoisonError of the module lock; policy_usage_sums_only_proven_receipts_in_the_window fails at line 23567 expecting 4 px_getHistory requests and seeing 6; native_policy_usage_refuses_a_page_without_a_proof fails on PoisonError of the history environment lock poisoned by the previous case."
symptom = "The retained settlement cases prepare a programs deploy (module 9 ordinal 1) and hand it to transaction_submission since the audit repair d693490680, while the fixture match (lines 20548 to 20584) builds only the governance lifecycle and bridge credit calls; the daemon has no deploy call encoder yet, the deploy selector of decision 2743 arrives with task 22.31.585. The policy reader on main pages through read_newest (read/history.rs lines 420 onward), which scans descending 64-block windows with ascending exclusive cursors, so the request count differs from the count the test was written against. Both module locks are taken with expect, so one panic poisons every later case."
fix = "9.98.4 now requires 22.31.585; the attempt-8 ruling adds the programs deploy arm with the codec encoder, asserts the request counts the current reader makes, and takes both locks poison-tolerant (decision 2749)."

[gotcha.3364]
title = "22.31.585 attempt 1: no change inside scope; the engineering process issued no command for its whole two-hour working time after the environment was prepared, recorded one note about a hook timeout clamp, and ended at the limit with an empty error stream."
symptom = "A stalled session that never reaches its first command leaves nothing to carry; the task starts again from current main."
fix = "Attempt 2 relaunches the task as specified; nothing of attempt 1 is carried."

[gotcha.3365]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 7: implemented-not-qualified with no gate run; the engineering process prepared the tree (the attempt-6 tree merged with current main after 22.31.577 landed, committed at launch) and then issued no command for the whole 150-minute working time, recording only one note about a timeout clamp, the same stall signature as 22.31.585 attempt 1 (gotcha 3364) launched forty minutes earlier; every attempt launched after 17:30Z ran normally."
symptom = "A session that stalls before its first command leaves the prepared tree untouched; the attempt-7 ruling (recorded with finding 6 of the task) was never acted on."
fix = "Attempt 8 continues on the attempt-7 tree and re-applies the attempt-7 ruling unchanged (decision 2750)."

[gotcha.3366]
title = "22.31.547 attempt 8 and 22.31.583 attempt 2: implemented-not-qualified with no gate run; in both the engineering process prepared the tree at launch and then issued no command for the whole working time (120 and 90 minutes), recording only one note about a timeout clamp, the third and fourth stall of this kind after 22.31.585 attempt 1 and 22.31.573 attempt 7 (gotchas 3364 and 3365); the model endpoint those sessions were given answered every request with a usage-limit refusal from about 15:40Z, which the session retried silently until its limit."
symptom = "The endpoint used by a session was chosen in rotation without checking that it could answer; a session whose first model request is refused with a usage limit retries until the working-time limit and never reaches a command."
fix = "The engineering process now checks the endpoint with a small request before a launch and uses another one when it is refused (decision 2751); both attempts continue on their prepared trees with their rulings re-applied unchanged (decision 2750)."

[gotcha.3367]
title = "Every feature 22 task references requirement 22998.1 in its reqs list, and the spec carries no [req.22998.1] block; the requirement index of the audit programme therefore pointed at nothing for the whole feature."
symptom = "The audit series was generated from a template whose requirement id was never materialised as a block; the lint checks block syntax, not requirement references."
fix = "Batch 581 creates [req.22998.1] with the feature-wide acceptance text; a new series creates its requirement blocks before its tasks and the generator asserts every reqs id has a block."

[gotcha.3368]
title = "The host boundary build target has failed on main since task 22.31.577 landed: the runtime writes the program replay record in its version-2 layout (domain, version 2, a u32 header length and the canonical header bytes of ReplayRecordHeader, then the profile bounds, the terminal status, the boundary count, the chunk-root boundary leaves and the witness digest) while the C decoder layerx_programs_call_replay_record_finish in src/modules/programs/call.c (line 3024) still parses the version-1 layout; the activity preparation of the short CALL replay capture answers non-canonical (status -3) and the host boundary proof stops before the ai-market build (22.99.77 attempt 20 at base 552412ccad; attempt 19 built at the base before 577)."
symptom = "Task 577 changed the record bytes in the Rust runtime and ported the Rust decoders, but the C host decoder of the same record was outside its touches and no gate of the task ran the host boundary target that decodes a live record."
fix = "Task 22.31.586 ports the C decoder to the version-2 layout under decision 2753; 22.99.77 and 22.38.13 require it; a task that changes a record layout lists every decoder of the record or a required follow-up for it, and its gates include the shared proof that decodes a live record."

[gotcha.3369]
title = "9.98.4 attempt 8: three retained-settlement tests fail with the bare value Refused at the must helper of human_runtime.rs (line 23748) because every refusal site of settle_retained_native_program_call (line 3799 and after) maps to the unit HumanOperationError::Refused through one closure, so the evidence cannot name the refusing check; and policy_usage_sums_only_proven_receipts_in_the_window counts six eth_blockNumber calls for four because the HistoryRpc double answers that method at two sites (lines 23425 and 23842)."
symptom = "A refusal type without a site field hides which of a dozen checks refused, and a test double that answers one method from two arms double-counts it."
fix = "Attempt 9 names the refusing site in a test-visible way before changing any check, and the double answers eth_blockNumber from one arm."

[gotcha.3370]
title = "Seven tasks of the inference series (22.38.23, 22.38.29, 22.38.30, 22.38.33, 22.38.35, 22.38.36 and 22.38.39) listed file paths in their symbols field; the graph check of the done gate treats every symbols entry as a code symbol, so 22.38.23 attempt 1 and 22.38.35 attempt 1 were refused with every test passing."
symptom = "The series generator accepted paths in the symbols lists; the graph check only resolves identifiers."
fix = "Batch 582 strips the path entries from the seven symbols lists and the generator refuses a symbols entry containing a slash or a file extension; the two refused attempts requalify on their trees."

[gotcha.3371]
title = "The precompile test package of the pay module has not compiled on main since task 22.33.1303 (2026-11-04) changed GetEscrow and GetEscrowResult of the pay keeper to return a third error value: thirteen call sites in precompiles/layerxpay (conformance_escrow_test.go, conformance_service_test.go, escrow_test.go and service_test.go) still take two values, so every go test of that package fails at compile time; 22.38.9 attempt 1 was refused that way with its own test never run."
symptom = "The keeper repair ported the production callers (escrow.go) but not the precompile tests, and its gate ran the keeper tests only."
fix = "Task 22.31.611 ports the thirteen call sites; 22.38.9 requires it; a signature change lists every caller the compiler names, tests included, and its gate compiles the test packages of every touched directory (go vet)."

[gotcha.3372]
title = "The availability width ruling for 22.38.1 named two of the five ten-entry literals in the ai-market crate tests: identity_section_sharing.rs line 619, repair_22_31_253.rs lines 749, 912 and 920 and view_binding.rs line 353 all spell the old width; attempt 2 widened the two named sites and the build stopped at view_binding.rs line 351 with the same mismatch."
symptom = "A failed cargo build names one test target at a time, so a ruling written from the compiler output of one attempt sees one site per build; the remaining sites surface one attempt each."
fix = "Decision 2757: a width change of a producer lists every literal of the old width across the crate tests from a search of the tests, not from the last compiler output; attempt 3 of 22.38.1 widens the three remaining sites."

[gotcha.3373]
title = "The host boundary proof still answers kernel status -3 at the first CALL after 22.31.586 attempt 1 ported the C replay record parser to the version-2 layout: the parser refusal recorder of that attempt reports no field, so the refusal is raised outside layerx_programs_call_replay_record_finish; 22.99.77 attempt 20 placed the same refusal in activity preparation (prepare_activity=-3), before any record is decoded, and the 22.31.577 commit 9fce5b6b84 changed no C source."
symptom = "Gotcha 3368 attributed the red proof to the record parser; the attempt-1 diagnostic shows the host refusing at preparation something the runtime or the guest emits differently since 577, at a site the diagnostic does not yet name, and the attempt exhausted its repair budget guessing."
fix = "Decision 2759: every refusal on the path the proof exercises names its site and stage in the diagnostic; attempt 2 of 22.31.586 instruments the preparation path first, reads the named site from one proof run, then repairs that site."

[gotcha.3374]
title = "22.31.600 attempt 1 removed .claude/settings.local.json from version control and its own test found the path tracked again at qualification: the qualification step records the content of every declared file that exists on disk into the candidate commit, so a file-level declaration of a path the task untracks puts the file back; the two directory-level declarations of the same task (the envs-validator and assemblyscript package trees) stayed untracked because a directory entry drops files the ignore rules exclude, as 22.31.480 did for apps/perps/node_modules."
symptom = "An untracking task declared the file it removes as a file entry; the candidate rule keeps declared files that are present on disk."
fix = "Decision 2758: a task that removes a path from version control declares the smallest directory holding it, never the file; 22.31.600 now declares .claude and attempt 2 reruns on the attempt-1 tree."

[gotcha.3375]
title = "precompiles/layerxpay/conformance_escrow_test.go line 28 asserts that an exhausted store iterator reports the error text invalid cacheMergeIterator; since the cachekv merge iterator repair (sdk/store/cachekv/mergeiterator.go, repair_m635_test.go) Error delegates to the parent and cache iterators and answers nil once the iterator is exhausted, while use of an invalid iterator panics; 22.31.611 attempt 1 ported the thirteen escrow view call sites, the package compiled again and TestPayEscrowPathMatchesHostExecute failed at that helper with an error expected and nil received."
symptom = "The test package had not compiled since 2026-11-04 (gotcha 3371), so the helper that asserted the pre-repair iterator behaviour went unseen until the port made the package compile."
fix = "Decision 2760: an exhausted iterator reports no error; the helper asserts Valid false and NoError; attempt 2 of 22.31.611 makes that one change and reruns."

[gotcha.3376]
title = "22.38.16 attempt 1 built the signal listener and its five chain-backed cases panicked at tests/inference_signal.rs line 24: the cases load the daemon inference configuration from the process environment (LAYERX_AGENT_INFERENCE_MODEL_DIGEST is required and must be nonblank) and expect LAYERX_AGENT_NODE_ENDPOINT, a bearer token, a chain id and an authority CA from the environment as well; no qualification run provides them, and tests/inference_profile_boot.rs builds the same configuration from a map of values in process. The listener also reads the peer enrolment record through the F11 peer read (peer_key and enrolled fields) that 22.38.8 serves and 22.38.15 writes, while the task required only 22.38.14."
symptom = "The spec listed the daemon profile as the only prerequisite of the listener and left the enrolment read and the enrolment write unlisted; the cases took their configuration and their node from the environment of the person who wrote them."
fix = "Decision 2761: 22.38.16 requires 22.38.8 and 22.38.15 and moves to wave 4; attempt 2 builds the configuration from values in process and reads the enrolment through the F11 read once it lands."

[gotcha.3377]
title = "9.98.4 attempt 9 instrumented the retained settlement path and the three library cases retained_settlement_settles_once_across_replay, retained_settlement_settles_after_the_head_advances and retained_settlement_refuses_a_failed_receipt refuse at the site lifecycle_settlement in stage Preparation: the EIP-1559 submission decodes, the signed activity decoder answers -101 at offset 0, and the refusal comes from read_retained_lifecycle_debit_settlement_at_execution in budget/program_settlement.rs, whose callees verify_wind_down_debits (line 4) and verify_remaining_lifecycle_debits (line 175) in budget/program_lifecycle_settlement.rs decode the submission as a kernel signed activity and compare encode_unsigned with the canonical bytes; the production signer (sign_verify.rs line 101) and the fixture both produce the EIP-1559 call form, so the decode fails on every retained submission."
symptom = "The cases passed at 331d5f481d while the fixture used the kernel signer; d693490680 (22.31.368) moved the fixture to the transaction submission form and the two lifecycle verifiers were never ported, which is the open do_10 finding of 22.31.217 whose attempt-10 tree already carries the native lifecycle settlement binder."
fix = "Decision 2762: 9.98.4 requires 22.31.217 and requalifies its attempt-9 tree after that task lands; attempt 11 of 22.31.217 ports the two verifiers to the EIP-1559 call form."

[gotcha.3378]
title = "22.31.611 attempt 2 repaired the iterator assertion and the four TestPayEscrowPathMatchesHostExecute cases then failed at conformance_escrow_test.go line 109: the precompile leg writes 22 store rows and the direct leg 21, the extra row keyed layerxpay/escrow-receipt/v1/ followed by the eight-byte big-endian global sequence with a 657-byte value; modules/layerxpay/keeper/execute.go lines 80 to 83 bind the escrow receipt under that key for every escrow module activity (escrow_receipt.go lines 44 to 72, introduced by e71fbafd7d for 22.31.131) while the direct leg calls HostExecute on the raw host and never binds."
symptom = "The row comparison was hidden in attempt 1 behind the iterator assertion at line 28; the receipt binding is production behaviour of the keeper path, not a conformance defect."
fix = "Decision 2763: the conformance equality excludes the one receipt row by key and asserts it through the keeper reader GetEscrowReceipt; attempt 3 of 22.31.611 makes that change."

[gotcha.3379]
title = "22.37.17 attempt 1 passed the batch suite, the retention race and the changed-tree receipt and failed at native_source_acceptance_actor.mjs line 181: the first lifecycle read after the fixture restart threw SourceControlError with code OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and retry RETRY_SAME_OPERATION (operation db7de69a-1817-46c0-94ed-65f1cd12defe), raised by the transport catch of the source-control client; the fixture restart closes the listener with closeIdleConnections then closeAllConnections and starts a new service on the same port while the client keeps using the global fetch connection pool."
symptom = "The lost request is the first use of a kept-alive connection to the closed listener; the SDK contract already names the recovery (reissue the same operation) and the actor did not follow it."
fix = "Decision 2764: a test that restarts the service reissues a lost read with the same operation a bounded number of times; attempt 2 of 22.37.17 adds that helper in the actor and routes the post-restart reads through it."

[gotcha.3380]
title = "22.38.1 attempt 3 widened the three remaining ten-entry literals of the ai-market crate tests and its build and verify passed; the dependent-crate check then failed with exit 101 in layerx-indexer: services/platform/hosted/indexer/src/ai_market.rs line 1465 (mismatched types) and line 2289 (cannot compare an eleven-entry Availability array with a ten-entry one), since FEATURES at line 64 of that file is 10, the three availability fields and RawRecord::decode (lines 1092 to 1098) use it, and ai_views.rs lines 179 and 183 spell F01 to F10 and the ten-entry parameter of components."
symptom = "Decision 2757 listed the old-width literals across the crate tests; the hosted indexer consumes feature_availability directly and was outside the task touches, so the width change could not reach it."
fix = "Decision 2765: a producer width change lists and touches every old-width literal in every dependent crate; the touches of 22.38.1 now include the two indexer files and attempt 4 widens them."

[gotcha.3381]
title = "22.31.586 attempt 2 widened the recorder into a site-and-stage recorder and the proof moved past preparation: the three CALL diagnostic lines answer execute type 0x90001 and 0x90002 with kernel status 0 and type 0x90003 with kernel status -3, site lxp_programs_call_execute, stage execute, field runtime.result, runtime status -741, which is LXP_ERR_ENGINE_FAULT; native_result.rs from_captured maps every ExecutionError::Fault of the runtime except the Bounds replay refusal to -741 and drops the variant (UnknownExport, BadSignature, OutOfFuel, EngineFault with its reason and the others) so the host cannot name the cause."
symptom = "The diagnostic now names the site but the fault variant stays on the Rust side of the native boundary; the short CALL of the proof runs the deployed guest with 256 units of guest fuel and any of several variants could answer -741."
fix = "Decision 2766: an executor fault that crosses the native boundary carries its variant text into the proof diagnostic; attempt 3 of 22.31.586 adds the accessor in the runtime crate, prints it and repairs the named cause."

[gotcha.3382]
title = "22.31.539 attempt 8 built and passed its own target and six of the listed regression targets; tests/repair_22_31_219.rs failed four of eight cases: three at line 750 where the owner fixture opens a store under a directory built by temp_dir join and a default-mode create_dir (lines 59 to 70), refused with store root is not a canonical owned private directory, and one at line 601 where read_policy_history_from_sources answers Sequencer(Malformed) against the Node fixture that serves px_getHistory and four other px_ methods."
symptom = "The target passed at ab3600e85a on 2026-11-04; fde2add099 (22.33.1516) tightened the store root rule after that and 3b27b8078f (22.34.5) moved the Rust sequencer clients to the node names at the root path; the fixture of the target was never ported and no pending task carries it, while 22.31.539 lists the target and already touches the file."
fix = "Decision 2768: attempt 9 of 22.31.539 ports the Directory fixture to the canonical private-directory pattern of repair_22_33_1513.rs and repairs the Node fixture to the request and response shape the client sends since 22.34.5."

[gotcha.3383]
title = "22.37.14 attempt 1 wired the WORKSPACE pins, the CANDIDATE roots, the per-object backup check and the lifecycle inspection and passed ten component checks; the API verification of the 2_3 case failed at the workspace checkpoint of native_source_collection_api.mjs (line 379) with SCOPE_DENIED, Source action is not authorized, raised by the capability authorizer (capabilities.ts denied, line 193) which names no branch; the attempt also left the EVIDENCE root acquisition at publication unwired because the evidence producer core/control-plane/src/assurance/native_source.ts was outside the task touches."
symptom = "The acceptance fixture issues a capability with every retention and workspace action and a root path prefix, the workspace opens in API_ONLY mode with root read and write paths, and the one working checkpoint pattern of the suite (native_source_api_actor.mjs line 41) passes both operation_id and idempotency_key call options on a SPARSE workspace; the authorizer declines capability rows silently in the paths, authority, revision, object access, managed binding and recovery admission branches, so the refusing branch is unknown."
fix = "Decision 2767: the touches of 22.37.14 gain the evidence producer; attempt 2 wires it, compares its checkpoint call with the working pattern, finds the declining branch and repairs it."

[gotcha.3384]
title = "22.37.2 attempt 1 wired the vendored baseline file, the subtree-id resolution of the ancestry and inventory checks, the receipt schema validation and the layout receipt gate with twelve passing fixture cases; the 0_9 case still ended BLOCKED with one missing evidence entry because the frozen baseline receipt build/layout/0.3/receipt.json is recreated by running the imported 0_3.py of the pinned subtree, which finds no platform/package.json after the relocation, delegates to 0_3_history.py and refuses with HISTORICAL_FILE_MISSING on build/layout/0.3-preserved-original/manifest.json."
symptom = "The pre-relocation evidence archive under build/layout was always an ignored directory of the upstream project and never entered this repository; the imported producer therefore can never recreate the frozen baseline here, while the inventory half of the producer (generate_inventory of tools/repository/layout-inventory.py against the pinned tree) needs no archive."
fix = "Decision 2769: the vendored baseline file is the frozen baseline; 0_9 recreates the 0.3 receipt from the pinned subtree through the inventory capture alone and records the historical verification as unavailable with its refusal code."

[gotcha.3385]
title = "22.38.15 attempt 1 built the v2 manifest measurement, the signed peer relay, the receipt waits and the named refusals and passed four of five cases of tests/inference_enrol.rs; the bond-lock case failed with Client(MissingOperation(LockBond)) at line 36 because named_market_operation looks LockBond up in the operation table of the ai-market program, which on main ends at APPOINT_OPERATOR: PostBid belongs to 22.38.3 (wave 2) and LockBond to 22.38.7 (wave 5), both pending, while the task required only 22.38.2 and 22.38.14 at wave 3."
symptom = "The refusal is the correct named refusal for an operation the program does not serve yet; the attempt-1 tree is sound and only the producers are missing."
fix = "Decision 2770: 22.38.15 requires 22.38.3 and 22.38.7 and moves to wave 5 with its dependents 22.38.16, 22.38.17 and 22.38.25; attempt 2 requalifies the attempt-1 tree once the producers land."

[gotcha.3386]
title = "22.37.12 attempt 1 landed the ancestry index migration, the server-held cursors, the resumable merge bases, the path redaction coverage, the admission classes and the replica-aware causal reads; verification 1 passed the cancellation, late-event and admission-isolation checks and failed the new redaction case of native_source_api_actor.mjs with deepStrictEqual: the strict JSON decoder returns null-prototype objects while the expected value used ordinary objects; the attempt repaired the expectation at b2a2d77d5707572c44a8e0560be760c20737f396, built it, and could not rerun the verify because its repair budget was spent."
symptom = "A deepStrictEqual between a null-prototype object and an object literal fails on the prototype alone; the final tree carries the repaired expectation unverified."
fix = "Attempt 2 reruns the build and the verify once on the attempt-1 tree; a remaining mismatch compares the entries through JSON round trips or Object.assign onto plain objects."

[gotcha.3387]
title = "22.31.217 attempt 11 exhausted its repair budget after its last verification, so the archived verify log describes aa510a73 while the final tree 9902a5e7 (build 3 exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0) was never verified; the log shows three failures of eighteen: repair_lifecycle_native_envelope_deploy_upgrade_wind_down_and_restart and repair_settlement_native_envelope_effect_receipt_and_restart at repair_22_31_217.rs line 494 with SummaryBody (peer log bytes match the signed log effects), raised only by decode_summary_body in layerx-proof sequencer_logs.rs lines 275 to 296, and repair_execution_account_exists_funded_unfrozen_wind_down at support/budget_native_capture.rs line 217 with ReceiptSignature (real nested account proof and signature), which is AccountProofError::ReceiptSignature at state.rs line 231 wrapping every signature refusal of the historical kernel key the authorization carries."
symptom = "The attempt was claimed before batch 584 landed do_27 (the lifecycle verifier port) and its final repairs ran after the last verify, so line-level reading of the log against the bundle is unreliable."
fix = "Decision 2771: the continuation runs the build and the verify first at the final tree and only then reads failures; attempt 12 carries the two decoder facts as repair guidance."

[gotcha.3388]
title = "22.31.611 attempt 3 passed the row-set equality with the receipt row excluded and the want-equals-got assertion of the direct leg, then failed four times at the stored-receipt equality that do_5 of batch 584 mandated (require.Equal of want.Encoded against the stored canonical bytes): the stored row under the escrow receipt key is the bound receipt, because bindEscrowReceipt (modules/layerxpay/keeper/escrow_receipt.go lines 44 to 67) replaces receipt.Encoded by the bytes the kernel binder returns, which set TransferSetRoot (layerxproof/codec/receipt.go line 103, bytes 0x220 to 0x23f of the 657-byte receipt), while the raw HostExecute leg never binds; the two byte strings differ in exactly that field."
symptom = "Decision 2763 was applied as a byte equality against the unbound producer, which cannot hold for a row the keeper binds before storing."
fix = "Decision 2772: the conformance decodes both receipts, asserts every field equal except TransferSetRoot, and asserts the stored TransferSetRoot nonzero and equal to the TransferSetRoot that GetEscrowResult returns for the same idempotency key, as repair_131_test.go line 230 already does."

[gotcha.3389]
title = "22.37.14 attempt 2 added source.operations.read to the collection case capability and still failed at native_source_collection_api.mjs line 521 with SCOPE_DENIED under source.publications.create: export.ts line 241 guards source.publications.create and then calls the acceptance callback registered at registration.ts line 97, whose guards at acceptance.ts lines 201 and 242 require source.acceptance.read; authorizeSource (capabilities.ts line 283 onward) denies when no capability row lists the action and the source_request_failed event names the outer action; the collection case actions (lines 73 to 104) list the acceptance.accept, candidates.read, publications, retention and collection actions but not source.acceptance.read, which the working actor native_source_api_actor.mjs grants through its full API_ACTIONS list."
symptom = "A refusal event names the action of the outer handler, so the agent kept adding actions near the outer name while the refuser was an inner guard."
fix = "Decision 2773: a fixture capability lists every action the handler chain guards; attempt 3 adds source.acceptance.read to the collection case."

[gotcha.3390]
title = "22.31.586 attempt 3 stopped on EngineFault execution trace exceeds commitment limit 128 at site lxp_programs_call_execute stage execute: the 128 is written by call_payload in tests/programs/test_ai_host_boundary.c line 314 as the maximum boundary count of the replay profile prefix (domain LXP/program-replay-profile/v1, version 1), decoded by lxp_programs_call_profile_decode (src/modules/programs/call.c lines 2902 to 2933) within the product bound LXP_PROGRAMS_REPLAY_MAX_BOUNDARIES and MAX_PROGRAM_REPLAY_BOUNDARIES of 4096 (replay_record.rs line 12), passed through layerx_programs_call_replay_profile (ffi_call.rs lines 1341 to 1353) into ProgramReplayProfile::new (replay_record.rs line 63), which builds TracePolicy::new(1, maximum_boundaries); the refusal is CommitmentError::CommitmentLimit from record_commitment in commit.rs when the recorded commitments reach policy.maximum_commitments. The product constants (MAX_TRACE_COMMITMENTS 65536, the 4096 bound, the 512 of calls.rs line 1682) are untouched."
symptom = "The agent read the never-loosen-a-bound rule of do_6 as covering the proof declaration, but the 128 is the declaration of the proof itself, exactly like the fuel declaration that do_6 raises to the measured need."
fix = "Decision 2774: a proof declares the measured need of the deployed guest for every budget dimension it declares (fuel, bytes, boundaries) while the product bounds stay; attempt 4 measures the boundary count and declares it."

[gotcha.3391]
title = "Thirteen first-party manifests carry a licence field other than the repository licence Apache-2.0: services/platform/perf-db/Cargo.toml (MIT OR Apache-2.0), tests/integration/dapp_tests/package.json and tests/integration/rpc_tests/package.json (MIT), tools/names/package.json, sdk/wallet/package.json, sdk/names/package.json, services/wallet/package.json and services/wallet/ceremony/legacy-import/package.json (UNLICENSED), contracts/package.json (ISC), contracts/launchpad/package.json (GPL-3.0) and the three sdk/launchpad packages ranking-algo-sdk, indexer-sdk and candles-sdk (a LicenseRef with no licence text anywhere in the repository); NOTICE lists the vendored trees under core/deps, sdk/js, tools/loadtest, tools/paxctl, tools/uci and tools/wasm-tools but not apps/explorer (GPL-3.0-only fork), services/explorer/backend (GPL-3.0), services/explorer/services/libs (MIT), the OpenZeppelin copy under tools/benchmark/loadtest/contracts/evm/lib or the MIT pooled inference engine that apps/inference-peer pins."
symptom = "The manifests were created by their sub-projects before the merge and no task compared licence fields with LICENSE and NOTICE."
fix = "Decision 2775 and task 22.31.612: first-party manifests carry Apache-2.0, vendored and forked trees keep their upstream field and are recorded in NOTICE, and a pytest sweep keeps future manifests aligned."

[gotcha.3392]
title = "22.31.539 attempt 9 repaired the store root fixture and the history case (both pass) and three cases of tests/repair_22_31_219.rs still fail on refusals that carry no check name: journey_wire_rotate_recover_bind_persisted_key_policy_over_socket at line 1104 where validate_authority_revocation answers Refused, and finalization_limit_and_reclaim_use_committed_receipts_and_independent_action_keys and finalization_rungs_and_session_observation_shape_survive_suspend_resume_archive_reopen at line 914 where apply_lifecycle_request over the socket answers Refused with reason operation.refused; every refusal site of services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/managed_agent.rs lines 140 to 545 returns the same bare HumanOperationError::Refused."
symptom = "Attempt 8 never reached these refusals because the store root fixture failed first; the refusing check cannot be named from the log because the variant carries no site."
fix = "Decision 2776: attempt 10 traces the refusal sites once inside the attempt to name the refusing check before any fixture change; a bare shared refusal variant is a diagnosis defect of the module, to be named by a later task."

[gotcha.3393]
title = "22.37.12 attempt 2 carried the attempt-1 tree unchanged, built and verified green (build 1 exit 0, verify 1 exit 0 with the API, causal-read, batch and graph checks) and was refused at publication because one changed file lies outside the task scope: the contracts module of the control-plane source_control directory, while the touches list names only the contracts module of the SDK source-control package; the thirteen other changed files are all in touches or planned_paths."
symptom = "The task lists one half of the wire contract (the SDK side) and the implementation necessarily changed the control-plane half too."
fix = "Decision 2777: the touches list gains the control-plane contracts module and attempt 3 requalifies the carried tree without edits."

[gotcha.3394]
title = "22.37.2 attempt 2 recreated the vendored inventory from the pinned subtree, passed the twelve gate fixture cases and the build, and the layout aggregation case 0_9.py still reports BLOCKED with 35 missing evidence items and zero regressions: one aggregation-input (the case reads build/layout/0.9/inputs.json, absent, with schema_version, layout_revision, authorized_followon_revisions and task_receipts), 29 follow-on-authorization items (every commit of the layout-to-head ancestry over the subtree prefixes must be in an explicit full-commit allowlist) and five task-runtime-receipt items (passing receipts of the driver cases 0.4 to 0.8, which run the package, runtime, packaging, routing and release assembly checks of the vendored project and are produced by no task of this feature)."
symptom = "The 0.9 case is the closure aggregation of the carried source-control specification and the task was given the aggregation itself as its verify, which no task-scoped change can turn green."
fix = "Decision 2778: the task writes the tracked aggregation input with the explicit follow-on allowlist and adds a pending-aggregation check that passes only when the sole missing evidence is the five driver receipts; the driver receipts become their own task."

[gotcha.3395]
title = "The layout driver receipts exist only in an untracked build directory"
symptom = "The five layout drivers 0_4.py to 0_8.py of the carried source-control specification write their receipts only under build/layout/<task>/receipt.json, an untracked directory, so the aggregation case 0_9.py finds no task-runtime-receipt at any revision: at d80dd7ef9388 it reported five task-runtime-receipt items among its 35 missing evidence entries, each a REQUIRED driver (0.4 to 0.8) with the assertion identifiers the case expects (root-workspace-membership, pinned-frozen-install, native-frontdoor-and-components, sdk-plugin-consumers, web-server-host-startup, installed-service-startup and the others), and nothing in the repository holds a receipt bound to the mapping digest, the layout generation and the source snapshot that task_receipt of 0_9.py compares."
fix = "A receipt that only exists in a build directory is never evidence for a tracked case; the drivers run once in the qualification environment and their PASS receipts are copied unchanged into a tracked receipts directory of the vendored spec dir, the aggregation input names them in its task_receipts map, and a test binds every tracked receipt to the current mapping digest so a mapping change fails loudly until the receipts are regenerated."

[gotcha.3396]
title = "Every managed-agent guard answers the one bare refusal, so the wire cannot name the refusing check"
symptom = "The managed-agent module of the agent daemon answers 232 guard sites outside its tests with the one bare refusal variant whose wire reason is operation.refused (the creation record shape, the stored record shape, the tenant guard, the budget owner guards, the session coordinate guards, the lifecycle kind guard, the revocation window and archived-state guards, the archive observation guard and the codec guards all share it), so a caller over the socket cannot tell which check refused a lifecycle request: 22.31.539 attempt 9 spent its budget on three cases that only saw operation.refused at line 914 and a bare Refused at line 1104 of tests/repair_22_31_219.rs."
fix = "A check enum in the managed-agent module with one variant per guard and a reason managed_agent.<check> carried by a new typed refusal variant; every guard on the lifecycle, revocation, finalization, snapshot, session and record paths returns its own variant and the bare variant stays only where no check applies."

[gotcha.3397]
title = "The licence alignment attempt committed a lockfile that the build step generated, so its verified revision was not its built revision"
symptom = "22.31.612 attempt 1 aligned the thirteen manifests, expanded NOTICE and wrote the fifteen test cases (verify 1 exit 0, every graph check green), and was refused at publication because the build ran at 6990b432 while the verification ran at 217fb415: the dependency installation of the build step reinstalls the packages of every directory whose package.json changed, which generated sdk/names/pnpm-lock.yaml (832 lines, no lockfile was tracked there) and the prepare outputs under tools/names/dist, and the agent committed the new lockfile after the build and before the verification; the drift list of the verification names 23 generated paths outside the touches."
fix = "The final tree is committed once before the build; a lockfile or a prepare output that the dependency installation generates in a directory the task does not name stays untracked, and the build and the verification run back to back on the same revision."

[gotcha.3398]
title = "The router plugin tests resolve the source-control SDK through its dist entries and the legacy queue is behind its own lockfile tests"
symptom = "22.37.18 attempt 1 built twice (exit 0) and failed both verifications in the router plugin test run: three suites (the routing module test, the runners test and the image builder test) and the new native outage case could not resolve the source-control SDK package because the plugin vitest configuration sets conditions source only under resolve and not under ssr, so externalised packages resolve through the import condition to dist entries that are never built, while the graph plugin configuration carries ssr resolve conditions source and externalConditions source and resolves the same package; the attempt changed the test script to node with conditions source, which does not reach the externalised resolution. Two legacy cases of queue.test.ts also failed at the base tree bf6c278443: regenerates a conflicting lockfile in a machine with merged manifests expects a conflict on platform/pnpm-lock.yaml to be regenerated with pnpm -C platform install --lockfile-only --no-frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts and merged, and machine failure leaves the integration branch intact expects the machine path to be reached for that conflict, while queue.ts lines 143 to 206 admit only a root pnpm-lock.yaml conflict and hold every other path with the reason Merge conflict."
fix = "The plugin vitest configuration gains the ssr resolve block of the graph plugin and keeps vitest run as its test script; the legacy queue admits a conflicting lockfile at any path, regenerates it in its own directory and adds it back, which the two landed cases already specify."

[gotcha.3399]
title = "Two same-wave room market tasks both extend the routing module of the ai-market program, so the second to land conflicts on the import list and the scratch maximum"
symptom = "22.38.5 attempt 1 (canary challenges with commit-reveal) built and verified green (build 1 exit 0, verify 1 exit 0 at 7926dcea0ed4) and was held at publication with a merge conflict on the routing module source file of the ai-market program: 22.38.3 (rooms, asks, bids and deals) landed meanwhile as 4e648d9573 and both attempts rewrite the same module import line (one adds the canary module, the other the rooms module), the same scratch maximum list (one adds the canary scratch bytes, the other the rooms scratch bytes) and neighbouring routing arms; the operation code ranges do not overlap."
fix = "The attempt rebases its tree onto the current main and resolves the routing module as the union: both modules imported, both scratch sizes in the maximum, the landed rooms arms unchanged and the canary score route added beside them, then builds and verifies at the final tree."

[gotcha.3400]
title = "A codec repair that writes its evidence record beside the tests is refused at publication for the record path"
symptom = "22.33.1135 attempt 1 (the Unicode normalisation tables of the codec, 2428 lines of src/codec/lxp_codec.c, the table generator, the two test files, the NormalizationTest-15.0.0.txt vectors with the UNICODE-LICENSE.txt) built and verified green at 5846420674 and was held because tests/repair_22_33_1135.kvx and the two vector files were outside touches and planned_paths at that revision of the spec; the vector directory is in touches today and the record path is not; the attempt tree merges cleanly onto the current main."
fix = "The planned paths of the task list the evidence record and the two vector files, and the attempt is relaunched with its tree standing."

[gotcha.3401]
title = "A test-gap repair of a shared agent daemon test file conflicts with the sibling part of the same audit record landed meanwhile"
symptom = "22.33.1536 attempt 8 (part 1 of 3 of audit record 22.30.95, 988 insertions over ten files, build 1 exit 0, verify green) was held with a merge conflict on services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/human_node_budgets.rs: part 2 of 3 landed as dbd4e68ed9 with a four-line change of that file while the attempt rewrites 59 lines of it; the other nine files merge cleanly."
fix = "The attempt rebases onto the current main, keeps the four-line change of the landed part and its own additions to the file, and reruns the build and the verification at the final tree."

[gotcha.3402]
title = "The tracked follow-on allowlist of the layout aggregation cannot contain the commit that carries it, so the candidate revision is always unauthorized"
symptom = "22.37.2 attempt 3 (build 2 exit 0, the fifteen gate fixtures green) failed its verification in the pending aggregation check: the aggregation report at b046a74dc9cf listed the five expected driver receipts and one unexpected missing evidence of kind follow-on-authorization for the candidate revision itself with eight changed paths, because the follow-on check of cases/source_control/0_9.py requires every commit of the layout-to-candidate ancestry to appear in authorized_followon_revisions of spec/<project>-source-control/layout-aggregation-input.json, and the commit that writes that list is created after the list is written; no tree can list its own commit id. The attempt also recorded the pre-existing clean-tree finding in the qualification record."
fix = "The commit that last changed the aggregation input is authorized by construction: the follow-on check resolves it with git log of the input path, excludes it from the commits that need listing, records it in the report as the self-authorized revision bound to the digest of the input, and still reports every later unlisted commit as missing evidence; the allowlist is regenerated at the final tree and the gate fixtures cover the self-authorized commit and a later unlisted one."

[gotcha.3403]
title = "The ask stream precompile methods are routed by a method family switch in a file the task did not name"
symptom = "22.38.9 attempt 2 (build 2 exit 0 at 0ab010459bb7) failed its verification with LXP_PRECOMPILE_UNKNOWN_METHOD: askStreamOf in every TestStreamAsk case: the attempt added streamOpenForAsk and askStreamOf to precompiles/layerxpay/stream.go, abi.json, events.go and gas.go, but the entry point precompiles/layerxpay/layerxpay.go routes state-changing calls through a switch over method names per family (the stream family case lists streamOpen, streamTopUp, streamMeter, streamSettle, streamPause, streamResume and streamClose) and routes reads through a view switch (getStream, getStreamResult, streamAccrued), neither of which names the two new methods, and the file was outside the touches of the task; the agent stopped at the touches boundary."
fix = "The touches of the task name the entry point; the stream family case gains streamOpenForAsk and the view switch gains askStreamOf, and the attempt is relaunched as a continuation."

[gotcha.3404]
title = "The wire test repair imports the custody modules of the crypto crate and the client crate, which its manifest never gives the tests"
symptom = "22.33.1523 attempt 1 rewrote hashing.rs, rejection.rs, structures.rs and wallet_vectors.rs and wrote the 749-line repair_22_33_1523.rs as the proposals ask (real native builders, signing, decoder and consumer), and its single build (exit 101 at 6511c613c254) failed with seven resolution errors: the test imports layerx_crypto::authority_grant, layerx_crypto::disclosure, layerx_crypto::evm_transaction, layerx_crypto::send and layerx_crypto::signer, which lib.rs gates behind the custody feature, while the dev-dependency in services/agent/crates/layerx-wire/Cargo.toml sets default-features = false, and it imports layerx_client::sequencer::SequencerEndpoint while layerx-client is not a dependency of the crate at all; the manifest was outside the touches, so the agent stopped at the build."
fix = "The manifest of the crate under test is a touch of the repair: the crypto dev-dependency keeps its default features so the custody modules are available to the tests, layerx-client is added as a path dev-dependency (a dev-dependency cycle through the crate under test is permitted), the lock is refreshed once without the locked flag and committed with the manifest, and the build and the verification run on that one revision."

[gotcha.3405]
title = "Four public workflows fail at the tip for reasons in the job environment and not in the product"
symptom = "At main 9ed1b836b1 the c17 gcc and clang jobs abort in make test-arena because the selected host preloads a library ahead of the ASan runtime and traces processes so LeakSanitizer refuses to run; every shard of the blocktests job refuses with RUNNER_TEMP must resolve below HOME because the prepare step assumes the temporary directory lives under HOME; the platform job calls mvn after a setup-java step that installs no Maven; and the release-build-alpine job of the wasm runtime fails on cp of libwasmvm_muslc.a because the published builder image writes the suffixed archive name that the tree script in wasm-runtime/builders/guest/build_muslc.sh never uses. The golangci job reports 92 findings (bodyclose in tools/flyci/controller/fly.go, errcheck in services/bridge/deploy)."
fix = "Each failure is one repair task of the 7.0.0 readiness series (22.39.3 to 22.39.7) with a test that pins the corrected workflow or Makefile text; the job host choices stay with the owner."

[gotcha.3406]
title = "The offline export consumer case refuses with the unit Contract variant after the committed level change and the log names no site"
symptom = "22.31.539 attempt 10 at ed476ecc007e built (exit 0) and failed exactly one case of tests/repair_22_33_1525.rs, offline_export_producer_rpc_consumer_and_mismatched_fact_refusal, with ExportProduceError::Contract raised through the must helper at line 63 while the six other cases of the file passed; attempt 9 never reached that file because repair_22_31_219.rs failed first, no commit under services/agent landed between the base trees of the two attempts, and the only edit of the attempt to that test is the identity fixture level at line 665 changed from CHECKPOINT_FINALISED to COMMITTED. Contract is a unit variant raised at more than sixty sites of export.rs (the validate call at line 192, the height and selector count check at line 196, the required account proof at line 307, the covering block at line 320, the retain_bundle path and the RLP decoders), so the test output alone cannot name the producer check."
fix = "One run of the single case with RUST_BACKTRACE=1 names the raising frame; the repair is made at that site on the producer side or, when the site reads the resolver level, by restoring the fixture level, never by weakening the consumer assertion."

[gotcha.3407]
title = "Two legacy suites of the router plugin specify the behaviour before manager planning that the base tree no longer has"
symptom = "22.37.18 attempt 2 at b34273fede built (exit 0) and failed the plugin test run with fifteen failures in two suites: the routing module test (ten cases: pause and cap controls, cancelled job, HTTP 429 retry and backoff, membership claims, cap reservations, availability, retry once, backoff ceiling, reconcile ledgers, cleanup when preparation fails, each finding an empty jobs list) and src/server-backend.test.ts (five cases: paused state, three registrations where two are expected, MANAGER_DECISION_REQUIRED, default server paused, ticks after resume), while the queue suite with its two lockfile cases, the runners, spec-source, builder and storage suites and the native outage case passed; the base tree 05002f9e4 already defaults to manager planning, requires an authenticated manager decision and registers three contracts, which the two suites predate and the task does not own."
fix = "The gate of the task is narrowed to the suites it owns and the 4.2 case; the two legacy suites are aligned with the landed manager-decision behaviour by a follow-on task of the same owner that requires this one and runs the full plugin test."

[gotcha.3408]
title = "The ai-market view binding test of the inventory repair carries the old width of the availability array"
symptom = "22.99.77 attempt 21 at dd94f1eed20d failed build 3 (exit 101) at tests/view_binding.rs line 332 where the carried tree asserts an availability array of ten entries while feature_availability returns eleven since the eleventh feature landed (b5a4f2ce26, task 22.38.1, an ancestor of the attempt); the main tree reads entry 0 at line 332 and asserts eleven NotYetProduced entries at line 353, so the stale literal is an edit the attempt carried from its earlier base and not a base mismatch."
fix = "The continuation takes the availability assertions of the main tree (eleven entries, entry 0) into tests/view_binding.rs, keeps every other attempt addition, and applies the attempt-21 ruling otherwise unchanged."

[gotcha.3409]
title = "The clean-revision check of the layout aggregation counts untracked outputs of the dependency installation as a dirty tree"
symptom = "22.37.2 attempt 4 at 97407a1e9e built (exit 0), passed the seventeen gate fixtures and recorded zero regressions and the five pending driver receipts, and the pending aggregation check refused on the one failed check source.final-revision-clean: cases/source_control/0_9.py line 542 reads git status with untracked-files set to all and requires an empty result, but the qualification environment installs dependencies before the build and that installation generates sdk/names/pnpm-lock.yaml and the tools/names/dist tree, which are untracked, not ignored and never part of the candidate revision (gotcha 3397, decision 2781); the same check already failed in attempts 1 and 3 behind the recapture and the authorization refusals, so the pending aggregation can never pass as written."
fix = "The check compares the tracked content with the committed revision only (git status with untracked-files set to no, or git diff --quiet HEAD) and records the untracked paths as evidence; a gate fixture proves that an untracked file leaves the check passing while a modified tracked file fails it."

[gotcha.3410]
title = "The platform lockfile is stale on the main tree, so the clock helper of every daemon verification refuses before a test runs"
symptom = "9.98.4 attempt 10 at aaf20e51047e built (exit 0) and failed its verification with exit 101 before any test ran: tools/runtime/run-with-clock.sh builds layerx-runtime-clock from services/platform/Cargo.toml with the locked flag and cargo refused because services/platform/Cargo.lock needs to be updated; the same refusal is reproducible on the main tree with cargo metadata --locked. The lock was last written on 2026-11-04 (ef11ec4bc2), no platform manifest changed a dependency since, but the platform crates carry path dependencies on layerx-agentd, layerx-wire, layerx-types, layerx-crypto, the program crates and the interop crates, and the agent manifests changed on 2026-11-05 and 2026-11-06 (6c7e27fb0d, 8e43ba58e4, c59eebe59b) without a platform lock refresh, so the platform resolution now needs entries the lock does not carry (the offline relock asks for rustls 0.23.46). Nine pending tasks verify through the clock helper (22.31.554, 22.31.555, 9.98.4, 9.35.19 to 9.35.24)."
fix = "One repair task refreshes services/platform/Cargo.lock with a single cargo resolution without the locked flag, records the entries that changed and the manifest change that required each, and every task whose verification runs the clock helper requires it; a task that changes the dependencies of a crate another lockfile resolves by path refreshes that lockfile in the same commit."

[gotcha.3411]
title = "The attestor real-profile gate omitted the compiled Rust custody consumer and the runtime clock that both tests require"
symptom = "22.39.8 attempt 1 at 072c86dbd9c7 built the native library and vetted the server package (exit 0), wired the inventory into the two real-profile tests, and failed the verification in both TestNativeCustodyRealProfiles and TestNativeSendPurposeRealProfiles at native_purpose_test.go lines 326 and 644 with prebuilt real Rust custody consumer is required: the tests read PAXEER_X_NATIVE_CUSTODY_RUST_TEST, the compiled attestor_native_profile test executable of layerx-human-kms that task 18.1110.1 builds with cargo test --no-run and exports in its gate, and the consumer entry points read the runtime clock socket that tools/runtime/run-with-clock.sh provides (repair_22_31_598.kvx); the gate of 22.39.8 was written with neither, and the go-cgo image carries no Rust toolchain."
fix = "The gate of 22.39.8 takes the consumer build and the exported executable path of 18.1110.1, runs the two tests through the clock helper under the mixed image, and the task requires 22.31.614 because the clock helper builds the platform runtime clock with the locked flag."

[gotcha.3412]
title = "The ai-market guest grew past the deployment payload bound on main while its gates never measured it"
symptom = "22.99.77 attempt 22 at 7d5daec19bd1 resolved the routing conflict against the room market family and corrected the availability assertions, and build 3 failed at the bound check of the host boundary target: the size-optimised guest measures 553180 bytes against the 524184-byte bound (524288 less the 104-byte deployment envelope, decision 2675, never raised). Attempt 10 had the guest at 512760 bytes; since then the room market family table (22.38.1), the participant manifest capability fields (22.38.2), rooms, asks, bids and deals (22.38.3) and the canary challenges (22.38.5) landed on main under gates that build the crate for its native tests only, so the bound was never checked at main while the guest grew by about forty kilobytes, and four pending tasks of the same family (22.38.4, 22.38.6, 22.38.7, 22.38.8, 22.38.11) add more operations under the same gates."
fix = "A repair task of the programs owner brings the guest at main at least twenty thousand bytes under the bound by code-size work inside the crate and records the sizes; every pending task that changes the guest source carries the host boundary target and the bound check in its build under the mixed image and requires the repair; 22.99.77 continues after the repair lands and measures the merged tree."

[gotcha.3413]
title = "The layout clean-revision check read the status of the whole repository while the task bookkeeping modifies two tracked root paths before every verification"
symptom = "22.37.2 attempt 5 at 279f4adf5f44 passed its build and all nineteen receipt-gate cases and was refused by the pending aggregation check at source.final-revision-clean: the check of cases/source_control/0_9.py now ignores untracked paths (decision 2789) but still reads git status from the layout root without a path limit, so the whole repository answers, and the engineering process records the task start in spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx and in .cgignore at the repository root before the verification runs; those two tracked modifications lie outside the vendored tree whose layout the candidate revision binds, and the attempt recorded them as a pre-existing finding instead of scoping the check."
fix = "The clean-revision check limits the status call to the layout root with the pathspec of that directory, so the candidate revision is bound to the tracked content of the vendored tree only; tracked modifications outside the root are listed in the report as outside_root_paths with their count and never fail the check."

[gotcha.3414]
title = "The human services lockfile is stale behind the attestor real-profile consumer build, and twelve more tracked lockfiles no longer resolve with the locked flag"
symptom = "22.39.8 attempt 2 at 5f8a72b33391 built the native library and vetted the server package (exit 0) and failed its build at the consumer step: cargo test --locked on services/human/Cargo.toml refuses because services/human/Cargo.lock needs to be updated, the same class as the platform lockfile of gotcha 3410, so neither real-profile test ran. A light check with cargo metadata --locked over every tracked Cargo.lock finds the same refusal at services/agent/fuzz, services/agent/qualification/pay2, services/agent/tests/boundary, services/agent/tests/isolation, services/agent/tests/parity, services/agent/tests/qualify, services/agent/tools/audit-verify, services/agent/tools/policy-harness, services/human/crates/layerx-intents/fuzz, services/interop, services/platform/examples/samples/verify-receipt-rust, services/platform/hosted/node/tests/probe and tools/platform: each resolves a path dependency to a crate whose manifest changed after the lock was last written (decision 2790)."
fix = "One refresh task per owner refreshes the stale lockfiles of its directories with exactly one resolution each and adds a public check that every refreshed lock resolves with the locked flag; 22.39.8 requires the human refresh and continues after it lands."

[gotcha.3415]
title = "Thirty-six decision records carry their affects field as a list of single characters"
symptom = "Decisions 2757 through 2792 were written with the affects argument as one sentence instead of a list of task identifiers, and the record writer stores affects as a list, so each of these records holds one character per list item and names no task; decisions through 2756 list identifiers."
fix = "Each of the thirty-six affects lists is rewritten with the task identifiers the sentence named; new decisions pass a list of identifiers."

[gotcha.3416]
title = "The lap settlement fixture admitted more participants in one epoch than the admission window holds and its repaired tree was never verified"
symptom = "22.38.4 attempt 1: build 3 passed at f22b7c0c5bc9 after a borrow lifetime error in build 1, and verification 1 at 9d6804ebcaad failed all five tests of tests/f11_lap_settlement.rs inside the fixture at the evaluator admission step with application error 2061, which is F08_ADMISSION_WINDOW_FULL: the admission table admits four participants per epoch (the successful_enrollments_per_epoch field of POLICY_V1 in admission.rs) and the fixture at that revision admitted more than four in the first epoch. The final tree admits the second peer at ORIGIN plus 130, after the next epoch opens, exactly as the landed canary test fixture keeps one peer and three evaluators in the first epoch, but both repair cycles were spent before that tree was verified, so the verification refused to run again."
fix = "Attempt 2 verifies the final tree first (decision 2771) and keeps at most four admissions per epoch in every fixture of the task; the task now carries the guest bound build of decision 2792 and the module mirror check of decision 2794."

[gotcha.3417]
title = "The gateway test that includes the ai-market sources by path stopped compiling when two modules were added to the crate"
symptom = "services/platform/hosted/gateway/tests/repair_22_33_1439.rs mirrors the module list of programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market through sixty-one path includes. 22.38.3 added the rooms module and 22.38.5 added the canary module to the crate and to the import list of its routing module, the mirror never followed, and the test target of the gateway now fails to compile at main with thirteen unresolved references. The dependent-crate check of every agent daemon task compiles that target, so 22.31.542 attempt 1 at b08b5e87298d and 22.31.555 attempt 1 at 318a3d72a8e6 passed their builds and were refused before verification by a failure that sits on main."
fix = "A repair task of the platform owner adds the two includes and a currency check in tests/ci that compares the include list with the module list of the crate; every pending agent daemon task and every pending guest task requires the repair, and every guest task runs the currency check in its build so a module added without its mirror line fails at its own gate."

[gotcha.3418]
title = "The assignment path creates workspace rows without the base retention pin the checkpoint path now requires"
symptom = "22.37.18 attempt 3 at c9194f8f7a59: the owned suites passed (23 tests) and the 4.2 case failed at the first checkpoint of the assigned participant with WORKSPACE_EXPIRED, Workspace base retention is unavailable. The checkpoint path of the workspaces module of the control plane source-control service looks up the retention pin row of the workspace since 22.37.14 landed at 7d92290fde (10:54Z on 2026-11-07), while the assignment adapter module inserts its workspace row without pinning the base root tree; the 4.1 case landed at 10:24Z, before that check existed, and the 4.2 case is the only case at main that drives the assignment path."
fix = "A repair task of the tools-ops owner pins the base root tree of every assigned workspace with the same retention the create path applies and proves it with a case that assigns one participant and checkpoints once; 22.37.18 requires the repair and verifies its final tree first."

[gotcha.3419]
title = "The human service receipt frame test imported the budget proof error type from a module that does not re-export it"
symptom = "22.31.540 attempt 1 at 95890bc63c80: build 3 failed because tests/repair_22_31_540.rs imports BudgetProofError from the budget module of the agent daemon, which re-exports only budget_proof_committed_head, verify_budget_proof, BudgetProofTrust and VerifiedBudgetProof; the type is public in the budget_proof submodule of that module and has the single variant Refused. The attempt also refreshed services/human/Cargo.lock, which 22.31.616 refreshes for every user of that manifest (decision 2790). Both repair cycles were spent and the verification never ran."
fix = "Attempt 2 imports the type from the submodule that defines it, takes the lockfile of main after 22.31.616 lands, and runs the build and the verification back to back at the final revision."

[gotcha.3420]
title = "A qualification audit case read every gateway container env item as a literal value while the deployment had moved two of them to config map references"
symptom = "22.39.26 attempt 1 at 5f695f6fb627 added the make target that runs the 327 Python suites under tools/qualification and a public check that hosts it; the verification stopped at collection on tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_33_1395.py line 23, which builds a name to value map over the env items of the gateway container of services/platform/hosted/gateway/deployment.yaml and raises KeyError value, because 8efee4ff17 (22.31.594) turned LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_URL and LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_URL into configMapKeyRef entries without a value key. The suites under tools/qualification never ran in a public check, so the break sat on main unnoticed since that commit, and the attempt spent both repair cycles on it."
fix = "A repair task runs the collection and the suites of tools/qualification at the starting revision, records every collection error and failure, and repairs each one to the current names of its producer (an env item is read by its name, with its literal value or its reference); the check task requires the repair and continues after it lands with its tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3421]
title = "The first size pass of the ai-market guest stopped 4825 bytes short of its target and the dependent-crate check refused the repair on the gateway mirror"
symptom = "22.31.615 attempt 1 at 273d1905d0e1 brought the size-optimised guest from 553180 to 509009 bytes in three builds by the techniques of decision 2792, 4825 bytes above the 504184-byte target, with both repair cycles spent; the dependent-crate check then refused the attempt on the fourteen errors of gotcha 3417 because the gateway mirror test compiles the ai-market sources, and the task did not require 22.31.620, which decision 2794 listed only for the tasks that add modules."
fix = "Every pending task whose touches name the ai-market crate source requires 22.31.620 while the mirror repair is pending; the size repair continues after it lands from the attempt-1 tree with a bounded list of remaining reductions and the same target."

[gotcha.3422]
title = "The five repository layout drivers of the carried source-control specification have no inputs in the qualification environment, so their receipts can never be PASS there"
symptom = "22.37.28 attempt 1 at 79746e9864 ran drivers 0.4 to 0.8 of tests/<project>/cases/source_control; none produced a PASS receipt: 0.4 to 0.6 found no layout build artifacts and no pinned Node installations, 0.7 found no runtime artifacts and no desktop or Android executor evidence, 0.8 failed the source-stamp check and found no release or prepared-image evidence. The attempt repaired the drivers that threw before writing a receipt and two checks that compared a project subtree against the host tree, then failed its own receipts test because the five tracked receipts under spec/<project>-source-control/receipts are absent. 22.37.3 attempt 1 at 2db44337329e passed its SDK test and then stopped at the aggregation check 0_10.py, which refuses with LAYOUT_RECEIPT_REQUIRED while build/layout/0.9/receipt.json is absent, so its contract consumer never ran."
fix = "Decision 2797: the receipts test and the aggregation consumer qualify in component mode (decision 2700): tracked receipts are validated when present and reported UNRUN when absent, the aggregation input shape, the driver modules and the regeneration section are validated either way, and the consumer runs directly; the five driver runs and the live aggregation are recorded UNRUN with their exact commands for the owner, who produces the receipts in an environment that holds the inputs."

[gotcha.3423]
title = "The conformance copy of the committed receipt vector was never refreshed after its source was re-recorded, and the only test that compares the two is red on main"
symptom = "Commit 74ef78b42b (22.31.486, 2026-11-04) re-recorded daemon/committed-fixture/vectors/vector-v4-committed.json under chain id 125 and refreshed the SDK, explorer and node consumers, but not services/interop/specs/conformance/committed/vector-v4-committed.json, which the script services/interop/crates/layerx-committed-proof/scripts/record_committed_vectors.py derives from it: the copy still carries chain id committed-fixture and a provenance sourceSha256 of a recording that no longer exists. tests/repair_22_31_156.rs of the human service asserts at line 113 that the signed receipt of the copy equals the positive receipt of the source, so its five committed-receipt tests fail at every revision since that day; 22.31.540 attempt 2 at 3810cd465592 exposed it because its verification names that test, while no public check runs it."
fix = "Repair task 22.31.622 of the interop owner reruns the recording script, refreshes every consumer that pins values of the old recording and adds a public check that the provenance digest of the copy equals the digest of the source; decision 2799 binds every later re-recording to the script; 22.31.540 requires the repair and continues unchanged."

[gotcha.3424]
title = "The gateway mirror of the ai-market modules rejects a comparison the crate itself accepts"
symptom = "22.31.620 attempt 1 at 34d49ec60d93 added the canary and rooms includes to services/platform/hosted/gateway/tests/repair_22_33_1439.rs and the mirror check, and the build then failed with E0277 at programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/src/rooms.rs line 572: the take_while comparison compares a byte slice of the table row against id.as_bytes(), which resolves to a 32-byte array reference in the mirrored compilation, and no PartialOrd between a slice and an array exists; the same line compiles inside the crate, where the receiver type of as_bytes differs. The task refused to touch the crate source because rooms.rs was outside its touches."
fix = "The comparison is written slice against slice (index the array with a full range or call as_slice), which compiles in both module trees; 22.31.620 gains rooms.rs in its touches and continues with that one change, records the type difference it finds, and the mirror check keeps the rest of the tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3425]
title = "The native custody profile gate never built the send consumer and its first consumer failed on a read timeout surfaced as a raw transport error"
symptom = "22.39.8 attempt 3 at 36cbc27b99 ran the Go native profiles through tools/runtime/run-with-clock.sh: the inventory refusal was asserted, then the Rust consumer of the attestor native profile failed after 0.88 seconds with Io(Os code 11, WouldBlock) while the Go side logged twenty-four TLS handshake errors with EOF in the same second, and TestNativeSendPurposeRealProfiles stopped because PAXEER_X_NATIVE_SEND_RUST_TEST was not set: the gate builds only the attestor_native_profile executable although the send profile needs the native_send_purpose executable of the human service (line 654 of native_purpose_test.go). Code 11 on a blocking socket is the read timeout set by SO_RCVTIMEO; the attestor client at services/human/crates/layerx-human-kms/src/attestor.rs maps only the Timeout variant of the HTTP client error to its Timeout error (transport_error, line 2058) and the error reached the test unmapped, so the per-call budget of the failing call (line 485) was near zero rather than the 120 seconds the test configures."
fix = "Decision 2798: the gate builds both consumers and exports both executables; attempt 4 traces the budget passed at the failing call under the test, derives it from the same clock as the deadline, and classifies an Io error of kind WouldBlock or TimedOut as Timeout."

[gotcha.3426]
title = "A protocol page of the documentation site links a repository file outside the site directory"
symptom = "22.39.39 attempt 1 at 76f5c401454d repaired the x402 page link named by the task and wrote the two tests; test_site_relative_links_stay_inside_docs_dir then found docs/site/docs/protocol/finality.md line 9 linking ../../../paxeer-network.md, which resolves to docs/paxeer-network.md outside docs/site/docs. The task text called the x402 link the only such link because the survey counted only links that did not resolve; this one resolves to a tracked file and still leaves the strict build."
fix = "22.39.39 gains the finality page in its touches and continues: the link points at the site page docs/site/docs/overview/unified-network.md when it covers the execution and finality model, otherwise at the repository URL of docs/paxeer-network.md on the main branch, and the test keeps both assertions."

[gotcha.3427]
title = "The tools/ci test suite fails twenty assertions at main once it is collected"
symptom = "22.39.47 attempt 1 at 4fae3a7ef385 made the tools/ci suite collectable (the completion gate moved beside its peers, the Makefile and the publish-images and runner-routing checks corrected) and the suite then failed 20 of 125 tests against the live tree: test_ci_loadtest_job expects a literal runs-on while ci.yml now carries the routing expression; test_foundry_profile and test_solidity_state_surface need forge, absent from the python image; the wave1 and wave2 Makefile tests pin an exclusion set the Makefile has since extended by the oracle adapter, oracle root and the challenge sources; the wave4 and wave6 dry-run tests see make -n exit 2 and miss the genesis build line; test_replay_golden_ci finds fixed runners in ci.yml, explorer-images.yml and launchpad-test.yml; seven test_wallet_check_live cases capture no probe paths from check-live.sh; test_wallet_gate_targets reports a malformed target line from gate-lint.sh; test_wallet_go_test_workflow misses the wire wallet vectors path in the paths filter; test_xweb_workflow_check exits 1 on xweb-workflow-check.sh; and the beta ledger path check counts 6434 violations. The attempt recorded the list in a task-local record and stopped, the verification never narrowed."
fix = "A repair task of the tools owner takes the recorded twenty as its baseline and settles each against the live rule (test stale, producer defect, or an absent tool recorded as a skip), and 22.39.47 continues after it lands."

[gotcha.3428]
title = "The real FUSE case cannot run in the qualification environment"
symptom = "22.37.15 attempt 1 at 705085632471 bound the virtual filesystem writes to the attempt expiry and ran the 3_2 case twice: the first run failed because the host daemon resolved the source-control SDK through its package link and the SDK dist was never built by the build command (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND on dist/host.js); the second run failed before any mounted assertion with the typed error Missing source object backend configuration, because the case defaults to the live object store and the environment carries no object store credentials, no /dev/fuse and no pinned mount helpers."
fix = "The build command builds the source-control SDK before the typecheck; the case gains a component mode that runs the write-expiry binding and the mounted-path assertions against the in-process object backend and the virtual filesystem; the live run stays recorded UNRUN with its exact command until the owner runs it (decision 2700)."

[gotcha.3429]
title = "Two site-check verifications point the platform site build at the filesystem root"
symptom = "22.39.30 attempt 1 at 97f1c0369a16 rewrote the six receipt pages and passed its thirteen tests, then the second half of the verification, the platform site check, failed with FileNotFoundError on /docs/platform/site.kvx: the check takes the repository path and the command passed ../.., which from the repository root is the filesystem root. 22.39.31 carries the same argument."
fix = "Both verifications pass the repository root as the single dot; a verification path argument is written relative to the repository root (decision 2802)."

[gotcha.3430]
title = "Three pages outside the inference market guides still cite task and decision records"
symptom = "22.39.37 attempt 1 at 3deb4f6cdbd5 removed the records from the eight pages in its touches and its repository-wide test then found three more pages: the source-control recovery page of the vendored project docs cites a task and a decision on one line, the perps ABI change history cites decisions on two lines, and the wallet service security review cites a decision reference on one line."
fix = "The three pages join the touches and the attempt continues; the facts stay, the record numbers go."

[gotcha.3431]
title = "The image namespace check read the Go module path as a registry namespace"
symptom = "22.39.48 attempt 1 at 8ff17c5a4935 moved the pax image under the registry namespace of the repository owner and its new test then asserted that no workflow contains the old repository name in any case, which failed on the db-tests workflow where the state database package prefix is the Go module path github.com/Sidiora-Labs/Paxeer-X-Network/storage/state_db. The module path is the import path of the root Go module and stays until the module is renamed, which is an owner decision."
fix = "The check asserts registry image references (ghcr.io namespaces, image and tag fields) and exempts Go import paths; the module rename is flagged to the owner (decision 2801)."

[gotcha.3432]
title = "The node image context drops an interop test target the manifest declares"
symptom = "22.39.53 attempt 1 at 47e49dfbb78e collected the websearch context module under pytest and its negative check refused the context: services/interop/tests/repair_22_33_95.rs is declared as a test target of layerx-portable by path, the Docker ignore file of the node image excludes services/interop and re-includes only the crates, the Cargo manifest and the lock file, so the manifest names a file the context does not carry and cargo refuses the manifest inside the image build."
fix = "The ignore file re-includes the declared test file; the task continues with the ignore file in its touches."

[gotcha.3433]
title = "The wallet surface suites load again and fail twenty-seven assertions"
symptom = "22.39.42 attempt 1 at e3a22cbc5a67 repaired the sdk/wallet package manager field and the apps/wallet environment so that every suite in its list collects and runs; the run then failed 27 assertions in seven suites (WebDataView 18, ExchangeView 4, BridgeView, FeeChoice, LaunchpadView, the chain surface test and the repair-22-33-206 test one each), all of the form condition not reached: receipt or a retired grant assertion, while the pwa suite and the three repair suites passed."
fix = "The loading task verifies collection of every suite and the four green suites; a repair task of the wallet owner takes the 27 as its baseline and settles each against the live receipt model (decision 2800)."

[gotcha.3434]
title = "Public pages still link the old repository name and carry dead vendored links"
symptom = "The link sweep at c42baaf772 found 14 English lines linking or cloning github.com/Sidiora-Labs/Paxeer-X-Network (the code of conduct, RELEASE.md, the consensus and bridge READMEs, the beta environment page, the wiki home, the programs README and the explorer backend devcontainer README), 20 badge and source lines in the de, es, pt-BR and zh-CN README translations pointing at the old name while fr, ja and ru are correct, the hpx README provenance example at v6.12.0, seven vendored wasm-tools crate READMEs linking a LICENSE file the vendored copy does not track, five vendored pages linking files the copy dropped, 30 relative links in the explorer backend changelog to upstream pages absent from the tree, placeholder wording in the loadtest README and the bundled libsecp256k1 README, and no repository-wide Markdown link check."
fix = "Four documentation tasks repair the pages and one adds the repository-wide guard that would have caught them."

[gotcha.3435]
title = "The qualification suites collect again and fail two hundred and sixty-seven cases"
symptom = "22.31.621 attempt 1 at baa4f93534f1 (final tree d186f583392a after two repair cycles) made every Python module under tools/qualification collect and the whole run then reported 4172 passed, 267 failed, 1 error and 5 skipped: recorded transaction envelopes compared against the live wire shape in the 22.33.809 repair test, the px_register and px_resolveAccount contract pins reported as changed or abbreviated, and further families the attempt listed in tools/qualification/repair_22_31_621.kvx before the verification could be rerun."
fix = "The collection task verifies collection, the first known break and the collection test; a repair task of the tools owner takes the 267 as its baseline, groups them by module family and reason, and settles each family against the live rule (decision 2800)."

[gotcha.3436]
title = "The native profile gate reached both Rust consumers and the repair it needs sits outside the task touches"
symptom = "22.39.8 attempt 4 at f0a1d7853316 built both Rust consumers and ran the Go gate through the runtime clock: both Go tests passed their signing, replay, restart and refusal assertions, then the custody consumer returned Io WouldBlock after 0.82 seconds exactly as attempt 3 did, and the send consumer, run for the first time, returned Mismatch on the native send domain after 1.14 seconds. The attempt stopped because the attestor client source that decision 2798 told it to repair is not in the touches of the task, and recorded the conflict instead of editing it."
fix = "The attestor client source, the send consumer test and the human service source join the touches; a continuation note that names a file to change adds that file to the touches in the same record (decision 2805); attempt 5 repairs the read timeout mapping and the budget derivation and traces the send domain disagreement between the Go server and the Rust consumer."

[gotcha.3437]
title = "The public tree carries stray files, duplicated assets, undeclared licences, provider host names and process numbering"
symptom = "The repository hygiene sweep at c42baaf772 found two empty files with run-together names, a dated patch directory with a bundle and two patch files, a 2.6 MB unreferenced model, 21 keep markers beside real files and a mis-encoded dash in a script header; 80 asset paths with spaces and raw design-export names, four assets stored four times (a 1.55 MB logo among them) and a byte-for-byte copy of the explorer base stylesheet in the perps app; 82 groups of byte-identical files over 20 KB (the explorer OpenAPI document twice, three precompile ABIs copied into the attestor policy, a retired inventory fixture equal to the live inventory, two generated statik bundles of 14 MB and 9.1 MB); 51 production and 32 example manifests without a licence field and six that disagree with the governing LICENSE; 12 manifests and 159 documentation links naming old repositories and a CITATION.cff at v6.12.0; a real hosting-provider public host in a gateway test input, 58 lines naming the hosting-provider private-network host form, fixed private peer names in deployment tables, a real public address in two example comments and private addresses in three scripts; 181 lines in 89 pages explaining the product by task, repair, gotcha and decision numbers; pages that instruct readers to run the engineering process; 11 key and certificate fixtures under src directories; 78 tracked files over 2 MB with no budget; logo assets of 1.5 to 7.3 MB served to every visitor; and 41 root directories without a layout table."
fix = "Twelve hygiene tasks of the docs, tools, web and platform owners repair each class and add the guard that keeps it out (decision 2803); the owner items (module renames, the vendored copies, the provider deployment tables, the domain list, the licence of the launchpad service, the large fixtures) are recorded for the owner."

[gotcha.3438]
title = "Large parts of the test tree are reached by no workflow"
symptom = "The CI coverage sweep at c42baaf772 found make recipes that workflows call naming three deleted scripts and a deleted fixture generator; the agent SDK Python suite (43 modules, 361 tests) with seven modules importing names retired by 22.33.16 and 22.33.17 and no workflow running it, a second 98-test SDK tree and eight agent crates with no runner; 11 of the 15 interop crates never tested in CI; about 690 launchpad Go test files behind a make ci target no workflow calls; 66 C suites reached only through the core-test-all target no workflow calls, four of them drifted from current headers; the explorer Rust and frontend suites only type-checked; the platform middleware node suites, the pay6 and example Python suites and the integration packages never run; the wallet gateway (69 files), ceremony import and demo suites never run; the iOS integration package only built, never tested; the forge step selecting no suite under the default profile; tag-gated Go tests and the hpx registry never run; Python suites under tests, cmd, scripts, services and tools with no runner; and JS packages with test scripts no workflow calls."
fix = "Fourteen wiring tasks give every suite a workflow-reached runner or a recorded exclusion and add a check per family (decision 2804)."

[gotcha.3439]
title = "The platform install page names a capability the capabilities document does not declare, and the site check fails for every page task"
symptom = "22.39.30 attempt 2 at 4622e0d9befc rewrote the six finality pages and passed its 13 tests, then the site check over the whole documentation root failed on a different page: the install page table row Native payment execution and block finality (landed with the documentation fold of 22.36.2) carries a label that no entry of docs/platform/capabilities.kvx declares, so the build refuses. Every page task whose gate runs the site check meets the same refusal until the row and the capabilities document agree."
fix = "Attempt 3 adds the install page and the capabilities document to its touches and makes the row name a declared capability (or declares the capability it names); 22.39.31, which runs the same check, now requires 22.39.30."

[gotcha.3440]
title = "A shared test support module carries its own fixture test and a gateway consumer that includes it by path runs that test without the Go step that writes the fixture"
symptom = "22.31.620 attempt 2 at ce6e7549ba08 built the gateway repair test and ran it: 39 tests passed and two failed. The ai-market support module repair_478_fixture.rs, which the gateway test includes by path for its decoders, also defines the test fund_entry_gas_for_committed_receipt_fixture_is_bounded, which reads the owner, asset and measurement files under programs/target/repair-478 that the rpc Go repair test writes; the gateway gate never runs that Go test, so the read fails with No such file or directory. The second failure is the test node_root_and_explicit_chain_paths_reject_router_paths at line 609: the eth_blockNumber result of the gateway was Null instead of 0xb for one of the three node path suffixes."
fix = "The fixture test moves into the fuel budget test of the ai-market crate, which already reads the same files, so the support module runs no test of its own in any consumer; the Null result is traced inside the attempt with the suffix and the full response printed once, and repaired where it lies."

[gotcha.3441]
title = "Fixing the standby commit hang exposed six node sequencer test failures that the hang had masked, and the new activation test iterates a store its commitment store does not mount"
symptom = "22.39.40 attempt 1 at 2ebcae0995a4 built, repaired the standby commit release and bounded its test, and the full node and sequencer test run then showed: in node, TestActivationStopsTheBlockWhoseStateCommitmentStoreServesAPlanStoreAsPending panics at upgrades_activation_test.go line 653 because the pending store iterator asks for the xweb store that the test commitment store never mounted; in node/sequencer, TestAddStartFlagsRegistersSequencerFlags expects 14 registered flags and finds 19, the three TestConsensusSource tests (retries seal batch failure, decode failure keeps batch, tx zero batch) expect the error no block is open and get nil, TestCrashAfterReceiptReplaysIdenticalReceipt finds 13 receipts where 12 are replayed in both the sequential and the microbatch mode, and TestProofSequencerExecutorTransportRecovery refuses its own configuration at node_start_test.go line 87 because replication TLS certificate, key, roots and peer identity are now required, then dereferences a nil harness in cleanup at line 69. The six sequencer failures appear in no other recorded run because the hang stopped the package before them."
fix = "Decision 2800: the six sequencer failures become repair task 22.39.86 of the node runtime owner with the recorded list as baseline; 22.39.40 repairs its own activation test, narrows its sequencer gate to the standby commit test it repaired, and 22.39.86 runs the whole package after 22.39.40 lands."

[gotcha.3442]
title = "A repository-wide guard written inside a scoped page repair fails on the vendored trees and on pages another task owns"
symptom = "22.39.56 attempt 1 at 016a2f12a44b repaired its 13 pages and wrote a guard over every tracked Markdown page: 372 lines failed, 339 of them links from the vendored project documentation and the vendored project directory to the upstream repository of that project (provenance, not the product repository), 54 from spec records, 83 from the documentation site and 6 from the platform pages that 22.39.64 rewrites, and the clone check found the root README clone command at line 332 with no cd line after it. 22.39.57 attempt 1 at ecccd4a4c554 repaired its three pages and its placeholder guard found five markers: two in vendored library READMEs (programs/vendor and the upstream libsecp256k1 disclaimer the task itself keeps) and three TODO lines in the example and plugin READMEs of the vendored project directory."
fix = "A guard written inside a scoped repair asserts over the pages of the task and names the vendored trees and the upstream provenance links in an allowlist inside the test; the repository-wide form of the guard belongs to the sweep task that rewrites the rest (22.39.64 for links). The root README gains its cd line and joins the touches of 22.39.56."

[gotcha.3443]
title = "The conformance vector refresh was refused before verification by the gateway mirror compile failure that 22.31.620 repairs"
symptom = "22.31.622 attempt 1 at 812ee7db75e9 refreshed the committed receipt vector copy from its re-recorded source, updated the seven consumer tests and the copy check, and built the two interop crates with exit 0; the dependent-crate check then compiled the gateway test target that mirrors the ai-market module list and met the thirteen unresolved references of gotcha 3417 (the rooms and canary modules without their mirror lines), so the verification never ran. The task did not require 22.31.620 because it is not an agent daemon task, yet its dependent-crate check reaches the same target."
fix = "22.31.622 now requires 22.31.620; attempt 2 continues from the attempt-1 tree once the mirror repair is on main, and every task whose dependent-crate check reaches the gateway test target carries that requirement until 22.31.620 lands."

[gotcha.3444]
title = "The README programme-reference guard reached two pages the task did not own"
symptom = "22.39.38 attempt 1 at 5b1a56176a9c cleaned its seven pages and its guard over every README found two remaining task numbers: sdk/contrib/rosetta/node/README.md line 29 explains the withdrawn container entry points by a task number, and tools/launchpad/production/load/README.md line 124 names a task number in a command. Both pages are outside the touches, so the attempt stopped."
fix = "Both pages join the touches of 22.39.38 and the two lines are rewritten as plain statements (the load README keeps its other lines for 22.39.67)."

[gotcha.3445]
title = "The beta ledger check reads the public qualification ledger and finds it is not a well-formed document"
symptom = "22.39.54 attempt 1 at 799a0dafcb68 settled 18 of the 19 baseline failures of the tools/ci suite (112 tests and 277 subtests passed) and the last one, test_ledger_check_reads_layerx_merge_ledger, runs scripts/ci/beta-ledger-check.sh over spec/layerx-merge/qualification.kvx and reports 6448 violations: an unterminated double-quoted string at line 494, and section headers repeated when a later attempt of the same task appended the same finding id again (finding.11.15.1 at lines 41 and 3681, finding.16.21.1 at lines 49 and 3689, and so on through the file), each repeat counted once per key. The ledger is appended by every attempt that records a finding and nothing ever checked that it still parses."
fix = "Repair task 22.39.87 normalises the ledger (every header unique, every string terminated, every record kept) and adds a parse test under tests/ci; 22.39.54 deselects the one ledger test until the repair lands and records it (decision 2800); a repeated finding id gains the attempt ordinal in its header from now on (decision 2806)."

[gotcha.3446]
title = "The action pin task named a repository-wide change but owned three workflow files"
symptom = "22.39.51 attempt 1 at b70c71c3cbf2 wrote tests/ci/test_action_pins_consistent.py and moved the pins of its three workflow files; the first test then found actions/checkout at conflicting SHAs across 51 workflow files and the third test rejected the toolchain pins of explorer-build.yml lines 92 and 138 and hosted-developer.yml line 28, whose comment carries the toolchain tag stable rather than a release number. Both findings lie outside the three files the touches named, so the attempt stopped at verification exit 1 (1 passed, 2 failed)."
fix = "22.39.51 now touches the whole .github/workflows directory; attempt 2 unifies every action across every workflow file and the comment test accepts the toolchain tag form (stable, nightly or a 1.NN number) for the toolchain action (decision 2807)."

[gotcha.3447]
title = "The submission stack test fixture of the vendored tree reads a fixed interpreter path"
symptom = "22.37.4 attempt 1 at 3ff690464a5b added the install status method, the live collector and the component cases; the vitest install status test then failed after 36 seconds because the inherited component check in tests of the vendored tree (integration/submission_stack.py line 91) builds its executable digest from /usr/bin/python3, which the qualification environment does not have (the interpreter lives under a version manager), raising FileNotFoundError through the interrupted-install case module. Two repair cycles were spent on the same fault; the live provider run stayed UNRUN per decision 2700."
fix = "Attempt 2 resolves the executable from sys.executable in the submission stack module and keeps the two modules in the touches; a test executable is never a fixed absolute path (decision 2808)."

[gotcha.3448]
title = "A declared capability had no content-page enforcement row because the reference page is generated"
symptom = "22.39.30 attempt 3 at fe2b3029520b declared the four install-page labels in docs/platform/capabilities.kvx and passed its 13 tests; the site check then refused: capabilities declared but documented on no page: Scheduled beta resets. The only row naming that capability is docs/platform/content/reference/enforcement.md line 60, a page the build generates from the registry and therefore skips when it counts surfaced capabilities, and no hand-written page under docs/platform/content carries the row. The fault pre-exists on main since the capability landed with 22.36.2."
fix = "Attempt 4 adds the Scheduled beta resets row to the enforcement table of docs/platform/content/environments/emulator.md, a page already in the touches, so every declared capability has a hand-written row."

[gotcha.3449]
title = "The key material move needed the destination directories and four consumer tests outside its touches"
symptom = "22.39.68 attempt 1 at 5ba896bc2b9b wrote tests/ci/test_key_material_only_in_fixtures.py and the two manifest entries, then stopped: the eleven files move into tests/fixtures directories of the two crates and are read by hosted/internal/tests/repair_22_33_1452.rs and ramps/toolkit/tests/proof_ramp_layerx_config.rs, repair_22_33_1486.rs and support/repair_22_33_1490.rs, none of which the touches named. The agent also found seven more key-like files outside fixture directories (four under services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/src and three under services/platform/ramps/reference/src) that the repository-wide check will flag. No gate ran."
fix = "22.39.68 now touches both tests directories and the four consumer tests; the repository-wide test carries the seven remaining paths as a recorded baseline in tests/ci/data/key_material_baseline.txt until 22.39.93 moves them (decision 2800)."

[gotcha.3450]
title = "Documented shell commands drifted from the tree in five groups"
symptom = "A read-only pass over 615 tracked README and docs pages (3665 command lines) at c6a45ed6d0 found: the six translated README pages of the vendored project docs still list a source map and a documentation map from before the layout change (162 entries); fifteen runtime, verification and operations pages of the vendored project docs name the old layout, three pnpm lines call the platform script by a name the root manifest no longer has, and four script paths moved; wasm/contrib/devtools/README.md line 32 calls a retired Makefile and docs/platform/content/framework/next.md line 142 runs a dev script the sample package does not define; the explorer backend devcontainer README clones a repository name that no longer exists and the compose README changes into directories relative to its parent; no test checks fenced shell commands against the tree. Cargo package names, Go paths, pnpm filters, CLI flags, environment names and the public RPC hosts all resolved."
fix = "Tasks 22.39.88 to 22.39.91 repair the four groups with one test module each and 22.39.92 adds the repository-wide command guard (decision 2809)."

[gotcha.3451]
title = "The launchpad web type check needs the launchpad SDK packages built first"
symptom = "22.39.61 attempt 1 at 7fd627359bac renamed 78 asset paths (44 launchpad, 34 perps), consolidated the six duplicate pairs per app, the chart declaration and the copied stylesheets, and wrote the three tests; the build then ran tsc in apps/launchpad/web straight after the install and failed with TS2307 on every import of the two launchpad SDK packages, which the install links from sdk/launchpad/packages but whose type declarations exist only after their build (the form task 18.1508.2 already uses). The agent also found two byte-identical launcher tile images under apps/perps/public/windows, a directory of platform-prescribed names outside the touches."
fix = "The build command of 22.39.61 now installs at the launchpad root, builds the two SDK packages and then type-checks the web app; the duplicate test exempts the launcher tile directory."

[gotcha.3452]
