[gotcha.3474]
title = "A default-policy block test fails under the mock block validation tag"
symptom = "22.39.82 attempt 2 at ddb3191922ab (the evidence revision; the attempt text quotes another) split the mock tags into separate legs over consensus/types and strengthened the wiring tests, which pass with the build; go test -tags=mock_block_validation ./consensus/types/... fails in TestBlockValidateBasic (consensus/types/block_test.go) because the test asserts the default validation policy that the mock tag replaces, while consensus/types/consensus_policy_test.go already carries the constraint !mock_block_validation && !mock_chain_validation for the same reason; the chain validation leg and the registry tests were not reached."
fix = "The default-policy assertions move behind the same build constraint; block_test.go and the consensus/types directory join the touches."

[gotcha.3475]
title = "A native-mode case of the plugin router fails on a readiness receipt the control plane now emits"
symptom = "22.37.18 attempt 4 at e5ec1ae9d850 (the evidence revision; the attempt text quotes 8cf8dd718c4f) passed all 23 plugin tests, then the component case 4_2 of the source control cases failed on a deep-equal assertion of the native source actor: the actual readiness value carried a receipt object (kind WORKSPACE_READINESS, closure_state INCOMPLETE, authority_epoch, base_revision_id, closure_manifest_digest, installed_entry_digest, receipt_digest, schema_version 1, a scope with organisation, repository and security domain ids, scope_generation) that the expected value lacked; the attempt repaired the assertion in its final tree but both repair cycles were spent, so the final tree was never verified."
fix = "Attempt 5 verifies the final tree first (decision 2771); if the receipt assertion still fails the case follows the producer receipt (gotcha 3046)."

[gotcha.3476]
title = "The image compile-input task fails its dependents check on a stale gateway mirror of the ai-market modules"
symptom = "22.39.107 attempt 1 at 5302b6de0464 (base deb2deb978c0) changed the layerx image ignore file, the Dockerfile and the settlement include and wrote the three image-input tests; the build passed, then the dependents check compiling 41 crates exited 101 in the hosted gateway test that mirrors the ai-market program modules through path attributes: unresolved imports crate::canary and crate::rooms, because the base predates bace946642 (22.31.620, 14:56Z), which added the two modules to that mirror; the verification was never reached."
fix = "Attempt 2 relaunches on current main with the attempt-1 tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3477]
title = "The platform site guard flags three hand-written pages outside the touches of the task that adds it"
symptom = "22.39.31 attempt 1 at 8f3bcecaca85 replaced LayerX Network on the nine listed pages and added test_platform_hand_written_pages_do_not_name_layerx_network, which walks every hand-written page; the guard failed naming docs/platform/content/concepts/enforcement.md, guide/reference-applications.md and quickstart/rust.md (line 3 of each), pages the task text did not list, and the site check was not reached."
fix = "Decision 2823: the three pages join the touches and get the same replacement; the guard keeps its tree-wide scope."

[gotcha.3478]
title = "The whole agent daemon library suite fails 24 tests under a by-path include task that only needed four modules of it"
symptom = "22.31.542 attempt 2 at 43cb551943d4 (base f90a43293b4a) removed the by-path includes from five integration tests, exposed test_support through lib.rs, built and passed all 16 dependent checks; the verification runs the whole layerx-agentd library suite and failed 24 of 333 tests, none in the modules the task changed: four approval tests whose hold_records are not empty, seven human_runtime tests (four retained settlement cases failing with Preparation then PoisonError, native_policy_usage_refuses_a_page_without_a_proof, policy_usage_sums_only_proven_receipts_in_the_window with ItemUnproven), the evm program submission test with Submit(Sequencer(Malformed)), program_views_decode_one_program_and_one_account_and_refuse_changed_settlement with SourceSnapshot, two TLS identity tests refusing because the boundary binary was not built (decision 2325), and nine store fixture cases (store root is not a canonical owned private directory, store root already has a writer, root left behind) that 22.31.555 owns (gotcha 3169)."
fix = "Decision 2824: the task-level library run narrows to the four modules the task changed and its build adds the boundary binary; repair task 22.39.122 owns the thirteen unowned failures and runs the whole suite after 22.31.555."

[gotcha.3479]
title = "The CLI wallet test asserts a finality-trust refusal that a zero-timeout wait no longer reaches"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 1 at 8aaa799401bd refreshed the embedded OpenRPC document and the two node URLs, built, and passed all 24 library tests and 79 of 80 binary tests; wallet::tests::policy_scope_and_sdk_wait_fail_closed (tools/platform/cli/src/wallet.rs line 2122) expects RpcError::MissingFinalityTrust from wait_for with Commitment::Finalised and a zero timeout, while the SDK producer (services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/src/rpc_verification.rs wait_for_authority) returns RpcError::Pending for every commitment before any network read when the timeout is zero."
fix = "Attempt 2 brings the consumer test to the producer contract (gotcha 3046): the Finalised zero-timeout call is asserted as Pending with the same activity id and the policy refusals stay."

[gotcha.3480]
title = "The perps type check fails on the agent SDK browser entry because the linked SDK is never built"
symptom = "22.39.61 attempt 4 at 4b2b61b87edf (base ee355f88697c, after the lockfile repair of 22.39.105 landed) kept the asset changes, built and passed all seven asset tests and the frozen install of apps/perps; pnpm exec tsc then failed in sdk/wallet/src/receipt.ts line 3 with TS2307 Cannot find module @sidiora/layerx-sdk/browser and four implicit-any errors that follow from it: apps/perps links the wallet SDK, which links services/agent/sdk/typescript, whose package exports point at dist/src/browser.js, an output of its tsc build that nothing in the verification produced; the wallet test workflow runs npm ci --workspaces=false and npm run build --workspaces=false in that directory before any dependent install."
fix = "Decision 2825: the verification builds the agent SDK first, as the wallet test workflow does; the asset tree of attempt 4 stands."

[gotcha.3481]
title = "The install status test is refused at the claim because the explicit grant tuple of the fixture omits the packet component"
symptom = "22.37.4 attempt 3 at 3c30292c67f3 (base ee355f88697c) applied the declaration repair of gotcha 3470 and built green; the first verification failed at the start of the retained install fixture because the source service lacked its object-store and budget settings, and the repair supplied them in the SDK status fixture; the second verification failed in test/install-status.test.ts line 188 when the status process it spawns (fixtures/install/sdk_status.py) drove the interrupted-install case to its claim and the signed service refused hierarchy.packet.create with AUTH_SCOPE_DENIED Operation outside granted run/action: sdk_status.py narrows every fixture credential to the actions of an explicit component tuple (14.1, 3.1, 5.1 to 5.4, 15.2, the two install delivery components, 12.4, 12.4-executor, 10.3, 1.1, 8.3, 16.1, 16.2) and that tuple omits component 3.2, whose hierarchy.packet.create the claim path of cases/tasks/5_1.py calls with the manager key before any install action; the identity component compares the action against allowed_actions and refuses."
fix = "Decision 2827: the explicit grant tuple adds component 3.2 and any other component whose action the claim path calls; attempt 4 reruns both gates on the final tree, live qualification stays UNRUN under decision 2700."

[gotcha.3482]
title = "The wallet drift task fails on fourteen tests in files it does not touch"
symptom = "22.39.43 attempt 2 at 732101e6cd82 (base ee355f88697c) passed the scope test and 644 wallet tests; 16 tests in 14 files fail and only one file (lib/portfolio-api/repair-22-31-235.test.ts, two lifecycle tests meeting Portfolio API error 400) is inside the eleven files the task touches; the other fourteen failures sit in untouched files: wallet/signer.test.ts, wallet/session.test.ts and wallet/repair-22-31-248.test.ts expect transaction objects without the chainId 125 the signer now emits; server/push-ownership.test.ts answers 500 for a wallet-signed subscription (endpoint is invalid) and server/repair-22-31-246.test.ts and server/repair-22-33-168.test.ts fail on the same push store; platform/storage/storage-forensics.test.ts finds direct browser storage access in lib/swap/storage.ts; account/HistoryView.test.tsx expects the explorer status 404 text; account/repair-22-33-161.test.ts expects numeric height decoding and the hosted origin refusal text; proof_wallet_app.test.ts and repair-22-33-152.test.ts compute a different hosted intent plan digest after the producer store reopens (account/test/hostedIntentRecording.ts line 120); the wallet-test public check runs the whole apps/wallet suite."
fix = "Decisions 2800 and 2824: 22.39.43 continues with its verification narrowed to its eleven files and repairs the two portfolio lifecycle tests; the fourteen other failures belong to the new repair task 22.39.123, which runs the whole apps/wallet suite."

[gotcha.3483]
title = "Wiring the whole interop workspace into the public check exposes 145 failing tests across twelve members"
symptom = "22.39.74 attempt 1 at dd1e10e4b474 (base f90a43293b4a) added the workspace tests job, the recipe and three wiring tests that pass; the first verification stopped in the recipe parser on two identical INTEROP_MANIFEST assignments (repaired by removing the duplicate declarations beside the recipes); the second ran make interop-test with --no-fail-fast and Cargo reported 52 failed targets and 145 failed tests across 12 of the 15 members while 350 tests in the failing targets passed: layerx-bridge-relayer 8 targets (37 equality assertions in loops, Configuration multiple paxeer endpoints require explicit independent backend identities in paxeer_rpc, operator_config and operator_cosign_contract, a real EVM host exit in repair_22_31_160, an unclassified shared receipt case in sequencer_receipt), layerx-x402 7 (UnsupportedOffer and PaymentIdentityMissing), layerx-ucp 4, x-websearch 7, layerx-gas-station 6 (journal version and empty journal assertions, an index out of bounds in station), layerx-interop-service 5 (activity_time_window_refused in the settlement fixture and a poisoned lock), layerx-interop-gateway lib (ledger producer and gateway consumer exit 1), layerx-migrate 2 (a genuine protected fixture required), layerx-committed-proof 4, layerx-portable 5, layerx-mirror 2 and layerx-fiat 1; none is in a file the task touches, and the interop-x402 check only ever ran the x402 transport job so none of these ran publicly before."
fix = "Decision 2826: attempt 2 records the 145 tests in tests/ci/data/interop_test_baseline.json with their retiring tasks 22.39.124 to 22.39.127 and runs the workspace through a runner that skips exactly those names; the four repair tasks remove their entries as they bring each member to green."

[gotcha.3484]
title = "The native send purpose test asks the attestor for a wallet identity the fixture never holds"
symptom = "22.39.8 attempt 6 at 30ec04278493 (base 7358f14a6aff) built the native library and both Rust binaries, serialized the runtime clock observations behind the quorum transport (the first verification lost two native requests to clock regression refusals and global timeouts) and brought TestNativeCustodyRealProfiles to a pass; TestNativeSendPurposeRealProfiles still fails: producer and consumer agree on LayerX/native/send-purpose/v2, the Rust consumer generates the ed25519 primary through /v1/keys/generate on all five nodes, then its public_wallet_identity call (evm operation 6) posts /v1/keys/public-wallet and every node answers 404 key_not_found; the Go handler in public_identity.go resolves the held primary, then lists the store for a secp256k1 record whose identity owner is the same owner and refuses with key_not_found (owner has no held wallet identity) when none exists; the send fixture in native_purpose_test.go approves and generates only the ed25519 primary, while e2e_test.go holds a secp256k1 key in each node store and approves it in the inventory for the owner before any wallet lookup."
fix = "The Go send fixture holds a secp256k1 wallet identity for the test owner in each node store with its inventory entry before launching the Rust consumer, as the end-to-end test does; the Rust consumer and the handler are unchanged."

[gotcha.3485]
title = "One CLI credential test bypasses the named skip guard and panics where dbus-daemon is absent"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 2 at 2366732b3535 (base af7d8469e2d7) applied the ruling of gotcha 3479 (the wallet test asserts Pending with the same activity id, the read policy refusals stay) and the rpc tests, the CLI library suite and the wallet binary tests passed (24, 80, 8 and 20); make platform-test-tooling then failed in the credential integration target: the same-alias profiles test at line 261 of tests/credential.rs (the one that preserves the OS-held credential across a failed publication) constructs the credential environment directly and the helper panics at tests/common/credential_environment.rs line 82 (dbus-daemon must be installed for real credential tests) in an environment without dbus-daemon, while the other credential tests call the credential_environment guard that prints skipped: dbus-daemon is not installed unless LAYERX_CLI_TESTS_REQUIRE_DBUS is set, and the platform check installs dbus and gnome-keyring before the tooling tests; no repair cycle was used."
fix = "Decision 2821: the test enters through the same guard as its siblings so it skips by name where the daemon is absent and runs where the public check installs it; the attempt-2 tree stands."

[gotcha.3486]
title = "The narrowed agent daemon gate names the committed documents consumer target without its producer"
symptom = "22.31.542 attempt 3 at 9e1018dc32ac (base af7d8469e2d7) built with the boundary binary, passed the dependent checks and the 29 library tests of the four modules named by the gotcha 3478 ruling; the verification then stopped at the first integration target, repair_22_31_535, whose consumer test reads the committed authority corpus that the producer test of services/platform/hosted/authority (repair_22_31_535_producers_emit_committed_documents) writes, and the gate command set by decision 2824 named the consumer target without that producer step, so the corpus was missing (decision 2325: producer-input tests are qualified by their producers) and the five integration targets of the task were never reached; no repair cycle was used."
fix = "Decision 2828: the gate runs the hosted authority producer target before the agent daemon integration targets; attempt 4 reruns on the unchanged tree."

[gotcha.3487]
title = "The subject identity label task refreshed the platform lockfile its record never listed"
symptom = "22.31.549 attempt 2 at ba94e7d6bd05 built and verified with exit 0 (the authority emits the committed verification label for subject identity and context, the daemon requires it) and the collector held the result because services/platform/Cargo.lock changed outside the touches and planned_paths: the task edits services/platform/hosted/authority/Cargo.toml, a manifest the platform workspace resolves by path, and decision 2259 requires the lockfile refresh in the same change, yet the task record lists only the three crate directories as planned paths, so a correct refresh reads as an out-of-scope change."
fix = "Decision 2829: the record lists services/platform/Cargo.lock among its planned paths and the held result is published as it stands; no rerun."

[gotcha.3488]
title = "The committed receipt vector refresh met a facilitator test red since the audit repair"
symptom = "22.31.622 attempt 2 at 6943962d5cb6 refreshed the conformance copy, passed both copy checks and the four committed-proof targets, then facilitator_reports_committed_only_with_a_proof of layerx-x402 panicked with settlement evidence does not match in its no-proof iteration: the test sets the evidence rung to Committed before the loop and expects a receipted response without a proof, while Seller::settled since f2d44220a6 (the 22.30.111 audit repair) refuses committed-rung evidence that carries no proof. The same test fails in the 22.39.74 attempt-1 run, so it is red on main independent of the recording and is already assigned to 22.39.127 (the x402 baseline retirement)."
fix = "Decision 2830: the task gate skips exactly that test name and 22.39.127 receives the fixture repair; the attempt-2 tree stands."

[gotcha.3489]
title = "The plugin router scheduler cases cannot reach the routing module through a manager decision"
symptom = "22.37.29 attempt 1 at 85ff403ccf24: the five server cases pass and the ten scheduler cases of the routing module test (pause and cap controls, cancelled job, HTTP 429 backoff, membership claims, cap reservations, availability, single retry, backoff ceiling, interrupted ledgers, preparation cleanup) still fail with zero jobs: the routing module starts in manager mode unless its planning option is legacy-nonadaptive or native, writes WAITING_FOR_MANAGER to the planning record of the shared store and returns before scheduling, while manager.ts forwards every manager decision to the external authority client and nothing in the plugin feeds a decision back into the routing module. The do item asked the cases to drive the manager decision path, which does not exist in process."
fix = "Decision 2831: the scheduler cases set the legacy planning option explicitly; the default-mode case added by the attempt covers the manager default."

[gotcha.3490]
title = "The CLI bootstrap test reads the install document at its pre-consolidation path"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 3 at 39533d5aec16: the three RPC tests, the wallet test and the eight credential tests pass (the same-alias test now returns through the guard), then make platform-test-tooling fails in bootstrap::clean_bootstrap of tools/platform/cli/tests/emulator.rs because published_bootstrap_sequence joins ../../../services/platform/docs/content/install.md, a path removed when 0295d41349 folded the platform documentation into docs/platform; tools/platform/cli/tests/clean-bootstrap.sh line 56 already reads docs/platform/content/install.md, which carries the one bootstrap marker. The attempt recorded the file as out of scope although touches names the directory tools/platform/cli that contains it."
fix = "Decision 2832: a directory in touches covers every file beneath it; attempt 4 corrects the path in emulator.rs."

[gotcha.3491]
title = "The wallet proxy refuses the chain identity the portfolio client sends on every read"
symptom = "22.39.43 attempt 3 at 5e1842ada7db: eighty wallet tests pass and the two lifecycle tests of lib/portfolio-api/repair-22-31-235.test.ts fail with Portfolio API error 400: portfolio-api/client.ts (bc1c4f4e78, audit record 22.30.114) routes every GET through walletReadUrl, which appends chain_id, and checks the x-wallet-chain-id acknowledgment with assertWalletReadResponse, while forwardPortfolio in app/api/wallet/[...path]/route.ts (64bdee97c4, audit record 22.30.118) admits only the address and limit query keys and answers QUERY_INVALID for chain_id, and copies no acknowledgment header. Two audit repairs of the same day left the producer and its consumer disagreeing; the task touches named only test files, so the attempt could not fix the proxy."
fix = "Decision 2833: the proxy admits and validates chain_id and acknowledges the served chain; the task touches gain the route and the read-contract module."

[gotcha.3492]
title = "The visitor asset weight test treats two empty vendored chart style files as budget offenders"
symptom = "22.39.70 attempt 1 at 1cedcb49d76f: the eight assets shrank by 93 percent at their display sizes and the route catalogue check passes, but test_public_assets_under_weight_cap in tests/ci/test_web_asset_weight.py requires 0 < size <= budget and lists apps/launchpad/web/public/charting_library/bundles/3060.fbb750fd312778403036.css and its rtl twin (0 bytes, emitted empty by the vendored chart bundle and tracked that way on main) as offenders; two repair cycles went to source-mapping fixes and left the condition."
fix = "Attempt 2 asserts the cap only (size <= budget); an empty vendored style is not weight."

[gotcha.3493]
title = "The schema coverage test counts a retired schema operation among the generated ones"
symptom = "22.31.542 attempt 4 at fdbd181e8ff0: build exit 0, verification exit 101; the hosted authority target, the agent library filters and four of the five integration targets pass; the schema coverage test of rpc_surface_major_two fails with faucet.claim present only on the schema side (53 generated operations against 54 schema sections). The test body is identical on main; the section carries disposition retired since 5b4f53b03f and the routing module refuses the wire name, which retired_faucet_claim_wire_name_is_refused already asserts."
fix = "The coverage test takes the sections whose disposition is retired out of the compared set (or asserts generated plus retired equals schema) and asserts each retired name is refused; no production change (decision 2762, gotcha 3046)."

[gotcha.3494]
title = "The budget verifier decodes the native carrier bytes as a typed transaction and refuses every retained native settlement"
symptom = "9.98.4 attempt 11 at 9194e2966f44: build exit 0, verification exit 101; eight retained settlement tests pass and four panic with retained settlement: Preparation; refused at None. The approval carrier of the native program path keeps the wire envelope canonical bytes that prepare::restore_canonical reproduces; validate_retained_preparation in budget/native_binding.rs (landed with 22.31.217 at 75df69e084) decodes the same bytes with the EIP-1559 decoder, maps the failure to NativeBindingError::Preparation, and validate_prepared of program_sources.rs refuses the settlement before any budget source is read."
fix = "Decision 2834 and task 22.39.128: the budget verifier binds the typed call through the retained signing preparation of the same preparation and never decodes the envelope bytes as a transaction; 9.98.4 requalifies after 22.39.128 lands."

[gotcha.3495]
title = "The interrupted-install case is refused on the provider pools action although its component holds the grant"
symptom = "22.37.4 attempt 4 at 6db52be61634: two repair cycles; the install status test of the client SDK fails because the interrupted-install case module is refused with AUTH_SCOPE_DENIED on provider.pools.configure for component 8.2 under the provisioner key, after the fixture restarted with the provisioner role. The grant tuple of sdk_status.py lists 8.2 and the component record lists the action; the refusal text names neither the principal row nor the run identity it compared."
fix = "The next attempt makes the refusal diagnosable from the case module (the principal row of the provisioner and the action and run identity of the invocation) and repairs the fixture side within touches; the live provider run stays UNRUN (decision 2700)."

[gotcha.3496]
title = "The ai-market suite carries thirty-four failures after the codec merge and the fuel budget test needs the Go producer"
symptom = "22.99.77 attempt 23 at 9ba14541e3d9: two repair cycles, guest 497897 bytes under the 524184 bound; twelve targets and thirty-four tests fail: the selector freeze test expects 55 operations while the crate exposes 72, eleven availability entries return NotEnabled, four application error codes differ from the expected ones, the f03 to f07 cases and the reputation public key case fail, and fuel_budget cannot find programs/target/repair-478 because the Go gate of 22.31.478 that writes it did not run. The attempt resolved six conflict files between the landed 22.31.615 codec and its own section reuse."
fix = "Decision 2828: the build command of the task runs the Go producer gate first; the attempt records the baseline of the unchanged merged main tree, repairs the failures the sweep owns and re-resolves the attempt-only ones with the landed producer shape winning; the freeze test asserts the live operation count."

[gotcha.3497]
title = "The qualification record names producers outside the touches of the record task"
symptom = "22.31.623 attempt 2 at 2dea78a64748: two repair cycles; 22 failed and 4408 passed. Eighteen cases are recorded blocked-scope and five recorded-unrelated because the producer the record names lies outside touches: the release identity reader indexes a field 22.31.587 removed from the version file (ten cases of 22.33.806), the agent guidance file and the ignore file of the vendored project directory under tools/ (three cases of 22.36.1), the receipt refusal fixture drift of 22.33.849, the native binding fixture of 22.33.865, the Android receipt gate states of 22.31.418, the sig-provider precompile inventory of 22.33.312, the kernel launcher of 22.33.769, the human step-up golden of the beta driver, and the Node version, OpenAPI header and swagger header cases."
fix = "Decision 2836: the producer modules the record names enter the touches of the record task; the next attempt repairs each named producer where it violates a live rule and rewrites the pin from the live producer where the pin is stale."

[gotcha.3498]
title = "Eighteen canonical repository links sit in files the link task does not touch"
symptom = "22.39.64 attempt 1 at 4048a95975b9: the canonical link test finds eighteen noncanonical links in eleven files under docs/site/docs, docs/platform/content and consensus/spec/README.md, outside the nine package manifests, three pom files, the citation file and the version file the task touches."
fix = "The three paths join touches; links pinned to old blob paths point at the current page of the canonical repository or the sentence is rewritten."

[gotcha.3499]
title = "The qualification host target fails while the qualification suite itself is red"
symptom = "22.39.26 attempt 2 at a5906618a6b0: two repair cycles; make test-qualification-python runs the whole tools/qualification tree and reports 324 failures and one error (jsonschema absent in the first run), the same tree 22.31.623 is bringing to green."
fix = "22.39.26 requires 22.31.623 and requalifies after it lands; the host target is not repaired twice."

[gotcha.3500]
title = "An attempt withheld the include edit its continuation note directed because the file was outside touches"
symptom = "22.38.4 attempt 2 at c1f66a1b05b2: the native build passes at 495478 bytes, the module mirror check fails because the hosted gateway test include file lacks the laps module, and the attempt stopped for a scope clarification although do_5 named services/platform/hosted/gateway/tests/repair_22_33_1439.rs as the file to edit."
fix = "Decision 2835: a file a continuation note directs an attempt to edit is listed in touches by the same batch; the file joins the touches of 22.38.4 and attempt 3 applies the include line."

[gotcha.3501]
title = "The faucet route tests invoke the faucet command without the service endpoint the command now requires"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 4 at b9073eb05083: build exit 0, verification exit 2; the rpc tests, the wallet test, the credential tests and the bootstrap test pass; both tests of tools/platform/cli/tests/faucet_route.rs fail: the identity test receives invalid_arguments instead of identity_session_required and the route test sees the command exit before sending. 7884cd3f83 (22.33.1492) made --service-endpoint a required argument of the faucet command and the tests still pass only --key."
fix = "The tests pass --service-endpoint with the listener address in both cases and keep their assertions; the file is inside the touched directory (gotcha 3046)."

[gotcha.3502]
title = "The x402 sequenced settlement document carries the transaction hash of the recording before the refresh"
symptom = "22.31.622 attempt 3 at 61134f40bb83: build exit 0, verification exit 1; the copy checks, the committed-proof targets and the three enabled facilitator tests pass; two sequenced_vectors tests fail at line 557 because services/interop/specs/conformance/x402/sequenced-settlement.json still names the earlier transaction hash while the committed recording the copy test follows names the current one; the document is outside touches."
fix = "The document joins the touches of 22.31.622; the next attempt refreshes its committed case from the same recording and keeps the assertion."

[gotcha.3503]
title = "The reverted swap test runs the in-process EVM without a time bound"
symptom = "22.39.43 attempt 4 at fadf6bebf6d1: two repair cycles; the inventory check and 89 wallet tests pass; execute_swap_refuses_a_reverted_swap times out at the default 5000 ms after the executor test moved from a spawned node to an in-process EVM compiled with solc at suite start (84 s for the four tests), while the two confirmed-quote tests of the same file carry a 15000 ms bound."
fix = "The reverted swap test carries the same bound as its siblings; the attempt-4 tree stands."

[gotcha.3504]
title = "A deselect list the continuation note directed was outside the planned paths"
symptom = "22.39.54 attempt 2 at f188e5ea648f: the attempt moved seven script jobs of the continuous integration workflow to the routing expression and kept the eighteen settlements, then stopped before any gate because do_7 directed it to create tests/ci/data/tools_ci_deselect.txt and neither touches nor planned_paths listed the file."
fix = "Decision 2835: the file joins planned_paths; attempt 3 creates it with the one ledger entry and runs the gates."

[gotcha.3505]
title = "The licence task was directed to set five authors in manifests outside its touches"
symptom = "22.39.63 attempt 2 at 7e9bfc50b82d: build exit 0, verification exit 1; the two licence tests pass and test_first_party_authors_are_organisation fails on contracts/package.json, the three chainflow SDK manifests and tests/integration/dapp_tests/package.json, the five files do_4 named for the author change while touches listed none of them."
fix = "Decision 2835: the three paths join touches (the chainflow directory covers its three manifests); attempt 3 sets the author and keeps the test."

[gotcha.3506]
title = "Eight regression suites folded into one test binary fail on shared state and a missing executable"
symptom = "22.31.613 attempt 1 at 50812234f9c1: build exit 0, verification exit 1; the three new cases and the 22.31.219 target pass; tests/repair_22_31_613.rs includes eight landed regression files as path modules, so 41 tests run in one process: three preview cases fail because the anvil executable the preview test spawns is absent, two cases fail on poisoned locks left by those panics, and three assertions differ (a rung count of 6 against 2 in the 22.31.562 suite, an export count of 0 against 1 in the projection suite, and a PREPARE answer whose refusal byte is 1 against 0 in the 22.31.571 suite) that cannot be attributed while the suites share a process."
fix = "Decision 2837: the regression suites run as their own targets; the next attempt removes the includes, runs each target alone and repairs any assertion that persists, since a typed refusal changes only the reason string and never the acceptance of a path."

[gotcha.3507]
title = "The budget verifier task could not reach the signing preparation from its three scoped files"
symptom = "22.39.128 attempt 1 at base e4c5b9476591: no change inside scope and no gate ran; the attempt found that the settlement path of human_runtime.rs calls read_program_budget_sources with a wire carrier at line 5840 and that the retained settlement fixture of the same file calls it at line 24015 and validates the sources before it creates the preparation, so passing the retained signing preparation to the verifier needs edits in a file the touches did not list."
fix = "Decision 2838: human_runtime.rs joins touches; attempt 2 passes the retained preparation from both callers and makes the fixture create it first."

[gotcha.3508]
title = "The node package behind the three-name skip failed sixteen tests and the time limit that the unskipped run had passed"
symptom = "22.39.40 attempt 3 at 9f57ad7d6553: build exit 0, verification exit 1; the whole node package with the three-name skip failed TestSidioraFeeTokenUpgradeServesThePrecompileOnlyAfterIt, the five TestV6120 cases, TestAnteChainRunsRevocationDecoratorAfterAuthzNested, TestFeeTokenGigaBlockRefusesUnusableRate, TestDecodeFailureTxReportsZeroGas, TestEvmEventsForCw1155, TestProofNodeGoApi, TestRepair_102_SchedulerFailureAtomic and four TestApp cases, then hit the fifteen-minute limit in TestFinalizeAdoptedSealedBlockMatchesReexecution after six minutes; attempt 2 ran the same node Go sources without the skip in 177 seconds with only the three recorded failures, and no Go source changed on main between the two bases."
fix = "The sixteen are not failures of the task sources; the next attempt runs the verification at the final tree first, runs a repeated failure alone, and traces a case that passes alone to the test whose state it needs."

[gotcha.3509]
title = "The keep-marker task was directed to delete sixteen launchpad markers outside its touches and its bundle test matched an export fixture"
symptom = "22.39.60 attempt 1 at ac30b2418bbc: build exit 0, verification exit 1; the strays, the re-saved script, five markers and four tests landed, test_no_gitkeep_beside_content fails on the sixteen launchpad meta-ag markers do_2 named and on services/platform/middleware/.gitkeep because touches listed none of those directories, and test_no_tracked_git_bundles_or_patch_dirs fails on services/human/schema/human-api/golden/current/activity.evidence.bundle, an LXHEXPV3 export fixture the human service reads, matched by its suffix alone."
fix = "Decision 2839: the five directories join touches; the test recognises a Git bundle by its signature line, and the export fixture stays."

[gotcha.3510]
title = "The vendored checksum guard found three unrecorded wasmi changes outside touches and flagged every crate whose manifest cargo normalised"
symptom = "22.39.121 attempt 1 at efca69139cec: build exit 0, verification exit 1 twice; the attempt reconciled the wasm-instrument manifest, wrote its PATCHES.md and the two tests, and after the second gate also refreshed the digests of src/gas_metering/mod.rs and src/gas_metering/validation.rs, which match at the final tree. test_every_vendored_crate_matches_its_manifest also fails on programs/vendor/wasmi-0.31.2, where src/engine/mod.rs, src/execution_trace.rs and src/store.rs were changed by daf26db476, bb8ccc51d6 and 41f31ec2fc without a manifest refresh, a crate outside touches that the registry image context check of build-env.sh line 37 refuses in the same way; and test_patched_vendored_crates_record_reasons as do_2 specified fails on 221 crates, because cargo vendor normalises every published Cargo.toml so it always differs from Cargo.toml.orig."
fix = "Decision 2812 puts wasmi in scope and decision 2840 defines a patched crate by a registered list; attempt 2 refreshes the three wasmi digests, records the crate, and rewrites the second test against the list."

[gotcha.3511]
title = "The agent daemon library suite kept six failures that belong to the budget verifier repair and to a session control fixture landed after the attempt base"
symptom = "22.39.122 attempt 1 at a6a4e6f9ff57 (base e4c5b9476591): build exit 0, verification exit 1 twice; 326 passed and six failed: four retained_settlement_tests cases (the first panics on a retained preparation at human_runtime.rs line 24174, the other three poison on the same lock), the budget verifier defect of 22.39.128 and decision 2834; and two session_control durable-write cases asserting a removed root at lines 3537 and 3637, whose control() fixture 22.31.555 rewrote in 2d40d3e17c after the attempt base; the attempt did not change session_control.rs."
fix = "The task now requires 22.39.128 as well as 22.31.555 and carries session_control.rs in touches; the relaunch rebases onto main and verifies the final tree first (decision 2771) before any repair."

[gotcha.3512]
title = "The vendored tree lockfile is behind the plugin router manifest on main, and the install-status case never reaches the dependency stage"
symptom = "22.37.4 attempt 5 at d997a969d711 (base 06535ba6d2): the first build failed with an outdated frozen lockfile because commit aeaf7a2fd0 (22.37.18) added a workspace dependency to the plugin router manifest without refreshing the lockfile, whose zod specifier also differs from the manifest; the repair cycle spent on it left one; verification exit 1: the install-status vitest case failed because the interrupted-install case module exited 1 with the dependency stage not reached, the job in state UNKNOWN and last_error RUNNER_EXECUTION_PROVIDER:REMOTE_OUTPUT_INCOMPLETE after the archive request of the fixture provider; the retained subreaper repair stays unverified."
fix = "Task 22.39.129 refreshes the lockfile (decision 2841); 22.37.4 requires it and attempt 6 makes the fixture provider serve the complete process output archive so the job leaves UNKNOWN; live provider qualification stays UNRUN (decision 2700)."

[gotcha.3513]
title = "The platform CLI RPC repair passed its own tests and failed two daemon-bound MCP binding tests under the tooling target"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 5 at f6555c81fb83 (base 5270ffe0c8): build exit 0, verification exit 1: the three rpc tests and the faucet route tests passed; make platform-test-tooling failed cli/tests/mcp_daemon_bound.rs twice: a_retired_core_sequence_binding_is_refused_before_installation_or_serving expects the code mcp.binding_retired_key for a binding document carrying the retired core_sequence field, but the loader refuses it first as an invalid enrolment shape (unknown field); an_explicit_binding_path_narrows_the_installed_surface_to_read_only is refused because the binding document at the explicit path is not owner-only."
fix = "Repair task 22.39.130 brings the binding loader and publisher to the contract the tests assert (decision 2800); 22.39.118 requires it and relaunches without touching the binding tests."

[gotcha.3514]
title = "The new Python suite target exposed eighty-eight failures in fourteen modules owned by done tasks, with no baseline mechanism"
symptom = "22.39.83 attempt 1 at 284c0a10932c (base e1c47b9ff1): build exit 0, verification exit 2: 366 passed, 88 failed in 958 seconds: tests/conformance/test_repair_22_33_886.py 31 (committed copy drift, explorer fixture path pattern, invalid-transaction-receipt, invalid_transaction), services/platform/tests/test_ramp_dependencies.py 17 (ramp crates depend on layerx-intents, paxeer-client and rusqlite, which the policy bans), tests/qualification/test_mcp_binding_receipt_keys.py 16 (mcp_binding_listener has no web_receipt_public_key), services/platform/hosted/node/tests/test_repair_22_33_1456.py 10, test_repair_22_31_355.py 4 and test_node_without_guarantor.py 1 (StopIteration and missing shareProcessNamespace and exec keys on the deployment manifests), the ramp journey test module of services/platform/tests 2 (help text and transaction-hash verification), tests/daemon/test_repair_22_33_1076.py 1 (invalid_transaction), services/platform/hosted/tests/test_workspace_manifest.py, test_sequencer_pins.py, test_retired_gateway_lifecycle.py and test_retired_gateway_helpers.py 1 each (verifier package retained, missing developer manifest, missing hosted-gateway local harness), services/platform/hosted/testnet/tests/test_repair_22_33_1447.py 1 (router path check against the kernel backend source) and cmd/layerx-module-registry/test_registry.py 1 (schema document differs); the owning tasks 22.33.886, 8.31.2, 18.1498.1, 22.33.1456, 22.31.355, 8.18.1, 22.33.1076, 8.9.1, 8.19.5, 8.19.11, 22.33.1447 and 22.1.9 are done."
fix = "Decision 2842: a baseline file under tests/ci/data names a retiring task per module, the runner ignores exactly those files, the runner test proves every entry, and tasks 22.39.131 to 22.39.134 repair the suites and delete their entries; a skip is never a pass (decision 2821)."

[gotcha.3515]
title = "The wallet repair left two failures and one suite-load error in producers outside touches, including a root marker the repository no longer holds"
symptom = "22.39.123 attempt 1 at 38aa1e8e41b6 (base 5270ffe0c8): build exit 0, verification exit 1 twice; 656 passed, two failed, one suite failed to load: the storage forensics test lists src/widgets/swap/useSwapExecution.ts as direct browser storage access outside the registered boundaries; the token detail precision test of record 22.33.140 receives Unknown where a null precision must render 0; src/surfaces/repair-22-31-250.test.ts locates the repository root by pnpm-workspace.yaml, which the repository root no longer holds, so the suite throws before collection."
fix = "The three producers enter touches (decision 2838); the relaunch routes the swap execution storage through the registered swap records module, brings the token detail precision to the recorded contract and locates the root by the tracked fixture the test reads (decision 2843)."

[gotcha.3516]
title = "The tools/ci suite failed on three Go workflow jobs landed with a fixed runner after the attempt base"
symptom = "22.39.54 attempt 3 at c45e603564a2 (base 9f1b304225): build exit 0, verification exit 1: the loadtest job test and the replay-golden test both run scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh, which reports the jobs tagged-tests, autobahn-integration and hpx-registry of .github/workflows/paxeer-go-test.yml, landed by 22.39.82 in 2fe29c1246, with the fixed runner ubuntu-latest; the deselection file tests/ci/data/tools_ci_deselect.txt and the runner test reading it are in place and the file was outside touches."
fix = "The workflow file enters touches (decision 2845); attempt 4 gives the three jobs the routing expression of the routed jobs of agent.yml and changes nothing else."

[gotcha.3517]
title = "The committed budget proof test replays a vector that lacks the owner account derivation the verifier now re-executes"
symptom = "22.31.540 attempt 3 at 9814e658da2c (base 06535ba6d2): build exit 0, verification exit 1 twice: three of the four regression tests passed; committed_budget_proof_is_accepted_and_state_proven_proof_is_refused_at_ingress panicked in the replay support on an unrecorded eth_call to the addr precompile 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001004 with selector c413bad3 and the owner key at height 0x8, so the real committed proof verifier refused; tests/vectors/budget-proof-v2/node-answers.json records px_getAccount for the owner but no derivation call, and the vector was outside touches."
fix = "The vector enters touches (decision 2844); attempt 4 records the derivation answer consistent with the evm_address of the px_getAccount answer, in the layout of the account-derivation conformance fixture, derived through the client decoder."

[gotcha.3518]
title = "The budget source readers gained a signing preparation parameter and a test outside touches still calls them with the old arity"
symptom = "22.39.128 attempt 2 at 29b48212d94c (base 9f1b304225): the build failed with exit 101: tests/repair_22_33_1520.rs lines 754 and 766 call read_native_effect_budget_sources with six arguments after the attempt added the Option of a SigningPreparation as the third parameter of the three budget source readers; the attempt bound the verifier through the preparation in native_binding.rs, program_sources.rs, human_runtime.rs and repair_22_31_217.rs, and stopped at the scope boundary without running the verification."
fix = "The calling test files enter touches (decision 2838): services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/budget/repair_22_31_217.kvx, services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_560.kvx, services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_33_1520.rs; attempt 3 passes the retained preparation at every call site and runs the build and the verification at the final tree."

[gotcha.3519]
title = "The ported parallel-preparation property compiles again and the kernel refuses its fixture with a fatal invariant at sample 0"
symptom = "22.39.76 attempt 1 at f78c369241b0 (base 901c8c13c8): the build passed, the first verification failed because the prerequisite test did not follow the include directive that defines test-sanitizers in tools/build/sanitizers.mk, and after the repair the four ported sources compiled while the new Makefile target test-core-ports failed at the case that compares a single-lane preparation with a four-lane preparation: status -1001 (LXP_FATAL_INVARIANT) at sample 0 with a retry prefix of 0. The property source was last changed by task 1.4.3 and never compiled since the kernel contract drifted: its sample helper still submits activities with protocol version LXP_PROTOCOL_VERSION_LEGACY, account sequence 1 and a hand-built 88-byte batch identity preimage, while the live caller tests/programs/test_metered_call.c submits LXP_PROTOCOL_VERSION_STATE_COMMITMENT activities, binds authority through lxp_authority_resolve_activity and derives the batch identity through lxp_batch_identity_activity. The kernel settles no activity of the sample and returns the invariant at the settled-count check of kernel_prepare_activity_batch in src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c."
fix = "Attempt 2 keeps the attempt-1 tree and ports the property fixture to the current preparation contract using the live caller as the reference; the kernel is never weakened and the case is never deleted."

[gotcha.3520]
title = "Two landed repair tasks disagree on whether the MCP submit tool reports a lost node response as an error"
symptom = "22.39.118 attempt 6 at 95ae016f9080 (base 9ac93b1ec6): the three RPC tests, the 24 library tests and the four daemon-bound binding tests passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in mcp_evm_submit at line 159: the case that closes the transport after reading the request expects toolset::invoke to return an error (a closed transport must not report submission success) while the toolset returned the unknown-rung value. Task 22.33.1493 (tools/platform/cli/src/toolset.rs, 2026-11-05) routed both toolset::invoke and toolset::invoke_task through rpc::submission_outcome, which maps SubmissionFailure::Indeterminate to Ok with rung unknown, and its suite repair_22_33_1493 asserts that both paths return the unknown rung; task 22.33.1495 (same day) rewrote mcp_evm_submit to assert the error. Each task ran only its own suite, so neither saw the other. The A2A runtime in tools/platform/cli/src/a2a.rs keeps the two shapes apart: its invoke_task returns the unknown rung with the local transaction hash (issue 1262) and its invoke turns that rung into the error submission <hash> is indeterminate."
fix = "Repair task 22.39.135 gives the toolset the A2A shape (invoke refuses an indeterminate submission with an error naming the hash, invoke_task keeps the unknown rung) and aligns both suites; 22.39.118 requires it and relaunches behind it."

[gotcha.3521]
title = "The interrupted-install case now reaches both terminal job states and its new archive accounting misses the reads it instruments"
symptom = "22.37.4 attempt 6 at 4531f377a727 (base 552a8697a2): the frozen install passed on the rebased tree (22.39.129). The first verification failed before any output read because the fixture provider answered 404 to the launch of /usr/bin/python3, absent in the qualification environment; the attempt bound that path to the running interpreter through the guest path resolver of the fixture. The second verification ran the interrupted install to a signed FAILED result with complete cleanup and the replacement execution to SUCCEEDED, then failed in the accounting the attempt added: it records archive reads in a request handler subclass whose route strips the collection prefix and resource segment using the name the fixture chose for its metadata, while the provider requests carry the resource identifier the control plane assigned (hf-<digest>) under the environment prefix; the route never matched, the base handler served the files from its /filesystem/ branch, and the attempt asserted that no complete receipt.json was served."
fix = "Attempt 7 keeps the tree and keys the archive accounting on the request path pattern (any resource identifier, then /filesystem/ and the output spool path of the process) or records the served bytes in the base /filesystem/ branch, so the assertion compares what the control plane actually read; nothing else changes."

[gotcha.3522]
title = "The Python payment modules lag the TypeScript peers on the wire and 22 cross-language conformance cases fail once the suite runs"
symptom = "22.39.78 attempt 1 at a177aacba81f (base 5989465ed9): the build and the three wiring tests passed; the pay6 conformance suite ran for the first time since 2026-11-02 and finished 22 failed, 62 passed. The groups: x402_http accepts only layerx:<name> networks (line 92) and raises unsupported-network for the eip155:125 identifier the TypeScript seller and buyer send (seven HttpTests cases); x402.verify_payment_receipt branches only on the committed flag, so invalid commitment values pass where the cases expect a refusal, and the payer binding rejects the peer receipt with payment binding payment mismatch (test_executed_payment_binding and test_no_commitment_downgrade in four modules, test_receipt_binding_and_pending); x402_agent rejects the prefixed asset identifiers of the peer and derives a different draw hash (two AgentBudgetTests cases); x402_rpc lacks HostedGatewayRpc, which test_rpc imports, and PaymentRpc.send submits a truncated raw transaction instead of refusing it. Task 18.1463.1 verified these four modules against pay6 on 2026-11-02; tasks 22.31.147, 22.31.510 and 22.31.514 changed x402.py, x402_http.py, x402_agent.py and x402_rpc.py on 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 with gates that ran only the local sequencer-named suites of the package."
fix = "Repair tasks 22.39.136 (x402, x402_http, x402_agent) and 22.39.137 (x402_rpc) port the modules to the wire the TypeScript peers produce, with the conformance suite in their verification; 22.39.78 requires both."

[gotcha.3523]
title = "Sixteen node package tests fail once three recorded failures are skipped, and each of the sixteen fails alone"
symptom = "Task 22.39.40 attempt 4 at d96e5a9eefb2 (base 0eb129eb57bc) ran the node package with the three recorded failures skipped and sixteen other tests failed in both verification runs: TestSidioraFeeTokenUpgradeServesThePrecompileOnlyAfterIt (EnsureSidioraDenom rejects chain id 1), the five TestV6120 tests (v6120 liveness true before the plan, spot module version 2 instead of 1), TestAnteChainRunsRevocationDecoratorAfterAuthzNested (LXP_AUTH_SCOPE, bank denomination has no canonical kernel asset), TestFeeTokenGigaBlockRefusesUnusableRate, TestAppOrdersStoreGenesisBeforeHostWriters and TestAppRegistersPayAndAgentModulesInGenesisOrder (the order ends with layerxchains where layerxagent is expected), TestAppMountsMergedModuleStores (37 stores instead of 43), TestAppBuildsPayKeeperOverSharedHost (LXP_NON_CANONICAL escrow genesis), TestDecodeFailureTxReportsZeroGas, TestProofNodeGoApi, TestEvmEventsForCw1155 and TestRepair_102_SchedulerFailureAtomic; TestFinalizeAdoptedSealedBlockMatchesReexecution blocks the package until the 15 minute limit because the snapshot restore waits on the state-store importer with an import parallelism of zero. The attempt record node/repair_22_39_40.kvx shows every one of the sixteen failing when run alone. Attempt 2 at d51cd029d92d (base 4526ea1b436d) ran the whole package without any skip in 177 seconds with only the three recorded failures, and the only build inputs of the package that differ between the two bases are the three precompile ABI files precompiles/layerxprograms/abi.json, precompiles/perps/abi/abi.json and precompiles/launchpad/abi.json that task 22.39.62 regenerated at a2bf776a9f together with their attestor copies."
fix = "Decision 2851: the sixteen tests are repaired by their own task 22.39.138, which first separates the two candidate causes (the skipped tests leaving package state the sixteen depend on, or the regenerated ABI files) by running the package without the skip at the current main and the sixteen names selected, then repairs the cause found: a test that passes only after another test ran establishes its own state, and a regenerated ABI that changed what the node serves is corrected at the generator output with the attestor copies following the precompile sources. Task 22.39.40 requires 22.39.138; a skip never stands in for the state a skipped test established."

[gotcha.3524]
title = "The retained-preparation binding refuses the recorded revocation-counter budget proof"
symptom = "Task 22.39.128 attempt 3 at f3749c56d963 (base 89c9fc5ef647) bound the retained native preparations through the signing preparation as decision 2834 requires; the build passed and eighteen cases of tests/repair_22_31_217.rs passed, but repair_proof_revocation_counter_exports_and_verifies panicked at line 1433 with counter above height must verify: Refused. The attempt changed only the helpers appended after line 1442 of that file; the recorded case proof_revocation_counter and the assertion are the main tree ones, and the case verified on main under task 22.31.217. The case export carries a payment and no native preparation, so the refusal comes from the attempt change to the budget proof path, not from the case. Because the first suite failed, the retained settlement tests of the library never ran."
fix = "Decision 2834 binds only an export that carries a retained native preparation; an export without one verifies exactly as on main. Attempt 4 keeps the tree, locates the refusing site by surfacing the BudgetProofError variant and the binding step that produced it, and makes the binding step a no-op for exports that carry no native preparation; the recorded case bytes and the test stay unchanged."

[gotcha.3525]
title = "The ai-market sweep tree adds 73 KB to a guest that leaves 16 KB of headroom"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 24 at 7e4373f372a9 (base d15ac4fd410f) failed the build gate three times: the producer gate of 22.31.478 measured the merged guest at 581212 bytes against the 524184 byte bound, two cycles of code-size work brought it to 550520 bytes, and the second cycle left two compile errors in the library. The main tree guest measures 508166 bytes in the size record of task 22.31.615 (programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/src/repair_22_31_615.kvx), so the attempt tree adds between 42 and 73 KB of guest code where main leaves 16 KB of headroom. Attempt 22 measured 553180 bytes on the same path; the 60 minute limit of the task covers one merged native build."
fix = "Decision 2852: a sweep repair carries no code the main tree already provides. Attempt 25 keeps only the changes that repair a failure present on main, drops every function, codec, table and helper the main tree provides in favour of the main form, and measures the leftover divergence as the guest size difference against the 508166 bytes of the size record; the final guest must satisfy the producer gate and the task record states both sizes. The task limit rises to 180 minutes so a merged native build and the crate suite fit."

[gotcha.3526]
title = "The payment conformance peer cannot start when the gate of a Python module never installs the TypeScript SDK dependencies"
symptom = "Task 22.39.136 attempt 1 at 2b5e3f351d63 (base 83246ad56769) ported the three Python payment modules; the build passed, 13 pay6 cases passed and 8 failed before any Python assertion ran: the TypeScript peer process exits with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for @noble/hashes imported from services/agent/sdk/typescript/src/committed-proof.ts, because the gate declared only a py_compile build step and nothing installed the dependencies of services/agent/sdk/typescript, services/platform/middleware/seller and services/platform/middleware/conformance; task 22.39.78 attempt 1 ran the same pay6 modules with those three dependency sets installed and reached the Python assertions (gotcha 3522). The local suites of the task were never reached."
fix = "The build step of every task whose verification drives the pay6 conformance peers installs the three Node dependency sets first: npm ci with scripts ignored in services/agent/sdk/typescript (it carries a lockfile) and npm install without a package lock in the seller and conformance directories, so no lockfile is created in the tree. Tasks 22.39.136 and 22.39.137 carry that build step from this round; the attempt-1 tree of 22.39.136 stands for the next attempt."

[gotcha.3527]
title = "The bridge test workflow installs pnpm 12 while the bridge manifest declares pnpm 10, and four more workflow pins disagree with their manifests"
symptom = "Task 22.39.54 attempt 4 at 15fc2db91b06 (base 83246ad56769) passed 110 tools/ci tests and failed only tools/ci/tests/test_bridge_workflow_app.py: the test asserts that .github/workflows/bridge-test.yml installs the pnpm release apps/bridge/package.json declares, the manifest declares pnpm@10.34.9 since task 22.39.106 changed it from pnpm@12.15.0 at 2b0a223f95, and line 143 of the workflow still installs pnpm@12.15.0. The pins test of 22.39.106, tests/ci/test_package_manager_pins_agree.py, covers container files only. The same disagreement exists at ci.yml lines 267 and 298 (pnpm@10.15.1 and pnpm@9.15.9 for services/wallet), wallet-go-test.yml line 74 (pnpm@9.15.9 for services/wallet/gateway) and platform.yml line 195 (pnpm@9.15.9 for services/wallet), while services/wallet, apps/wallet and apps/perps declare pnpm@10.34.9 and apps/launchpad declares pnpm@9.15.0."
fix = "Decision 2853: every public workflow line that installs pnpm for a working directory installs exactly the release the manifest of that directory declares, and the pins test covers workflow install lines next to container files. Repair task 22.39.139 corrects the five workflow lines and extends the pins test; task 22.39.54 requires it."

[gotcha.3528]
title = "The recorded committed receipt is refused at the agent ingress because the recording peer serves no committed header"
symptom = "Task 22.33.50 attempt 6 at 68eb25c760dc (base 654b52826928, after 22.31.539 and 22.31.540 landed) passed the build and failed the verification with 1 passed and 2 failed: finding12_recorded_paxd_receipt_transport_recovers_before_replay and finding12_control_transport_preserves_checkpoint_verification both panic in the checked helper at tests/repair_22_33_50.rs line 70 with ReceiptStoreError::UnauthenticatedIngress. The test function authenticate_recording serves the recording tests/fixtures/repair_22_33_50/paxd-v4-committed.json through a local peer that answers pax_sequencerReceipt with the committed recording and eth_getTransactionReceipt with null, and store_verified_if_absent then calls AuthenticatedTransactionReceipt::from_authenticated in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs lines 58 to 64 (task 22.33.1513 at bfc86ded84), which refuses a receipt at rung committed, or one with a covering block, that carries no committed header. The attempt-5 failure at line 297 never reached this guard."
fix = "The guard is the producer contract of the agent daemon ingress and stands. The test presents the header the producer requires: the recording already holds positive.header and positive.header_signature, so the peer answers the commit lookup as well and the test authenticates through lookup_authenticated_with_commit (services/agent/crates/layerx-client/src/rpc/receipt.rs line 201); the stored rung assertion then follows the producer (gotcha 3046), which supersedes the attempt-5 instruction to keep that one assertion unchanged. Attempt 7 of 22.33.50 continues from the attempt-6 tree."

[gotcha.3529]
title = "The ramp toolkit contract tests carry three protected-input cases and one assertion left behind by the payment authority move"
symptom = "Task 22.39.68 attempt 3 at 092fca9bb7f0 (base 654b52826928) moved the eleven certificate and key fixtures out of src, passed the build, the key-material test and the hosted internal crate (7, 0 and 2 passed), and failed the ramp toolkit crate with 7 passed and 4 failed, all in services/platform/ramps/toolkit/tests/contracts.rs and none touched by the attempt: failed_callback_apply_retains_no_event_and_retry_is_idempotent, mismatched_pending_append_prefix_preserves_history_and_refuses_recovery and interrupted_callback_write_recovers_on_restart_without_repair panic at line 461 because LAYERX_RAMP_RECOVERY_CONTRACT_CONFIG is unset (the ramp recovery workflow sets it from a protected variable), and payment_direction_selects_direct_send_or_customer_grant fails at line 225 asserting that the payer grant draw targets LEDGER_ADDRESS 0x101a while compile_payer_grant_draw has targeted PAY_ADDRESS 0x101b since task 22.31.211 at 5febff359b. Task 22.99.69 ran the crate with the protected cases skipped before 22.31.211 landed, so the stale assertion has been red on main since 2026-11-04."
fix = "Decision 2325: the three protected-input cases are qualified by the ramp recovery workflow that sets their input, so the verification of 22.39.68 skips exactly those three names. The stale assertion is a repair task of the platform owner, 22.39.140, which 22.39.68 requires; attempt 4 of 22.39.68 continues from the attempt-3 tree."

[gotcha.3530]
title = "The program call test still asserts an error for a lost node response that the CLI has retained as the unknown rung since the restart-recovery repair"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 7 at 323c07506d2a (base b6e2f6e6651a, main merged with 22.39.135) passed the build and the 94 library tests and failed make platform-test-tooling at one case: program_call_submits_raw_transaction in tools/platform/cli/tests/program_evm_calls.rs line 261 asserts that programs::submit_program_transaction returns an error when the capture peer reads the request and closes the connection without answering. Since task 22.33.1493 at c239354b90 the function rpc::submission_outcome maps SubmissionFailure::Indeterminate to the value with txHash, rung unknown and detail, and submit_program_transaction returns it with tx_hash added, so the assertion fails at main; attempt 6 never reached it because the test run stopped at the mcp_evm_submit failure that 22.39.135 repaired. The attempt changed neither programs.rs nor the test."
fix = "Decision 2854: the CLI program call keeps the recoverable form of 22.33.1493 and the consumer test asserts it. Repair task 22.39.141 of the platform owner rewrites the assertion; 22.39.118 requires it and attempt 8 continues from the attempt-7 tree."

[gotcha.3531]
title = "The payout split adds twenty-six kilobytes to a guest that already exceeds the qualification bound of its size record"
symptom = "Task 22.38.6 attempt 1 at e8614e7d1265 (base c9515ebed298) implemented the payout split in rewards.rs and reward_math.rs with an 820-line test file and failed the build gate three times: the size-optimised guest measured 533903 bytes at the first build and 534099 bytes after the second repair cycle, above the deployment bound 524184 of the size record programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/src/repair_22_31_615.kvx; the two repair cycles removed duplication in the payout path and state copies and gained nothing. The base tree carries at least the 508166 bytes gotcha 3525 recorded, above the qualification bound 504184 of the same record, so no pending guest operation of the 22.38 series fits under the deployment bound without a reduction first."
fix = "Decision 2792 applies as written: a guest above the qualification bound at main is a repair task of the programs owner that every pending guest task requires, working only inside the crate (shared codec helpers, status codes instead of formatted messages, static tables, removal of dead code) with the bound, the release profile and the make target unchanged. Task 22.39.142 brings the guest to at most 484184 bytes, forty thousand bytes of headroom because the payout split alone measured twenty-six thousand; 22.38.6 and 22.38.7 require it, and attempt 2 of 22.38.6 applies the same techniques to its own additions."

[gotcha.3532]
title = "The recorded budget proof case is refused because the verifier now authenticates the owner address through three capability reads the recording never answers"
symptom = "Task 22.39.128 attempt 4 at 75cdab1dfc4c (base 708e71968aab) ran the named case with --nocapture as instructed: build exit 0, verification exit 1 with 18 passed and 1 failed, repair_proof_revocation_counter_exports_and_verifies panicking at tests/repair_22_31_217.rs line 1433 with counter above height must verify: Refused. The refusing step is not the native binding of decision 2834: task 22.33.1520 at c88f78b406 added the function authenticated_owner_address to services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/budget/budget_proof.rs, which reads getEvmAddrByLayerX(bytes32), getUnifiedAccount(address) and accountOwner(bytes32) through the committed reads at the checkpoint and refuses when any answer is missing. The recorded corpus tests/fixtures/repair_22_31_217/corpus.json carries rpc_answers for no such read in any of its twelve cases, the test helper add_account_and_fee_answers synthesises only account and fee answers, and the verification of 22.33.1520 ran only its own test file, so the case passed at 22.31.217 attempt 12 (75df69e084) and has been red at main since c88f78b406 landed."
fix = "Decision 2855: a producer repair that adds a read to a verifier extends every recorded case the verifier is exercised against in the same change, and a consumer that meets the missing answer records it following the producer. Attempt 5 of 22.39.128 records the three capability answers in the test helper after the form of tests/repair_22_31_560.rs line 132, with the corpus bytes, the export bytes and the assertion at line 1433 unchanged."

[gotcha.3533]
title = "The per-directory dependency installs of the payment module gates ask the registry for the workspace SDK, which only a root workspace install resolves"
symptom = "Task 22.39.136 attempt 3 at 6a49f8b1242e (base b87f19d0d7) failed its build step before the Python compile: npm install in services/platform/middleware/seller returned E404 for @sidiora/layerx-sdk@0.1.0, because the seller manifest names the SDK by version and the repository root package.json declares the SDK, the seller, the conformance package and sixteen more directories as one npm workspace, so the version resolves to the workspace package only when the install runs at the root. The public workflow installs every one of those packages with npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund at the repository root (ci.yml, the js-workspace-tests job), task 22.39.78 attempt 1 reached the Python assertions of pay6 because its node dependency step ran that root install, and the per-directory form that round 228 (gotcha 3526) wrote into the build steps of 22.39.136 and 22.39.137 was never the form the repository supports. The task code was again not exercised."
fix = "Decision 2856: a gate that needs Node dependencies of workspace packages runs the root workspace install exactly as the public workflow does, never a per-directory install. The build steps of 22.39.136 and 22.39.137 carry the root install from this round; attempt 4 of 22.39.136 continues from the attempt-3 tree and corrects the record entry the attempt wrote."

[gotcha.3534]
title = "The ramp payment direction test also asserts a retired error variant for the on-ramp draw"
symptom = "Task 22.39.140 attempt 1 at e7b1e04f43fa (base 3d1eff197f5a) corrected the draw destination to PAY_ADDRESS and added the budgetSpend selector assertion; the build passed and the verification failed at the next assertion of the same test, services/platform/ramps/toolkit/tests/contracts.rs line 237, which expects compile_payer_grant_draw on an on-ramp order to return RampError::PayerGrantRequired while the producer returns RampError::InvalidOrder: since task 22.31.211 at 5febff359b compile_payer_grant_draw is the compatibility entry of compile_customer_payment (src/lib.rs lines 357 to 375), which validates the bound order and its customer payment authorization and refuses an on-ramp order as InvalidOrder. The attempt left the assertion as instructed and recorded the mismatch; 7 of 8 selected cases passed."
fix = "The whole test follows the producer, not only the two assertions round 229 named: attempt 2 of 22.39.140 asserts InvalidOrder for the on-ramp draw, records every corrected assertion with the producer line it follows, and the instruction to leave the other assertions unchanged yields where the producer contract differs."

[gotcha.3535]
title = "Eight node package tests fail at main on stale assertions against producer changes and one unregistered fee-token refusal"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 attempt 1 at 95a1cd16f850 (base b6e2f6e6651a) repaired the fixture setup of the sixteen tests and the snapshot import count, built twice with exit 0 and failed the selected run twice with 9 of 17 passing; the record shows every remaining failure is an assertion that disagrees with the current producer: TestAppMountsMergedModuleStores expects the mounted count to be the canonical list plus six while keys.MemIAVLStoreKeys already carries the six merged stores and App mounts 37; TestAppOrdersStoreGenesisBeforeHostWriters and TestAppRegistersPayAndAgentModulesInGenesisOrder expect layerxagent right after layerxpay while App registers layerxchains between them; TestV6120InitialisesTheNewModulesOnAPreUpgradeChain expects version 1 for every new module while spot declares consensus version 2 and the migration records each module version; TestProofNodeGoApi expects method not found for the receipt method over the websocket while rpc/server.go now registers that service on both transports; TestFeeTokenGigaBlockRefusesUnusableRate and TestRepair_102_SchedulerFailureAtomic expect raw error text while node/abci.go and node/app.go build every response with debug false, so an unregistered error arrives as internal error with code 1; TestEvmEventsForCw1155 returns code 1 under the fresh-application fixture of the attempt. The fee-token rate errors of modules/evm/keeper/params.go lines 16 to 19 are plain errors, so a client never learns why a transfer was refused."
fix = "Decisions 2857 and 2858: the eight tests follow their producers in attempt 2 of 22.39.138, recording each corrected assertion with its producer line; task 22.39.143 registers the four fee-token rate errors under the EVM module codespace so the response carries code and reason, and 22.39.138 requires it."

[gotcha.3536]
title = "The tools Python suite wiring reaches a release candidate suite that never ran from a workflow and fails on 21 cases and 24 setup errors"
symptom = "Task 22.39.84 attempt 1 at c3d9e7cd1bb1 (base be867b849efe) added the test-tools-python make target, its workflow job with Go, the per-suite make fragments and the deferred contract read of tools/paxeer-x/candidate.py, built with exit 0 and failed the verification twice: tools/paxeer-x/tests/ai_evidence_test.py errors in 24 cases at setup because safe_path requires a string and the cases pass path objects; 18 cases of the gate test module and 2 of candidate_test.py fail because candidate create exits 2 with the generic refusal while candidate.py line 51 discards the stderr of the contract program; test_gov_templates.py reports a release name missing in tools/hpx/publish.sh, test_retired_catalogue_deleted.py finds the tree services/agent/crates/layerx-client/src/lni still present, and test_signature_route_catalogued.py finds no sig provider run by the explorer gate; the wiring test test_paxeer_x_collects_without_go asserts the substring skipped is absent from the collect-only output, which the name of one test contains. The make target was never reached."
fix = "Decision 2820: attempt 2 of 22.39.84 records the failing cases of the release candidate suite in tests/ci/data/tools_python_suite_baseline.json with their reasons and 22.39.144 as the retiring task, derives the deselection of the paxeer-x recipe from that file, corrects its own collection guard and captures the contract program stderr once to name the refusal cause; task 22.39.144 repairs the suite following its producers and retires the entries."

[gotcha.3537]
title = "The launchpad Go recipe waits ten minutes per package for an Anvil process the qualification environment never provided and two NATS driver tests refuse a duplicates window under 100 ms"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 2 at 6188bc589702 (base 708e71968aab) built with exit 0 and passed its 14 wiring tests; make -C services/launchpad ci then timed out after 600 seconds in shared/config/capabilities and shared/config/deployment, whose tests start a private Anvil process and wait when the executable is absent (attempt 1 logged the NotFound spawn at attest_test.go and revision_test.go), and failed TestPhase3ActualRelayCrashAndConsumerRestart and TestPhase3ActualOrderedPoisonAndHundredDuplicates in shared/delivery/natsdriver because the embedded NATS server answers that the duplicates window needs to be at least 100 ms. The verification command never named anvil, so the qualification environment did not provide the Foundry binaries (decisions 2068 and 2719), and the matrix job the task adds installs no Foundry toolchain either."
fix = "Decision 2859: the verification of 22.39.75 opens with anvil --version, the matrix job installs the Foundry toolchain with the pinned action the solidity job of ci.yml uses, and the two NATS driver tests enter the baseline with their reason and 22.39.117 as retiring task."

[gotcha.3538]
title = "core-test-all reaches the Solidity state surface recipe, which runs forge the qualification environment never provided"
symptom = "Task 22.39.76 attempt 2 at d887ecbc3a8c (base b6e2f6e6651a) ported the parallel-preparation property to the current preparation contract; the build passed, the wiring tests and all four ported suites passed, and make core-test-all then failed at Makefile line 1135, test-contract-state-surface, with forge not found. The verification command never named forge, so the qualification environment did not provide the Foundry binaries (decisions 2068 and 2719); the workflow step the task adds after make test runs in a job without the Foundry toolchain, which only the solidity job installs (ci.yml line 105)."
fix = "Decision 2859: the verification of 22.39.76 opens with forge --version, the core-test-all step lives in a job that installs the Foundry toolchain before it, and the wiring test asserts the install and the step share a job."

[gotcha.3539]
title = "The Foundry profile test of the tools ci suite forbids the root project to select tests/solidity after 22.39.81 made it select exactly that"
symptom = "Task 22.39.54 attempt 5 at ac334536eba1 (base fba11291a3ae) merged the workflow pin repair of 22.39.139 and the bridge workflow test passed; tools/ci/tests/test_foundry_profile.py line 27 then failed, asserting that the root profile test directory differs from tests/solidity while task 22.39.81 at 2c80a502c8 made the root kernel-contract project select tests/solidity on purpose (foundry.toml lines 1 and 5) and ran no tools/ci test. 110 cases passed, 1 failed, the second suite did not run."
fix = "Decision 2857: the assertion follows the producer and asserts the root profile test directory is tests/solidity, keeping the two retired-permission assertions; attempt 6 of 22.39.54 makes that change after merging main."

[gotcha.3540]
title = "Four TypeScript market encoders wait for payload layouts two pending program tasks define"
symptom = "Task 22.38.31 attempt 1 at 3ac7e5e8c7c5 (base 61e3d6e79583) added src/inference_market.ts with eight operation encoders, the view decoders, the px reads and the ask funding helper; the build passed and 14 of 15 cases passed; the failing case at test/inference-market.test.ts line 318 is the placeholder for splitPayout, lockBond, slashBond and refundBond, whose payload layouts 22.38.6 (payout split) and 22.38.7 (bond lock, slash and refund) define and whose fixture bytes their program tests record; both are pending behind the ai-market headroom repair 22.39.142. The task required only 22.38.12."
fix = "22.38.31 requires 22.38.6 and 22.38.7 from this round; attempt 2 completes the four encoders from the landed layouts and fixtures and replaces the placeholder with byte assertions."

[gotcha.3541]
title = "The committed control recordings achieve the committed verification level while the retained export assertion expects checkpoint finalisation"
symptom = "Task 22.33.50 attempt 7 at 959a8f8113b8 (base 3d1eff197f5a) let the local peer answer the commit lookup from the header and header signature the recordings hold, so the ingress guard of the agent daemon accepted the receipts and stored the Committed rung (tests/repair_22_33_50.rs line 248 passes); both cases then failed at line 294, where verify_receipt_export_with_consensus achieves COMMITTED for the retained export while the assertion expects CHECKPOINT_FINALISED. The evidence the test persists (receipt bytes, receipt proof, canonical header and header signature) supports exactly the committed level, which is the real committed evidence finding 12 asks to retain; no checkpoint record is part of these recordings."
fix = "Decision 2857 and gotcha 3046: the assertion follows the producer and asserts that the achieved level equals the level the ingest stored and that both are COMMITTED; attempt 8 of 22.33.50 makes that change and nothing else."

[gotcha.3542]
title = "The program lifecycle test keeps the stale indeterminate submission assertion 22.39.141 corrected only in the program call test"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 8 at 05b9761fffef (base 2402fdbcce9c) updated the contract fixture and the exact method list; the build passed, the three required rpc tests and the library tests passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in tests/program_evm_lifecycle.rs, where line 150 asserts in program_deploy_calldata_matches_vector and program_wind_down_modes_use_layerxprograms that the lifecycle submission returns an error when the capturing peer closes without answering, while since 22.33.1493 at c239354b90 the submission outcome returns Ok with the unknown rung and the local hash (decision 2854, gotcha 3530); 22.39.141 corrected the same form in program_evm_calls.rs only."
fix = "Decision 2857: attempt 9 of 22.39.118 makes both lifecycle cases assert the producer shape, as 22.39.141 did for the program call test, and changes nothing in src."

[gotcha.3543]
title = "The reconciled guest of 22.99.77 remains 3545 bytes over the deployment bound before the headroom repair lands"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 25 at e686d446206d (base 17705776aa8f) reconciled the attempt-24 tree with main as instructed; the build measured the guest at 528427 bytes, then 527729 bytes after the two repair cycles, against the 524184 byte bound, so the verification never ran (attempt 24 had measured 581212 and 550520 bytes). The task required 22.31.615 and 22.31.620, both done, but not the headroom repair 22.39.142 that decision 2792 makes every pending guest task require."
fix = "22.99.77 requires 22.39.142 from this round; attempt 26 merges main once the guest is under 484184 bytes and fits its additions in the headroom, trimming only its own files."

[gotcha.3544]
title = "The wallet SDK suite fails 31 cases in ten files at main, so the public wallet job and every gate that runs the whole suite are red"
symptom = "Task 22.39.94 attempt 1 at 8e020814aea8 (base e7d1456b92) routed the launchpad matrix through the launchpad workspace and the wallet suite through the ignore-workspace form; the build passed, the three wiring tests passed and the frozen install of sdk/wallet resolved, then pnpm exec vitest run in sdk/wallet reported 31 failed, 109 passed and 38 todo across test/agent.test.ts, client.test.ts, endpoint.test.ts, kernel-reads.test.ts, ladder.test.ts, modules.test.ts, provider.test.ts, receipt.test.ts, repair-22-31-238.test.ts and repair-22-33-135.test.ts. The error classes are consumer assertions behind producer changes: the receipt tests expect the pre-authentication receipt shapes while src/receipt.ts authenticates every receipt through the key pins and refuses an invalid receipt request; the module tests read payer grants and funded accounts the SDK retired (WebPayerGrantsRetiredError, FundedUnsupportedError); the provider tests expect eth_accounts and the hosted px_resolveAccount route that moved to the node root; the endpoint batch test receives answers that do not match their request ids from its fixture; the ladder tests compare the golden journey against a schema that gained states; the React refresh test loses its renderer. The task touched none of these files and the public wallet workflow runs the same command in sdk/wallet, so the job is red at main independent of this task (decisions 3052 and 3053 of the gotcha record)."
fix = "Decisions 2820 and 2860: attempt 2 of 22.39.94 records the 31 cases in tests/ci/data/wallet_vitest_baseline.json with their reasons and 22.39.145 as retiring task, runs the suite through a name filter derived from that file in both the public wallet job and its own verification, and task 22.39.145 makes the cases follow their producers and retires the entries."

[gotcha.3545]
title = "The duplicate make-target check of the release workflow repair refuses a shared dependency install, and six other workflow tests assume the inline platform jobs it moved"
symptom = "Task 22.39.103 attempt 1 at fe038cf56879 (base 40f92a32c3) created the release toolchain action, routed the sanitizer, long fuzz and programs lanes through the agent and programs workflows called from platform.yml and wrote the two checks; the build passed and test_no_make_target_duplicated_across_automatic_workflows failed on chain.mk install, which both .github/workflows/paxeer-cross-arch-build.yml (line 184) and paxeer-eth-blocktests.yml run before their own lanes: a dependency install of the same class as the allowlisted paxd-native-libs, not a check lane. The attempt also reports that the existing tests that read platform.yml (tests/ci/test_platform_release_gate_calls.py, test_workflow_push_concurrency.py, test_make_recipe_paths_exist.py, test_package_manager_pins_agree.py, test_platform_workflow_maven.py, test_workflow_live_inputs_guarded.py and tools/ci/tests/test_replay_golden_ci.py and test_wire_codec_ci.py) assume the inline platform jobs and literal concurrency strings the repair replaced, and its verification never ran them."
fix = "Decisions 2857 and 3052 of the record: attempt 2 of 22.39.103 adds chain.mk install to the allowlist with its reason, runs every test that reads the three changed workflows and makes each assertion that assumes the inline jobs follow the new producer shape; the verification of the task runs those tests from this round."

[gotcha.3546]
title = "The program lifecycle test omits the receipt policy argument the lifecycle commands require since 22.33.1492"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 9 at 992ae4771ccd (base 40f92a32c3) changed the two lifecycle assertions as instructed; the build passed and both cases then failed earlier, at tools/platform/cli/tests/program_evm_lifecycle.rs line 58, because the command refused with invalid_arguments: the required --receipt-policy argument was not provided. ProgramLifecycleArgs in tools/platform/cli/src/main.rs (line 366) requires receipt_policy since the 22.33.1492 repair at 7884cd3f83, and tests/repair_22_33_1494.rs lines 403 to 405 and 433 to 434 show the pinned receipt policy file the wallet writes pass; the lifecycle test builds its arguments at lines 215 to 217 without it, so the capturing peer never receives a request and the attempt-9 assertion about the response shape was never reached."
fix = "Decision 2857: attempt 10 of 22.39.118 passes --receipt-policy with a policy file written after the repair_22_33_1494 form from the lifecycle test, keeps the attempt-9 assertions, and records the producer line."

[gotcha.3547]
title = "The retained settlement fixture of the agent daemon lacks the paymentDenom the receipt evidence requires since the 22.30.94 repair"
symptom = "Task 22.39.128 attempt 5 at fb5a29eb0340 (base e7d1456b92) recorded the three owner capability answers in the test helper as instructed and all 19 repair_22_31_217 cases passed; the library suite human_runtime::retained_settlement_tests then failed its first case with Refused at the must helper (human_runtime.rs line 23586), and the three remaining cases failed on the poisoned environment lock. The attempt traced the refusal to the fixture receipt of that module, which carries no paymentDenom, while the receipt evidence requires it since the 22.30.94 repair at 08a6418214 (protocol_evidence_time_tests.rs line 381 sets paymentDenom usid for the same reason). The verification of that repair never ran the retained settlement module."
fix = "Decisions 2855 and 2857: attempt 6 of 22.39.128 adds paymentDenom to the fixture receipt of retained_settlement_tests following protocol_evidence_time_tests.rs, changes nothing else, and runs the whole declared verification once."

[gotcha.3548]
title = "The pay6 node fixtures hash the receipt the way the verifier does not, and the HTTP case expects the Python validator to refuse the metered and subscription schemes the seller accepts"
symptom = "Task 22.39.136 attempt 5 at fc0b73e9b64c (base 40f92a32c3) ran the root workspace install, reached the pay6 peers and reported 17 passed, 4 failed and 3 teardown errors. Three failures and the teardown errors come from the seller: services/platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/node-fixtures.mjs line 18 sets receiptDigest to Keccak-256 of the signed receipt bytes, while the verifier of the client SDK (services/agent/sdk/typescript/src/verifier.ts line 558) computes the SHA-256 domain digest of the canonical receipt encoding and the seller compares the two in verifyReceiptDigest (seller/src/index.ts line 883), so every capture answers 500 verification-failure before the Python buyer is reached; the fixture landed at b32474c131 after the verifier repairs ef62b3d0e2 and d42a3df0c5 without running against them. The fourth failure is test_http.py line 122, which expects validate_required of the Python module to raise for the metered and subscription schemes, while the seller parseRequirements (index.ts lines 819 to 847) accepts both with their window terms and the Python port handles both (x402.py line 172); only the unknown scheme is refused by every producer. Both are outside the six files of 22.39.136."
fix = "Decision 2861: task 22.39.146 makes the fixture digest come from the verifier function and the scheme assertion follow the seller, and 22.39.136 requires it; attempt 6 of 22.39.136 continues once it lands."

[gotcha.3549]
title = "The ai-market guest reduction reached 504844 bytes, 20660 above the qualification bound, when the repair units ran out"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 attempt 1 at 4140d2b8a2f5 (base 3d1eff197f5a) measured the guest at 511946 bytes, grew it to 523935 in a first candidate that changed representations, restored them, and ended at 504844 bytes with the shared typed field writer, the ordered destination reader, the streaming rewards-account derivation, the checkpointed replay state and the moved control values recorded per module in src/repair_22_39_142.kvx; the final build passed and the verification was refused because both repair units were spent, so the four f11 binaries never ran. The largest modules of the crate remain rewards.rs (107 kB of source), codec.rs, evidence.rs, the routing entry, epoch.rs, admission.rs and queries.rs."
fix = "Attempt 2 of 22.39.142 continues from the attempt-1 tree with the same techniques on the largest modules until the guest measures at most 484184 bytes, then runs the build once and the verification once; the time limit rises to 240 minutes."

[gotcha.3550]
title = "The core C suite target reaches the arithmetic proof, which refuses without CBMC and Z3, and neither the public job nor the qualification environment carries them"
symptom = "Task 22.39.76 attempt 3 at 230d5e312987 (base 40f92a32c3) pinned the Foundry installation of the new ci.yml step, strengthened the wiring test and kept the four ported sources; the build passed, both CI tests and the four suites passed, and make core-test-all then stopped at Makefile line 1233: qualify-arith runs tools/lxp_arith_proof.sh, which resolves cbmc, z3 and clang on PATH or under LXP_QUAL_TOOL_ROOT and exits with required qualification tool is unavailable: cbmc. docs/QUALIFICATION.md line 85 documents the requirement; no workflow installs the two tools and the public step the task adds would fail the same way on the hosted runner."
fix = "Decision 2862: a gate whose target reaches the arithmetic proof names cbmc and z3 the way Foundry gates name forge and anvil (decision 2859), the public step installs them with apt before the target, and the wiring test asserts the install step precedes the suite step. The verification of 22.39.76 names both binaries from this round; attempt 4 adds the apt step."

[gotcha.3551]
title = "Running the ethereum_jsonrpc suite from its application directory lacks the Mint adapter the umbrella configures, so every Tesla case fails before the task code"
symptom = "Task 22.39.97 attempt 1 at 3286fc0c29eb (base e7d1456b92) tagged the compiler cases, made the builder script exclude them when Node, solc and vyper are absent, repaired the throttle restart and the websocket lifecycle support, and passed the build and both Python tests; the verification then reported 18 ExUnit failures, 17 of them UndefinedFunctionError Tesla.Adapter.Mint.call/2 in the repair_22_33_436, 442, 443 and 445 cases. The verification of this task ran mix test inside services/explorer/backend/apps/ethereum_jsonrpc, whose mix.exs lists tesla and hackney but not mint, while the umbrella root mix.exs (lines 108 to 109) carries mint and apps/block_scout_web/config/config.exs line 95 sets the Tesla adapter to Mint for every application; Tesla compiles its Mint adapter only when mint is in the dependency set of the project that compiles it. The four earlier repairs qualified through services/explorer/deploy/tools/mix-in-builder.sh test apps/ethereum_jsonrpc/test/... from the backend root, where the set is the umbrella set. The eighteenth failure, ws-termination-envelope of Repair2233431Test, times out waiting for the eth_subscribe newHeads request after the lifecycle support change of this attempt."
fix = "Decision 2863: an explorer backend suite is verified through the builder script from the backend root, never through mix test inside one application directory. The verification of 22.39.97 takes that form from this round; attempt 2 keeps the tree and repairs the one lifecycle case."

[gotcha.3552]
title = "The recorded controls test persists version-one evidence beside the version-two record the authenticated ingress already stored, and the inventory refuses the legacy record"
symptom = "Task 22.33.50 attempt 8 at 6a0da097460a (base 1a48f8023d) applied the attempt-8 correction (the export and the stored level both COMMITTED) and the consensus case passed; the two transport cases failed at the checked helper (tests/repair_22_33_50.rs line 71) with ReceiptStoreError::EvidenceVersion from receipt::evidence_inventory (services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs line 525), called by retained_recording at line 315. persist_recording stores the committed receipt through store_verified_if_absent with the authenticated receipt, whose ingress (human_runtime.rs lines 1083 to 1101) calls persist_authenticated_receipt and writes the version-two transaction evidence under the public evidence key (receipt.rs line 779); the test then also calls receipt::persist_evidence with a RawReceiptEvidence (lines 250 to 266), the version-one path, which finds the version-two record at the public key and writes the legacy record under the legacy key (receipt.rs lines 424 to 428), and the inventory refuses any legacy record since 22.31.559 and any version-one public record since 22.33.1537 at dbd4e68ed9. The version-one call predates the committed ingress the attempt-7 ruling introduced."
fix = "Decision 2857: attempt 9 of 22.33.50 drops the version-one persistence from the test, reads the retained evidence through receipt::serve_evidence by transaction hash, and keeps every other assertion; nothing under services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src changes."

[gotcha.3553]
title = "Twenty-three qualification suite cases remain after the third settlement pass"
symptom = "Task 22.31.623 attempt 3 at 9b83f21f4914 (base fba11291a3) repaired the producers named by the attempt-3 ruling and settled 80 more cases: the first verification reported 103 failures of 4449 cases and the second 23 of 4462, with both repair units spent and the collect test of tests/ci never reached. The 23 remaining cases are the seven test_px_node_root_design cases (the seventeen-method inventory, the five px_getInference method contract cases and the three-group partition), test_repair_22_31_418 finding 31, test_repair_22_31_455 contracts/launchpad, test_repair_22_31_612 licence drift, test_repair_22_33_1231 finding 17, test_repair_22_33_1443 production method inventory, test_repair_22_33_29 evidence route, test_repair_22_33_626 finding 39, test_repair_22_33_634 OpenRPC introduction, test_repair_22_33_849 f066, test_repair_22_33_875 f008, test_repair_22_36_1 code specs dot directories, the three test_repair_22_36_2 cases (documentation tree and samples, node workspace entries and npm lock, pnpm importers), test_repair_22_33_877 f018 and the beta driver multichain inventory case."
fix = "Attempt 4 of 22.31.623 continues from the attempt-3 tree and settles the 23 named cases under the do_2 rules, then runs the whole verification once."

[gotcha.3554]
title = "The live-input guard repair pinned seven routed jobs to a fixed runner, and the routing check that the tools/ci suite runs refuses them"
symptom = "Task 22.39.54 attempt 6 at d1ba75e3c32a (base d52cc786f1) corrected the Foundry profile assertion as ruled, passed the build, and the verification reported 2 failed and 110 passed: tools/ci/tests/test_ci_loadtest_job.py line 66 and the routing subtest of test_replay_golden_ci.py both run scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh, which refuses routed job has a fixed runner: ubuntu-24.04 for human.yml build-lint-test and intent-fuzz and for platform.yml android-application-artifact, programs-acceptance, agent-sanitizers, agent-fuzz-corpus and release-promotion. Task 22.39.98 at 7008181d46 (landed 2026-11-07) replaced the routed runs-on expression of those seven jobs (the pull-request fork condition, vars.CI_LINUX_RUNNER, the ubuntu-24.04 fallback, the form ROUTED at scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh line 83 accepts) with the fixed label while guarding the live inputs; its own test asserts only the guards and its verification never ran the routing check, so the check has been red at main since that commit. The attempt stopped at the inherited failure as its ruling required."
fix = "Decision 2864: a workflow repair keeps the runs-on line of every routed job in the routed form and its verification runs the routing check when it edits a workflow. Task 22.39.147 restores the seven lines and adds the check to the live-input test file; 22.39.54 requires it and attempt 7 continues once it lands."

[gotcha.3555]
title = "The emulator route-absence test receives an InvalidRequest refusal from the token listing where it expects the InvalidResponse of the absent route"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 10 at e47769c1851256419a503fe4c1890f283112fe0e (base d52cc786f1) brought the three CLI RPC tests to the published contract and the root endpoint; the build passed, the library tests and the 94 lifecycle cases passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in one case of proof_cli_cli_commands: emulator_rpc_route_absence_is_a_negative_boundary at tests/proof_cli_cli_commands.rs line 77, where the token list step (token list with limit 1 against the emulator root) returned the envelope detail rpc_method_unavailable: wallet RPC failed: InvalidRequest while the test expects InvalidResponse, the variant the SDK returns for a non-200 answer. The attempt changed no source under src, so the refusal is in the base: the static readers of the asset page path (list_custody_assets_page of the SDK rpc module, its page decoder, call_bounded, the CLI read_asset and asset_read_error) show no InvalidRequest for a page request without a cursor and with limit 1, so the producing line is not pinned from the sources alone."
fix = "Attempt 11 localizes the refusal by exercising the token list step against the emulator in the task tree and records the producing line; a refusal the CLI raises before the transport is repaired in tools/platform/cli, a refusal inside the SDK is recorded with its line and stops the attempt for a producer task. The test assertions stay."

[gotcha.3556]
title = "A registered fee-token error wrapped with the percent-w verb of fmt.Errorf loses its ABCI code because the fork unwraps only through Cause"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 attempt 2 at 83c683f4987e3847d4a7d4c0d0727420743e17ab (base 1a48f8023d) brought the fee-token and CW1155 receipt tests to the producer contract; the build passed and the verification reported 15 of 17 cases passed. TestFeeTokenGigaBlockRefusesUnusableRate at node/app_feetoken_test.go line 202 expected codespace evm and received undefined with code 1 and the log internal error: modules/evm/keeper/params.go lines 323, 327 and 331 wrap ErrFeeTokenRateInvalid with fmt.Errorf and the percent-w verb, and sdk/types/errors/abci.go (abciCode and abciCodespace, lines 130 to 170) unwraps only through the Cause method of the causer interface, never through errors.Unwrap, so the registered code is invisible to sdkerrors.ABCIInfo and refuseGigaEVMTx in node/app.go reports the internal error. The keeper test TestFeeTokenRateErrorsCarryTheirCodeAndMessage in params_test.go asserts ABCIInfo only on the bare error and on an sdkerrors.Wrap of it, never on the value GetFeeTokenRate returns. TestEvmEventsForCw1155 at node/receipt_test.go line 837 expected status 0x0 for the burn-on-behalf message the recipient sends and received 0x1 with codespace undefined, the log internal error and 168948 of 300000 gas; the real error text is hidden by the same ABCI formatting and the fresh application fixture does not enable the trace that returns it."
fix = "Decision 2865: a registered error that reaches an ABCI result is wrapped with sdkerrors.Wrap or Wrapf, never with the percent-w verb, and the keeper test asserts the ABCI code through the producer function. Task 22.39.148 repairs params.go and its test; 22.39.138 requires it, and attempt 3 reads the CW1155 error through the trace option before any change."

[gotcha.3557]
title = "The retained settlement fixture writes a zero asset word where the exact fee debit requires the digest of the fee denomination"
symptom = "Task 22.39.128 attempt 6 at e49db43c7aa431bbb12c55ff717764a21acb7f95 (base d52cc786f1) passed the build and the nineteen integration tests, and the library retained_settlement_tests reported 0 passed and 4 failed: retained_settlement_settles_after_the_head_advances panicked at human_runtime.rs line 23586 with retained settlement: Refused, and the three sibling cases reported PoisonError because they share the static ENVIRONMENT mutex the first panic poisoned. The fixture (human_runtime.rs near line 23882) writes the reservation charge words with a zero 32-byte asset, while exact_fee_debit in approval/call_bound.rs (function at line 218, check at line 234) requires the first charge asset to equal the SHA-256 digest of the fee denomination bytes of the summary, usid, and returns DebitProofRequired otherwise, which the settlement reports as Refused. The attempt diagnosed the mismatch and stopped as instructed."
fix = "Attempt 7 writes the digest of the fee denomination usid as the charge asset word following call_bound.rs line 234; nothing else changes, and the three PoisonError cases follow once the first case passes."

[gotcha.3558]
title = "The Python x402 attempt ran from a main revision that predates the conformance digest derivation it depends on"
symptom = "Task 22.39.136 attempt 6 at 64215035d88ffcc9e8f5eb008f1a095363c35d44 (base 014174f743) passed the build (the root workspace install and the py_compile step) and the pay6 verification reported 20 passed and 1 failed: test_agent.py line 42, test_budget_receipt_commit_and_replay, where the produced proof differs from the recorded receipt of the fixture. The base 014174f743 does not contain 908d90b5c5, the commit of task 22.39.146 that derives the node fixture digest through the verifier (gotcha 3553); that commit reached main through acd8cd6831 after the attempt started, and the task tree is otherwise complete."
fix = "Attempt 7 merges current main and runs the verification once; no change in the task tree."

[gotcha.3559]
title = "The ramp toolkit submit test still expects the retired off-ramp success of the native receive preparation, and the first failing binary hid the later ones"
symptom = "Task 22.39.68 attempt 4 at 3a7e53ed604a8812edda6c4e7d5e3ff8168be317 (base d52cc786f1) moved the tracked certificate and key fixtures out of src, passed the key-material test and the hosted internal tests, and failed in the ramp toolkit tests: submit_prepared_sends_raw_transaction_once in services/platform/ramps/toolkit/tests/evm_submit.rs panicked at line 473 with prepare and authenticate transaction: PayerGrantRequired (3 passed, 1 failed). The off-ramp branch of that test asserts that prepare_native_receive with a mismatched payload returns PayerGrantRequired and then expects the same call with the matching payload to succeed, while prepare_payment in src/clients.rs lines 1067 to 1069 returns RampError::PayerGrantRequired for every off-ramp order since task 22.31.211 at 5febff359bf, so the second expectation has been stale since 2026-11-04. cargo test stops at the first failing test binary, and evm_submit was the last of the seventeen binaries, so the earlier sixteen passed while nothing later was exercised; a crate-wide gate that stops at the first binary leaves the other stale assertions unknown."
fix = "Decision 2866: a verification that runs every test binary of a crate passes --no-fail-fast so each binary reports. Task 22.39.149 settles the ramp toolkit test binaries against their producers; 22.39.68 requires it and attempt 5 continues once it lands."

[gotcha.3560]
title = "The arithmetic proof script resolves clang as well as cbmc and z3, and the core suite job installs only the latter two"
symptom = "Task 22.39.76 attempt 4 at 1ab4401a1dc7e419f0b75677eda2a3b80897f8c0 (gates at 241427cee6, base 014174f743) added the cbmc and z3 installation step before the core suite step of ci.yml (line 101) and the ordering assertion in tests/ci/test_core_test_all_wired.py; the build passed, forge, cbmc and z3 answered, both wiring tests and the four ported suites passed, and make core-test-all stopped at qualify-arith (Makefile line 1233): tools/lxp_arith_proof.sh resolves cbmc, z3 and clang in turn (lines 23 to 25, command -v or the qualification tool root under build/qualification/toolchain/root) and refused with required qualification tool is unavailable: clang, because the proof compiles the sanitizer builds with clang (lines 68 to 96, with the llvm-18 resource directory or the one clang reports). The verification opened with the three tools round 236 named and never with clang, and the only ci.yml job that installs clang is the C17 matrix job (line 88), not the core suite job."
fix = "Decision 2867: a gate that runs a proof or qualification script names every tool the script resolves, read from the script, and the workflow job installs the same set. The core suite job installs clang beside cbmc and z3, the wiring test asserts it, and the verification of 22.39.76 opens with clang --version; attempt 5 continues from the attempt-4 tree."

[gotcha.3561]
title = "Two rounds of guest reduction by technique saved eleven thousand bytes and left the ai-market guest sixteen thousand over the bound without a per-function size table"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 attempt 2 at 77bfba6a279be09fc90f7172b752ba9290e372d2 (base d52cc786f1) continued the attempt-1 tree with the shared typed field writer, the ordered destination reader, the streaming rewards-account derivation and the checkpointed replay state applied to the remaining modules: the build and every dependent check passed and the verification failed at the size assertion before the four f11 binaries ran, the packaged guest measuring 500894 bytes against the 484184 bound, 16710 over, after 511946 at the starting tree and 504844 after attempt 1. Both attempts chose their targets by reading the sources (271 Debug derives, no unwrap outside the test modules, seven asserts, two panics, one write, the SDK panic handler already the wasm32 unreachable trap) and never read the per-function sizes of the packaged artifact, so the record lists techniques per module with their bytes but not where the remaining half megabyte sits; the release profile already carries opt-level z, lto, one codegen unit, panic abort and strip, and the host boundary target already runs wasm-opt -Oz, so the ordinary profile levers are spent."
fix = "Decision 2868: a size reduction measures the packaged artifact with the per-function metrics of the packaging tool before and after and targets the largest functions, recording the table. Attempt 3 of 22.39.142 starts from the table, applies the two remaining structural techniques (no re-inlining of shared helpers, no formatting machinery outside the tests) and stops with the table recorded if the bound still is not met."

[gotcha.3562]
title = "The routing check the runs-on restoration added to its gate refuses thirteen fixed runners that five other repairs introduced"
symptom = "Task 22.39.147 attempt 1 at 94f1769f81b7be0ae0070751721ff5075a9ad9d8 (base b62e2aa496) restored the seven routed runs-on lines of human.yml and platform.yml, wrote the routed-form test and the record, and passed the build; the verification stopped at its second step, scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh, which refused thirteen jobs outside the task touches: in ci.yml the c17 job (task 22.39.3 at a6dc9b69de, which moved it to hosted Ubuntu because the routed host preloads a library and traces processes, breaking the sanitizer rules) and the seven js jobs js-suite-inventory, js-node-tests, js-npm-tests, js-workspace-tests, js-pnpm-tests, js-wallet-gateway-tests and js-explorer-env-tests (task 22.39.85 at b05c9aead5); explorer-backend-test in explorer-images.yml (task 22.31.605 at 20b07243e3); launchpad-test in launchpad-test.yml (task 22.39.10 at a14fa92845, ubuntu-latest); and tagged-tests, autobahn-integration and hpx-registry in paxeer-go-test.yml (task 22.39.82 at 2fe29c1246, ubuntu-latest). None of the thirteen declares a container or services block; the check exits 0 only when every job is routed or listed in its exclusion table with a reason class from REASONS (line 67), and the deliberate c17 pin has no entry there. The pytest step never ran."
fix = "The restoration settles every refusal the check reports in the same change: twelve jobs return to the routed form, the c17 job gets an exclusion entry with a sanitizer reason class added to REASONS, and a job whose commands match the container-runtime pattern of the check gets a docker-command entry; 22.39.147 touches the four workflows and the check script from this round and attempt 2 continues."

[gotcha.3563]
title = "The control case of the recorded controls repair refuses at the agent lookup because the agent it finalizes was never installed, and its helper still asserts the finalised level the producer does not store"
symptom = "Task 22.33.50 attempt 9 at 25a24db46b439d58676e672db44e5f371bfcffa8 (base b62e2aa496) removed the version-one evidence path as ruled, repaired the loopback peer to return the trace envelope production requires, passed the build and the dependent checks, and the verification reported 1 passed and 2 failed. finding12_recorded_paxd_receipt_transport_recovers_before_replay fails at tests/repair_22_33_50.rs line 473 inside assert_material, which asserts VerificationLevel CHECKPOINT_FINALISED while the material carries Committed: the same stale expectation the attempt-8 ruling corrected at line 294 (the retained export follows COMMITTED), left in the helper because that ruling named one line. finding12_control_transport_preserves_checkpoint_verification fails at line 574, where the loopback peer calls managed_agent::finalize_limit for agt_recorded_controls and asserts the generic HumanOperationError::Refused: the producer returns HumanOperationError::Typed(HumanRefusal::ManagedAgent(ManagedAgentCheck::AgentLookup)) because validate_finalization_source (managed_agent.rs line 2544) reaches the aggregate lookup for an agent no record of the case ever installed, so the refusal the case observes is a missing record, not the check its comment claims (a genuine committed payment must never authorize a budget change); with the agent present the producer continues into validate_projected_effect (line 2830), which first restores the owner outbox transaction of the activity and refuses with a typed ManagedAgent variant when the store holds none. The attempt recorded the conflict and stopped as instructed."
fix = "Decision 2870: a control case installs every record the production path reads before the check it asserts, and asserts the typed refusal the producer returns, never a generic one or a lookup failure. Attempt 10 installs the managed agent through publish_creation in the form of the install helper of the agent daemon repair test 22.33.1525, asserts the typed ManagedAgent refusal and records its variant, and corrects assert_material to the COMMITTED level the attempt-8 ruling already set."

[gotcha.3564]
title = "The emulator boundary test expects a hex decode refusal from a token list cursor the client SDK parses as a decimal registration cursor"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 11 at 281da58eedc4 (base 03eb3ce720) ran the localization round 238 asked for: the build passed, 24 library tests, the lifecycle suite and 55 of 56 command-boundary cases passed, and emulator_rpc_route_absence_is_a_negative_boundary failed at the refusal helper of tests/proof_cli_cli_commands.rs (line 77) during the loop at lines 399 to 415, which asserts that every malformed-argument refusal carries hex in its detail. The valid token list page step passes with InvalidResponse as the test expects; the failing step is token list --cursor bad id: since task 22.31.212 at e7bafe13a5 the CLI parses the cursor with registration_cursor of the client SDK (services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/src/rpc.rs line 1693), which treats it as a positive decimal integer and never as a hex asset identifier, refuses bad id with RpcError::InvalidRequest, and asset_read_error (tools/platform/cli/src/wallet.rs line 932) renders the refusal as rpc_method_unavailable: wallet RPC failed: InvalidRequest. The hex expectation predates that parser; the attempt recorded the producer line and stopped without a repair cycle as instructed."
fix = "Decision 2871: the SDK parser refusal is the contract and the consumer test asserts its variant; no producer task follows. Attempt 12 of 22.39.118 moves the cursor step out of the hex loop and asserts InvalidRequest, the five other steps keep hex."

[gotcha.3565]
title = "The Python mirror of the payment conformance fixture still derives the receipt digest as Keccak-256 after the TypeScript fixture moved to the verifier digest"
symptom = "Task 22.39.136 attempt 7 at 61093e3df534 (base bde55cd44e) merged main with the digest derivation of task 22.39.146 (908d90b5c5) and ran the gates: the build passed and the verification failed with 20 passed and 1 failed, test_budget_receipt_commit_and_replay at services/platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/test_agent.py line 42, which asserts the proof the node peer produces equals FIXTURE of test_commitment.py before any Python payment module runs. Task 22.39.146 derived receiptDigest of node-fixtures.mjs (line 17) through verifySequencerReceipt of the client SDK, the SHA-256 domain digest of the unsigned receipt encoding, and corrected test_http.py, but left test_commitment.py line 23, where FIXTURE still sets receiptDigest to the Keccak-256 of the signed receipt bytes, and test_agent.py line 50, which asserts the Keccak-256 of the same bytes against the digest the agent peer returns. The two Python files sit outside the declared touches of 22.39.136, so the attempt recorded the difference and stopped; the two local suites never ran."
fix = "Decision 2872: a conformance fixture repair covers every language mirror of the fixture set. Task 22.39.136 now touches the two Python conformance files; attempt 8 derives FIXTURE through the Python verifier and asserts the same digest at line 50."

[gotcha.3566]
title = "The crate-wide ramp toolkit gate runs a source settlement case that reads a protected contract file the qualification environment never carries"
symptom = "Task 22.39.149 attempt 1 at 2206b5ecde00 (base 03eb3ce720) repaired the off-ramp preparation and transport assertions of evm_submit.rs and, in its two repair cycles, the expiry, account hash, budget and draw assertions of the 0x101a proof test, and every binary of the crate-wide gate passed except tests/source_settlement.rs, where genuine_source_finality_binds_orders_and_claims_before_any_funded_transition (line 103) calls contract() at line 77, which reads the path in the LAYERX_RAMP_SOURCE_CONTRACT_FILE variable through SecretFile and panics with genuine finalized Ethereum and Solana source contract required when the variable is absent. The case verifies a genuine finalized Ethereum and Solana source contract that the evidence policy keeps in access-controlled storage; no public workflow runs the ramp toolkit tests, and the task text never named the exclusion, so both repair cycles went to the two real assertion differences and the gate still ended red on the protected case."
fix = "Decision 2873: a test that reads protected material through an environment variable is excluded by name from a crate-wide gate and the record names the exclusion and its reason. The verification of 22.39.149 carries the exclusion from this round; attempt 2 reruns the gates at the attempt-1 tree."

[gotcha.3567]
title = "The loadtest workflow test pins its job to the runner of the sanitizer job, which the routing repair deliberately leaves on the hosted runner"
symptom = "Task 22.39.147 attempt 2 at 06d1b91e2627 (base bde55cd44e) settled every refusal of the routing check as round 239 asked: eighteen jobs carry the routed expression, explorer-backend-test holds a docker-command exclusion for the mix-in builder and c17 the new sanitizer exclusion, tests/ci/test_workflow_runs_on_routed.py covers every disposition, the build and the routing check passed and the verification ended 29 passed, 1 failed: tools/ci/tests/test_ci_loadtest_job.py line 16 asserts that the loadtest job of ci.yml runs on the same runner as the c17 job. That assertion dates from task 16.4.5 (b27b4bd1c9), when both jobs sat on ubuntu-24.04 and c17 served as the hosted-runner reference; on main the loadtest job is routed and c17 is pinned for the sanitizer, so the test has been red since the routing landed and is red at the attempt tree for the same reason. The attempt left both the workflow and the test unchanged and recorded the conflict; tools/ci/tests sits outside the declared touches of the task."
fix = "Decision 2874: a workflow test that equates two jobs on runs-on names a sibling of the same routing disposition. Task 22.39.147 now touches the loadtest test; attempt 3 compares the loadtest job with repository-audit, the routed job whose first step the same test already uses as its reference."

[gotcha.3568]
title = "The CW1155 burn-on-behalf delivery answers an unregistered error the node response redacts, and tracing the base application cannot expose it"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 attempt 3 at 733e82e76991 (base d865171f50) merged the fee-token rate repair of 22.39.148, after which 16 of the 17 selected node tests pass, and passed baseapp.SetTrace(true) through the Setup options as round 238 asked; TestEvmEventsForCw1155 still fails at the burn-on-behalf step (node/receipt_test.go line 843) with codespace undefined, code 1, log internal error, gas 168948 of 300000. The attempt established why the trace shows nothing: node/abci.go lines 225 to 227 pass debug=false to sdkerrors.ResponseDeliverTxWithEvents on both error branches, and defaultErrEncoder (sdk/types/errors/abci.go lines 104 to 120) prints internal error for every error that is not a registered sdkerrors value; codespace undefined with code 1 is errInternal, the code ABCIInfo assigns to an error no registry knows, so the refusal is a plain Go error, not a contract refusal, which the wasm module would report in its own codespace. The response carried only the ante events, so replaying them through AddCosmosEventsToEVMReceiptIfApplicable (the attempt-3 diagnostic at line 838) returned nil and localized nothing; both repair cycles went to that diagnostic."
fix = "Decision 2875: when the delivery response redacts an error, the consumer test localizes it by re-running the message through the module keeper in a discarded cache context and passing the events that context emits through the receipt translator, reading both raw errors. Attempt 4 of 22.39.138 performs that localization and stops at the producer line."

[gotcha.3569]
title = "The recorded RPC server of the wallet repair tests still serves the retired /rpc path, which the node client refuses since the root endpoint became the contract"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 12 at 07484f057fd9 (base e0a89071ca) corrected the cursor step as round 241 asked and advanced the gate: the build passed, all 24 library tests and all 56 command-boundary cases passed, and make platform-test-tooling then failed in tests/repair_22_31_212.rs, where wallet_bind_rpc returns the error node RPC URL must name the root endpoint. The Server fixture of that file (line 30) publishes its endpoint as http://host/rpc and its request reader (line 55) asserts the request line POST /rpc; the four sibling tests of the file reach the hosted-service path of the client, which accepts any path, while wallet_bind_rpc binds through the node client, whose connect (tools/platform/cli/src/rpc.rs lines 47 to 49, task 22.33.1493 at c239354b90 under decision 2521) refuses every node URL whose path is not the root. The fixture predates the root-endpoint contract; the attempt stopped at the gate result without a repair cycle."
fix = "The fixture follows the contract (decision 2521): attempt 13 of 22.39.118 serves the fixture at the root path and asserts the request line POST /, so the node client and the hosted-service client both accept it, and the gate proceeds."

[gotcha.3570]
title = "The F11 family table test still asserts the pre-settlement payload bounds of the SettleLaps operation"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 attempt 3 at 4e3940dd51bf (base 02e58faceab) reduced the size-optimised guest to 483154 bytes, within the 484184 bound; the build passed and the verification failed in f11_family_table at tests/f11_family_table.rs line 191, where the selector table test expects the SettleLaps payload bounds (92, 92) while the operation table of the crate declares laps::SETTLE_FIXED_BYTES plus evidence::MANIFEST_FIXED_BYTES (480) and laps::SETTLE_FIXED_BYTES plus evidence::MAX_MANIFEST_BYTES (4190). Task 22.38.4 at 73d57e4523 changed those bounds with the lap settlement manifest and ran only its own test file, so the row of the family table test has been red at main since; every other F11 row matches the table, and the base tree fails the same way. The task touched only the crate sources, so the attempt could not correct the row."
fix = "Decision 2877: an operation payload-bounds change updates the family table test in the same change. The task now touches tests/f11_family_table.rs; attempt 4 corrects the SettleLaps row to the producer constants and reruns the gates once."

[gotcha.3571]
title = "The launchpad Go gate needs the fixture environment of its workflow job, and one database cancellation test fails under it"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 3 (final tree bc20b425e5cf, gate at c2a82f8b0c7e, base 142ee9c654) installed the Foundry toolchain, passed the build and the fifteen wiring tests, and make -C services/launchpad ci then failed in three places of sdk/launchpad/shared: auth TestRealEVMContractMagicAndRevocation refused because no local chain answered at the L34_ANVIL_URL address the job env names (the test skips only when the variable is unset), the delivery package refused the inherited non-fixture DELIVERY_TEST_DSN (delivery_test.go line 98, ordered_test.go line 124) and TestWebhookTargetsResumeIndependentlyPostgresTLS required the explicit private DSN (webhook_test.go line 40), and db/production TestPhase3CancellationAndAuthorization failed at production_test.go line 421 because a cancelled SQL connection was neither reusable nor discarded within one second. The workflow job of the attempt tree (.github/workflows/launchpad-test.yml lines 104 to 118 and 150 to 175) sets every DSN to the kindle_fixture role at 127.0.0.1 port 25432, the schema name, the chain URL, creates the kindle_test database and starts anvil on port 28545 with chain id 125 before the Go test step; the qualification environment ran the gate without that environment and the second verification was refused for budget."
fix = "Decision 2878: a Go test gate the public workflow runs under a job fixture environment is qualified under that same environment, and a module failure under it goes to the reviewed baseline with its reason. Attempt 4 reproduces the job environment, records the cancellation case in tests/ci/data/launchpad_go_test_baseline.json for retiring task 22.39.117, which owns the db/production package, and reruns the gates once."

[gotcha.3572]
title = "The control transport test compares the committed rung rank the producer carries with a verification level rank"
symptom = "Task 22.33.50 attempt 10 at 3db4141c19ba (base fae0d0941041) installed the managed agent, asserted VerificationLevel::COMMITTED in assert_material and the typed refusal HumanRefusal::ManagedAgent(ManagedAgentCheck::FinalizationEvidenceLookup) the producer returns for a committed payment receipt offered as a budget finalization (managed_agent.rs lines 2587 to 2594); the build passed, two of three cases passed and finding12_control_transport_preserves_checkpoint_verification failed at tests/repair_22_33_50.rs line 644, where the test compares consumed.verification with VerificationLevel::COMMITTED.wire_rank(), rank 6. The producer carries the rung rank in that field: the request closure of the same test asserts evidence.rung equals Rung::Committed.wire_rank(), FinalizationEvidence::from (managed_agent.rs lines 656 to 666) copies HumanFinalizationEvidence.rung into verification, and valid_finalization_shape (line 3214) requires Rung::Committed.wire_rank(), rank 2. The comment above the assertion claims the real consumer requires the verification level rank; the producer lines show the opposite. The attempt also recorded that receipt.rs lines 1301 to 1304 require a native commit key the authenticated transaction ingress and the retained payment recording never persist, so committed evidence lookups refuse before the receipt binding checks."
fix = "Decision 2857, gotcha 3046: the final assertion follows the producer and compares consumed.verification with Rung::Committed.wire_rank(); the comment states the producer fact. The native commit key requirement is recorded as an open finding of the agent domain, not repaired by this task."

[gotcha.3573]
title = "The Python payment RPC verifier lets a receipt decoding failure escape as an SDK error where the reference and the conformance case expect one verification failure"
symptom = "Task 22.39.137 attempt 1 at 73ee319e281b (base fae0d0941041) added HostedGatewayRpc with the origin separation of the TypeScript class and the pre-request decoding of PaymentRpc.send; the build passed, the first verification failed because a committed rung claim passed with a receipted commitment, the repair authenticated every committed result through rpc_committed_evidence, and the second verification failed one assertion later: in the change loop of services/platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/test_rpc.py line 65 a malformed receipt made verify_sequencer_receipt raise SequencerReceiptVerificationError (verifier.py line 366), which the attempt re-raises unchanged at x402_rpc.py lines 350 and 351 while the case asserts ValueError. The reference services/platform/middleware/seller/src/rpc.ts lines 151 to 155 catches every verifySequencerReceipt failure and throws MiddlewareError verification-failure; the Python entry maps every other PlatformSdkError to ValueError payment-binding-mismatch but exempts this one class. The local suite did not run; seven conformance cases passed."
fix = "Decision 2879: the Python mirror maps every SDK verification failure of the reference path to the error class and name the conformance case asserts. Attempt 2 removes the re-raise exemption and reruns the gates once."

[gotcha.3574]
title = "The CW721 pre-transfer owner lookup of the wasm keeper refuses every CW1155 burn as an internal error"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 attempt 4 at 1f95eb51246e (base 41090ab4d3) ran the localization of decision 2875: the burn-on-behalf payload executed through wasmKeeper.Execute in a discarded cache context returned the raw error required CW721 pretransfer owner lookup failed, contract pax18cs... token 1, Error parsing into type Cw1155QueryMsg, unknown variant owner_of (wasm/x/wasm/keeper/keeper.go line 755), so the refusal never reaches the receipt translation. The producer is emitCW721OwnerBeforeTransferIfApplicable (keeper.go lines 1179 to 1233, from task 22.31.184 at 6ae9e2abf8), called before Execute at line 424: it treats every transfer_nft, send_nft or burn message that carries token_id as a CW721 transfer and queries owner_of, and a CW1155 burn message (from, token_id, amount) takes the same path, the contract refuses the query, and the keeper returns ErrCW721OwnerLookup as an unregistered error that DeliverTx reports as undefined/1 internal error. Sixteen of seventeen selected node tests passed; only TestEvmEventsForCw1155 failed at receipt_test.go line 847 on status 0x1."
fix = "Decision 2880: the CW721 lookup classifies by the CW721 message shape, never by the action name alone. Task 22.39.150 repairs the keeper and tests both shapes; 22.39.138 requires it and attempt 5 removes the diagnostic once it lands."

[gotcha.3575]
title = "The README examples of the hosted px_ reads and account writes omit the explicit hosted URL option the CLI requires once --rpc names the node root"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 13 at 31157b57e4d8 (base 3dea4efda456) corrected the README of tools/platform/cli and its integration test to the root-path contract of decision 2521: CLI_RPC_URL is the hosted service origin at the root path, the loopback test server asserts POST at the root, a public root node URL is accepted and the retired rpc suffix is refused. Build exit 0 twice; the verification still failed two README tests at tests/repair_22_33_1499.rs line 72 (the successful helper): readme_retired_endpoint running the documented wallet balance example received the refusal gateway_rpc_required for hosted px_ balances, and readme_operator_contract running the documented token create example received the same refusal for hosted px_ account queries. Both refusals are the producer contract of task 22.33.1494 at 3f380f6199: src/wallet.rs lines 709 and 1025 send every hosted px_ read and every account query of a write through the URL of the --gateway-rpc option and refuse without it, while the README examples at lines 215 to 227 (token create, wallet open-account, token mint, token burn) and 320 to 324 (wallet balance twice, token info, token list) name only --rpc and --gateway-credential; only the wallet send and token transfer examples carry --gateway-rpc. The repair budget was spent before the attempt reached these examples."
fix = "Decision 2881: every README example that runs a hosted px_ read or an account query of a write carries the explicit hosted URL option the CLI requires, and the README states that --rpc names a node root while hosted methods go through that option. Attempt 14 of 22.39.118 adds the option to the eight examples and leaves the CLI sources unchanged."

[gotcha.3576]
title = "The F11 family table test still expects the roster-only section list for BookView after the placement book moved it to the policy and settlement sections"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 attempt 4 at 146d4fa84434 (base 5eec969fb07b) corrected the SettleLaps row of programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/tests/f11_family_table.rs to the producer constants and rebuilt the guest (483,154 bytes, 41,030 bytes of headroom); the build passed and the verification failed at the next assertion of the same test, line 235 of f11_selectors_route_to_their_operation_metadata, where the selector table expects BookView (0x0B14) to carry the section list IdentityRoster alone while the operation table declares PolicyLifecycle and SettlementClaims: task 22.38.11 at de71ebe300 made BookView a public read of the placement book kept per model digest, which lives in the policy lifecycle and settlement claims sections and touches no roster entry, and its own test file f11_placement_book.rs covers the read; the family table test was written at 22.38.4 and never followed. The attempt recorded the mismatch and left it unchanged under the round-245 note, which limited the repair to the SettleLaps row."
fix = "Decision 2882: the family table test asserts the section list of each selector as the operation table declares it, and the roster-everywhere invariant holds only for operations that act for a roster member, never for a public read of a per-model book. Attempt 5 of 22.39.142 corrects the BookView row and the invariant under decision 2857, and the narrowing of the round-245 note yields."

[gotcha.3577]
title = "The read operations test asserts the retired pending freshness marker for the receipt proof bundle after the agent api encoding gave every freshness a block coordinate"
symptom = "Task 9.98.4 attempt 12 at 53bcaadeeacf (base 09d9ec823cd8) merged current main onto the attempt-11 tree, kept the paymentDenom fixtures, and passed the build and the twelve unit targets; its first verification failed in tests/program_adapters_rungs.rs at the store directory the test created twice, which the one repair removed, and the second verification failed only read_proof_bundle_operation_returns_receipt_proof_v2 at tests/read_ops_rpc.rs line 201: the test expects the freshness field relative_to of the receipt proof bundle to be the string pending while the response carries the block coordinate object with the hash of the 0x09 block and the height 150. The producer is task 21.29.1 at 4a365a3015: proof_bundle_operation_value in src/human_runtime.rs encodes the verified read through VerifiedRead::encode_json of the agent api crate, whose freshness encoding (layerx-agent-api src/read.rs line 1028) always writes relative_to as the object with height and hash, and the pending string of task 9.5.6 remains only in the ordinary_read helper of the human runtime for the reads that helper answers. The read operations test has been red at main for that case since 4a365a3015 and the verification of 9.98.4 runs the whole file."
fix = "Attempt 13 of 9.98.4 corrects the assertion to the block coordinate object the agent api encodes (height 150 as a decimal string and the hash of the 0x09 block as the hex string) and records it with the producer line, under decisions 2762, 2800 and 2857; nothing in the daemon sources changes for it."

[gotcha.3578]
title = "The primary platform build job is gated behind the quickstart benchmark registry variables, so it never runs in a repository without a private registry"
symptom = "Task 22.39.78 attempt 2 at 9ef4fa446c98 (base 5810900680) rebased the middleware suite wiring onto main, passed the build and failed its wiring test at tests/ci/test_platform_middleware_suites_wired.py line 32, which asserts that the build-lint-test job of .github/workflows/platform.yml carries no job-level condition: task 22.39.98 at 7008181d46 moved the two registry variables LAYERX_TEN_LINE_REGISTRY_SNAPSHOT and LAYERX_TEN_LINE_REGISTRY_URL from the workflow environment into the job environment and gave the whole job a presence condition on them, because its guard test tests/ci/test_workflow_live_inputs_guarded.py requires a job-level presence guard on every automatic job that references a variable or secret anywhere outside the exact routed runs-on form. Only one of the twenty-seven steps of that job reads the registry: the quickstart benchmark step runs tools/paxeer-x/gates/104.16.5.sh, whose verify function requires the snapshot or the URL (line 241). Every other step (the beta contract check, the workspace build, the platform tests, the conformance runs, the CLI end-to-end run, the middleware build, the reference applications, the documentation site) needs neither, so on every push and pull request of a repository without the registry variables the primary build, lint and test job of the platform workflow is skipped, and the decision-3052 class of a red public workflow is reached silently."
fix = "Decision 2883: a primary automatic job never carries a job-level condition on an input that a single step reads; that step carries the presence condition and the guard test accepts a step-level guard. Task 22.39.151 removes the job condition, guards the benchmark step and its upload step, and extends the guard test; 22.39.78 requires it."

[gotcha.3579]
title = "The public qualification ledger carries twenty-one severity words and twelve free-form section names where the beta ledger check admits four severities and three section grammars"
symptom = "Task 22.39.87 attempt 1 at 8141143a2ae5 (base 61b1cd9c81) normalised spec/layerx-merge/qualification.kvx as instructed: 456 repeated headers gained the .a2 suffix, the two strings with an unescaped interior quote were repaired, the checker admits the attempt suffix, the three parse tests exist and the deselection file is empty; the build passed and test_beta_ledger_check_passes failed with 3,412 violations the normalisation did not cover: 3,398 finding records carry a severity outside the vocabulary of scripts/ci/beta-ledger-check.sh (blocker, suspect, assumption or note since the ledger tools of 16.5.1 at 8d93db30a8), among them 767 medium, 747 low, 700 high, 590 major, 293 minor, 141 cross-task, 81 owner, 33 task, 15 blocking, 10 cross_task, 9 environment, 7 critical and single-digit task-scoped, spec, pre-existing, needs-ruling and advisory; ten sections carry a non-numeric suffix or a kind the grammar does not know (finding.17.3.4.attempt1 to attempt3, repair.22.37.30, finding.22.31.615.measurement and gateway-dependent, observation.22.31.622.snapshot, finding.22.31.622.dependency_gate, attempt_2_facilitator and attempt_3_snapshot_gate); finding.22.31.620.2 and .3 lack the symbol key; finding.17.0.1.1 and its .a2 copy carry an empty observed string. The 700 high values come from the finding records the engineering process has written for every continue and requalify note since round one, whose default severity word was high; the rest come from attempt records written in free form. The attempt preserved them under the do_1 instruction to keep every key unchanged."
fix = "Decision 2884: the four-word severity vocabulary and the three section grammars of the beta ledger check are the contract of the public ledger; every existing record is mapped onto them by meaning and every new record is written in them. The default severity of the finding records written at each round is blocker from this round. Attempt 2 of 22.39.87 applies the mapping and the grammar repairs on top of the attempt-1 tree."

[gotcha.3580]
title = "The README integration test of the CLI asserts a parser refusal and an absent verification marker where the producer refuses in the handler and marks hosted balances"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 14 at 27007fa945cf (base 61b1cd9c81) added the explicit hosted URL option to the eight README examples as round 247 ruled; the build passed and make platform-test-tooling failed two cases of tools/platform/cli/tests/repair_22_33_1499.rs. readme_retired_endpoint asserts at line 397 that the hosted balance read carries no verification field, while wallet.rs line 720 has set verification to unverified_node_observation for every hosted balance read outside the emulator since task 22.31.212 at e7bafe13a5. readme_operator_contract asserts at its end that running the documented wallet send without --evm-key-file is refused with the parser placeholder --evm-key-file <EVM_KEY_FILE>, while main.rs declares the option optional and the refusal is the handler text provide --evm-key-file from wallet derive --export-private-keys at wallet.rs line 1504 (task 8.48.1 at a3d452df16), raised before any request reaches the recorded server. The attempt stopped as instructed."
fix = "Decisions 2857 and 2885: attempt 15 corrects both assertions to the producer text, states the verification marker in the README balance paragraph, and leaves everything under src unchanged."

[gotcha.3581]
title = "The protected source contract exclusion ruled for one ramp toolkit gate was not carried into the sibling gate that runs the same binaries"
symptom = "Task 22.39.68 attempt 5 at d2643125cac1 (base 0afb3102d0) merged main after 22.39.149 landed, kept all eleven certificate and key moves, and passed the hosted internal and key-material gates; the ramp toolkit run failed only genuine_source_finality_binds_orders_and_claims_before_any_funded_transition at services/platform/ramps/toolkit/tests/source_settlement.rs line 78, which panics when the LAYERX_RAMP_SOURCE_CONTRACT_FILE variable names no protected genuine source contract (5c53fe2876). Round 237 (gotcha 3566, decision 2873) excluded that case by name from the gate of 22.39.149 and the record services/platform/ramps/toolkit/tests/repair_22_39_149.kvx names the gap, but the gate of 22.39.68 runs the same binaries with only the three earlier exclusions, so a case already ruled a protected-material gap failed the sibling task."
fix = "Decision 2886: a by-name exclusion ruled for a protected-material case carries into every gate that runs the same test binary, recorded as a gap each time. The gate of 22.39.68 excludes the case from this round; attempt 6 continues from the attempt-5 tree and records the gap."

[gotcha.3582]
title = "The Makefile repair of the tools/ci wiring dropped the two explicit tests/ci paths the settled wave-six test still requires and shares the ledger failure of 22.39.87"
symptom = "Task 22.39.47 attempt 2 at dac8a1270116 (base 61b1cd9c81) wired tools/ci/tests and the two shell suites into test-tests-python, wrote tests/ci/test_tools_ci_suites_collected.py and the record, and failed two cases: tools/ci/tests/test_makefile_wave6.py test_aggregates_dry_run_clean at line 118 requires the pytest line of the target to name tests/ci/test_real_node_build_ownership.py and tests/ci/test_runner_routing_container_runtime.py explicitly (settled by 22.39.54 at 2c0db3df4c after the task text was written), while do_3 of the task told the attempt to drop those two explicit paths as duplicates; and tools/ci/tests/test_beta_ledger_paths.py test_ledger_check_reads_layerx_merge_ledger fails on the public qualification ledger severities that task 22.39.87 (wave 2) maps under decision 2884. The gate of 22.39.47 runs the whole tools/ci/tests directory, so it depended on 22.39.87 without naming it, and the task sat in wave 1."
fix = "Decisions 2800 and 2857: the landed wave-six settlement governs the Makefile line, so the two explicit paths stay and tools/ci/tests is added; pytest ignores a path given twice unless asked to keep duplicates, so the explicit paths are no defect. 22.39.47 now requires 22.39.87 and sits in wave 3; attempt 3 continues once 22.39.87 lands."

[gotcha.3583]
title = "The intentional-copy inventory still lists the twelve launchpad and perps source asset copies the rename task removed"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 attempt 5 at f01c678451d5 (base 21e8032a6f) passed its build and all seventeen selected node tests, then failed the python step of its gate: seven of the nine cases of tests/ci/test_copied_artifacts_in_sync.py refuse at line 72 with Missing intentional artifact for apps/launchpad/web/src/assets/icons/airdrop_background.png. Task 22.39.62 at a2bf776a9f wrote tests/ci/data/intentional_copies.txt with ninety-one rows, twelve of them pairing the launchpad public icons with copies under apps/launchpad/web/src/assets/icons and apps/perps/src/assets; task 22.39.61 at 637c9c63da then gave every asset one copy and removed those twelve source copies (apps/launchpad/web/asset-renames.kvx lines 226 to 251 record the removals, and both asset index files already point at the public paths), but its gate ran only test_frontend_asset_names.py and the two app builds, so the inventory went stale at main and the sync test has been red since 637c9c63da landed."
fix = "Decision 2887: an asset move updates the intentional-copy inventory in the same change and its gate runs the sync test. Task 22.39.152 removes the twelve stale rows and records the reconciliation; attempt 6 of 22.39.138 continues without the foreign test in its gate."

[gotcha.3584]
title = "The gate of the node selection task carried the sync test of the copy inventory task since its creation"
symptom = "Task 22.39.138 was written in the same round as 22.39.62 and received the tests key and the trailing python step of that task: tests names tests/ci/test_copied_artifacts_in_sync.py and verify_cmd ends with python3 -m pytest -q on that file after the go test selection, although no do item of 22.39.138 names the inventory and every ledger record of the task files its findings under that test name. The python step only ran once the seventeen node tests passed at attempt 5, which is why four attempts never exposed it."
fix = "Round 251 corrects the gate of 22.39.138 to the go test selection alone and its tests key to the node test files it repairs; the ledger records keep their filed names."

[gotcha.3585]
title = "The shared-budget capacity test of the rooms binary fills one model with twice the open bids the placement book admits"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 attempt 5 at 81922d66a65c (base 3f300e10cc) brought the guest to 483154 bytes under the 484184 bound, corrected the BookView row and the roster assertion of f11_family_table.rs as round 248 ruled, passed the build, the family table, the canary and the module mirror checks, and failed one case of tests/f11_rooms_and_deals.rs: all_room_ask_and_bid_capacities_fit_together_in_the_shared_state_budget posts BID_CAPACITY (128) bids into room digest(100) and the sixty-fifth PostBid refuses with CAPACITY. Every room of that test carries the model digest digest(50), and since task 22.38.11 at de71ebe300 the placement book of src/placement.rs keeps at most SIDE_CAPACITY (64) open asks and 64 open bids per model digest, refusing the next placement at line 90; the gate of 22.38.11 ran only f11_placement_book, so the test of 22.38.3 has been red at main since de71ebe300 landed. The attempt diagnosed the mismatch in both producers at its base, recorded it and stopped, as its do_3 forbids changing a test."
fix = "Decision 2888 (owner ruling, flagged): the per-model side cap of the placement book governs alongside the aggregate room book, and the capacity test spreads its bids over two model digests. Task 22.39.153 settles the test; attempt 6 of 22.39.142 continues once it lands."

[gotcha.3586]
title = "The receipt store tests submit raw evidence to an ingress that has refused everything but the authenticated capability since the medium audit repair"
symptom = "Task 9.98.4 attempt 13 at fc2cdfba14aa (base 58b52ce384) corrected the freshness assertion of tests/read_ops_rpc.rs as round 248 ruled; the build and the twelve selected unit tests passed, read_ops_rpc passed, and the gate then failed both cases of services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/receipt_store_v2.rs: receipt_evidence_round_trips_by_transaction_hash panics at line 120 with store receipt UnauthenticatedIngress and version_one_receipt_evidence_is_refused at line 339 receives receipt.unauthenticated_ingress where it expects receipt.evidence_version. Both cases build TransactionReceiptEvidence through the record helper and pass it to store_verified_if_absent directly, as task 9.4.2 wrote them at a284d6993d; since task 22.33.1513 at bfc86ded84 the raw evidence ingress of src/receipt.rs (lines 953 to 967) returns BelowReceipted for a submitted rung and UnauthenticatedIngress for every other, and only AuthenticatedTransactionReceipt::from_authenticated over the verified receipt of the node verifier (lines 57 to 66) persists through persist_transaction_evidence. The gate of 22.33.1513 ran only its own binary, and the gate of 9.98.4 runs its test binaries in name order and stops at the first failing one, so receipt_store_v2 never ran in attempts 1 to 12 while read_ops_rpc, which sorts before it, was failing."
fix = "Decisions 2857, 2866 and 2889: attempt 14 builds the stored evidence of both cases through the authenticated capability the way tests/repair_22_33_1513.rs does, keeps the refusal assertions the raw ingress still satisfies, and the gate of 9.98.4 passes --no-fail-fast so every binary reports."

[gotcha.3587]
title = "A shared test-data directory touch holds the whole baseline family behind any one live task of it"
symptom = "Twenty-six open tasks (22.31.623, 22.39.40, 22.39.59, 22.39.68, 22.39.75, 22.39.84, 22.39.92, 22.39.94, 22.39.102, 22.39.103, 22.39.112, 22.39.113, 22.39.116, 22.39.117, 22.39.119, 22.39.120, 22.39.124 to 22.39.127, 22.39.131 to 22.39.134, 22.39.144 and 22.39.145) declare tests/ci/data, tests/ci or .github/workflows as a directory touch, so while one of them is in progress every other is held back by the touch rule: at 01:49Z on 2026-11-08 the queue reported 21 eligible tasks held behind 22.39.75 attempt 4 alone, although the files they write never meet (22.39.75 attempt 3 at bc20b425e5cf changed only tests/ci/data/launchpad_go_test_baseline.json and tests/ci/data/launchpad_go_tests.py under that directory, and each other task writes its own baseline file). Two tasks were live at 01:51Z with 86 pending."
fix = "Decision 2890: touches name the files a task edits; a file the task creates goes to planned_paths; a shared directory entry is retired. This round narrows the touches of twenty-four tasks and extends the planned paths of five (22.39.102 keeps .github/workflows because it edits every workflow; 22.39.92 keeps tests/ci/data until the data file it creates exists, since a touch must name an existing path)."

[gotcha.3588]
title = "The CLI readme test asserts a transport error for a retired path the client constructor already refuses"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 15 at 8b84628f5540 (base 2c237932ad29) moved the fixture server, the connect helper and the README to the root transport and brought the hosted verification and the faucet endpoint assertions to the producers; verification 1 at 103e46115bdf failed at tests/repair_22_33_1499.rs line 74 and the attempt repaired it, verification 2 at the final revision failed at line 89 (the refused helper) for the assertion at lines 411 to 427: the wallet watch run against the retired path (the public root plus rpc) expects InvalidRequest, while RpcClient::new refuses the URL at src/rpc.rs lines 47 to 49 with node RPC URL must name the root endpoint before any request, exactly the text the assertion at lines 361 to 366 of the same test already expects. 2 passed, 1 failed; both repair cycles were spent."
fix = "Decision 2891 extends 2871 and 2885 to a command run against a retired path: the expected text is the constructor refusal and the request count stays unchanged. Attempt 16 of 22.39.118 continues from the attempt-15 tree with that one assertion changed."

[gotcha.3589]
title = "The budget proof vector was extended by hand without its generator, and the durable-write repair was not attempted"
symptom = "Task 22.39.122 attempt 2 at 5d5c4a51b325 (base 79b47a737349) rebased the attempt-1 tree onto the current main and ran the library suite once: 330 passed, 3 failed. budget_proof_v2_node_answers_fixture_is_current compares the committed tests/vectors/budget-proof-v2/node-answers.json (252 lines) against the answers generated_answers in the test module of src/budget/budget_proof.rs produces (219 lines): commit ba761d6c5d of task 22.31.540 appended three eth_call answers to the committed vector (getEvmAddrByLayerX and getUnifiedAccount against the address precompile at 0x1004 and accountOwner against the ledger at 0x101a, each at height 0x8, the reads the owner authentication of 22.33.1520 performs) for the human service replay without extending the generator, which last changed at c88f78b406; attempt 1 at base e4c5b9476591 predates that commit and passed the case. The two session_control durable-write cases (admit_write_with_a_failed_durable_write_releases_its_hold at line 3537 and submit_rewrite_with_a_failed_durable_write_leaves_the_limiter_as_it_was at line 3637, both asserting that the removed store root stays absent after the failed write) failed at attempt 1 as well; the attempt-2 note asked for their repair in session_control.rs, but the attempt made no repair and left no closing message after one verification run."
fix = "Decision 2892: a committed vector another test regenerates follows its generator; a change that appends answers extends the generator in the same change, and a consumer that meets the drift extends the generator to the committed bytes. Attempt 3 of 22.39.122 extends generated_answers (budget_proof.rs now in touches) and performs the durable-write repair with the recreating re-open named."

[gotcha.3590]
title = "The launchpad Go job never names the test services the API module documents and its test target stops at the first failing module"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 4 at f11cfdbbeabc (base 9b2c85fd7c52) reproduced the job environment as instructed: both SDK modules passed under the baseline (three protocol entries recorded with retiring task 22.39.117, which touches only sdk/launchpad/shared), and the api service module failed in five packages for causes the job never provides. Some forty tests of app, cache, rest and store stop at CORE_API_TEST_POSTGRES_URL is not set, at CORE_API_TEST_REDIS_URL, at CORE_API_TEST_NATS_URL or at the allocated real PostgreSQL, Redis and lane namespace the cache tests require, because services/launchpad/api/internal/internaltest/containers.go lines 1 to 9 document those variables as the already running servers the tests use, while the env block of .github/workflows/launchpad-test.yml lines 104 to 118 defines none of them although the job runs postgres:16 and redis:7 and installs nats-server; two broker stream tests read L11_POSTGRES_DSN, also undefined, and time out after 180 s at postgres_stream_test.go lines 198 and 297; two authority tests read contracts/launchpad/artifacts/contracts/base/BeaconProxy.sol/BeaconProxy.json, a compile output no job step produces; and two tests are stale consumers, TestDevelopmentTransactionStatusFromChainRPC (dev_network_reads_test.go line 279) and TestRepair_27_log_free_receipts (repair_27_test.go line 240) still expect the log-free receipt refusal ErrReceiptPosition that sdk/launchpad/shared/chain/client.go line 1123 marks deprecated since repair 26 of the shared chain package, which projects valid log-free receipts through the shared v2 receipt projection. The test target of services/launchpad/Makefile line 74 exits at the first failing module, so the fourteen modules after api never ran."
fix = "Decision 2893 and task 22.39.154: attempt 5 of 22.39.75 gives the job the three CORE_API_TEST variables and L11_POSTGRES_DSN from its own fixtures, starts the NATS server it installs, compiles the launchpad contracts before the Go test step, reproduces that environment in the qualification environment and records only tests that still fail under it; 22.39.154 follows the shared projection in the two log-free receipt tests and retires their entries; 22.39.117 gains sdk/launchpad/protocol."

[gotcha.3591]
title = "The copy inventory task removed the twelve named rows and the sync test reported a thirteenth stale row and three unlisted pairs"
symptom = "Task 22.39.152 attempt 1 at e5efb803e2b4 (base 8f21858e00): build exit 0, verification exit 1 with 7 passed and 2 failed. test_other_intentional_copies_match_sources fails at the first row of tests/ci/data/intentional_copies.txt because commit 637c9c63da of task 22.39.61, the same commit that removed the twelve copies, replaced apps/perps/src/styles/.scss/base.css with a one-line import of apps/explorer/.scss/base.css, so the bytes no longer match; test_no_unlisted_byte_identical_copies_over_20kb reports three byte-identical pairs over 20000 bytes without a row: precompiles/layerxpay/abi.json (2026-10-12) with services/wallet/attestor/internal/policy/evm/abi/layerxpay.json (added 2026-10-26, outside the ATTESTOR_ABIS names of the attestor test), tools/bringup/tests/fixtures/repair_m793/committed.json (2026-11-04) with services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/tests/fixtures/repair_22_33_50/conformance-v4-committed.json (2026-11-08), and services/platform/hosted/gateway/tests/fixtures/repair_22_31_202/node-committed.json (2026-11-04) with the repair_22_33_50 fixture paxd-v4-committed.json (2026-11-08). The attempt recorded the twelve removals and stopped."
fix = "Decision 2894: attempt 2 of 22.39.152 removes the stylesheet row with the same commit recorded and adds the three rows, the older file as source, with the bytes comparison, test_other_intentional_copies_match_sources and the purpose; the test file and the artifacts stay unchanged."

[gotcha.3592]
title = "The agent SDK suite task names the package test directory while the tests it repairs live in the central tree"
symptom = "Task 22.39.119 attempt 1 at base 8f21858e00 made no change: its touches name services/agent/sdk/python/tests, but the seventeen test files its do_1 lists live in tests/agent/sdk/python since commit ec75ccbc59 of task 22.99.42 (2026-11-03), every one of the 95 nodeids of tests/ci/data/agent_sdk_python_baseline.json starts with tests/agent/sdk/python, and the build and verification commands of the task collect only services/agent/sdk/python/tests, whose conftest applies the baseline to both trees only when that directory is collected. Task 22.39.120 carries the same touches and the same commands for its five payment test files, which also live in the central tree. Task 22.39.73 ran both trees together."
fix = "Decision 2895: both tasks touch the central test files they repair, the SDK package and the baseline file, and their gates collect the central tree together with services/agent/sdk/python/tests so the baseline conftest loads; 22.39.119 relaunches with those paths."

[gotcha.3593]
title = "The tools Python suites fail in seven families once wired, five of them for toolchains and build outputs the job never provided"
symptom = "Task 22.39.84 attempt 2 at 1f802c791b33 (base 8f21858e00) wired thirteen suite directories into make test-tools-python and a tools-python job of ci.yml, the four wiring tests passed, and the suite run finished with 117 failed, 689 passed, 10 skipped, 44 deselected and 14 errors in 896 seconds. Five families are configuration gaps of the job and of the qualification: the load test suite under tools/benchmark (26 failures, 3 errors) runs build/loadtest, which make build-loadtest produces, and asks forge for its binding checks; the rehearsal genesis tests of tools/release (5 errors) link the native library that make build/liblayerx.a produces; the signing rewind tests of tools/release (6) call zstd; the container tests (7) call docker build --check, which needs the buildx component; the bringup tests (6 failures, 1 error) call bringup-inspect, which tools/bringup/tests/foundation-artifacts.py line 203 builds from tools/bringup/cmd/bringup-inspect, read the loader tools/bringup/tests/xweb-loader/target/debug/bringup-xweb-config-loader (or XWEB_CONFIG_LOADER) and probe localhost over ssh, as does the inputs phase case of the release check test module; the job installed openssh-server and never started it. Two families are consumer drift: the jev suites (24 failures of test_failures.py because the five log fixtures its lines 37 to 42 name were never committed under the root ignore rule for *.log, six of test_docs.py and five of test_repair_22_33_705.py because README.md gained five headings and lost the curl --max-time 10 line the expected lists carry, two of test_ledger.py and one of test_pr.py because the fake answers carry no probability distribution and the Cargo.lock anchors point at moved lines, three lockfile anchor cases of test_repair_22_33_705.py), the release suites (test_repair_22_33_889.py six cases and test_upgrade_info.py one case assert the paxeer-network/v7.0.0 tag that tools/release/version.json declares while the release check module line 18 still declares v6.12.0 and snapshot.sh line 253 names a pre-v6.12.0 archive, test_programme.py expects the v6.12.0 upgrade name and a spot share ABI golden the precompile left behind, the local chain class of the release check test module builds with a hard-coded /usr/local/go/bin/go at line 717, its market phase case expects a POOL_COUNT refusal and meets PRODUCTION_REQUIRES_ROLLBACK_RECEIPT, test_repair_22_33_893.py copies a tree without version.json), the container scope tests (four tracked recipes without a scope entry: the two rosetta node recipes under sdk/contrib/rosetta/node and two recipes of the vendored tree; test_kernel_init.py finds no scheduled role in docker/kernel/init.sh; the image check trips over Dockerfile string literals in services/platform/hosted/tests/beta_runtime.go), the two generator tests of tools/docs/gen (the precompiles page now opens with a preserve note instead of the generated-by header and the generator exits non-zero on the fixture directory) and test_go_root_checksums.py (go list -mod=readonly -deps -test exits 1 in the nested module tools/paxctl). The attempt recorded its findings only in the output spool path and wrote no repair record or baseline entry."
fix = "Decision 2896: the job and the qualification provide every toolchain, service and build output the suites document before the run, and baseline entries are written only under that complete environment. Attempt 3 of 22.39.84 adds the Foundry, zstd, buildx, native library, load test, bringup inspector, xweb loader and local ssh steps, records the drift families in tests/ci/data/tools_python_suite_baseline.json against the retiring tasks 22.39.156 to 22.39.160 this round creates, and writes tests/ci/repair_22_39_84.kvx."

[gotcha.3594]
title = "The wallet write tests of the platform CLI pass only --rpc while the write path reads the source account through the hosted px_ client since the audit repair"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 16 at f081b1c8ccf8 (base 8f21858e00) corrected the readme_retired_endpoint assertion, the 24 library tests passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in tools/platform/cli/tests/wallet_evm_writes.rs: wallet_send_submits_raw_evm_transaction (line 683), wallet_send_reports_receipted_revert (line 862) and wallet_send_refuses_mismatched_account_reads_before_submission (line 795) receive the refusal gateway_rpc_required: provide --gateway-rpc for hosted px_ account queries, and token_writes_never_call_lx_methods (line 633) expects the checksummed address text in the eth_getTransactionCount parameters where the command sends the lowercase hexadecimal form. Since 3f380f6199 (the audit record 22.30.89 repair of tools/platform/cli/src, 2026-11-05) the write path of wallet.rs (lines 1023 to 1030) reads the source account, the destination and the asset account through sdk_rpc at the explicit hosted URL of --gateway-rpc, as decision 2521 requires until the node root serves the px_ family, and the WalletFixture command (lines 596 to 606) passes --rpc to its recording server only; the attempt-16 source changes (the inference room methods in rpc.rs and the root endpoint in two library tests) are not the cause."
fix = "Decision 2897: a CLI test that drives hosted px_ account reads passes --gateway-rpc with the recording server address and asserts the refusal text the hosted client returns through rpc_error. Attempt 17 of 22.39.118 adds the flag to the fixture command, follows the producer in the four assertions, records each with the producer line, and changes nothing under src."

[gotcha.3595]
title = "Three node package tests outside the activation and standby release paths fail on main for the replication TLS requirement and the custody consensus version"
symptom = "Task 22.39.40 attempt 5 at fb5eda5a2e03 (base 8f21858e00) merged the 22.39.138 repair as instructed; the build passed and go test ./node/ with the three recorded names skipped failed in three tests that no earlier attempt met because the sixteen tests of 22.39.138 failed first: TestEVMServerServesSequencerReceiptOption (node/sequencer_rpc_option_test.go line 165) dials its standby without replication TLS and NewReplicator refuses with replication TLS configuration is required (node/sequencer/dial.go line 87), TestStandbyReplicatesRecorderGroupsThroughOpenAccount (node/standby_recorder_replication_test.go line 127) starts a standby whose configuration carries no ReplicationTLS and StartStandby refuses with replication TLS certificate, key, roots and peer identity are required (dial.go line 30); both requirements came with 26d76c1236 (the audit record 22.30.51 repair of node/sequencer, 2026-11-04), and Repair103TLSFixture in node/sequencer/replication_tls_test.go builds the configurations the replication tests of that package use. TestV640ToV66UpgradeServesTheExchangeBridgeAndLaunchpadPrecompiles (node/upgrade_test.go line 218) expects module version 1 for layerxcustody after the v6.6 plan while modules/layerxcustody/module.go line 122 declares consensus version 2 since e3d6107cb9 (task 21.89.1). The attempt recorded the three in node/repair_22_39_40.kvx and stopped without a repair cycle, as its attempt-5 note instructed; the chained standby and Python checks did not run."
fix = "Retiring task 22.39.155 brings the three tests to their producers. Attempt 6 of 22.39.40 records the three names in tests/ci/data/node_go_test_baseline.json against 22.39.155 under decision 2820, extends the skip pattern of the node test step and of its verification with them, and runs the whole gate once."

[gotcha.3596]
title = "The copy inventory reconciliation repaired the stylesheet rows one failing pair at a time and ran out of repair cycles with two rows left"
symptom = "Task 22.39.152 attempt 2 at 722ed1a6cbfc (base ad045b706f) removed the base.css row and added the three unlisted pairs as instructed, then met the next differing pair at each verification: the perps stylesheets under apps/perps/src/styles/.scss became imports of the explorer stylesheets at 637c9c63da (task 22.39.61), so the attempt removed six more rows as removed.13 to removed.18 across its two repair cycles and the second verification still failed on apps/perps/public/static/charting_library/charting_library.d.ts. One pass over the 76 rows of the attempt-2 inventory against main shows exactly two rows left: apps/launchpad/web/public/charting_library/charting_library.d.ts became a 116-byte re-export of the perps copy at 637c9c63da, and apps/launchpad/web/public/icons/logo.svg (38350 bytes) and apps/perps/public/assets/logo.svg (1626439 bytes) are different artworks since the same commit. The sync test stops at the first differing pair, so each cycle exposed one row."
fix = "Decision 2898: an inventory reconciliation compares every row of the inventory against the tree in one pass before its first edit and repairs all differing rows together. Attempt 3 of 22.39.152 removes the two remaining rows as removed.19 and removed.20 with commit 637c9c63da and runs the verification once."

[gotcha.3597]
title = "The agent SDK payment suite repair ran under the earlier task text and wrote its corrected tests into the retired test tree"
symptom = "Task 22.39.120 attempt 1 at 424d36488609 (base 96e76c855e2e) launched under the task text before round 255 pointed the task at tests/agent/sdk/python (gotcha 3592): it wrote full copies of test_ai_market.py, test_web_search.py, test_x402.py, test_repair_22_33_16.py and test_repair_22_33_702.py with its corrections, plus payment_receipt_evidence.py, test_receipt_fixture.py and an __init__.py, under services/agent/sdk/python/tests, deleted 245 lines of tests/ci/data/agent_sdk_python_baseline.json, and changed the producer web_search.py of layerx_sdk (a ledger_rpc parameter beside payer_rpc, the payer read from the decoded payment transaction instead of ledger_payment_payer) with its .pyi. After two repair cycles five cases still failed: the four web-search cases and the search payer address case of test_repair_22_33_702.py record an eth_call to the address precompile 0x101a that the replay server never answers (rpc_errors at test_web_search.py line 256) and the HTTP replay returns 500."
fix = "Attempt 2 of 22.39.120 continues under the current text: the layerx_sdk changes stand where the record names the x402 producer line they follow, the copies under services/agent/sdk/python/tests are deleted, the corrections move into the five files of touches under tests/agent/sdk/python, the replay server answers the address precompile read as the ledger does (decision 2855), and the baseline keeps the entries of 22.39.119."

[gotcha.3598]
title = "The scripts/ci exclusion row of the Python suite runner went stale when the last test beneath it was deleted"
symptom = "Task 22.39.131 attempt 1 at 199d2c9c2940 (base f3d4455deff4) repaired the copy checker, the module registry and the daemon admission suites, deleted their three baseline entries and wrote tests/conformance/repair_22_39_131.kvx; collection passed and the verification failed before any suite ran, at tests/ci/test_python_suites_have_runner.py line 275 (test_exclusion_list_entries_exist): the row scripts/ci of tests/ci/data/python_suite_exclusions.txt (line 23) is no tracked test root or file, because 995a25e5af (task 22.39.47, 2026-11-08 01:23Z) deleted scripts/ci/test_repair_22_31_317.py, the only Python test beneath that directory, and left the row. The attempt recorded the row as out of scope and stopped. The four pending tasks 22.39.131 to 22.39.134 run the same gate and none of them touched the exclusion list."
fix = "Attempt 2 of 22.39.131 removes the row and records the commit; the exclusion list joins the touches of the four tasks, and 22.39.132 to 22.39.134 carry the same removal for the case the row is still present when they start."

[gotcha.3599]
title = "The two failed durable-write tests of the agent daemon assert an absent store root that the tenant authorization audit sink recreates"
symptom = "Task 22.39.122 attempt 3 at 9391a017048e (base 3615c117190f) extended generated_answers so the committed budget vector test passes and the four retained settlement cases passed on the merged main; the library suite ended with 331 passed and 2 failed: session_control::tests::admit_write_with_a_failed_durable_write_releases_its_hold (session_control.rs line 3537) and submit_rewrite_with_a_failed_durable_write_leaves_the_limiter_as_it_was (line 3637) remove the store root to force the durable-write refusal, receive Unavailable with every hold released and the store key absent as asserted, and then fail the final assertion that the root no longer exists. The attempt recorded the chain: OperationPermit::resolve_at (session_control.rs line 2588) and SessionControl::resolve_credential (line 362) call tenant::resolve, TenantObservability::record (tenant.rs lines 500 and 537) flushes the authentication outcome through flush_to (line 392), and audit Log::open (audit/log.rs line 159) creates the tenant-authorization audit directory under the root with create_dir_all before the admission reaches its durable write. The sink has written under the root since bfc86ded84 (the audit record 22.30.91 repair of the daemon sources, 2026-11-05); the two assertions predate it. The attempt stopped at the boundary its note set and left the tests as they were."
fix = "Decision 2899: a test that removes a store root to force a durable-write failure asserts the absence of the artifacts the refused write would have created, not of the root, wherever an audit sink of the daemon records the refusal under that root. Attempt 4 of 22.39.122 follows the producer in the two assertions and records the producer lines."

[gotcha.3600]
title = "The ai-market crate suite fails in eighteen targets after the attempt and main both reshaped its codecs, and no main baseline was recorded"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 26 at c7bbaef169b0 (base 41b3da3118e0, which carries the guest size rewrite 075a770edb of task 22.39.142) brought the guest to 483167 bytes and the Fund operation under the CPU fuel cap after two build cycles, then the crate suite ran once: 49 targets, 411 passed, 129 failed in 18 targets (artifact_binding 13, f03_evaluator_admission 10, f03_evaluator_host 17, f04_canonical 1, f04_windows 17, f05_aggregation_runtime 20, fuel_budget 1, host_boundary 4, market_protocol_boundary 4, proof_ai_market_guest 1, repair_22_31_253 1, repair_22_33_217 1, reputation_lifecycle 4, rewards_native 2, roster_transition 14, task_admission_boundary 1, task_state_boundary 17 and the participant lifecycle target 1). The refusal codes name three families (the Debug form prints the wire code): BAD_VERSION (0x0001) where a semantic refusal is expected (task_state_boundary.rs line 1713 expects WRONG_EPOCH, market_protocol_boundary.rs line 1447 expects F01_OBLIGATIONS_OUTSTANDING, rewards_native.rs lines 1149 and 2197 expect WRONG_PHASE), so the requests those tests encode are refused at the envelope before the operation runs; NON_CANONICAL where CAPACITY or BAD_VERSION is expected (f04_canonical.rs line 394, the manifest grammar case at line 607 of the participant lifecycle target), and the attempt itself made that change in src/codec.rs, whose reveal decoder now returns NON_CANONICAL for oversized input where main returned CAPACITY and whose report decoders take their refusal pair as parameters; UNAUTHORIZED where the F07 unknown participant refusal (0x0704) is expected on selector 0x0702 (host_boundary.rs line 1017) with a written count of 0 instead of 1. Further failures are value mismatches: proof_ai_market_guest.rs line 350 (evidence rank 0 instead of 4), repair_22_31_253.rs line 912 (every availability entry Available), repair_22_33_260.rs line 531 (three reputation cases compare a different public key) and reputation_lifecycle.rs line 2106 (coverage 6 instead of 7). The guest size rewrite 075a770edb changed 36 source files and was qualified by four f11 targets and the module mirror test only, and the attempt-24 note that asked for one suite run on the unchanged merged main before any change produced no recorded list, so the share of these failures that main already carries is unknown. The attempt wrote the sweep record with result repaired although the verification failed."
fix = "Decision 2900: a task that rewrites production sources of a crate runs the whole crate suite before and after its change and records both failing lists; no name may fail after that passed before. Attempt 27 of 22.99.77 starts with the recorded main baseline, restores the refusal codes the attempt changed, and repairs the families against the frozen error sets of decision 2800."

[gotcha.3601]
title = "Five qualification suite cases remain and four of them pin consumer copies that their producers moved past, while the fifth is the human API schema check failing on main"
symptom = "Task 22.31.623 attempt 4 at fd32601f860e (base 8f21858e0002) settled 17 more cases and ended with 5 failed and 4445 passed. test_repair_22_33_19 (line 63) pins the local SDK test modules and the tree now carries test_x402_rpc_surface.py, added at a7d39f7f68 by task 22.39.137 on 2026-11-08, which the record does not list. test_repair_22_33_626 finding 39 (line 323) compares the recorded transcript sdk/integrations/agents/test/fixtures/daemon-submission-transcript.json (last written 00a533e508, 2026-11-04) with the submission transcript constant of the agent RPC operation table source of the daemon, which 3831896949 and 2d40d3e17c changed on 2026-11-07 (COMMITTED everywhere, the middleware transcript case); the committed receipt differs. test_repair_22_33_849 runs the owner tools/paxeer-x/gates/receipt_refusals.py, which requires the V3 copy sdk/platform/conformance/fixtures/vector-v3-receipt-refusals.json to name the source sdk/platform/conformance/fixtures/sequencer-receipt-v1.json and the producer rpc/sequencer_receipt_vectors_test.go in its provenance and to carry the six V3 cases of that source; on main the copy still names a retired daemon committed-fixture producer and predates 21e7fad723 (task 22.31.491, 2026-11-05) which added a committed preexecution refusal, so the drift exists on main and the 22 lines the attempt added to the producer test did not regenerate the copy. test_repair_22_36_1 (line 133) walks the snapshot inventory ebcb190287 of the vendored tree and finds one dot-directory configuration file missing under tools/, because the root ignore file line 135 ignores that dot directory by name everywhere and the move 0bb8393cc6 (task 22.36.1) could not carry it. test_beta_driver multichain inventory (line 323) requires the human API schema check to exit 0 and it exits 1 on main: 27 golden scalar values (challenge_id, confirms, step_up_evidence) keep a 26-character base-32 form while identity.kvx line 51 declares chg_ followed by 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters and opd_ followed by 64, the form the service mints in auth/mod.rs line 1967 from 16 entropy bytes; five golden directories (current, historical-decode, historical, negative, producer, added at b2dac8a13d and b23bb5871e by tasks 22.33.29 and 22.33.30) belong to no declared operation (lib.rs line 2322 of the schema check); and baseline.kvx (last written 7c4892fa49, 2026-11-04) reports breaking-declaration-change against agents.kvx, program-approvals.kvx, intent.kvx and journeys.kvx, whose declarations 7e32286b9a (task 22.31.384) moved step_up_evidence from EvidenceId to StepUpChallengeId and whose module texts changed, without a --write-baseline pass. No public workflow runs the schema check; the qualification suite is the only gate that does."
fix = "Decision 2903 and task 22.39.161 own the human API schema check (goldens to the declared formats, the five golden sets placed under declared operations or moved out, the baseline re-blessed with every breaking change recorded). Task 22.31.623 now requires 22.39.161; attempt 5 settles the four consumer copies against their producers and restores the vendored file with a negation line in the ignore file."

[gotcha.3602]
title = "The launchpad indexer module fails under the Go job for three distinct reasons that the baseline cannot hold in one list"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 5 at f5b177749477 (base ad045b706f73) ran the wiring tests (21 passed) and make -C services/launchpad ci; 42 packages passed and the indexer module failed in nine packages: thirteen cases name a missing service variable (INDEXER_TEST_POSTGRES_URL in source and store, INDEXER_TEST_REDIS_URL in publisher, L06_POSTGRES_DSN in store), which the Go job can provide from the PostgreSQL and Redis services it already runs; eleven cases fail with receipt qualification rejected from internal/receipt/qualified.go line 25 (app render_test.go line 111 and repair_55_test.go lines 384 and 628, config repair_m999_test.go line 304, decode repair_m995_test.go line 254, runtimedocs paxeer_test.go lines 112, 260, 308 and 330, source repair_56_test.go lines 115 and 191), so the recorded receipts those tests carry no longer qualify under the current receipt rule; the httpapi case TestRepairM_996_NoCompatibilityDeadLetterEscape panics at publisher.go line 136 because publisher.New refuses the retired compatibility webhook delivery the test still constructs; three cases need bound fixture state (chainreader TestActualNFTOwnerRemainsPinnedAfterTwoTransfers waits 180 seconds for an actual mined transaction, source TestSourceCapacityCandidate wants a bound owned source capacity configuration, source TestHistoricalRealRangeExplorerSuffixAndParity compares a real log range); and the processor package does not build because repair_m1000_test.go (81ce5e05f9, 2026-11-04) imports github.com/elliots/go-pglite, which services/launchpad/indexer/go.mod does not require, while the source package prints that go.mod needs an update for modernc.org/sqlite. A package that fails to build is not reached by the per-package skip pattern, so the module manifest has to be repaired before any baseline entry can carry the rest."
fix = "Decision 2901 separates the three kinds. Attempt 6 of 22.39.75 adds the four service variables to the job env block and the qualification environment, tidies the indexer module manifest, and records the receipt, panic and fixture-bound cases in the baseline with the retiring task 22.39.162, which brings the indexer module to green."

[gotcha.3603]
title = "The launchpad web suite needs the Foundry binary and the chain fixture inputs its own generators produce, and the public job never runs them"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 1 at 535cb99c795a (base 6a1f86168db9) mocked the wallet reads the task named (the 15 wallet_read_failed cases pass) and the web suite still ended with 23 failed and 1239 passed in 15 files: three files throw anvil binary unavailable (set ANVIL_BIN or PATH) from src/core/test-anvil.ts, and the rest refuse to run without generated inputs (L25 requires an owned loopback Anvil port, L28_CHAIN_FIXTURE_JSON must select a funded private deployment, the owned creation fixture, the phase2 and phase4 inputs, the bound actual chain125 deployment fixture, the joined configuration fields); the repository carries the generators (run-l25-check.py under core/wallet-sdk/test-fixtures, run-creation-chain.py under widgets/create, run-phase2.py and run-phase4.py under widgets/trading/transaction-controls, connected-chain-inputs.mjs under widgets/meta-ag) and documents them in apps/launchpad/qualification/account-ui/README.md, but the web job of .github/workflows/launchpad-test.yml installs Node and runs vitest only, and the last completed run of that workflow on main (2026-11-07) fails in the web, mobile and three SDK package jobs. Three further failures are not fixture bound: repair-22-33-901 (three cases) fails at deployment-generation.cjs line 36 with Reviewed deployment manifest mismatch, so the reviewed deployment record no longer matches the source manifest digest; breakpoints.test.ts line 40 expects the 2xl variant that tokens.css line 359 declares at 90rem and the compiled rule carries no media query; and revision-projection.test.ts is a node:test module that the vitest include glob collects and reports as no test suite found."
fix = "Decision 2902: the web job and the qualification environment install Foundry and run the fixture generators in their documented order before vitest. Attempt 2 of 22.39.95 wires that into the job, reproduces it before its own verification and repairs the three non-fixture failures against their producers."

[gotcha.3604]
title = "The ramp suites repair ran under the text that predates the stale exclusion row ruling and stopped on that row"
symptom = "Task 22.39.134 attempt 1 at eac6fce0c1f6 (base 1ef04160d147) repaired the ramp dependency policy and ramp journey suites and removed both baseline entries; the build passed and the verification failed in the one case round 256 described: test_exclusion_list_entries_exist refuses the scripts/ci row of tests/ci/data/python_suite_exclusions.txt that 995a25e5af left behind. The attempt started at 02:57Z, before the round that added do_3 to the task landed, so its text did not yet carry the instruction to remove the row."
fix = "Attempt 2 of 22.39.134 keeps the attempt-1 tree, merges main, removes the row if 22.39.131 has not landed it, and runs both gates once."

[gotcha.3605]
title = "The key fixture move deleted the PEM and PKCS12 fixtures that the root ignore patterns kept out of the tree, and two test targets stopped compiling on main"
symptom = "Task 22.39.93 attempt 1 at 70fb314c8d (published 2026-11-08) moved the key fixtures of the agent SDK crate and of the ramps reference crate into tests/fixtures directories and its verification passed on the on-disk tree, but the root .gitignore ignores *.pem (line 73) and *.p12 (line 75), so the moved copies services/platform/ramps/reference/tests/fixtures/repair_fixtures/localhost.pem, localhost.p12 beside it and services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/tests/fixtures/repair_22_31_227_fixture/ca.pem were never tracked while the same commit deleted the three source copies. On main the ramps reference test target repair_22_33_1487 (lines 37 and 38 include the two files) no longer compiles, the agent SDK audit support (tests/support/audit_22_30_99.rs line 2033) reads a ca.pem that is absent, and tests/ci/data/key_material_fixture_paths.json still lists the retired src paths. Task 22.38.6 attempt 2 at 842c354bb012 (base 3a0f70d0fc) built the ai-market guest and then failed the dependents check (32 crates, exit 101, the ramps reference crate among them) before its verification ran, for this reason alone."
fix = "Decision 2904 and task 22.39.163: restore the three files byte for byte from the history blobs of the parent of 70fb314c8d under their tests/fixtures paths, add one negation line per file to the root .gitignore, prove tracking with git ls-files, and refresh the fixture path list and its test; 22.38.6 requires 22.39.163 and attempt 3 continues from the attempt-2 tree. An attempt whose dependents check fails only at the ramps reference test target before 22.39.163 lands is relaunched unchanged after it."

[gotcha.3606]
title = "The CLI hosted-read test asserts a balance read without the required --gateway-rpc flag and a token.list kind the producer never prints"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 17 at 0001759ad503 (base 3a0f70d0fc) passed the lib rpc tests and failed make platform-test-tooling in tools/platform/cli/tests/wallet_px_reads.rs: wallet_balance_reads_px_get_balances (line 236) passes only --rpc and expects a hosted px_getBalances read, while wallet.rs line 710 refuses hosted balances without --gateway-rpc since task 22.33.1494 (3f380f6199, 2026-11-05); token_list_reads_px_list_assets (line 296) expects the kind token.list for the list command, while run_token routes the info and the list command through read_asset, which prints the kind token.read (wallet.rs line 929) since task 8.48.3 (9456895dab). The test module was written by task 22.33.1497 the same day, sits in no baseline, and the tooling gate has been red on main since then; the attempt recorded both cases as pre-existing and stopped."
fix = "Attempt 18 of 22.39.118 corrects both assertions to the producer contract under decision 2857 and records them with the producer lines; nothing under tools/platform/cli/src changes."

[gotcha.3607]
title = "The Python payment suites of the SDK package drift from the hosted gateway client, the committed-evidence requirement and the current payment binding, and the attempt changed the conftest outside its paths"
symptom = "Task 22.39.120 attempt 2 at 8173d0a942f1 (base 3a0f70d0fc) removed the twenty baseline entries it retired and left six failures in services/agent/sdk/python/tests: test_ai_market_commit.py line 430 calls receipt_keys on PaymentRpc, which task 22.39.137 (a7d39f7f68, in the base) moved to HostedGatewayRpc (x402_rpc.py line 233) under decision 2521; test_x402_http_sequencer.py expects a committed receipt to verify without finality evidence while verify_rpc_payment raises missing-committed-evidence (x402_rpc.py line 360) for a committed rung without the two-part finality since the same task; the two test_sequencer_receipt.py cases fail with payment binding payer mismatch (x402.py line 65) against a recording made before 18880543d1 ported the verifier to the TypeScript wire; the two test_x402_rpc_surface.py cases start the node peer, which cannot find @noble/hashes because the build step never ran the root workspace install (decision 2856). The attempt also changed services/agent/sdk/python/tests/conftest.py, which do_3 asked for and the touches did not list, so the publication was refused for scope."
fix = "The touches now include services/agent/sdk/python/tests and the build step starts with the root workspace install; attempt 3 continues and corrects the six cases to the producer contract (decisions 2857 and 2901): the hosted client for receipt keys, finality evidence in the committed fixture, a recording regenerated with the current binding, and the peer with its dependencies."

[gotcha.3608]
title = "The native-effect signature change left thirteen callers behind, four of them in a test file outside the task paths"
symptom = "Task 9.35.19 attempt 9 at ed9425eba451 (base 67b4aa3287) changed the argument lists and result types of the native-effect preparation functions as the task asks and ran three builds that each exited 101 with E0061 and E0308 at the callers it did not migrate: nine sites in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs (lines 5868, 8244, 8256, 8263, 8273, 8465, 8477, 8484 and 8494 at the attempt revision), a file inside the paths, and four in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_217.rs (lines 1876, 2026, 2029 and 2481, the matches_prepared calls), a file outside the paths; the verification never ran."
fix = "The touches now include tests/repair_22_31_217.rs; attempt 10 continues from the attempt-9 tree, migrates every caller to the new signatures (the consumer follows the producer, decision 2771), records each site, and builds once."

[gotcha.3609]
title = "The tools Python target runs thirteen suites but its baseline families cover six, so fifteen inherited failures of the release, bringup and benchmark suites stopped the wiring task"
symptom = "Task 22.39.84 attempt 3 at 581f4166326e (verified at 068cca699aa8, base 3a0f70d0fc) passed its build and the four wiring tests, and make test-tools-python reported 79 failures and 7 errors against 736 passes in 814 seconds. The attempt recorded 66 failing cases in tests/ci/data/tools_python_suite_baseline.json under the six retiring tasks the wiring test permits (22.39.144 for tools/paxeer-x, 22.39.156 for tools/jev, 22.39.157 for a prefix list of tools/release, 22.39.158 for tools/containers, 22.39.159 for tools/docs/gen and 22.39.160 for tools/deps) and stopped under decision 2896 at fifteen names no family covers: the five rewind refusal cases of tools/release/tests/test_repair_22_31_331.py (lines 132, 179 and 206 expect post-halt signing, fresh consensus identities and different consensus chain identity refusals and receive rollback: no snapshot for the validator), eight bringup cases (test_repair_22_31_319.py lines 44, 213, 565 and 770: nginx absent from the qualification environment, the hosts file variable unset for the search front render, the xweb render refusing shared transports, the kernel identity probe answers; test_bringup_fixtures_retired.py line 39, test_spec_paths.py line 26 with docs-names refusing README.md as an unpublished public name, test_xweb_config.py line 38 with the loader refusing a placeholder peer list) and two benchmark cases (the MyNFT mint parameter named tokenId in the artifact and id in the binding at test_sources_match_bindings.py line 60; a statistics tuple differing in the sixth decimal at test_repair_22_31_431.py line 103). Twenty-four of the jev failures and the six release check failures that open /usr/local/go/bin/go (the release check test module line 717) sit inside permitted families already."
fix = "Decision 2905 and task 22.39.164: the families cover every suite the target runs, the release family widens to all of tools/release/tests and tools/release/rehearsal under 22.39.157, and the bringup and benchmark suites get 22.39.164 as their retiring task, which also provides nginx in the tools-python job; attempt 4 of 22.39.84 adds the fifteen entries and reruns once."

[gotcha.3610]
title = "The signer deadline test of the hosted node asserts wall-clock margins that the full Python suite run misses"
symptom = "Task 22.39.132 attempt 1 at 26ad9e4f4845 (verified at f0867e7ba859, base 3a0f70d0fc) implemented the public-key reader and passed its 29 focused tests, and make test-python-suites failed one case of 255: services/platform/hosted/node/signer/test_repair_22_33_1454.py test_signer_deadline_spans_provider_operations configures a 0.45 second public-key delay and a 0.6 second sign delay against a 0.9 second server deadline and asserts at line 219 that a sign call was recorded before the busy refusal; under the load of the full suite (318 seconds) the deadline fired before the public-key step returned, so no sign call existed. The module passed in no earlier full run because none had run it; the attempt left the module untouched as out of scope."
fix = "Attempt 2 of 22.39.132 records the module in tests/ci/data/python_suite_baseline.txt with 22.39.133 as the retiring task and reruns once; 22.39.133 makes the deadline test deterministic (a controllable clock or ordering-only assertions) and removes the entry."

[gotcha.3611]
title = "The node merge-test task repaired its restart test after the one verification and could not retire the baseline entries its paths did not include"
symptom = "Task 22.39.116 attempt 1 at c8f1f9e1cf2a (verified at e26283413c3a, base f4da299f15 plus the qualified node-runtime work) brought TestMergePlanReturnsGuarantorBonds and TestHostedKernelProgramsABIFollowsTheMergeUpgrade to a pass and removed the skip pattern from the node test step of .github/workflows/node-build.yml, but TestHostedKernelProgramsABISurvivesRestart failed at node/upgrades_merge_programs_abi_test.go line 269 because its new setup finalized height 42 on a chain whose next height was 1 (ProcessBlock panic: invalid height: 42; expected: 1); the attempt repaired the setup to commit the preceding blocks and schedule the merge at height 42, then the verification step refused a second run because three builds and two repair cycles were spent. The do_2 instruction to delete the three entries of tests/ci/data/node_go_test_baseline.json could not be followed because the touches did not list that file."
fix = "The touches of 22.39.116 now include the baseline file; attempt 2 continues from the attempt-1 tree, deletes the three entries, and runs the build once and the verification once."

[gotcha.3612]
title = "The durable-write failure tests of the daemon were told to expect one audit sink directory while the tenant observability flush opens two"
symptom = "Task 22.39.122 attempt 4 at 545af8953d2a (verified at 919231dd61d2, base f4da299f15) followed the round-257 instruction literally: the two session_control tests admit_write_with_a_failed_durable_write_releases_its_hold and submit_rewrite_with_a_failed_durable_write_leaves_the_limiter_as_it_was now assert the inventory under the store root after the refusal, and both failed at session_control.rs line 3530 because the inventory holds tenant-authorization and tenant-traces while the instruction named tenant-authorization alone. The producer TenantObservability::flush_to (tenant.rs line 392) opens both sinks through audit Log::open, the authorization log at line 395 and the trace log at line 430, since bfc86ded84; the instruction was read from the first sink only. 331 of 333 library tests passed; the attempt recorded the contradiction and stopped, as it should."
fix = "Decision 2907: an inventory a test must assert is listed from every sink the producer opens at the revision, never from the first one found; attempt 5 of 22.39.122 asserts both directories and nothing else under the root."

[gotcha.3613]
title = "The explorer receipt vector copy the conformance checker compares sat outside the task touches, so every copy-check case reported its drift first"
symptom = "Task 22.39.131 attempt 2 at f13f810b7948 (verified at 456110947bf3, base 26703a14fd) removed the stale scripts/ci exclusion row as instructed; the five inventory tests passed and make test-python-suites reported 22 failures in tests/conformance/test_repair_22_33_886.py with one cause: services/explorer/backend/apps/explorer/test/support/fixture/paxeer_x/committed_vectors.json still pins the producer digest fc3fe1494c91 while the re-recorded producer 74ef78b42b and the SDK and interop copies pin 5013cd232ee9, so the checker reports that file first (17 regex assertions and 3 list assertions see the explorer line instead of the drift they planted) and the real RPC transport case feeds the stale explorer recording to HostedGatewayRpc.status, which refuses the receipt as invalid-transaction-receipt at x402_rpc.py line 148 because the recorded transaction hash is the old one. The previous continuation told the attempt to refresh that copy and left the file outside touches; the attempt recorded the contradiction and stopped without its repair cycle."
fix = "Decision 2906 applied to the file this round: the explorer copy joins the touches of 22.39.131 and attempt 3 regenerates it through refresh_explorer_copy at tests/conformance/check_receipt_vector_copies.py line 200."

[gotcha.3614]
title = "Four more node sequencer package tests fail once the six named failures are repaired: a wall-clock latency bound, a standby lease renewal, a renewal at the expiry instant and an evmone library the repository never tracks"
symptom = "Task 22.39.86 attempt 1 at b4feb369d1cd (verified at f6629b5bd988, base f4da299f15) repaired the six tests gotcha 3441 names; go test over node/sequencer then failed four others: TestReceiptLatencyP99UnderBound (receipt_latency_test.go line 221, p99 bucket 100 ms against the strict 50 ms bound, maximum 146 ms for 500 transfers over a real replicator in the loaded qualification environment), TestDriverReleasesNextOpenAcrossStandbyCommit (commit_release_test.go line 264, the primary log holds eleven entries and the standby ten, the extra one an epoch-one lease renewal the lease holder released while the test ran), the signed_receipt_survives_restart_and_failover case of TestProofSequencerWal (proof_sequencer_wal_test.go line 219 renews at holder.Expiry() and lease_renew.go line 24 fences any renewal not strictly before the expiry) and TestSealBatchEqualsGigaProcessBlock (seal_giga_test.go line 49: GigaEvmKeeper.EvmoneVM is nil because engine/executor/lib/evmlib.go line 21 loads libevmone.0.12.0_linux_amd64.so from the package directory, the file matches the .gitignore line 16 pattern, was never tracked, and no make target builds it). The public node-build check runs ./node/... so the same four are red on main."
fix = "Decision 2908: the package gate owner owns the four; decision 2909 and task 22.39.165 provide the evmone library through a make target built from the pinned upstream source; attempt 2 of 22.39.86 follows the producers for the other three."

[gotcha.3615]
title = "The platform tooling gate runs the emulator test that drives the TypeScript SDK, so the CLI read-kind task needs the root workspace install too"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 18 at a047230ba6a1 (verified at 4fa9f049aafd, base 23e48352d6) made the wallet read tests follow the hosted gateway client and the CLI read kinds as instructed; the CLI build and every CLI test passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in the emulator target repair_22_31_200 at line 121 because the real middleware path imports the TypeScript SDK and Node cannot find @noble/hashes: the verification exercises the Node workspace packages and the build step of this task never ran the root workspace install decision 2856 requires."
fix = "The build step of 22.39.118 runs npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund at the repository root before the cargo build; the next attempt continues from the attempt-18 tree."

[gotcha.3616]
title = "The ai-market crate task failed its dependents check on the dropped ramps key fixtures before its own suite ran"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 27 at 83bfb74875a2 (base 09673a24d2) built, then the dependents check compiled the consumers of the ai-market crate and failed in the layerx-reference-ramp test repair_22_33_1487 (lines 37 and 38 include localhost.pem and localhost.p12, the key fixtures 70fb314c8d dropped, gotcha 3605) before the verification ran; task 22.39.163 restored them (merged at 2b1c74ac68) after the attempt began. The crate suite of the task was not exercised at this revision."
fix = "Decision 2904: 22.99.77 requires 22.39.163 and attempt 28 relaunches the attempt-27 tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3617]
title = "The v6.6 upgrade test rebuilt a retired module inside the application manager and then called the exchange ABI at an address the current contract set serves to the perpetuals contract"
symptom = "Task 22.39.155 attempt 1 at f40645593a30 (verified at 880ac81a4998 then f40645593a30, base 23e48352d6) gave both standby replication tests mutual TLS fixtures and retired the three baseline entries; both replication tests passed. TestV640ToV66UpgradeServesTheExchangeBridgeAndLaunchpadPrecompiles then failed at node/upgrade_test.go line 226 because the version map after the v6.6 plan carries no layerxanchor entry: node/app.go line 1169 builds the module manager without the anchor module and line 1314 registers only its services, and activationModulesPresent at node/upgrades.go line 769 skips the anchor by design. The attempt answered by moving the test into package app and registering the real anchor module into a.mm.Modules before applying the plan, which reconstructs an inventory the producer retired; the second verification then failed at line 246 because the view of layerxExchange.intentNonce at 0x1015 reverted: the v6.12.0 contract set (node/app.go v6120Contracts, line 4093 onward) serves the perpetuals contract at 0x1015 (precompiles/perps/perps.go line 25) and node/repair_m1142_test.go lines 21 to 31 already select the ABI the application serves there. The record calls the revert pre-existing; it is a stale assertion of the test the task owns. The attempt also found tests/ci/test_node_build_workflow_scope.py hard-coding the six baseline names (line 15) outside its touches."
fix = "Decision 2910: a test asserts the retirement the producer made and never rebuilds a retired module inside the application manager; attempt 2 of 22.39.155 follows the producer for the anchor entry and the 0x1015 contract, and the node check inventory test joins the touches of 22.39.155 and 22.39.116."

[gotcha.3618]
title = "The daemon signature migration stopped at the callers the previous round named while six more sites sit in a test target outside touches"
symptom = "Task 9.35.19 attempt 10 at f64707374e5c (base 01f2f5ac27) migrated the thirteen callers the previous continuation named; the all-targets build then failed at six more sites in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_545.rs (lines 321, 340, 404, 424, 448 and 530), each passing a prepare::Prepared reference where verify_native_owner_send_purpose and inspect_native_send_capability now take prepare::evm::Prepared, a file outside the task touches; the verification never ran. On the main tree the two functions are called from that test target, from src/human_runtime.rs and from src/capability/binding.rs only."
fix = "Decision 2911: a signature migration enumerates every caller the all-targets build names and the touches of such a task cover the whole tests directory of the crate; attempt 11 of 9.35.19 migrates the six sites and the touches list carries services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests from this round."

[gotcha.3619]
title = "The platform CLI continuation began before the root install reached its build step and failed at the same TypeScript SDK dependency"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 19 at bbb71aa07459 (base d5ab6bfac8a0) started with the build step of the previous spec revision; the build passed, every CLI test passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed again in emulator/tests/repair_22_31_200.rs line 121 with the TypeScript SDK unable to resolve @noble/hashes, the failure gotcha 3615 recorded for attempt 18. The build step with the root workspace install (decision 2856) landed in the previous round after this attempt had begun, so the attempt never ran it."
fix = "Attempt 20 of 22.39.118 runs with the root install build step; the attempt-19 tree stands as the attempt-18 tree did."

[gotcha.3620]
title = "The wired tools Python suite compiles the loadtest contracts offline and the compiler the sources pin is absent until an online build fetches it"
symptom = "Task 22.39.84 attempt 4 at dbfdb5affdcf (verified at 37b951f36d76, base 52d45600b0) wired the suites, the baseline families and the workflow job; the four wiring cases passed and make test-tools-python recorded 733 passes, 8 skips, 460 subtests and one setup error: the module fixture compiled_contracts of tools/benchmark/loadtest/contracts/evm/test_sources_match_bindings.py runs forge build --offline, which cannot install solc 0.8.20 while the compiler cache is empty. The workflow job the attempt wrote runs forge build --root tools/benchmark/loadtest/contracts/evm online before the suite (ci.yml line 80), which fills that cache; the build step of the task did not, and the first build also found zstd absent until the attempt installed it. After the attempt installed the compiler the repair build passed, but the repair budget was spent."
fix = "Decision 2912: a build step whose suite compiles pinned Solidity sources offline runs the online forge build of those sources first, as the workflow job does; the build step of 22.39.84 carries it from this round and attempt 5 continues from the attempt-4 tree."

[gotcha.3621]
title = "The hosted-program restart test added one hand-placed occupancy finalization and the kernel refused its context"
symptom = "Task 22.39.116 attempt 2 at 23e73a8366a8 (verified at 7259c57975b8 then 23e73a8366a8, base 18f732b327) emptied the three baseline entries and kept the node test step without the skip pattern; TestMergePlanReturnsGuarantorBonds and TestHostedKernelProgramsABIFollowsTheMergeUpgrade passed. TestHostedKernelProgramsABISurvivesRestart first failed at node/upgrades_merge_programs_abi_test.go line 312: the restarted application selected ABI 5 after LoadLatestVersion, and the program call at height 43 returned LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED (code -736) while the same call at height 42 before the restart passed. The attempt answered with one Host.FinalizeProgramsOccupancy call at height 42 using lxphost.NextSequence of the store, and the second verification failed at line 287 with LXP_ERR_CONTEXT_MISMATCH (code -213) from the kernel. The application never calls that method in its block flow (node/app.go reaches the host only through Close; the kernel runs the occupancy transition inside its batch snapshot finalization, src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c near line 4780); the only callers are host-driven tests, which finalize every block from the fee record onward with the sequence read through host.ReadLastSequence for the fixture DID plus one (rpc/repair_478_test.go lines 302 to 311, rpc/sequencer_receipt_vectors_test.go line 653). The attempt wrote no task record and the task lists no record path."
fix = "Decision 2913: a test that drives the kernel host directly across blocks settles occupancy the way the host precedent tests do, for every block and with the sequence read through the host, or it records the kernel site that refuses; attempt 3 of 22.39.116 follows that precedent and the task gains its record path."

[gotcha.3622]
title = "The supervisor socket of the hosted node is visible with its creation mode before the server narrows it, and the reset-state test observes that window"
symptom = "Task 22.39.131 attempt 3 at fe42850a8737 (verified at cebafc5a10b6, base ed28b38287) regenerated the explorer vector copy, repaired the three suites and retired their baseline entries; the five runner cases passed and make test-python-suites recorded 313 passes and one failure outside the task: services/platform/hosted/node/tests/test_reset_state.py line 347 asserts mode 0o660 on supervisor.sock as soon as the path exists, while generation_transport.py serve (lines 248 to 250) binds the listener first and then chowns and chmods the socket, so the test can observe the creation mode 0o755 between the bind and the chmod. The same module passed in the full-suite runs of attempt 2 and of task 22.39.132 attempt 2. The module sits under services/platform/hosted/node, which task 22.39.133 owns and touches."
fix = "Decision 2914: a timing window between a producer creating a file and narrowing its mode is a producer defect of the module owner; the whole-suite gate of another task records it as a baseline entry under that owner. Attempt 4 of 22.39.131 adds the entry for test_reset_state.py under 22.39.133, and 22.39.133 creates the socket under a umask of 0o117 so it never exists with a wider mode, then deletes the entry."

[gotcha.3623]
title = "The emulator middleware path still computes the receipt digest from the signed receipt bytes, which the seller refuses since the receipt-signature digest repair"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 20 at 578dd31cdd2b (base 44213279e4) ran the root workspace install and the cargo build, every CLI read-kind test passed, and make platform-test-tooling failed in the emulator crate: tools/platform/emulator/tests/repair_22_31_200.rs line 121 reports the real middleware path failed because the seller refused the receipt at services/platform/middleware/seller/src/index.ts verifyReceiptDigest. The embedded script at line 268 of that test computes receiptDigest as the keccak-256 of the signed receipt, while task 22.31.492 at 797a092bfa made the seller verify the receipt-signature digest verifySequencerReceipt returns and refuse the keccak form (its record names that refusal); the buyer, agent and conformance middleware were refreshed (services/platform/middleware/conformance/src/receipts.ts line 208 records hex(verified.receiptDigest)) and the emulator test under tools/ was not. The crate sits outside the touches of 22.39.118, the test belongs to the done task 22.31.200, and the public platform workflow runs the same make target, so main is red there."
fix = "Decision 2915 and task 22.39.166: the emulator middleware path carries the digest the verifier returns; 22.39.118 requires 22.39.166 and relaunches unchanged under decision 2904."

[gotcha.3624]
title = "The budget sources read the call sender of a call-bound disclosure as an actor DID and refuse source ownership"
symptom = "Task 9.35.19 attempt 11 at 07c500d028d5 (base 44213279e4) migrated the twelve callers round 265 named, built after one repair of two test targets, and the verification ran 331 tests of which four failed, all in the human_runtime retained_settlement_tests module, each refusing with ProgramSourceError SourceOwnership before any settlement. The test binds the call with prepare::disclose::bind(call, sender) and passes the resulting EvmPrepared through read_program_budget_sources, whose call-bound form reads the actor DID from prepared.disclosure.actor; the call binding producer stores the twenty-byte call sender there (layerx-crypto src/disclosure/call.rs line 974, src/disclosure.rs line 1148, asserted by the producer test at call.rs line 1362) while the struct comment at src/disclosure.rs line 254 still calls the field the actor DID of the canonical envelope. verify_fee_payer (program_sources.rs lines 1312 to 1343) turns those bytes into text, strips the did:layerx: prefix and refuses SourceOwnership; the principal_source calls at lines 608 and 641, the owner comparison of read_program_budget_sources_call, program_settlement.rs lines 1142 and 1193 and the approval carrier of native_effect.rs (which now stores the disclosure actor and compares it with owner.agent_did at program_settlement.rs lines 181 and 278) read the field the same stale way."
fix = "Decision 2916: the actor of a call-bound disclosure is the call sender; attempt 12 of 9.35.19 takes the owner DID from the record each consumer holds and binds sender to owner once in verify_fee_payer."

[gotcha.3625]
title = "The node test selection of the v6.6 upgrade task passed its three names to go test as an unquoted alternation, so the shell split the gate at the bars"
symptom = "Task 22.39.155 attempt 2 at 5053a52d7a06 (base 525495e593) implemented round 264 (the two replication fixtures, the v6.6 assertions following the producer, the inventory test, the record); the build passed and the wiring suite passed (3 passed), then the Go step exited 127 with sh reporting the second and third test names as commands not found: the verification command written in round 264 passes the three names to go test -run without quotes, so the shell ran go test with the first name only and piped its output into two nonexistent commands, and the result of the Go tests was never observed. The tree is unchanged by this round."
fix = "The verification command of 22.39.155 quotes and anchors the alternation from this round; attempt 3 continues from the attempt-2 tree with the build and the verification run once each."

[gotcha.3626]
title = "The second launchpad verification run met the role and the relation the first run created on the same fixture server"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 6 at e72144476b81 (gate first at a0b54a05f384, base f4da299f15) added the four service variables, tidied the indexer module and recorded the baseline entries as round 258 instructed. The first verification run passed the wiring suite (26 passed) and the shared modules and stopped at the ten-minute package timeout of protocol/bindings in TestRepair_37_native_family_events, which was cold-building the indexer consumer under a mixed Go toolchain; the attempt pinned Go 1.27.3 in the job and the Makefile (recorded as the mixed toolchain finding) and the second run reached every module and failed only in sdk/launchpad/shared/db/production: production_test.go line 153 found the role l07_stats_owner and line 266 the relation l07_rollback already present, both created by the first run against the same fixture server, which the public job never sees because its database service starts fresh for every run."
fix = "Decision 2917: a gate that drives tests against fixture databases the public job provisions fresh drops the roles the tests create and recreates those databases before every gate run; attempt 7 of 22.39.75 continues from the attempt-6 tree with that reset."

[gotcha.3627]
title = "The two container inventory tests hard-code the out-of-scope recipe list and its count, so the scope repair of the container check failed in two modules outside its touches"
symptom = "Task 22.39.158 attempt 1 at 02ab95dc5e3d (base 215e9d31d250) brought the out-of-scope list of tools/containers/check.sh to the current tree: it removed three rows whose recipes no longer exist on main (the simd-dlv image, the rosetta node recipe without a suffix and the retired platform-node recipe), added the two rosetta node recipes with the historical and paxd suffixes and the two recipes of the vendored tree, kept the redis recipe, exempted the audit repair records from the reference scan, added a root recipe reference pattern and tightened the build boundary and the multi-stage copy handling; the four named tests passed. The package gate then recorded 51 passes and four failures in two modules outside the touches: tools/containers/test_out_of_scope_list.py line 20 asserts the previous thirty-four rows verbatim (index 15 names the simd-dlv recipe where the tree now lists simd-env, and the redis row is one more), and tools/containers/test_repair_22_33_776.py lines 27, 43 and 53 reuse that assertion and assert a count of thirty-four. The record calls the two modules a blocker outside scope."
fix = "Decision 2918 with 2907, 2908 and 2910: a test that hard-codes a producer list follows the producer and belongs to the touches of the task that changes the list. Attempt 2 of 22.39.158 keeps the attempt-1 tree, carries both inventory modules in its touches and makes them assert the thirty-five current rows and the count."

[gotcha.3628]
title = "The signer binding test still runs its request deadline on the wall clock against two real subprocess spawns, and the hosted node tree started before the socket creation mode item landed"
symptom = "Task 22.39.133 attempt 1 at b1bfe1a0dc2c (base 8b994ac86f09) repaired the eight hosted node, testnet and platform manifest suites, retired their nine baseline rows and drove the signer deadline test from a request-scoped clock as do_4 asks. The first verification at 71b43b5948e1 recorded 371 passes and one failure at services/platform/hosted/node/tests/test_repair_22_31_355.py line 763 (a Readiness attribute the deployed kernel runtime module no longer exports), repaired; the second at b1bfe1a0dc2c recorded 371 passes and one failure in services/platform/hosted/node/signer/test_repair_22_33_1454.py test_signer_binding_deadline_and_signature_checks line 258: the third bind call received the busy refusal because the serving fixture at line 243 keeps a 0.7 second request timeout on the real monotonic clock while the command backend spawns one subprocess for the public key and another for the binding (provider.py line 89), which the loaded full-suite run cannot finish inside the deadline. The attempt claimed its tree at 04:49Z, before do_5 (the umask of 0o117 around the supervisor socket bind, gotcha 3622) landed, so the tree carries no umask in services/platform/hosted/node/generation_transport.py."
fix = "Decision 2919 extends 2901: every deadline of a test that exercises a subprocess-backed signer runs on the controllable clock, and only a deadline the test means to expire advances it. Attempt 2 of 22.39.133 keeps the tree, gives the binding test the same clock as the deadline test, implements do_5 and deletes the reset-state baseline row when the merged tree carries it."

[gotcha.3629]
title = "The release candidate suite gate ran the whole tools target without the prerequisites the public job builds, its baseline rows sit outside its touches, and the AI evidence cases load private records of one approved candidate from the environment"
symptom = "Task 22.39.144 attempt 1 at bd0358e55efa (final tree 187162452818, base 215e9d31d250) repaired the release candidate consumers against their producers (environment strings at the authority boundary, the forty-service catalogue in the gate test module fixture, the sequencer identity in the inventory fixtures, the publisher manifest binding in the governance check, the retained lni tree in the catalogue test, the signature route) and left all forty-four baseline rows in place because tests/ci/data/tools_python_suite_baseline.json is outside its touches although do_3 asks it to delete the rows of passing cases; tests/ci/test_tools_python_suites_wired.py line 84 also hard-codes that count. The verification ran make test-tools-python without the prerequisites the public tools-python job of .github/workflows/ci.yml builds before the same target (lines 58 to 93: zstd, Foundry, buildx, build/liblayerx.a, build/loadtest, the forge build of the loadtest contracts, bringup-inspect, the xweb loader and a localhost SSH service), so it recorded 689 passes, 41 failures and 6 errors, all outside tools/paxeer-x and all environmental: thirty-three loadtest envelope cases and one changed-parameter case without build/loadtest, four container cases run by the legacy builder, one release check case without SSH to localhost, one forward recovery case without zstd, one edge manifest case without bringup-inspect, one bindings setup without forge and five genesis rewrite setups whose fixture build failed. The twenty-four cases of tools/paxeer-x/tests/ai_evidence_test.py load the admission and approval records of the approved candidate from two environment variables in setUpClass, while ai_evidence.py pins that candidate (base ce269bfe23c1, branch px26/fm1/ai-workspace, issuance 1791454712, Python 3.12.3; validate_structure lines 370 to 379, validate_workspace lines 461 to 480), so the module passes only inside that workspace, and the record retains the twenty-four rows pending genuine authority."
fix = "Decisions 2878, 2906, 2908, 2918 and 2920: the whole-target gate of 22.39.144 asserts the public prerequisites in its build command (as 22.39.164 does, plus zstd, buildx and localhost SSH, which 22.39.164 now asserts as well), the task carries the baseline file and the wired inventory test in its touches, requires 22.39.157, 22.39.158 and 22.39.164 whose packages share the target, and attempt 2 builds the authority fixture from the pinned constants."

[gotcha.3630]
title = "The integration script test reads the kernel state of a killed descendant before it reaches the zombie state, so the whole-suite gate of the conformance repair failed on a race outside the task"
symptom = "Task 22.39.131 attempt 4 at 3468ec6ceca2 (final tree 80deacfdd281, base e29019b56d12) kept the attempt-3 tree and appended the reset-state baseline row under 22.39.133; the five runner cases passed and make test-python-suites recorded 289 passes and one failure outside the task: tests/integration/scripts/test_repair_22_33_758.py line 245 (test_python_status_timeout_kills_process_group_and_stops_setup) reads the stat file of the killed descendant right after the runner kills the process group and asserts the zombie state, and read R because the kernel had not finished tearing the process down. The same case passed in the full-suite runs of attempts 2 and 3 and of 22.39.133 attempt 1. No open task touches tests/integration/scripts."
fix = "Decision 2921 with 2901 and 2908: a test that asserts the kernel state of a process after a signal waits under a bound for the transition. Attempt 5 of 22.39.131 carries the module in its touches and makes the assertion poll the stat file until it is gone or reads the zombie state within three seconds."

[gotcha.3631]
title = "The production allowance test measures the raw ai-market guest against the deployment bound that production applies to the optimised artifact, so the merged payout split pushed the sweep tree over it"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 28 at d4a3a88fab8f (final tree ffd215bdea94, base cfe6c8212d04) carried the attempt-27 tree onto a main that now holds the payout split of 22.38.6. The build gate failed three times in rpc/repair_478_test.go line 127 (TestRepair478_FundWithinProductionAllowance): repair478Guests builds the historical and the candidate guest in an isolated workspace with opt-level z and no post-pass and requires the raw artifact at or under 524184 bytes; it measured 536740, 537201 and 536580 bytes across the two repair cycles, which the attempt spent on guest sharing changes outside its instructions. The same tree measured 514143 raw bytes at base 09673a24d2af in attempt 27, where the Go gate passed, so the merge of the payout split added about twenty-two thousand raw bytes; the gate of 22.38.6 measured the optimised artifact of the make target (484316 bytes for the attempt-27 tree; the make target bound of 524184 applies after wasm-opt by decision 94). Decision 2733 already makes the authority receipt proof build the guest exactly as the make target does and assert the optimised artifact; the production allowance test of 22.31.478 never followed."
fix = "Decision 2922 with 94 and 2733: a test that builds the ai-market guest from source applies the production post-pass before measuring and deploying it. Attempt 29 of 22.99.77 carries rpc/repair_478_test.go in its touches, gives repair478Guests the wasm-opt step of the make target for both revisions, records raw and optimised sizes, and spends no cycle on source size."

[gotcha.3632]
title = "Four bringup cases of the tools-python gate fail from producers outside tools/bringup/tests: a repository root resolved through a process substitution, a retired relay variable, a stale import graph digest and a percent-encoded media host"
symptom = "Task 22.39.164 attempt 1 at 444720c13af8 and dd34403c55d1 (base 215e9d31d250) corrected the benchmark binding, the hosts file, the transcript and the baseline rows, and make test-tools-python then reported 8 failed and 738 passed. tools/bringup/search-front.sh line 12 sources the check-live functions through a process substitution, so tools/bringup/check-live.sh line 296 resolves repo_root from /dev/fd and line 305 pins rpc_inventory under the filesystem root before search-front.sh line 13 recomputes repo_root; bringup-inspect rpc-names therefore reports public inventory unreadable. tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh line 1193 still passes LAYERX_INDEXER_RELAY_URL and LAYERX_INDEXER_RELAY_CA_DER to the indexer stand-in while the indexer config test relay_variables_are_not_read retires them and test_bringup_fixtures_retired asserts their absence. tools/bringup/runtime-dependencies.json records a digest of docs/swagger/statik.go that no longer matches the tree, so the foundation artifact check refuses the producer import graph. ValidateDocumentNames in tools/bringup/live_repair.go line 465 scans the lowercased document text for served names, and the README.md line 3 header image URL carries the media host percent-encoded, which the scan reads as 2fwww.paxeer.network, a name neither the inventory docs/site/docs/reference/public-rpc.md nor the public names section lists. Four container cases failed on the legacy docker builder without buildx, the environmental case of gotcha 3629. Task 22.39.84 attempt 3 recorded the four bringup producers as pre-existing findings and attempt 1 of 22.39.164 left them unchanged as outside its touches."
fix = "Decision 2908 makes the whole-package gate owner own every failure nobody else records: the touches of 22.39.164 widen from tools/bringup/tests to tools/bringup, attempt 2 corrects the four producers, regenerates the import graph record with tools/bringup/tests/runtime-dependencies.py, percent-decodes the document text before the host scan (decision 2923) and sets up the public prerequisites of the tools-python job before the build gate; the public names section names the website."

[gotcha.3633]
title = "The platform tooling gate imports the python cryptography module through the testnet chain id test, which neither the public platform job step nor the qualification environment installs"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 21 at 043ac50c1f65 (base 0a3c76a05374) built, and make platform-test-tooling failed in layerx-platform-testnet: testnet_chain_id_parameters_to_signed_transaction at services/platform/hosted/testnet/tests/repair_22_31_351.rs line 206 runs python3 with an inline program whose line 51 imports cryptography, and the interpreter answered ModuleNotFoundError. The public platform job step at .github/workflows/platform.yml line 70 installs dbus, gnome-keyring, python3-pytest and python3-yaml only; the hosted job at line 1569 installs python3-cryptography. Attempts 16 and 18 of 22.39.118 never reached the testnet crate, and 22.31.351 attempt 1 passed the test in an environment that had the module."
fix = "Decision 2924: the public job step that runs a wired suite installs every interpreter module its tests import; the touches of 22.39.118 carry .github/workflows/platform.yml, the step at line 70 adds python3-cryptography, the qualification environment installs the same package before the build command, and the build command asserts the import first."

[gotcha.3634]
title = "The budget module re-exports the carrier readers but not the call-bound readers that the Human API preparation consumers name"
symptom = "Task 9.35.20 attempt 1 at 25a272675293 (base 0a3c76a05374) failed its build with E0425: cargo build -p layerx-agentd --tests cannot find read_program_budget_sources_call and read_native_effect_budget_sources_call in module crate::budget. Task 9.35.19 (41390400af) added both readers in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/budget/program_sources.rs lines 413 and 552, but the re-export list of budget/mod.rs line 43 carries only read_program_budget_sources, read_native_effect_budget_sources and read_native_lifecycle_budget_sources, and program_sources is a private module, so the consumers in human_runtime.rs and agent_rpc_adapters.rs cannot reach the call-bound readers; the budget module is outside the touches of 9.35.20 and no open task touches it."
fix = "Decision 2925: a producer module re-exports every reader its consumer task names; the touches of 9.35.20 carry budget/mod.rs for the two export names only, and attempt 2 relaunches on the attempt-1 tree."

[gotcha.3635]
title = "The launchpad preparation script waits for operator-admitted inputs that the repository is meant to generate from owned private fixtures, so ten web cases still refuse to run"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 2 at 9857111ec409 and 4078ebdbf4a0 (base 64113cfe7faf) added the pinned Foundry step and scripts/prepare-test-environment.py to the web job, and the web suite ended with 10 failed and 1266 passed in 7 files. The script reads an admission map from LAUNCHPAD_TEST_INPUTS, requires eleven pre-existing variables in its first stage (L25_QUALIFICATION_CONFIG_FILE and SHA256, L25_ADMITTED_SOURCE_SHA256, L27_AUTHORITY_PROFILE, L28_CHAIN_FIXTURE_JSON and SHA256, L26_MEASUREMENT_CONFIG and SHA256, JOINED_CONFIG_FILE, JOINED_CONFIG_SHA256, JOINED_CHAIN_FILE) and runs the advanced and trading generators only when their outputs already exist, so nothing was generated: the trade journey, measurement, connected journeys, creation journey, three wallet runtime and four chart recovery cases threw for absent bound inputs, while the repository carries producers for every L26 variable (run-phase2.py and run-phase4.py under widgets/trading/transaction-controls), for L27_PHASE2_FIXTURE (run-creation-chain.py under widgets/create) and for every L28 variable (connected-chain-inputs.mjs under widgets/meta-ag). The remaining inputs have no producer yet and are private-fixture records by their own checks: the joined chain file must carry realm private-anvil125 with productionActivation false, the creation case asks for the owned private-fixture authority profile, and the wallet runtime case asks for admitted network, head, deposit and challenge evidence with a source digest. The embedded sign-in modal test timed out in its setup step at 10000 ms while importing four application modules."
fix = "Decision 2926: every environment input a launchpad web case reads is produced by a repository generator that the preparation script runs unconditionally in the documented order on owned Anvil children; attempt 3 of 22.39.95 removes the admission map and the gated stages and adds the three missing producers."

[gotcha.3636]
title = "The peer bond operations add twenty-five thousand bytes to a guest with twenty thousand bytes of headroom and refuse the bids of every existing test setup"
symptom = "Task 22.38.7 attempt 1 at 3964ef3fa398 (base e5a65a27e50b) failed the size test of its build gate three times: the packaged guest measured 529219 bytes at the first build and 529811 bytes at the final tree against the 524184 bound, while the main tree after the payout split of 22.38.6 measures 504494 bytes (the attempt-3 record of 22.38.6), so the bond module (src/bonds.rs, 940 lines with a private region decoder, writer, footer and a 512-slot fault table) with the routing and reward changes adds about twenty-five thousand bytes where main leaves under twenty thousand, and two repair cycles inside the five touched files recovered nothing. At the final tree the crate suite showed 36 previously passing cases failing across the f04, f05 and f11 targets, because PostBid now refuses a bid without a persisted lock and the existing test setups post bids without one (the test files were outside the touches, so the attempt left them unchanged), and four f11_bonds cases failed (slash after a resolved miss, double slash for one lap, refund after the window, missed countersign deadline); the task record states that a sealed single-lap batch carries only its quorum count, so the guest cannot name the peer that missed the countersign deadline. The verification never ran."
fix = "Decisions 2792 and 2927 to 2929: task 22.39.167 brings the guest back to at most 484184 bytes driven by the function metrics table before the bond operations land and 22.38.7 requires it; attempt 2 fits the bond module into the shared helpers and the placement book region, locks a bond in every existing test setup that posts a bid, and the lap batch records the peers that did not countersign."

[gotcha.3637]
title = "The hosted testnet README documents fifteen of the seventeen inputs the smoke script requires, so the documentation test of the platform tooling target fails"
symptom = "Task 22.39.118 attempt 22 at 6f42e123e276 (base e8cd0764863d) passed its build (the python cryptography import, the root install, the CLI test build) and the CLI rpc tests, and the platform tooling target then failed in one case: doc_testnet_readme_native_smoke_inputs of services/platform/hosted/testnet/tests/repair_22_33_1449.rs line 184 panicked with the message undocumented required input LAYERX_TEST_ACCOUNTS_FILE. The test walks every presence assertion at the head of tests/hosted-smoke.sh (seventeen inputs) and requires the README to name each one; the README names fifteen and omits LAYERX_TEST_ACCOUNTS_FILE (line 17 of the script, the explicit DID to EVM smoke account bindings that tests/smoke_accounts.py writes as smoke-accounts.json) and LAYERX_TEST_SOURCE_EVM_KEY_FILE (line 18, the PEM key file of the paying EVM signer that the same helper writes). The record of the earlier documentation repair (tests/repair_22_33_1447.kvx line 28) requests both lines, and the README on main does not carry them. No pending task touches the hosted testnet directory, so the whole-package gate owner carries the two lines under decision 2908."
fix = "Decision 2930: the README of the hosted testnet names every input the smoke script asserts, and the task whose gate runs the documentation test adds the missing lines with the README in its touches; 22.39.118 attempt 23 documents the two inputs beside the other smoke inputs."

[gotcha.3638]
title = "The EVM write path test creates its durable store roots with the default directory mode, which the protected store root check refuses"
symptom = "Task 9.35.20 attempt 2 at 2fc5394b7570 (base e8cd0764863d) added the two budget re-exports and passed its build and four of its five test targets; the fifth, tests/write_path_evm.rs, failed four cases at lines 27 and 158, each unwrapping Store::open with the refusal store root is not a canonical owned private directory. The store validates its root since the restart-recovery repair of 22.30.91 (src/store/protected.rs line 86: a directory owned by the effective user, mode exactly 0700, and a path equal to its canonical form), and the test creates its roots under the temporary directory with std::fs::create_dir, which applies the default mode 0755; every other integration test of the crate creates its root through DirBuilder with mode 0700 (approval expiry, budget reserve, capability consume, the host tests). The test has not run under a gate since the store check landed on 2026-11-04 and is a target of this gate only."
fix = "Decision 2931: a test that opens the durable store creates its root as a canonical owned private directory, and the gate owner whose targets run the test corrects its setup; 9.35.20 attempt 3 creates both roots through DirBuilder with mode 0700 and canonicalises them, with the test file in its touches."

[gotcha.3639]
title = "The launchpad toolchain pin leaks into the node overlay test, where the pinned swiss map dependency of pebble does not compile under Go 1.27"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 7 at 357e916cb654 (record tree dec46c1d7c43, base 2c0d3e303058) passed its build and the 26 wiring tests, the database reset of decision 2917 removed the earlier leftovers, and make ci then failed in one case: TestRepair_37_native_family_events of sdk/launchpad/protocol/bindings/repair_37_test.go line 93. The helper repair37Run runs go test inside the node module (precompiles/launchpad) with the environment of the calling process, and services/launchpad/Makefile line 16 exports GOTOOLCHAIN go1.27.3 for the launchpad modules, so the node module compiled under Go 1.27.3 although its go.mod pins go 1.25.8 and the node workflow builds it with go-version-file. The indirect dependency github.com/cockroachdb/swiss at v0.0.0-20251224182025-b0f6560f979b (through pebble v2.1.3) provides hashFn, getRuntimeHasher and fastrand64 only in runtime_go1.20.go, whose build tag is go1.20 and not go1.27, so the package failed with seven undefined symbols and the overlay proof never ran. Every other node gate pins the toolchain of the root go.mod; the launchpad pin is right for the launchpad modules and wrong for the node module the overlay test compiles."
fix = "Decision 2932: a launchpad test that compiles the node module runs it with the toolchain of the root go.mod, setting GOTOOLCHAIN for that command from the go directive of the node module; 22.39.75 attempt 8 corrects repair37Run with the test file in its touches."

[gotcha.3640]
title = "The documentation names check refuses every prefixed faucet variable name and the bare parent domain of the node names, so the docs-names case fails on the main tree"
symptom = "Task 22.39.164 attempt 2 at c8e49bb70d6a (base e8cd0764863d) repaired the search front discovery assertion and the percent-encoded README name, and its second verification then failed one case of 769: test_docs_names_reads_existing_spec of tools/bringup/tests/test_spec_paths.py, because bringup-inspect docs-names refused docs/ci/secrets-and-runners.md as unpublished faucet configuration. ValidateDocumentNames of tools/bringup/live_repair.go line 461 refuses any document containing the substring FAUCET_URL; the shell check it replaced in the 22.30.177 repair (6fce495bf8, 2026-11-04) used git grep -w, which matched only the bare whole word FAUCET_URL, so the prefixed inputs LAYERX_FAUCET_URL, LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_URL and LAYERX_SCHEDULED_FAUCET_URL passed. Eight documents in the docs-names scope on main carry such prefixed names: the CI secrets inventory that 22.39.49 requires to list every public check variable (its test tests/ci/test_workflow_secrets_documented.py), the faucet, hosted gateway and beta control pages of docs/site and the wiki, and the quickstart. After the faucet refusal, the public name scan would refuse seven more documents (docs/paxeer-network.md, docs/perps/data-api.md, the three 7.0.0 release documents, docs/wiki/PublicRpc.md and docs/wiki/Sequencing.md) for the bare parent domain mainnet-beta.paxeer.network, which they name when they describe api1 through api14 under that domain or write the node name with a placeholder label; the parent domain of the declared node names serves nothing and is not an unpublished name. The check stops at the first refused document, so the attempt saw only the first one in tracked-file order."
fix = "Decision 2933: the check refuses the bare whole-word configuration name FAUCET_URL only, as the shell check did, and accepts the parent domain of every declared node name; 22.39.164 attempt 3 corrects ValidateDocumentNames with its policy test extended for both rules."

[gotcha.3641]
title = "The launchpad preparation script treats the phase-four measurement configuration as a producer input, but the phase-four measurement is a release run whose validator binds a qualified serial gate and a retired spec path"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 3 at cba4f786e00a (base 59c437e6cb1c) removed the admission map and generated the wallet, creation and advanced inputs from owned fixtures; its first verification stopped at the advanced stage (the deployment descriptor was not yet exported, repaired within the cycle) and its second at the trading phase four stage with Missing producer input L26_MEASUREMENT_CONFIG, so no suite ran. The script expects the measurement configuration from the environment because nothing in the repository can produce it: configure of src/widgets/trading/transaction-controls/run-phase4.py requires a prior gate record of the serial task 3.99 marked qualified and canonically integrated, the digest of spec/production-system/spec.kvx (a path the tree no longer carries), a browser bundle, a browser executable, a playwright entry and fault controls bound to the current source digest. The measurement case measurement.integration.test.tsx reads that configuration at module load and is the only case that needs it (the optimistic receipt integration test touches its output only when L26_PHASE4 is set); the phase two vitest configuration of the trading widget already includes the measurement case only under L26_PHASE4, while the workspace configuration apps/launchpad/web/vitest.config.ts includes every test file, so the plain test run collects a release measurement harness. The do item of attempt 3 listed L26_MEASUREMENT_CONFIG among the generator outputs; run-phase4.py consumes it as its --config argument and produces nothing of the kind."
fix = "Decision 2934: the phase-four measurement runs only through run-phase4.py with an operator configuration and is excluded from the workspace test run; 22.39.95 attempt 4 removes the phase four stage from the preparation script and excludes the measurement case in the workspace vitest configuration."

[gotcha.3642]
title = "The AI market suite owner made its own guest size changes on a base that already carried the size task, breaking twelve test targets"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 29 at 3588221d01e2 (base 95c2388776a4, which already carries the 22.39.142 size tree 075a770edb with the guest at 483154 bytes) first failed its build at 6ebb141df125 because wasm-opt refused the historical guest for undeclared bulk memory (repaired by stripping only debug information so the target features section survives), passed the build at the final tree, and then failed the crate suite in 12 of its targets with about sixty cases: artifact_binding, f03_evaluator_admission, f03_evaluator_host, f04_windows, f05_aggregation_runtime, fuel_budget, host_boundary, manifest_v2_capabilities, repair_22_33_261, reputation_lifecycle, rewards_native and task_state_boundary. The attempt changed 18 source files of the crate for guest size although the bound was already met: it routed the reputation admission reads of the evaluator admission, evidence and roster modules through a joint table wrapper, so the reopened reward test of repair_22_33_261.rs line 1280 fails with the message that the F06 decoder requires the F08 table and not the joint F07 and F08 prefix, and the sealed task set view refuses with 2305; it added a BAD_VERSION refusal for a version-2 manifest body that ends before its capability fields, so the framing test of manifest_v2_capabilities.rs line 243 receives BAD_VERSION where it asserts NON_CANONICAL, and the record calls that test and the grammar case of the participant lifecycle target contradictory although both are unchanged main tests that the decoder main carries satisfies; it also changed the rollover scratch constant, the guest copy of types.rs and added never-inline attributes. The host boundary target reported runtime status -736 at heights 1000 and 1001 where the reader expected the CandidateV4 terminal."
fix = "Decision 2935: the suite owner of the AI market crate makes no guest size change and restores any decoder, refusal code or section layout an unchanged test asserts; 22.99.77 attempt 30 restores the crate sources to the merged base apart from the functional repairs a failing assertion required, keeps the post-pass test and the record, and repairs the remaining failures at the sites their assertions name."

[gotcha.3643]
title = "The sdk lib suite asserts two registration parameters where the hosted gateway publishes an optional third, and its TLS identity cases need the boundary binary the gate never built"
symptom = "Task 9.35.23 attempt 1 at eccc16297056 (base cb96b80a5c25) bound the served call in the sdk and mcp native disclosure checks, passed its build twice and the mcp lib suite, and failed four cases of the layerx-sdk lib suite that its two touched files do not reach. rpc::tests::register_method_and_params_are_the_ones_the_gateway_publishes (src/rpc.rs line 1738) asserts the px_register parameter names signer_public_key and registration_signature, while services/platform/hosted/gateway/openrpc.json has published the optional third parameter email_or_verification_token since the 22.30.81 repair (44a718e948, 2026-11-04, the record of 22.31.202 names it): the consumer test predates the producer change and the SDK call at line 1111 sends only the two required arguments, which the handler accepts. The three cases rpc_system_tls_checks_the_actual_server_identity, rpc_private_ca_tls_checks_the_actual_server_identity and rpc_subscription_private_ca_checks_the_actual_server_identity start the real TLS boundary through services/platform/tests/support/tls_boundary.rs line 186, which refuses with the producer-input message of decision 2325 unless layerx-paxeer-boundary is built and LAYERX_PAXEER_BOUNDARY_BIN names it; the build command of the task builds only the two agent crates and its verification sets no such variable, where the sibling gates that run an agent lib suite (22.39.122 among them) build the boundary from services/platform/Cargo.toml and point the variable at its target directory."
fix = "Decision 2936: the registration test asserts the published parameter list with the third optional, and every gate running the sdk lib suite builds the boundary binary and names it; 9.35.23 attempt 2 corrects the test with src/rpc.rs in its touches under the corrected build and verification commands."

[gotcha.3644]
title = "The agent daemon test port leaves the legacy preparation calls of two repair test targets outside its touches, so its own retired-name search refuses the tree"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 1 at 7e0e122f6a7b (base c1cec79b2794) ported the nine test files it declares (the support module, the owner binding, proof, disclosure, prepare expiry, core time, budget durable limits and human node preparation targets and the exactly-once limits test) from the activity envelope to the ledger payment call, passed its build, and failed at the first half of its verification: the search for the retired names over services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests still finds restore_canonical in tests/repair_22_31_217.rs line 2402 (the wire carrier restart test rebuilds the retained authorization from the unsigned wire envelope and asserts it equals the native restoration) and prepare_activity_for_protocol and restore_canonical in tests/repair_22_31_545.rs lines 91 and 516 (the retained authorization helper prepares a human activity through the production preparation boundary and the consent reopen test restores the stored authorization bytes). Both files are repair targets of done tasks (22.31.217 with 22.39.128, 22.31.545 with 22.31.613) that no pending task declares; the do_4 search of 9.35.22 covers the whole tests directory, and 9.35.24, which requires 9.35.22, deletes the legacy module and asserts the same search over the whole crate, so the three call sites must move to the call-bound preparation before the module can go. The tests the task ported never ran because the search refused first."
fix = "Decision 2937: the test port owns every retired preparation call under the tests directory of the crate, so 9.35.22 attempt 2 ports the two repair targets with both files in its touches and runs them in its verification."

[gotcha.3645]
title = "The second ai-market size task left the routing transition untouched although the metrics table names it as two fifths of the guest, and treated the packaging measurement as a gate build"
symptom = "Task 22.39.167 attempt 1 at 35bc97a9686d (base d996be5f0c2c) changed twelve source files of programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market (codec, types, epoch, rewards, placement, laps, canary, roster and the reputation and aggregation codecs) and brought the packaged guest from 505711 to 505461 bytes, 21277 bytes above the 484184 qualification bound, after both repair cycles; the five f11 targets never ran. The function metrics table the attempt recorded at its first packaged build names layerx_programs_ai_market routing transition_inner (the routing module source line 1622) at 208055 bytes, two fifths of the guest, followed by layerx_call at 21572, epoch compose at 19949 and the epoch aggregate closure at 19721, with every other function under 5100 bytes; the final table shows transition_inner at 208092 bytes, so none of the steps reached it. The transition match routes about forty operation ranges to the module entry points of registry, epoch, tasks, identity, admission, rooms, laps, rewards and canary, and those entry points are inlined into the one body with their decoders, so the never-inline helper technique of 22.39.142 (decision 2927) was never applied where the table points. The attempt also never measured the starting tree as do_1 requires: the record labels the inherited 504494 bytes of the payout split as not independently measured, on the reading that the packaging target counts as a gate build, where the gate builds are only the recorded build and verification commands and the packaging target is the measurement the task is told to repeat after every step."
fix = "Decision 2938: a size task of the ai-market guest measures the starting tree and after every step through the packaging target without counting those runs as gates, and starts where the metrics table points, the routing transition whose per-operation handlers become never-inlined entry points; 22.39.167 attempt 2 applies it."

[gotcha.3646]
title = "The launchpad indexer module fails eighteen cases of its processor, receipt and source packages the first time the Go gate reaches it, with the same result on PostgreSQL 16 and 18"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 8 at 9621d9237eec (base d996be5f0c2c) passed its build, the 26 wiring tests, both SDK modules including the overlay proof that decision 2932 repaired, and the api module, and then failed in services/launchpad/indexer in eighteen cases that no earlier attempt had reached (every earlier verification stopped in a module before it): thirteen in internal/processor (TestCanonicalProcessorConcurrentFencingPostgres, canonical_test.go line 286, cannot truncate a table referenced in a foreign key constraint; TestCanonicalDatabaseOutageAcknowledgesNothingPostgres, line 399, cannot disallow connections for the current database; TestQualifiedProductionIngestionRealMarketPostgres and the four TestRepair54 and TestRepair_54 live recovery and recorded qualification cases, receipt qualification rejected; the two TestRepair_54 and TestRepair54Postgres NativeReadModelProjection cases, whose HTTP consumer answers status unavailable with mode in the unavailable components; and the five replay_postgres_test.go cases TestReplayCheckpointAtomicAndLiveCursorIndependent, TestReplayCancellationRollbackAndResumePostgres, TestReplayPausedOldLeaderCannotPauseReplacementPostgres, TestPrivateReplayAuthorizationPostgres and TestReplayQuotaAndUnavailableRangePostgres, each refused by the server with inconsistent types deduced for parameter ten, SQLSTATE 42P08), three in internal/receipt (the TestRepair_53 native swap, tenant transaction and approved history cases, receipt qualification rejected) and two in internal/source (TestRepair56Postgres_ExplorerDynamicDiscoveries and TestRepair56Postgres_DiscoveryEpochBounds, receipt qualification rejected). The attempt replaced the PostgreSQL 18 and Redis of the qualification environment with the postgres 16 and redis 7 images the job declares and reran: the same eighteen cases failed, so the service versions are not the cause. The module manifest the attempt-6 tidy produced raised github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 from v5.10.0 to v5.11.0 beside the go-pglite test import, which is the first suspect for the five parameter typing refusals; the receipt rejections are the class 22.39.162 already owns for eleven indexer cases of app, config, decode, runtimedocs and source. The thirteen modules after the indexer never ran."
fix = "Decision 2939: the eighteen cases join the reviewed baseline with retiring task 22.39.162, which is widened to the three packages and the four failure classes with the pgx upgrade named as the first suspect; 22.39.75 attempt 9 adds the exact entries and runs the gate to its end."

[gotcha.3647]
title = "The restored ai-market guest exceeds the production CPU fuel allowance of Fund, which only the suite owner gate measures"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 30 at 42fc4308cf0d (base efeceb3a897a) restored the guest sources to the merged base apart from the functional repairs decision 2935 allows, and changed the allowance test of rpc/repair_478_test.go so that every guest it builds is packaged with wasm-opt -Oz as the host boundary target does (adding a third guest at the merge base for size evidence, and setting strip to debuginfo in its isolated manifest where the release profile of programs/Cargo.toml says true). The build gate then failed in every build at TestRepair478_FundWithinProductionAllowance: the production kernel ran the candidate Fund with the 1000000 CPU allowance and refused it with BudgetExceeded at attempted 1000018 (build-1.log) and, after the request digest was computed once before routing, at attempted 1000008 (build-2.log), while the kernel gas stayed at 635 against its 10000000 allowance; the test requires the candidate to complete under 999968 and under the historical guest of revision 71ea2b5cfcf9. The attempted figure is the first charge that crossed the allowance, so the actual consumption of Fund is unknown. Since 22.31.478 landed, the commits of eight tasks changed the guest source without this test in their gates (22.39.142 at 075a770edb, verified by four f11 targets, and the payout split of 22.38.6 at 2d8083af02 the most recent); the test on main measures an unoptimised guest built from an isolated manifest rather than the wasm-opt module the packaging target ships; and the crate test every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap of tests/fuel_budget.rs passed at the same tree because it meters the native replay and not the kernel. The verification never ran."
fix = "Decision 2940: the Fund allowance is an invariant of the packaged guest measured by the allowance test in the gate of every pending task that changes the guest source; 22.99.77 attempt 31 measures the actual Fund fuel of the historical, merged-base and candidate guests in both forms, attributes the overrun and repairs the Fund path; 22.39.167 and 22.38.7 run the test in their build gates."

[gotcha.3648]
title = "A preparation test ported off the legacy boundary keeps the legacy second-resolution expectation of the protocol timestamp"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 2 at 3e725f8c5739 (base efeceb3a897a) ported the remaining eleven test files to decode_unsigned, bind_call and prepare_bound and passed its build; the first verification failed three cases of budget_durable_limits.rs whose harness no longer admitted its charges, the one allowed repair corrected the harness (twelve cases pass at the second verification), and the second verification failed preparation_state_reads_chain_id_pending_nonce_and_block_time of tests/human_node_preparation.rs line 116 with left 1700000000000 and right 1700000000. The test now constructs ProductionCorePreparationBoundary from prepare instead of prepare::legacy, and the production producer (prepare/mod.rs) converts the head block timestamp from seconds to milliseconds per decision 2704, while the test still asserts the block timestamps it serves (1700000000 and 1700000012) in seconds at lines 116 and 124. The four later targets (outbox, limits-exactly-once, repair_22_31_217 and repair_22_31_545) did not run."
fix = "Decision 2941: a test ported from the legacy preparation boundary asserts the millisecond protocol timestamp of the production producer; 9.35.22 attempt 3 asserts 1700000000000 and 1700000012000 and reruns every declared target."

[gotcha.3649]
title = "The verification of the ported preparation tests exited 127 because the qualification environment of the attempt could not download Foundry"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 3 at 3d51904624f8 (base 95ab7359d7c5) corrected both protocol_timestamp expectations of tests/human_node_preparation.rs to milliseconds per decision 2941, recorded the producer reference, and passed its build with exit 0. The verification then stopped at its first step, anvil --version, with the shell refusal anvil: not found and exit 127, because the Foundry installation step of the qualification environment failed before the task ran: six downloads of the foundryup release attestation from GitHub answered 504 and the installer gave up after its fifth retry, so no Anvil binary existed although the same step installed Anvil 1.9.0 in attempt 2 of the same task. The eleven changed test files of the attempt are complete and the gate never reached a test."
fix = "Decision 2942: a verification that exits 127 because the qualification environment failed to provide a tool the command requires is an environmental failure; the attempt tree stands and the task relaunches unchanged as attempt 4 of 9.35.22."

[gotcha.3650]
title = "The documentation command guard reads the output lines of a prompt-led console block as commands, and the public RPC page documents a WebSocket upgrade at a path the guard refuses"
symptom = "Task 22.39.92 attempt 1 at 5220cd82bc6b (base 95ab7359d7c5) wrote the guard and its root map; its build passed and eight of the ten tests failed twice for two reasons. First, in a block of the Jev command page of the vendored tree documentation (the block at line 89, whose first line begins with a dollar prompt and whose two following lines are the refusal the command prints) the parser treats a line that begins with a shell word as a further command once the prompt line is consumed: the second output line begins with the word export and carries an apostrophe, so the tokenizer sees an unterminated quote and every test that walks the blocks fails with incomplete shell command at line 91. Second, test_doc_public_rpc_hosts_use_root_path refuses docs/readme/PUBLIC-RPC.md line 59, which records an observed WebSocket upgrade at the /ws path of the canonical alias host beside the upgrade at the root; decision 2810 documents no path other than the root. The page tree carries no other unresolved command."
fix = "Decision 2943: a block in which a line begins with a dollar prompt is prompt-led and only its prompt lines are commands; decision 2944: the WebSocket upgrade is documented at the root of the public hosts only; 22.39.92 attempt 2 corrects the parser and the page with the page in its touches."

[gotcha.3651]
title = "The first complete launchpad web suite run leaves ten failures in six files behind the development stream, the split deployment, the challenge endpoint, the approval spender and one deadline case"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 4 at fc0aaaac88dc (base 9d651f013b53) passed its build twice and ran the whole web suite for the first time: 1267 cases passed, 10 failed in 6 files, mobile was not reached (verify-2 exit 1, 989 seconds, 330 of them module imports). Its first verification stopped before Vitest because the joined services readiness probe of /health/ready exited 1 once. The ten failures fall in five groups. (1) Four chart recovery cases and the browser chart case fail behind CapabilityUnavailableError Unavailable endpoint /v2/snapshots (twelve occurrences): the joined API answers 503 for /v2/snapshots and /v2/stream whenever newDevelopmentStream of services/launchpad/api/internal/app/dev_stream.go leaves the stream nil (its constructor failed, or NETWORK_RPC_URL is unset and the projection stays idle), while /health/ready still answers, so the readiness probe of run-joined-services.py admits a service without market data; the advanced lifecycle case fails on Required price source stale for the same reason (priceFresh of advanced-provider.ts derives from the snapshot). (2) Two creation journey cases fail with Creation and trade deployment identities differ: creation-adapters.ts line 31 requires the trade deployment to carry the revision, router, usdl and registry of the creation deployment, and the creation generator and the trading phase two generator deploy separately. (3) The challenge case of runtime.integration.test.tsx posts to /v2/auth/challenges at the identity origin of the qualification record and the answer is not ok. (4) The trade journey case stops in approvalMayContinue of transaction-controls/runtime.ts line 110 with Refreshed allowance does not match approved amount; the record of the attempt already names the spender conflict (the carried test asserts the native spender 0x1017 while the owned Solidity fixture declares its Router proxy as usdlSpender). (5) socialRequestDeadline of widgets/social/repair-22-33-921.test.ts times out at its 15000 millisecond budget under the full workspace run. The attempt also changed apps/launchpad/web/package.json (the test script and the playwright 1.58.2 development dependency) without the workspace lockfile among its planned paths."
fix = "Decision 2945 and the attempt-5 note: readiness of the joined services includes a 200 answer of /v2/snapshots; one owned deployment feeds creation and trading; the spender follows the owned fixture; the lockfile is a planned path per decision 2829."

[gotcha.3652]
title = "The port task misses Anvil a second consecutive time while the GitHub release host answers 504, and the stop rule skips the verification"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 4 at 7d1de9dc8f41 (base 6f806bb8dd) stood on the attempt-3 tree, corrected both protocol timestamp assertions to milliseconds per decision 2941, passed its build (exit 0) and found no anvil on the path: the Foundry installer requested its attestation from the GitHub release host six times and received HTTP 504 each time, as attempt 3 had for the installer script and the release tarball (gotcha 3649). Following the attempt-4 note the attempt recorded the environment log by reference and stopped before the verification without a repair cycle, so neither declared target ran. The same host answered 504 from a second network at 09:24Z and 09:26Z and 200 again at 09:32Z while its status page listed every component operational. Decision 2942 names a second consecutive miss of the same tool as the trigger to review the profile of the task; the profile is right, the release host is the single point of failure."
fix = "Decision 2946: when the release host of a toolchain fails, the qualification environment installs the same version from its container registry image (ghcr.io/foundry-rs/foundry at v1.9.0 for Foundry) and the profile of the task stays as its language declares; 9.35.22 attempt 5 relaunches the attempt-4 tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3653]
title = "The launchpad Go gate learns its failing modules one module per attempt, and a vet refusal in ranking-algo fails a package build that no baseline skip can carry"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 9 at 0e4c9cbbabfc (base 78d0581353) kept the attempt-8 tree, added the eighteen indexer entries, passed its build and the twenty-eight wiring tests; its first verification passed shared, protocol, api and indexer and failed pnl-tracker with 114 cases across eleven packages (test fixtures that run node scripts without their packages, migration, handler and SQL mismatches), which the attempt recorded as baseline entries, and its second verification passed pnl-tracker and failed ranking-algo: go vet refuses internal/app/repair_m934_test.go line 227 (suspect or: len(produced) != len(ranker.Categories) || len(produced) != 8), which fails the package build before any test runs, and the httpapi, ranker and store packages fail because RANKING_TEST_REDIS_URL, RANKING_TEST_POSTGRES_DSN, L19_REDIS_URL and their siblings are unset, variables the module documents and decision 2893 assigns to the job env block. The eleven modules after ranking-algo were never exercised; at two repair cycles per attempt the gate learns one module per attempt. The baseline validator maps every package outside the api, pnl-tracker and indexer sets to 22.39.117, whose scope is the shared and protocol packages."
fix = "Decisions 2947 and 2948: attempt 10 surveys every remaining module before its first gate run and classifies each failing case (configuration gap of the job, vet refusal corrected at its site, baseline entry), and the new task 22.39.168 is the retiring owner of the twelve remaining modules."

[gotcha.3654]
title = "The exactly-once recovery cases assert that a repeated store of the same verified receipt returns the first result, which the receipt store no longer does"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 8 at 4a9d044d4868 (base 2b62d97c5a) kept the attempt-4 tree, received Foundry from the registry image in fourteen seconds after the installer failed (decision 2946), passed its build and ran budget_durable_limits, disclosure and human_node_preparation green before limits-exactly-once failed node_recovery::persisted_receipt_recovers_unsettled_budget_once and node_recovery::lost_response_recovers_receipt_balances_and_budget_once at services/agent/tests/limits/exactly_once.rs line 1640 (left 0, right 1), where the second call of receipt::store_verified_if_absent for the same key is asserted equal to the first. The receipt store changed its ingress path in the restart-recovery repair of 22.30.91 (bfc86ded84, 2026-11-05), the target last ran green under 9.35.17 on 2026-11-03, and the port of this task changed only the authorization construction of the file. Decision 2908 places the failure with the gate owner."
fix = "9.35.22 attempt 9 asserts at line 1640, in both cases, the value the producer defines for a repeated store of the same verified receipt and keeps the exactly-once assertions that follow; a producer that returns a different observation for the same key is recorded as a finding."

[gotcha.3655]
title = "Two real-HTTPS gas station cases read protected material through environment variables and fail instead of skipping when it is absent"
symptom = "Task 22.39.126 attempt 1 at 5f8324a70466 (base 78d0581353) repaired the fourteen interop targets, removed forty-nine baseline entries, passed its build and the wiring test, and both verifications failed only in the station target of layerx-gas-station: authenticated_retry_real_https_retains_unknown_liability_within_deadline (tests/station.rs line 1363) and first_use_replay_state_real_https_preserves_retained_storage (line 1462) return NotPresent for PAXEER_X_STATION_RECOVERY_MATERIAL and PAXEER_X_STATION_FIRST_USE_MATERIAL, the protected material that the owner-run qualification case tools/paxeer-x/gates/20.2.sh requires and that no public job holds. The two migrate cases already skip naming their variables under decision 2821 (do_2), and the repair budget was spent before the station cases were reached."
fix = "Decision 2949: the two station cases follow decision 2821 like the migrate cases; 22.39.126 attempt 2 makes them skip with a reason naming the variable when it is absent."

[gotcha.3656]
title = "The ai-market guest stops 16316 bytes over the bound after the routing function is split into four handler families"
symptom = "Task 22.39.167 attempt 2 at 3445279503f3 (base c26e4bd47049) measured the attempt-1 tree at 505461 bytes, split the 208092-byte routing function transition_inner of the routing module source into the handler families handle_settlement (35992 bytes), handle_assessment (35027), handle_identity (25657) and handle_admission (20701) beside the entry wrapper layerx_call (21278) and epoch::compose (19964), reached 500500 bytes with every step measured through the packaging target and the function metrics pass, passed its build and the dependent check, and stopped at the size test of the verification under the above-bound rule of do_2 with the tables recorded in src/repair_22_39_167.kvx; the five f11 binaries and the module mirror test did not run."
fix = "Decision 2950: attempt 3 outlines one level further (one never-inline body per operation arm, one shared prologue and one shared epilogue, the entry wrapper folded onto the epilogue, the duplicated epoch bodies shared), measured per step, and stops for an owner ruling on a staged bound if the guest is still above it."

[gotcha.3657]
title = "The agent SDK Python suite gate collects two payment test files that still call the retired hosted gateway constructor argument, a lifecycle test that encodes an oversized payload outside its refusal block, a baseline-preservation assertion that forbids the retirement it is asked to make and a TypeScript peer the build step never installs"
symptom = "Task 22.39.119 attempts 2 and 3 at 15297431f074 and 51d796cb3476 (bases 5ce127e35a and 7dc80ac4fc) repaired the seventeen test files of do_1 against their producers, retired forty-six baseline entries, passed the build and verified with forty-seven failures left, none of them in a baseline entry: tests/agent/sdk/python/test_repair_22_31_147.py (24 cases) and test_repair_22_33_17.py (18 cases) call PaymentRpc with the hosted_gateway_endpoint argument and read PaymentRpc.receipt_keys, which the payment RPC module retired when 22.39.137 (a7d39f7f68) gave hosted reads their own client HostedGatewayRpc; that gate ran services/agent/sdk/python/tests only, so the two consumer files were never collected after the producer change. test_program_lifecycle.py test_c_signed_fixtures_and_refusals encodes a 524289-byte deploy payload outside its assertRaises block and the current encoder refuses it at the 524288 bound. test_repair_22_33_702.py line 409 asserts that every baseline entry of 22.39.119 at 3a0f70d0fc remains, which contradicts the retirement this task performs. The two cases of services/agent/sdk/python/tests/test_x402_rpc_surface.py start the TypeScript peer, which fails with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for @noble/hashes because the build step of the task runs no npm ci, while the build step of 22.39.120 does."
fix = "Decisions 2951 and 2952: 22.39.119 attempt 4 carries the two payment files and the baseline-preservation test in its touches, routes hosted reads through HostedGatewayRpc as 22.39.137 recorded, moves the oversized encoding inside the refusal block, rewrites the preservation assertion to the retained-subset form, and its build step installs the TypeScript peer first."

[gotcha.3658]
title = "The journey vocabulary test of the human API schema check asserts one optional field on the evidence material type that has carried three since the receipt-proof v2 change"
symptom = "Task 22.39.161 attempt 1 at f23ff5483369 (base 7dc80ac4fc) rewrote the twenty-seven golden scalar values, placed the golden sets under their operations, re-blessed baseline.kvx, added the schema check step to the human workflow, passed its build, the schema check command (1343 declarations, 95 operations, 285 golden vectors) and the conformance target after one repair cycle, and then failed one case: verification_level_retires_settlement_values_and_maps_rungs of services/human/tools/schema-check/tests/journey_vocabulary.rs line 191 asserts that both type.EvidenceRef and type.EvidenceMaterial declare optional equal to settlement_domain alone, while journeys.kvx line 58 declares optional of EvidenceMaterial as settlement_domain, rung and inclusion_height since the receipt-proof v2 change of 10.92.1 (c55d8901a7, 2026-11-01); the test file last changed on 2026-10-26 and no gate ran it since. The beta driver tests were not reached."
fix = "Decision 2953: the vocabulary test asserts the optional list each section declares; 22.39.161 attempt 2 corrects the assertion at line 191 for EvidenceMaterial, keeps every retired settlement assertion and runs the beta driver tests."

[gotcha.3659]
title = "The first ai-market size reduction was qualified by four f11 targets, so two size passes over the shared helpers of the guest ran without the rest of the crate suite"
symptom = "Task 22.39.142 closed with a verification of four f11 test binaries (f11_family_table, f11_rooms_and_deals, f11_canary_challenge, f11_views) and the module mirror test, and task 22.39.167 names five; the crate programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market holds further f04, f05 and f11 targets (the lap settlement, placement book, payout split and bond targets among them) that no size pass ran, although both passes rewrite the shared helpers, region decoders and status paths every target exercises. The owner ruled on 2026-11-08 that the whole crate suite is run and repaired before the bond operations of 22.38.7 proceed."
fix = "Decision 2955: task 22.39.169 runs the whole crate test suite with no-fail-fast at the current main, repairs every red case following its producer, and 22.38.7 requires it."

[gotcha.3660]
title = "The exactly-once recovery cases assert the receipt in the without-evidence bucket of the inventory, which the authenticated receipt ingress has not produced since the current evidence record landed"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 9 at 63ef7855ac5c (base aa0364696612) corrected the repeated-store assertion as attempt 9 was ruled and passed its build, the preparation targets and the repeated-receipt checks; both node_recovery cases of services/agent/tests/limits/exactly_once.rs then failed at line 1649, where the test expects one entry in inventory.without_evidence and finds none. The ingress the test uses, AuthenticatedTransactionReceipt::store_if_absent of src/receipt.rs (line 971), writes the current transaction evidence record (version 2) under the evidence key of the transaction hash when it stores the receipt (line 1007), and evidence_inventory (line 513) places such a receipt in with_current_evidence, the bucket 22.31.559 added on 2026-11-05 (8950f604bf) so that restart recovery reads budgets from current evidence; without_evidence holds only older store records that carry no evidence at all. The sibling consumer tests/outbox_recover.rs line 381 already asserts with_current_evidence for the same path; the exactly-once suite last changed on 2026-11-05 (be51963de0) without following the new bucket, and the attempt-9 ruling repeated the stale bucket name when it told the attempt to keep the assertion. The attempt recorded the conflict and stopped, as ruled."
fix = "Decision 2958: the inventory assertion of a consumer test names the bucket the ingress path it uses writes; 9.35.22 attempt 10 asserts one with_current_evidence record for the stored transaction hash and empty with_evidence and without_evidence lists."

[gotcha.3661]
title = "The container check scans the qualification ledger fixture of the decision tool for unflagged docker build mentions, so the tools Python gate fails on prose"
symptom = "Task 22.39.144 attempt 2 at 9fcc072c7f2c (base 78d058135385) repaired every selected paxeer-x case and retired forty-three baseline entries; its second verification left two cases red in tools/containers: test_check_all_services_scope and test_paxd_images, both running tools/containers/check.sh, which failed with the message that docker build invocations without --file rely on a Dockerfile at the context root. The hits it printed are six lines of tools/jev/tests/fixtures/ledger/beta-qualification.kvx (3811, 3819, 5179, 5618, 11064 and 11088), assumption and observed sentences of a committed qualification ledger that mention docker build in prose. The scan of check.sh (lines 262 to 281, brought to the current tree by 22.39.158 at 59516c3c0b on 2026-11-08 05:39Z) greps the whole tree with two exclusion lists; REFERENCE_EXEMPT names the spec tree, the changelogs, GOTCHA.kvx and the audit repair records as history or data, and the jev ledger fixture, committed by 1c428496c4 at 05:04Z the same morning, is the same kind of data and is not in the list. No open task touches tools/containers, so the whole-package gate owner carries the exclusion under decision 2908."
fix = "Decision 2959: committed qualification ledgers under tools/jev/tests/fixtures are reference-exempt in the container scan; 22.39.144 attempt 3 adds the exclusion with check.sh in its touches."

[gotcha.3662]
title = "The gate shell of the qualification environment drops variables whose names contain KEY or SECRET, so the live campaign verification ran without the two store access values"
symptom = "Task 22.37.31 attempt 1 at 13886c82d8c3 (base fe41f662e5) passed its build and wrote the 29-case inventory spec/layerx-merge/source-control/live-campaign.kvx, the campaign runner in the support directory of the vendored tree, the admitted statuses of the registry and the redaction of store values in the sparse host fixture; the verification exited 77 because the sparse live proof reported S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY absent while S3_ENDPOINT, S3_REGION and S3_BUCKET were present (the gate asserts S3_BUCKET itself). The qualification environment supplied all five at launch; the shell the agent runs its gate commands from removes, by its policy, every variable whose name contains KEY, SECRET or TOKEN, so only the three names without those words reached the driver, the sparse proof was recorded UNRUN with the two names, and every object-store case stayed UNRUN with the same two names. Separately the campaign runner returns 1 whenever any registry case is UNRUN, so the gate could not pass even with the proof executed while the manifest-bound, failover and provider cases that decision 2957 leaves UNRUN remain so."
fix = "Decision 2960: the environment passes the five store variables through to the gate shell of the 22.37 tasks with every other credential class still excluded, and the campaign runner exits 0 when the sparse proof passed against the real store and no executed case failed, recording every unexecuted case UNRUN with its named missing input; 22.37.31 attempt 2 reruns the campaign on that basis."

[gotcha.3663]
title = "The lifecycle registration of a prepared call records only the envelope bound, so a preparation whose payload bound is earlier never expires at it"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 10 at 3456c981b1be (base c72a7872d0) passed its build, the two node_recovery cases of the exactly-once suite with the receipt evidence inventory of decision 2958, and every target of the verification except prepare_expiry, where two cases failed at lines 169 and 238 expecting preparations 11 and 12, then 13, expired at sequence 1011 and finding none. The test prepares its call through prepare_bound since task 9.35.19 landed (41390400af, 2026-11-08); that disclosure carries payload_expires_at 1010 and a later envelope not_after, and the same commit changed register_inner of src/prepare/expiry.rs from the retired lifecycle facts helper to prepared.disclosure.expiry.not_after alone, while the durable preparation record of the same file (line 1370) and its restore check (line 1446) take the earlier of not_after and payload_expires_at. The in-memory lifecycle therefore keeps a preparation alive past its payload bound, admits its submission and holds its reservations; the test asserts the earlier bound the durable record already applies. Attempt 9 never reached this target because the exactly-once suite failed first."
fix = "Decision 2961: a retained preparation expires at the earlier of its envelope bound and its payload bound in every record form; 9.35.22 attempt 11 aligns register_inner with the durable record and carries the source file in its touches."

[gotcha.3664]
title = "The command guard resolves the package scripts of a page that states its working directory against the root, and parses a comma-joined endpoint list as one URL"
symptom = "Task 22.39.92 attempt 2 at 3b492a1345 (base 1f7197cc70) passed its build and eight of the ten guard cases after two repair cycles; two remain. test_doc_package_scripts_exist resolves the npm run commands of tests/integration/rpc_tests/README.md (lines 138 to 152) against the root package.json although the page states that all commands run from tests/integration/rpc_tests/ and that directory holds a package.json defining rpc:geth, rpc:fork, rpc:bootstrap, rpc:run and rpc:ci; the guard honours a preceding sentence of the form run from this directory and the page_roots map of tests/ci/data/docs_command_roots.json, which maps only the hardhat subpath of that page. test_doc_public_rpc_hosts_use_root_path reads the value of ETHEREUM_JSONRPC_HTTP_URLS in services/explorer/backend/apps/ethereum_jsonrpc/README.md line 31, a comma-joined list of two root endpoints, as one URL whose path then holds the second endpoint, and refuses it although both endpoints satisfy decision 2521."
fix = "Decision 2962: the guard maps a page that states its working directory through page_roots and checks each endpoint of a comma-joined list on its own; 22.39.92 attempt 3 adds the page root and the split."

[gotcha.3665]
title = "The proof test opens the idempotency store on the root the outbox already wrote, where the outbox pending marker of kind Idempotency does not decode as an idempotency record"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 11 at 390327c4ad89 (base ca33c0c50b) applied the register_inner alignment of decision 2961 and the canonical private test directory of decision 2931 to tests/proof_agentd.rs, passed its build, and the verification then failed one case: pending_attempt_recovers_original_hash_height_and_exact_request panicked with Corrupt at the checked helper (line 36). The ported case now enqueues the signed transaction through the raw submit route of the human API into the outbox on the test root before it opens the idempotency store on the same root; the outbox writes a pending marker under ObjectKind::Idempotency keyed by the submission id (src/outbox/mod.rs line 288), and idempotency::Store::open (src/idempotency.rs line 115) restores every Idempotency object of the tenant and refuses one that does not decode as an LXID record. The human runtime and the session control write further objects of that kind under string prefixes (human-owner-action-v1, mcp-invocation-v1), so the idempotency store can only ever open on a directory of its own: the daemon opens it per tenant under the idempotency root (src/human_runtime.rs line 2621), and the sibling case prepared_signatures_cross_the_human_api_and_recover_exact_outbox_bytes already opens it on a second Directory (lines 271 and 321). The case on main never shared the root because it did not enqueue; the port introduced the sharing."
fix = "Decision 2963: a test that opens the idempotency store beside the shared store gives it a directory of its own, the daemon layout; 9.35.22 attempt 12 opens the three sites of the pending case on a second Directory."

[gotcha.3666]
title = "The interop suite repair refreshed the workspace lockfile its crate-directory touches do not cover, so the passing result is held"
symptom = "Task 22.39.126 attempt 2 at 496fe1c9bd77 (base e586fd17d347) passed its build and its verification (every suite of the four crates green, the 49 baseline entries retired) and its result was held with one finding: services/interop/Cargo.lock changed outside touches and planned paths. The attempt added libtest-mimic 0.8.1 and sha2 as test dependencies of layerx-gas-station and layerx-migrate in their Cargo.toml files and refreshed the lockfile of the interop workspace as decisions 2513 and 2790 require; the touches of the task name the four crate directories rather than their manifests, so the exception of decision 2829 (a lockfile beside a manifest named in touches) did not apply, and the planned paths list only the record file. The lockfile refresh follows the two added dependencies and nothing else."
fix = "Decision 2964: a task whose touches cover a crate directory lists the lockfile of every workspace that resolves the crate among its planned paths, and a held result whose only finding is that lockfile is published once the record is corrected; 22.39.126 lists services/interop/Cargo.lock from this round and attempt 2 publishes without a rerun."

[gotcha.3667]
title = "Two consecutive calls of the free port helper of the launchpad gateway tests hand PostgreSQL and Redis the same port, so the export capability case fails"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 10 at 5bc20d955595 passed its build, repaired one wiring case of tests/ci/test_launchpad_go_tests_wired.py within its one cycle, and the second verification then passed every launchpad module from shared to trading-charts before the gateway module failed one case: TestRepair_48_export_capability of services/launchpad/gateway/internal/proxy/proof_launchpad_gateway_test.go line 465. The helper freePort at line 363 opens a listener on port zero, reads the port and closes the listener, and line 441 calls it twice in one statement for the PostgreSQL and the Redis service, so both received port 33641 and the second service could not bind. The app package carries the same helper twice (internal/app/app_test.go line 306 and internal/app/identity_peers_test.go line 348) with eleven callers across the three files. A port chosen and released before the next one is chosen is free only until the next choice; the helper has to hold every listener until all ports of the test are chosen."
fix = "Decision 2965: a test that starts several owned services chooses distinct ports with the listeners held together until all are chosen, and the gate owner corrects the helper and its sibling copies; 22.39.75 attempt 11 corrects the three files."

[gotcha.3668]
title = "Three launchpad modules fail before any test runs and the remaining Makefile stages were never reached, so the whole-package gate owner carries the module manifests and a separate task carries the stages"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 10 stopped at the gateway module, and the modules after it in the services/launchpad/Makefile list cannot run as the tree stands: go list ./... in notifications and in security answers that the module requires updates to go.mod (both declare their shared and discovery dependencies with a replace to the sibling directory but their go.sum and requirements are stale under GOWORK off), and user imports core/notifications from internal/app/repair_m1062_test.go line 20 while user/go.mod carries no require and no replace for that module. The baseline of the per-module runner can carry failing test case names only, never a discovery or compile failure, so 22.39.168 cannot absorb these three modules. The ci target of the Makefile (line 42) chains build, vet, fmt-check, lint, race and cover-check after the tests; no public workflow and no document runs those stages, the lint stage needs golangci-lint which the qualification environment does not carry, and the race stage repeats every module under the race detector, so the gate of 22.39.75 could not finish within its limit even with every test green."
fix = "Decisions 2966 and 2967: the manifest repairs of notifications, security and user belong to 22.39.75 under decision 2908, the gate of 22.39.75 runs what the public job runs (the wiring suite and make test), and task 22.39.170 brings the remaining ci stages to green and runs them from the public launchpad workflow."

[gotcha.3669]
title = "The AI market suite repair attributed its fuel regression, lost a build cycle to a dependency download and left four classes of refusal mismatch, one of them a regression of its own reader repair"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 31 at 568123b3f048 (base 7dc80ac4fc2f) used three builds, one verification and two repair cycles. The first build at 0a1746a443bf failed because the archive download of a dependency answered HTTP 504, the only such failure across the recent logs of the crate; the second build at e24f0abd2ec7 passed; the verification at that revision failed seventeen targets. The attempt attributed the fuel regression per decision 2940: at 075a770edb the guest index copy became a never-inline per-element copy (plus 970383 fuel, minus 17443 bytes) and the payout split moved Fund by 7 fuel; restoring the inlined slice copy brought the packaged Fund measurement to 802503 (197465 under the 999968 allowance) with the packaged guest at 485540 bytes (38644 under the bound), apply_fund writing the authenticated replay digest instead of rehashing, and the routing module passing the validated request digest. The attempt then made a reader repair (the direct evidence, evaluator admission, commit-reveal, task, reward and closure readers validate the joint F07 and F08 section through the shared producer decoder before decoding the F08 suffix) and the third build at 568123b3 passed with no verification budget left. Four classes remain: (a) a13_manifest_grammar_refusals_before_mutation in the lifecycle target of the identity module (line 607) expects BAD_VERSION for a version-1 body tagged 2 while the manifest decoder of the identity module (line 583) accepts versions 1 and 2 and answers NON_CANONICAL, which the capabilities test of the version-2 manifest requires for a truncated body, and the case fails at the restored main tree as well; (b) a09_dropped_responses_reconcile_by_query_and_retry_until_expiry of f04_recovery.rs (line 1440) expects F03_REPORT_ALREADY_FINAL while commit_reveal.rs answers CONFLICT, a case absent from the main baseline, so the reader repair reordered the admission checks; (c) native_selectors_preserve_exact_routed_refusals of host_boundary.rs (line 1029) expects the F07 refusal for a missing record (errors.rs line 215) for the selectors 0x0701 to 0x0703 with an outsider principal while the producer answers UNAUTHORIZED, and the documentation of epoch.rs lines 1600 to 1608 states the missing-record refusal without an F07 region or record and UNAUTHORIZED for any other actor; (d) native_f03_schedule_capacity_role_conflicts_and_revocation and three native host_boundary cases decode a stage 5 callback failure with status minus 3 (NON_CANONICAL) published by the runtime at programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_call.rs line 3446 after the call occupancy settlement at the second native call of the case, because the native replay support of the crate (tests/support/native_replay.rs) does not carry the published occupancy ledger from one call to the next."
fix = "Decision 2968: the suite owner follows the landed producer for (a), restores the producer order for (b) and (c) and carries the occupancy ledger in the native replay support for (d) with the runtime unchanged; 22.99.77 attempt 32 runs the full suite first, records the after list and then makes the four repairs."

[gotcha.3670]
title = "The native lifecycle debit settlement identifies the actor by the call disclosure actor while its own allocation check uses the envelope actor DID, so the wind-down cases of the lifecycle repair test fail"
symptom = "Task 9.35.22 attempt 12 at c96ee7ed4414 (base 7d49f6b87c) corrected the three idempotency opens, passed its build and every target up to repair_22_31_217, where two cases failed at line 1807 (repair_execution_account_exists_funded_unfrozen_wind_down and repair_lifecycle_native_envelope_deploy_upgrade_wind_down_and_restart): settle(&store) answered Err(Preparation). The helper restored() of the test is identical on main and in the attempt and binds the EVM sender bytes as the actor of the retained carrier. The producer src/budget/program_lifecycle_settlement.rs line 1904 (native_lifecycle_debits) derives the actor it passes to committed_exit_debit from the disclosure actor of the prepared call, while src/budget/native_settlement.rs line 170 compares the owner of the human subject with the envelope actor DID and derives the allocation actor from the same envelope actor, so the owner check and the allocation check of one settlement see two actors. The target never ran in attempt 11 because cargo stops at the first failing target and proof_agentd sorts before it; the only agent-daemon change between the two bases is the agent SDK Python suite."
fix = "Decision 2969: the lifecycle debit settlement identifies the actor by the envelope actor DID, 9.35.22 owns the two settlement sources, and declared-target daemon gates run with no-fail-fast so every target reports; 9.35.22 attempt 13 corrects native_lifecycle_debits."

[gotcha.3671]
title = "The human API schema check and its crate tests are green while the beta driver inventory fails inside the same gate without per-case output, and the inventory belongs to the qualification suite owner"
symptom = "Task 22.39.161 attempt 2 at d85c25147bc4 (verified revision c2899bf12994, base 0edc903b4a) passed its build, the schema check of services/human/schema/human-api and every schema-check crate test; the verification then failed two cases of tools/qualification/test_beta_driver.py (test_adoption_inventory_executes_against_the_local_paxd_stack and test_multichain_inventory_reports_absent_infrastructure_as_failed) after 279 seconds, each asserting at line 256 that the real_stack flag of the evidence is true. The flag is true only when every case record of the inventory passed with evidence from the replay peer the suite starts; the driver runs cargo tests, Go sample runs and make targets per case and writes per-case output under build/beta-driver-test, which the attempt did not collect, so the failing case is unknown. No public workflow runs the file; 22.31.623 (pending, wave 2) owns tools/qualification, already requires 22.39.161 and runs the whole qualification directory. The record commit came after the verified revision, so the candidate did not match even for the green part."
fix = "Decision 2970: the schema-check gate of 22.39.161 runs the schema check and its crate tests, and the beta driver inventory is proven by 22.31.623; 22.39.161 attempt 3 runs the narrowed gate once at its final revision."

[gotcha.3672]
title = "The joined-service preparation of the launchpad web suite fails at a readiness URL without naming the role, loses its evidence directory with the environment and discovers service startup requirements one at a time"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 5 at 9cac716c3d5e (base 1d56709c2764) passed both builds; the first verification at ed4c35130cf9 stopped before Vitest because the indexer requires RPC_URLS when its log source is rpc-getlogs while the producer supplied RPC_URL; the attempt reproduced the preparation outside the gate and found two further startup refusals (the retired webhook delivery configuration, which the indexer refuses in favour of its Redis fan-out, and the gateway identity configuration requiring a bare HTTPS PUBLIC_URL and HTTPS origins while the chart harness declares a loopback HTTP browser origin), repaired all three, and the second verification at 9cac716c3d5e failed again at Preparing joined services with the only message Joined process exited 1 followed by a readiness URL on port 39843. The producer src/widgets/trading/run-joined-services.py names no role in that message, writes its result and every service log into a private temporary directory that does not survive the environment, and chooses the six role ports one at a time through a helper that binds port zero and closes the listener before the next choice (the pattern of gotcha 3667), so the failing role, its exit reason and its log are unknown and neither suite ran. Every service documents its required configuration in its own configuration loader under services/launchpad, so the requirement set is derivable before a gate run rather than by one refusal per run."
fix = "Decision 2971: a joined-service preparation names the failing role and keeps its result and logs under the repository build directory, chooses its ports per decision 2965, and is reproduced to readiness of every role outside the gate before the gate pair runs; 22.39.95 attempt 6 applies it."

[gotcha.3673]
title = "The record of the legacy preparation deletion names the active EVM files instead of the legacy ones, and the legacy types have sixty-four consumer sites in nine sources outside its seven touches"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 1 at bd82359bfca3 (base 097581705c2e) followed its record and deleted src/prepare/disclose.rs and src/prepare/restore_tests.rs of the agent daemon crate, which are the active EVM binding and its fixture since the audit repairs of 2026-11-04 (7527715d65 and d693490680) moved the legacy module to src/prepare/legacy_disclose.rs and src/prepare/legacy_restore_tests.rs under a path attribute block pub mod legacy at src/prepare/mod.rs lines 433 to 951 and the kernel signing helpers to src/sign_legacy.rs included by src/sign.rs lines 42 to 44; the first build failed because test_support.rs still includes restore_tests.rs, the attempt restored that fixture, and the second build failed with sixty-four errors in budget/native_binding.rs (30), human_runtime.rs (17), budget/native_settlement.rs (9), session_control.rs (4), policy/approval.rs and admin.rs: the fields envelope, signing_preimage and observed_head_sequence of the legacy Prepared, the idempotency_key of the legacy PrepareRequest and the items CorePreparationBoundary, CorePreparationState, CoreStateError and ProductionCorePreparationBoundary, which pub use legacy::* exports as the prepare root items and which budget/program_lifecycle_settlement.rs, budget/program_settlement.rs, budget/program_sources.rs and seven integration tests name as well. The task carried seven touches and a thirty-minute limit for a migration of the whole crate, and its grep gate matches the two audit records and tests/repair_22_33_1532.rs on main, so it could not pass even after a complete deletion."
fix = "Decision 2972: the deletion owns every consumer of the legacy types in the crate, names the live legacy files, derives each legacy field from the EVM preparation with the producer it follows, and its gate greps Rust sources only and runs the consumer test targets; 9.35.24 attempt 2 starts again from main with the widened touches and a 300-minute limit."

[gotcha.3674]
title = "Two tasks repaired the whole AI market crate suite in parallel, and the requalification build omits the funding fixture producer while a source change grew a native trace past the published replay profile"
symptom = "Task 22.39.169 attempt 1 at 6b55e8a57398 (base 0edc903b4a41) passed its build twice (guest 504779 bytes under the 524184 bound) and failed the whole-crate verification twice: 21 targets and 161 cases at the first sweep, 11 targets and 84 cases at the final tree. Task 22.99.77 attempt 31 at 568123b3f048 repaired the same suite from the same main with 17 failing targets, and the two attempts changed the same five production files (closure.rs, commit_reveal.rs, evaluators/admission.rs, evidence.rs, tasks.rs) and twelve of the same test files, so two tasks carried one repair in parallel and neither could land on the other. The record of attempt 1 names three external blockers. The funding fixture under programs/target/repair-478 that the fuel budget cases read is written by the Go fixture test of rpc/repair_478_test.go, which the build command of 22.99.77 runs and the build command of 22.39.169 does not. The native f03 schedule case failed at both revisions because the execution trace of its short CALL exceeded the 256-boundary replay profile the C harness publishes (tests/programs/test_ai_host_boundary.c line 331: the deployed guest records 227 boundaries), while attempt 31 of 22.99.77 at the same main showed no such refusal, so a source change of attempt 1 grew the trace. The identity-section refusal case (feature_availability returning ContentUnavailable where the test requires NON_CANONICAL) is one of the refusal classes decision 2968 assigns to 22.99.77."
fix = "Decision 2973: 22.39.169 requires 22.99.77 and requalifies the suite on the main tree that carries the inventory repair, its build produces the funding fixture before the guest build, and a source change that makes a native case exceed the published replay profile is restored; attempt 2 starts from main after 22.99.77 lands."

[gotcha.3675]
title = "The launchpad api module manifest declares go 1.25.0 while the notifications module it requires now declares 1.27.0, so go vet refuses the api module"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 11 at 240a6b6d5fa9 (base d448f80c159b) carried the distinct-port helper of decision 2965 (services/launchpad/gateway/internal/internaltest/ports.go and its three callers) and the module manifest repairs of decision 2966 for the notifications, security and user modules, and its build failed at go vet in services/launchpad/api with the message updates to go.mod needed: the tidy of the notifications module raised its go directive to 1.27.0 because its go-pglite dependency requires it, the api module requires the notifications module and still declares go 1.25.0, and the Go tool refuses to vet it until its manifest states 1.27.0 and its checksum file follows. The api manifests are outside the touches of the task (the record names the notifications, security and user directories but not api), the agent asked for the two files and stopped, the verification never ran, and a one-line manifest change cost the attempt."
fix = "Decision 2974: a launchpad module tidy that raises a go directive raises the directive of every module that requires it in the same attempt, and the gate owner carries those manifests by file; 22.39.75 attempt 12 raises the api manifest to go 1.27.0 with its checksum file in the touches."

[gotcha.3676]
title = "The legacy preparation deletion compiles its own crate but two test targets of other crates in the cross-root dependents check still import the removed core preparation names"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 2 at 95fa8138cbb6 (build revision 5186826b1866, base 81f0e5a93ff9) restored the attempt-1 files to main, deleted the three legacy files and the legacy region of prepare/mod.rs, migrated the twenty-two in-crate consumers its record lists to the EVM preparation producers, and passed its build of the daemon and every test target without a repair. The gate then ran the cross-root dependents check before the verification and it failed with exit 101 at two test targets outside the crate: the SDK test services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/tests/repair_22_31_547.rs line 16 imports CorePreparationBoundary and ProductionCorePreparationBoundary to read observed_head_sequence from a preparation state, and the human intents compile test services/human/crates/layerx-intents/tests/compile.rs lines 1 to 4 imports prepare_activity, verify_disclosure_binding, CorePreparationBoundary, CorePreparationState, CoreStateError, DisclosureBindingError, PreparationDefaults, PrepareError and PrepareRequest unaliased, implements the removed trait on a recorded double (line 58) and drives prepare_activity and verify_disclosure_binding in two cases (lines 209 to 230 and 374). Both files are outside the touches of the task, so the agent recorded the two blockers and stopped before the verification. The EVM producers the consumers follow are in prepare/mod.rs: EvmPreparationState with head_height (line 15), evm::prepare_activity over the production EVM boundary (line 310), prepare_bound as the deterministic construction from an observed state (line 332), verify_call_binding with CallBindingError (line 371), and the aliased EvmPreparationDefaults, EvmPrepareRequest and EvmPrepareError."
fix = "Decision 2975: the deletion owns every consumer of the removed names that the cross-root dependents check compiles, in whichever crate it lives; the two test files join the touches of 9.35.24 and its verification checks both crates, and attempt 3 migrates them to the EVM producers."

[gotcha.3677]
title = "The cross-root dependents check stops at the first crate that fails, so a deletion of public names learns one out-of-crate consumer per attempt unless the owner enumerates them all first"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 3 at 622839667701 (build revision 63965127afc7, base bff9de79e47f) migrated the SDK test and the human intents compile test the previous round named, passed its build without a repair, and the cross-root dependents check failed again at the next crate in its order: services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/tests/session_keys.rs line 19 imports the removed CorePreparationBoundary, CorePreparationState and CoreStateError, so the attempt recorded the blocker and stopped before the verification, exactly as attempt 2 had for the first two consumers. A search of the agent, human and interop roots for the removed names shows that the human service test targets carry seven such consumers in all, every one a journey test that implements the removed core boundary trait on its own double of the daemon boundary while the production sources of the human service no longer consume the trait: agent_controls_rungs.rs, custody.rs, journey_faults.rs, move_money.rs and session_keys.rs import the trait, its state and its error; key_export.rs also calls verify_disclosure_binding and restore_canonical (lines 311 to 313); wallet_identity_e2e.rs also calls prepare_activity_for_protocol, attach_kernel_signature and verify_kernel_before_submit. Four of them already build the EVM transaction of the same journey through prepare_bound (agent_controls_rungs.rs line 1214, journey_faults.rs line 290, move_money.rs line 210), so the legacy branch of each case sits beside its EVM branch. The check compiles nineteen crates in a fixed order and reports only the first failure, so the record of the task can never be completed from the check alone."
fix = "Decision 2976: a task that removes public names enumerates every out-of-crate consumer with a search of the three workspace roots before its attempt and carries them all in its touches; 9.35.24 attempt 4 migrates the seven human service test targets together and its verification compiles that crate."

[gotcha.3678]
title = "The ai-market inventory repair spends both gate reruns on a stale verification and a fuel refusal, so a thirteen-file repair of the crate suite ends unverified"
symptom = "Task 22.99.77 attempt 32 at 4206f461379d (base 81f0e5a93ff9) ran its first build at 0bcb816315a0 (Fund 802503 CPU fuel, guest 505918 bytes) and the declared verification at the same tree, which failed twelve targets: the F03 evaluator host (six cases whose refusals stayed in place for unsorted and duplicate vectors, an empty vector, a wrong domain, a corrupted roster and role conflicts), the F04 windows (five cases), the F05 aggregation runtime (five cases), the fuel budget (OPEN_EPOCH at 1000010 and three RevealScore calls between 1000001 and 1000008 against the 1000000 CPU cap), the host boundary (nine native cases; the first occupancy finalization at block 10 refused with CONTEXT_MISMATCH -213 because the C harness started below block height one against a genesis last occupancy batch of zero), the reward reopen case of repair_22_33_261 line 1280 (rewards::apply accepted a joint F07/F08 section that the landed test refuses with BAD_VERSION), the reputation lifecycle (four cases), the reputation vectors (one), the native rewards (three) and the task state boundary (one). The agent then repaired the suite across thirteen source files, the C harness and the replay support (state reuse without re-serializing the stripped frame, the F03 boundary decoder, root scratch capacity, fixture atomicity in four test helpers, the harness block height), spent the second build on a Fund refusal (802525 against 802503), passed the third build at the final tree and was refused a second verification, so the attempt ended implemented-not-qualified with none of that repair verified; its record still claims the reader repair rightly accepts the joint section that the landed consumer test refuses. No gate command was preceded by a local run of the suite it had to pass."
fix = "Decision 2977: a whole-crate gate owner brings the crate suite to green locally before its single build and verification pair, and rewards::apply keeps its strict section version check while callers read the admission suffix through the joint table; 22.99.77 attempt 33 continues from 4206f461379d with a 300 minute limit."

[gotcha.3679]
title = "The reclaim journey case asserts a legacy preparation record of its own boundary double, whose context-bound defund disclosure no EVM call binder produces"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 4 at base 20cf44679e3f (tree fffb576516ea) stopped before any gate under the legacy-only-field clause of decision 2976: the reclaim case of services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/tests/agent_controls_rungs.rs (every_reclaim_mechanism_uses_real_agent_receipts_and_projects_activity) decodes the reclaim type-2 transaction, asserts the Pay precompile target, the budgetDefund selector, the budget id, the amount, nonce, fee, sender, receipt and activity projection on the EVM branch, and then looks up a preparation record of the test boundary double (the 0x71 preparation) and asserts its envelope activity type and a DisclosedNativeOperation::BudgetDefund context with balance, asset, budget account, owner, source account and observed head. That context is produced only by the legacy envelope binder bind_budget_mutation through prepare_budget_mutation_for_protocol, both deleted by the task; the call binder of layerx-crypto (disclosure/call.rs lines 1260 to 1281) sets a Payer counterparty and a Transfer amount for PayBudgetDefund and leaves native_operation and budget_context unset. The record also shows that human_runtime.rs prepared_budget_context (line 19746) reads a budget fund, defund or revoke native operation from an EVM preparation that the call binder never produces, and that budget_mutation_context (line 12486) has no caller."
fix = "Decision 2978: the preparation-record block goes with the removed boundary double, the case asserts the call disclosure and the budget facts through the EVM producers, and the human runtime budget path observation is recorded as a finding; 9.35.24 attempt 5 continues from fffb576516ea."

[gotcha.3680]
title = "The social module of the launchpad refuses its manifest under the raised toolchain exactly as the api module did, and the gate finds it one module per attempt"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 12 at f5056671f0c6 (base 1d8f18989ce7) raised the api manifest and passed its build; its first verification failed in the proxy package of the gateway module, where four callers of repair_48_test.go still named the port helper removed by the previous attempt (repaired within the cycle onto the shared helper), and the second verification at the final tree failed in the two gateway proofs that build the social daemon: go refused services/launchpad/social/cmd/sociald with the message that go.mod needs an update, the same manifest refusal gotcha 3675 recorded for the api module, since services/launchpad/social/go.mod declares go 1.25.0 while its requirements now need a higher directive. Both repair cycles were spent and the attempt ended implemented-not-qualified. Every launchpad module shares the go.work, so a manifest refusal in any of them is visible to one local go build across the work file before any gate."
fix = "Decision 2979: a launchpad gate owner builds and vets every module of the go.work and every daemon the proofs build locally before the gate pair, raising each refused directive in one pass; 22.39.75 attempt 13 does so from f5056671f0c6."

[gotcha.3681]
title = "Eighty-six qualification suite cases assert the former native library recipe and three former workflow commands after their producers moved on main"
symptom = "Task 22.31.623 attempt 5 at aa2a06c06db1 (base 1d8f18989ce7) settled its four authorized cases and passed its build twice; the verification failed twice (89 then 86 of about 4450 cases, 535 seconds at the final tree). Eighty-odd cases across tools/qualification/audit_repairs assert that the root Makefile recipe paxd-native-libs reads $(LIBRARY) programs-release-build, as a literal or as a parsed prerequisite list, while main since 8ea5577a87 (2026-11-08, the evmone shared library target) reads $(LIBRARY) programs-release-build evmone-lib; test_repair_22_33_699 asserts the node job runs go test ./node/... while the job now passes timeout and count flags; test_repair_22_31_605 asserts a literal vitest command where the wallet job now expands a matrix expression; test_repair_22_33_700 holds a workflow digest baseline the landed workflows no longer match; test_repair_22_33_898 asserts a wallet manifest dependency set that changed; test_repair_22_33_850 indexes a container check list that is shorter than it expects. All of them are consumers of producers that landed on main after the attempt tree was cut, and the gate owner of the whole suite owns them under decision 2908."
fix = "Decision 2980: a qualification suite case that asserts a recipe or command states the producer content on main, and the whole-suite gate owner settles every producer move the merged tree shows in one attempt; 22.31.623 attempt 6 settles the 86 cases grouped by producer after a local run to green."

[gotcha.3682]
title = "The joined-services setup of the launchpad web tests asks the rest role for the public snapshot route, which the api mounts under the test environment only on a process that runs the stream"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 6 at 30d180caaaa2 (base 8e8996fbd8) passed its build and the mobile suite, and the web suite stopped in the trade journey at the joined-services step: the readiness probe of run-joined-services.py (stream_ready, line 48) asks the api process started with API_ROLE rest for GET /v2/snapshots and received 404 page not found, so the setup refused with the message that the required public snapshot route is not mounted. The api mounts that route in two places only: rest.RegisterProductionReads with RegisterSnapshots true, which registerREST of app.go (line 398) reaches only when NODE_ENV is production, and the hub of internal/ws (ws.go line 147), which app.go registers only on a process whose role is not rest (line 325) together with the development stream (line 369). The setup exports NODE_ENV test to every process, so its rest process registers the development reads and returns before the snapshot route; the development stream test of the api (dev_stream_test.go line 305) boots the application under the development environment with no role and reads /v2/snapshots from that one process. The same probe existed in the attempt-5 tree, so the refusal predates attempt 6; the api code is outside the touches of the task and needs no change."
fix = "Decision 2981: under the test environment the joined-services setup runs the api as one process without a role, the configuration the development stream test proves, and points the REST upstream, the stream origin and the readiness probe at it; 22.39.95 attempt 7 corrects the setup and keeps the api unchanged."

[gotcha.3683]
title = "The whole-crate gate of the legacy preparation deletion runs the TLS identity cases without the boundary executable they need and an approval stream case that opens the durable store on a default-mode root"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 5 at 1c8c961ddb28 (record tree 05d2264af3a8, base c920132492) passed its build, the removed-name greps, the SDK and human check targets and every migration target, and the crate suite failed three cases in two targets. The two lib cases outbound_tls::private_ca_checks_the_actual_server_identity and ops::program::simulation_tls_checks_the_actual_server_identity panic at services/platform/tests/support/tls_boundary.rs line 186 with the producer input message of decision 2325: the layerx-paxeer-boundary executable of services/platform/Cargo.toml must be built before the case runs, and the gate of the task builds only the agent daemon and never exports LAYERX_PAXEER_BOUNDARY_BIN, while every other gate that runs the lib target of the daemon builds the boundary in its build step and names the executable through that variable (the gates of 22.31.535 and the ops::program repairs). The approval_events case approval_lifecycle_stream_resumes_after_gap_and_exports_digest_evidence (line 405) creates its store root with create_dir_all and opens Store on it, which the protected root check of src/store/protected.rs refuses as not a canonical owned private directory, the same setup defect gotcha 3638 and decision 2931 ruled for write_path_evm.rs; the file is in the touches of the task and no gate ran it since the check landed. The attempt recorded both as blockers and stopped at one build and one verification."
fix = "Decision 2982: a gate that runs the lib target of the agent daemon builds the boundary executable in its build step and exports LAYERX_PAXEER_BOUNDARY_BIN in its verification step; the gate of 9.35.24 carries both from this round, and attempt 6 corrects the approval stream root per decision 2931 and runs the crate suite locally to green before the single build and verification pair per decision 2977."

[gotcha.3684]
title = "The Fund production allowance test measures the unprocessed ai-market guest against the deployment bound, so the size task that packages the guest under the bound cannot pass its build gate"
symptom = "Task 22.39.167 attempt 3 at d59fd29efb2f (base 20cf44679e) applied the decision 2950 steps and brought the packaged guest from 500500 to 498845 bytes, under the 500000 bound of decision 2954, with every test unchanged and the tables recorded in src/repair_22_39_167.kvx. Its build gate, which since decision 2940 runs the Fund production allowance test before the packaging target, failed at rpc/repair_478_test.go line 127: the helper repair478Guests compiles the historical and the candidate source in an isolated manifest with the size profile and the Wasm flags of the crate, then asserts the 524184 deployment bound and runs Fund on the raw release module, while the packaging target of the Makefile (paxai-host-boundary-build) passes that module through wasm-opt with the Oz, strip-debug and strip-producers flags before it applies the same bound and the host boundary check; the raw candidate measures 536267 bytes where the packaged one measures 498845, and the raw starting tree 3445279503f3 measured 536460, so the refusal predates the attempt and no size work inside the crate can satisfy a bound the deployment never applies to the raw module. Decision 2940 states the allowance for the packaged production module, and the verification was never reached (one build, no verification)."
fix = "Decision 2983: the Fund production allowance test packages each guest it builds with the wasm-opt pass of the packaging target before the bound and the Fund run, and the task whose gate runs the test corrects the helper with the test file in its touches; 22.39.167 attempt 4 applies it and the attempt-3 tree stands."

[gotcha.3685]
title = "Chain-positioned logs and local-only daemon events share one subscription cursor space, so a recovered chain log is refused as out of order after the ordinal cursors of the approval events"
symptom = "Task 9.35.24 attempt 6 at 92818149c731 (base 403a6bf491) passed its build, the removed-name greps, the SDK and human check targets, the two TLS identity cases with the boundary executable and every migration target, and the approval_events target failed one case at line 342: after the four local-only approval lifecycle events were delivered, accept_front refused the recovered chain log of block 1 with delivery cursor (1, 0, 0) arrived out of order, expected (4, 0, 1). Since the interface-mismatch repair of 22.31.215 (0404bde158, 2026-11-04) the delivery engine derives the cursor of a chain-positioned event from its log position (block height, transaction index, log index) while a daemon event without a position keeps the ordinal cursor (global sequence plus one, 0, 0), and mark_delivered_inner of the subscription store refuses any cursor at or below the last delivery; the four approval events therefore occupy the cursors (1, 0, 0) to (4, 0, 0) and the chain log of block 1 that the ingestor admits after them cannot follow. The approval stream restore case has asserted since 18.1150.1 (3a21c8716) that the recovered log is delivered once after the four approvals, the gate of 22.31.215 ran only its own repair target, and the case has not run under any gate since the protected store root check landed, so the conflict is a producer defect of the cursor derivation that the deletion task neither caused nor owns."
fix = "Decision 2984 and task 22.39.171: one strictly increasing cursor space per subscription covers local-only events and chain-positioned logs in ingestion order, the repair task designs and proves the local cursor derivation, and 9.35.24 requires it; attempt 7 of 9.35.24 continues after it lands."

[gotcha.3686]
title = "The subscription cursor format cannot place a local-only event strictly between two adjacent logs of one block, and the ingestor never admits that order"
symptom = "Task 22.39.171 attempt 1 at af91dcafa5a4 (base 996b8669da) implemented the anchored cursors of decision 2984 and recorded a departure: adjacent raw positions such as block 12, transaction 0, log 0 and log 1 have no strictly intermediate triple in the unchanged u64, u32, u32 cursor format, so to satisfy the requested case of a local-only event between two chain logs of one block the attempt added the count of preceding local insertions within the block to the raw lower bits of every chain log cursor in a mixed stream, captured the anchor in an optional trailer of the event metadata, and added a prefix admission function to the ingestor that journals part of a pending block, which the test uses to interleave. On main the ingestor queues every chain log as pending in ingest_log and journals the logs of a block at new_head, once the block is closed, so a local-only event is only ever journaled between two closed blocks and never between two logs of one block; the adjacent-log case was an artificial order of the task text, and shifting chain cursors breaks the contract of decision 2763 that a chain log is delivered at its block, transaction and log position. The approval stream restore case passed at the attempt tree once its root was created by Store::open, and the six new cases, delivery, gaps, history_block_cursor, subscription_ops_cursor, w7_subscription_permit and repair_22_31_215 passed."
fix = "Decision 2985 amends decision 2984: a local-only event is anchored after the last journaled chain position at the block boundary with cursor (that block height, u32 maximum, a per-anchor counter), chain log cursors stay exact, the prefix admission function and the adjacent-log case are removed, and 22.39.171 attempt 2 reworks the derivation."

[gotcha.3687]
title = "Four pre-existing consumer tests in the agent daemon gate of the cursor task assert interfaces their producers changed on 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-07"
symptom = "At the attempt tree of 22.39.171 attempt 1 four targets failed on cases the attempt did not touch. The legacy reset cases of tests/subscription.rs (line 360) and tests/subscription_cursor_v3.rs (line 205) assert CursorResetRequired, while since the restart-recovery repair of 22.33.1506 (a64f426f67, 2026-11-04) SubscriptionStore::open maps that refusal to UpgradeRequired with the tenant and the subscription identifier, and the record of 22.33.1506 (finding subscription-upgrade-recovery, wiring_request) asked the owning task of the two tests to update their assertions, which never happened. The eight read_account cases of tests/history_served_contract.rs assert that the first page request carries a null cursor, while since the medium repair of 22.33.1521 (4ff5236340, 2026-11-07) HistoryPage::read_account sends the exclusive position (from_height minus one, u32 maximum, u32 maximum) for a request without a cursor, following the record of 22.31.218 that the hosted producer only supports ascending exclusive cursors, and 22.33.1521 touched no contract test. The cross-UID case of tests/repair_22_33_1506.rs (line 750) sets the store root to mode 0777 so the receiver process under uid 65534 can bind its sockets inside it, and the protected root check of 22.30.91 (fde2add099, 2026-11-04) then refuses every later store operation because the root is no longer mode 0700. None of the four targets ran under a gate after those producers landed."
fix = "Decisions 2986 and 2987: the two legacy reset cases assert the UpgradeRequired interface of 22.33.1506 and 22.39.171 attempt 2 owns them with its own targets; task 22.39.172 updates the history contract test to the exclusive cursor of 22.33.1521 and moves the receiver sockets of the cross-UID case out of the store root, and the two targets leave the gate of 22.39.171."

[gotcha.3688]
title = "The history contract fixtures serve a three-field page envelope while the hosted page decoder has required account, chainHeight and freshness since the client repair"
symptom = "Task 22.39.172 attempt 1 at 4a9a0751ef1b (base 6eeea3b075) passed its build, the cross-UID case and the whole repair_22_33_1506 target with the receiver sockets in a sibling directory, and the three cases of repair_22_33_1521; after the first-page cursor update, seven read_account cases of tests/history_served_contract.rs still failed with Sequencer(Malformed) (the eighth, the served refusal, passed), and the reverse window case of tests/repair_22_31_218.rs failed at line 976 with Connection(Malformed). The page helper of the contract test (line 86) and the px_getHistory arm of the local node fixture of repair_22_31_218.rs (line 633) serve the envelope items, next_cursor and indexedHeight only, while the hosted page decoder of layerx-client (sequencer.rs line 877) has required account, indexedHeight, chainHeight and freshness since the interface-mismatch repair of 22.31.221 (fe2e725ea8, 2026-11-04), and HistoryPage::read_account has refused a page whose account differs from the requested account since 22.33.1521 (4ff5236340, 2026-11-07); the own test of 22.33.1521 (line 156) serves the full envelope with the freshness value of apps/web/e2e/fixtures/px-get-unified-history.json. No gate ran either target after 22.33.1521 landed, and the attempt stopped after one verification without using its repair cycle because it read the envelope as outside its task text."
fix = "Decision 2988: the two fixtures serve the hosted history envelope of the producer, and 22.39.172 attempt 2 carries the update with tests/repair_22_31_218.rs added to its touches."

[gotcha.3689]
title = "The whole qualification Python directory under one public check fails 111 cases for a missing cipher module, unpinned versions and a job-layout contract"
symptom = "Task 22.39.26 attempt 3 at 2fba7fe3796d (base 563d285011) added the make target test-qualification-python (python3 -m pytest -q tools/qualification), called it from a step inside the tests-python job of ci.yml, widened the pip line of that job with cryptography and jsonschema, and wrote tests/ci/test_qualification_suites_have_ci_host.py; the first verification stopped on a missing jsonschema module, and the second ran the directory to 111 failed, 4339 passed and 13 skipped in 1196 seconds. Eighty-five failures across tools/qualification/paxeer-x/tests (the repair suites 22.31.318, 22.33.778, 22.33.810, 22.33.861, 22.33.877, 22.33.779, 22.33.791 and 22.33.860) and audit_repairs are one cause, the Crypto package of pycryptodome that tools/qualification/requirements.txt lists and neither the gate interpreter nor the widened pip line installs. Nine failures of test_repair_22_31_451.py (eight advisory cases and the frozen-lock case) assert that the installed cryptography, pytest and jsonschema equal the pinned versions of tools/launchpad/production/load/requirements.lock, which tools/qualification/requirements.txt mirrors, while the gate interpreter and the widened pip line installed cryptography 50.0.2 unpinned. test_ci_runs_both_make_targets_in_separate_jobs of test_repair_22_31_605.py line 79 asserts the exact pip line of the tests-python job and fails on the widened line. One case of test_repair_22_33_761.py line 215 finds no opened durable peer line in the stalled peer log of the upgrade fixture; its cause is undetermined. The remaining two cases are gotchas 3690 and 3691. The task touches only the Makefile and ci.yml, so the attempt recorded the scope conflict with do_2 and stopped."
fix = "Decision 2989: the qualification check runs in its own job that installs tools/qualification/requirements.txt, the tests-python pip line stays as asserted, and the gate of the owner installs the same file before the build; 22.39.26 attempt 4 carries the directory, tests/ci and the two workflows in its touches and requires 22.39.173."

[gotcha.3690]
title = "The relocation of the vendored tree left its six .codify scripts uncommitted because the ignore file of the tree excludes the directory"
symptom = "test_code_specs_dot_directories_and_assets_are_preserved of tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_36_1.py line 133 walks the base snapshot 2e0a668a793a7b5c0469b44950808547467f017e and requires every file outside docs and the removed set to exist under tools with its original bytes; under the public check of 22.39.26 attempt 3 it failed on the first of six executable scripts in the .codify directory of the vendored tree, and the directory does not exist on main. The ignore file of the vendored tree excludes the directory at its line 24, so the relocation of 22.36.1 moved the six files on disk, where the test of its own gate saw them, and the commit never carried them; the earlier snapshot import had added them explicitly."
fix = "Decision 2991: the vendored tree carries every file of its base snapshot outside the removed set, added explicitly where its own ignore file excludes it; task 22.39.173 restores the six scripts and 22.39.26 requires it."

[gotcha.3691]
title = "One beta driver case compiles the Go node with the native libraries, which no Python job provides"
symptom = "test_multichain_inventory_reports_absent_infrastructure_as_failed of tools/qualification/test_beta_driver.py requires the native-ledger-boundary-rejections step of the driver (beta_driver.py line 1743, go test ./node for four repair tests) to exit 0; under the public check of 22.39.26 attempt 3 the link step failed with cannot find -llayerx and the node package reported build failed, because the Go node links the Rust static libraries the node build job produces and neither the gate interpreter nor a Python job builds them. The case is the only one in the directory that compiles the node; every other case of the file passed."
fix = "Decision 2990: qualification cases that compile the node carry the pytest marker native, the Python check deselects the marker, and the node build job runs the marked cases after it builds the node; 22.39.26 attempt 4 applies it."

[gotcha.3692]
title = "The relocation of the vendored tree dropped twenty-three files, the six .codify scripts and seventeen image assets above 256 KiB, and the restoring attempt restored only the six"
symptom = "Task 22.39.173 attempt 1 at 761a7c479bd4 (base dd4addbf677b) restored the six executable scripts of the .codify directory with their original bytes, staged them explicitly past the ignore rule of the vendored tree, passed its build and failed its verification twice on the same case: test_code_specs_dot_directories_and_assets_are_preserved of tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_36_1.py line 133 stopped at apps/desktop/assets/icon-dev.png. A walk of the base snapshot 2e0a668a793a7b5c0469b44950808547467f017e against the tree on main shows twenty-three absent files, the six scripts and seventeen image assets (five under apps/desktop/assets, six under apps/mobile/assets, two under apps/web/public, three under assets and extensions/vscode/media/icon.png), every one between 265500 and 1349746 bytes while the largest image the tree still carries is 243003 bytes. The qualification environment of the relocation classed an unstaged binary above 256 KiB under a directory path as build output, so the relocation commit 0bb8393cc6 deleted the seventeen at their old paths and never added them at the new ones; the environment now recognises a binary whose bytes the repository history already holds as a restored file, and a staged file was never affected. The attempt had no second repair cycle left and stopped."
fix = "Decision 2992: the restoring task restores every absent file of the base snapshot, the seventeen image assets included, stages each explicitly before its gates and records all twenty-three with their sizes; 22.39.173 attempt 2 completes the restoration."

[gotcha.3693]
title = "The launchpad gate reaches the user module for the first time and two development profile cases fail against the signed-operation and app repairs of 2026-11-04"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 13 at 6fd12004277d (base c92013249283) passed its build twice and the 39 wiring cases, raised the social manifest to Go 1.27.0 per decision 2979, and ran the whole launchpad test target. The first verification lost the protocol bindings package to the ten-minute package limit because TestRepair_37_native_family_events spent 480 seconds downloading and compiling the node producer dependencies cold before the overlay proof ran; the attempt added a compilation step for the proof dependencies ahead of the timed tests, and in the second verification the package passed in 375 seconds. The second verification then failed only in services/launchpad/user/internal/app, a module no earlier attempt had reached: TestDevelopmentProfileWrite (development_profile_writes_test.go line 328, the legacy read of /users/{owner} after an edit still returns the display name and bio from before the edit) and TestDevelopmentProfileReads (development_profiles_test.go line 136, the legacy save returns 400 with the message Missing signed operation). The signed-operation requirement of the legacy write landed with 22.33.1064 (92d4e7c7b4, 2026-11-04) and the app repairs with 22.33.1062 (c87e5e46a5) and 22.31.77 (44c092b520), while both tests date from 2026-10-21 and no gate ran them since; the user module is in the touches of task 22.39.168, which retires the baseline entries of the twelve later modules."
fix = "Decision 2993: the two cases enter the baseline with retiring task 22.39.168, which follows the signed-operation producer in the test and repairs the legacy read path if the edit no longer invalidates it; 22.39.75 attempt 14 records the entries and reruns."

[gotcha.3694]
title = "The codec retirement task names five test files of the crypto crate while two support modules and three other test sources consume the retired items, and the verification census excludes the platform guard test by a name it does not carry"
symptom = "Task 9.35.7 attempt 5 at d6ead3a72927 (base dd4addbf677b with 9.35.24 merged) deleted exactly the items do_2 to do_4 name from src/disclosure.rs, src/send.rs and src/signer.rs and rewrote the five test files the touches list. The first build failed because the call module lost decode_session_key from its scope with the deleted imports; the second build compiled the library and failed every test target on unresolved imports of encode_send_envelope, DisclosedEnvelope, EnvelopeOptions and sign_disclosed from tests/support/signing.rs (four references), tests/support/mod.rs (two), tests/repair_22_33_1560.rs (twelve), tests/repair_22_33_1558.rs (fourteen) and tests/proof_crypto.rs (two), none of them in the touches, so the verification never ran and the attempt reported the files as out of scope. Outside the crate the census of the verification is already empty on main except one hit: services/platform/hosted/core/tests/no_kernel_disclosure_codec.rs names sign_disclosed as a forbidden string, and the census excludes files matching no_kernel_codec, which that name does not contain, so the verification could not pass on any tree. The time limit of thirty minutes predates the agent daemon family of decision 2357 and is too small for a change across the crate and its tests."
fix = "Decision 2994: a task that deletes public items of a crate owns every test source of the crate that consumes them and carries the tests directory in its touches; the census exclusion names the guard test by its no_kernel_ prefix, the time limit is 240 minutes, and 9.35.7 attempt 6 restarts from main with the crate test consumers migrated onto sign_disclosed_call and bind_call."

[gotcha.3695]
title = "The history contract test asserts the response size of the full served envelope while the hosted history reader has measured the four page fields since the account check landed"
symptom = "Task 22.39.172 attempt 2 at dd47d3970a57 (base dd4addbf677b) served the hosted envelope of decision 2988 from both fixtures, kept every cursor, bound and refusal assertion, and passed 25 of the 26 cases of its four targets; read_account_decodes_a_served_gateway_page failed its exact response-size assertion at tests/history_served_contract.rs line 157 (495 against 643). The assertion compares response_bytes to the serialized length of the whole served result (account, items, next_cursor, indexedHeight, chainHeight and freshness, 643 bytes), while HistoryPage::from_hosted in src/read/history.rs line 198 has measured response_bytes as the serialized length of the four page fields items, next_cursor, indexedHeight and chainHeight (495 bytes) since 22.33.1521 and bounds that measure by maximum_response_bytes; the oversized case of the same file (line 481) already builds its limit from the four-field measure. Decision 2988 asked every response-size assertion to stay as it is, which left the contradiction unresolvable inside the attempt, and the attempt recorded it as a blocker finding instead of weakening the case."
fix = "Decision 2995: response_bytes is the four-field measure the producer defines, the exact-count assertion of the contract test asserts that measure built from the served page, src/read stays unchanged, and 22.39.172 attempt 3 applies it."

[gotcha.3696]
title = "The joined launchpad preparation leaves the stats schema unmigrated and probes the snapshot route without a pause under the default rate limit, so the api is rate limited for the whole readiness window"
symptom = "Task 22.39.95 attempt 7 at f9670ab45d4e (base c0859a9d080c) ran the api as one process under the test environment as decision 2981 requires and reproduced the preparation outside the gate as decision 2971 requires; the api came up, subscribed its broker channels and answered its health check, and the snapshot readiness probe then timed out after ninety seconds with HTTP 429 RATE_LIMITED (retry after sixty seconds). Two defects of the preparation script compose. First, its comment states that service startup runs the same embedded migrations as the PostgreSQL tests, which holds for the indexer and the charts roles but not for the stats schema: stats.pool_stats belongs to the stats module, whose process applies its goose migrations through its migrate package at startup, and that process is not a role of the preparation and cannot be one (its configuration requires NATS credentials, delivery and schema documents); the own PostgreSQL fixture of the api creates the table inline instead, so the api logged development stream projection degraded (relation stats.pool_stats does not exist) on every five-second stats sweep. Second, the readiness loop of the snapshot route issues its next request immediately after any answer it does not treat as final, and the api keeps its default of one hundred requests per sixty seconds per address (the development stream test of the api boots with one thousand), so the first not-yet-projected answer for the market trades topic became more than one hundred requests within a second and the route stayed rate limited until the window and the probe both expired."
fix = "Decision 2996: the stats module exposes its schema migration as a command the preparation runs over the private database before the api, the readiness probe pauses between requests and honours Retry-After, and the api role carries the rate limit of its own development stream test; 22.39.95 attempt 8 applies both with the stats module directory in its touches."

[gotcha.3697]
title = "The indexer sweep target asserts a reward availability value its producer no longer returns, and its total-deadline test bounds a sixteen-megabyte write at one second"
symptom = "Task 22.99.155 attempt 6 at 61c5e13929ea (base c0859a9d080c) passed its build twice and failed its verification twice; at the final tree two targets failed. a02_only_a_rank4_checkpoint_for_the_same_root_finalizes of services/platform/hosted/indexer/tests/ai_snapshot_minimal.rs line 617 expects availability slot F06 to be NotEnabled and received NotYetProduced: the attempt-5 base 471d207b0eef still set the slot to NotEnabled unconditionally (queries.rs line 539 of the ai-market program), the 22.30.122 repair 837619acf7 on the attempt-6 base derives it from the settlement section (empty before the first funding, so NotYetProduced), and the producer test programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/tests/view_binding.rs line 315 from 22.99.77 asserts NotYetProduced and refuses NotEnabled; the test passed at attempt 5 only because its base predates the rule. request_writes_obey_total_deadline of tests/repair_22_33_1445.rs line 644 sends a sixteen-megabyte request against a 350 ms total deadline while the peer holds the connection three seconds and asserts the elapsed time below one second; it measured 1.26 s under the parallel suite after passing in the first verification of the attempt. The record of the attempt calls the first case pre-existing and the second unrelated; neither word names the producer fact."
fix = "Decisions 2997 and 2998: indexer consumers assert the availability the program producer returns, and the deadline test proves the deadline by returning before the peer hold; 22.99.155 attempt 7 corrects both expectations with the record naming the producers."

[gotcha.3698]
title = "The bridge relayer test support includes a lock file main never tracked, and the crypto deletion meets a malformed-header row the binder admits since the key-rotation task"
symptom = "Task 9.35.7 attempt 6 at 21576b957f45 (base 29e8b1130a) passed its build and the census of the deleted names over its tree, and its verification never ran: the compile check of the dependent crates exited 101 because services/interop/crates/layerx-bridge-relayer/tests/support/evm_dependencies.rs line 17 includes evm/package-lock.json through include_str and main tracks only evm/package.json beside it, so every test target of the bridge relayer crate fails to compile since d884878611 (22.39.124). The change set of that task carried the lock file, its published tree omitted it, and no gate compiled the crate test targets since. The whole crate suite the attempt ran locally per decision 2994 failed one case, auth_lifecycle_call_discloses_the_governance_payload of services/agent/crates/layerx-crypto/tests/disclosure_call.rs line 411: the malformed-header table at line 391 lists (0x71, 2, 0, 4, 92) as a shape bind_call refuses, while the key-rotation repair 47e3f12fba (22.31.496) admits exactly that shape in src/disclosure/call.rs; the gate of 22.31.496 ran the agent daemon and module tests and never the crypto test file, so the row went stale on main."
fix = "Decisions 2999 and 3000: task 22.39.174 generates and tracks the lock file beside its manifest, and the lifecycle table of the crypto tests follows the binder; 9.35.7 requires 22.39.174 and attempt 7 drops the stale row inside the crate suite it owns."

[gotcha.3699]
title = "The qualification suite host fails on one audit test that quotes harness source the inventory sweep of the ai-market program rewrote"
symptom = "Task 22.39.26 attempt 4 at af2711cdcd84 (base d27e49f022) passed its build twice and ran the whole qualification suite twice under the new make target: 4448 cases passed and one failed both times, test_finding_7_final_bytes_are_bounded_deployed_and_then_published of tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_33_788.py. The test quotes source lines of two consumers of the host boundary manifest. The first verification failed at line 105 because programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/tests/host_boundary.rs no longer stores the manifest fields with to_owned but resolves each path against the manifest directory (the resolve closure of 22.99.77, commit 101f526f03); the attempt followed that producer in its one repair cycle. The second verification failed at line 119 because the same commit rewrote deploy of tests/programs/test_ai_host_boundary.c to read the artifact into an exact-length heap buffer (fread(wasm, 1U, (size_t)length, artifact) != (size_t)length) and hand it to deploy_bytes, where the hashing and the deploy and upgrade executions the test quotes still live; the quoted fread into payload+104U is gone. Both producers moved after the audit test landed, and no gate ran the test between: the gate of 22.99.77 runs the ai-market program targets, and the qualification suite had no host until this task. The host test of the task was never reached."
fix = "Decision 3001: an audit test that quotes producer source follows the producer, and the host of the qualification suite owns every stale quotation its run exposes; 22.39.26 attempt 5 replaces the fread fact with the exact-length buffer read and keeps the rest of the fact set."

[gotcha.3700]
title = "The bridge relayer lock file lands and compiles every test target, and the real EVM host test then resets one connection and poisons its shared host lock for four more cases"
symptom = "Task 22.39.174 attempt 1 at bc0483b770c3 (base f6511609fe) generated services/interop/crates/layerx-bridge-relayer/tests/support/evm/package-lock.json (lockfile version 3, 384 entries with integrity fields, the four pinned versions) and the build compiled every test target of the crate for the first time since 22.39.124. The whole-crate verification then failed one target, tests/repair_22_31_160.rs: two cases passed and five failed. directional_policy_keeps_thresholds_in_both_orders_and_after_restart received from the EVM host helper src/repair_22_31_160_vault.cjs the answer read ECONNRESET at TCP.onStreamRead during its deploy command (line 123), and the four other cases failed at line 160 with PoisonError because the host lives behind one static Mutex that the first panic poisoned. The helper runs ganache 7.9.2 in process; on the Node build of the gate environment (ABI 137) ganache prints that its native websocket module is incompatible and falls back to its Node implementation, in this run and in the passing run of 22.39.124 alike, and that run also warned of eleven close listeners on the server, one per kept-alive connection. The ethers JsonRpcProvider of the helper reuses connections, and the fallback server reset a reused one; the earlier run passed on timing. The attempt record calls the reset unrelated; the task that runs the whole crate suite owns it under decision 2908, and the five names it reports hide the single cause behind four poison failures."
fix = "Decisions 3002 and 3003: the helper opens a fresh connection per request and retries one transport reset of an idempotent read, and the shared host lock of the test recovers from poison and relaunches a dead host; 22.39.174 attempt 2 carries both with the crate in its touches."

[gotcha.3701]
title = "The launchpad security module reaches its first gate run without a survey, and its request parsing case still posts the lowercase alias the canonical-name repair refuses"
symptom = "Task 22.39.75 attempt 14 at 1ab84c3c6b85 (record tree 16947cc1cf6f, base d27e49f022cc) passed its build, the 40 wiring cases and the first fifteen launchpad modules under the reviewed baseline, and the module test of services/launchpad/security then failed one case: TestRequestParsing of security/policy/policy_test.go line 66, where the one valid body of the case (an object with the single lowercase key name) posted into a destination struct with the untagged field Name returns policy denied. The audit repair of 22.33.1021 (2026-11-04) made DecodeMutation admit only the exact canonical field names of the destination (mutationFields and canonicalMutationFields of policy.go), and its own test parsing_test.go asserts that the capitalised key reaches the untagged field and that a lowercase alias is refused; the gate of that repair ran its new tests only, so the older case of policy_test.go never ran against the new contract until this attempt. The module itself was never surveyed under decision 2947: discovery of the security manifest was blocked until attempt 11 tidied its go.mod, and no survey followed, so the baseline carries no entry for security/policy while security/control has its one. The attempt record classifies the case for the retiring owner 22.39.168 and stops with the repair budget spent on the proof dependency setup."
fix = "Decision 3004: a launchpad module whose survey was blocked is surveyed before the next gate run once the blocker is gone, and a case the gate finds without a survey is classified and baselined the same way; 22.39.75 attempt 15 surveys security and security/control, adds the entry for TestRequestParsing naming 22.39.168, and 22.39.168 corrects the case to the canonical key name."

[gotcha.3702]
title = "The ai-market guest spends CPU fuel in proportion to the whole shared state, so at the maximum roster and task set every operation on the path and both read operations exceed the protocol cap"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 10 at 8dba3555d904 (record tree 4554880b80e1, base ae54d4a258f2) merged the attempt-9 tree over 22.99.77, extended the compiled fuel inventory from 55 to all 72 selectors of the routing metadata (17 F11 selectors had landed since attempt 9, and the three reserved bond selectors are proved as refusals), passed its build, the 32 dependent crates and 15 of the 16 verification cases, and failed the all-selector fuel case at the maximum state twice: at the second gate 66 rows of the maximum journey report no measured fuel because the host refused them at the 1000000 CPU cap. The refused rows are OPEN_EPOCH at height 1408 with a 63175-byte state (attempted 1000013), the 64 ADMIT_TASK rows at height 1410 with states from 75953 to 90632 bytes (attempted 1000001 to 1000041, the meter stopping at the cap), and READ_HEADER and READ_STATE_CHUNK at height 1505 with a 108746-byte state (attempted 1090822 and 1090463, the true cost of the read path). CANCEL_TASK and SEAL_TASK_SET at the same state measure 930690 to 965163. The cost grows with the state bytes at roughly ten fuel per byte, so the guest validates or decodes the whole shared state on every operation, including the two reads that only return bytes, and the maximum state of 196608 bytes that MAX_STATE_BYTES admits fits no operation at all. The attempt optimised the roster, admission, score and reward paths (binary lookups, decoded-input reuse, occupied-slot scans) and brought the aggregation and prune rows under the cap, then spent its two gate cycles; the final source changes and the regenerated fixture guest (516432 bytes) carry no gate evidence."
fix = "Decision 3005: the fuel of an ai-market operation is bounded by the sections it reads and writes, never by the whole shared state; the two read operations copy without decoding; attempt 11 measures every maximum-state row with a four-fold measurement budget first, then removes the whole-state work from the refused paths, with the cap unchanged."

[gotcha.3703]
title = "The kernel activity codec of layerx-wire already lives behind a historical module with deprecated root re-exports, and twenty-two files in five crates still name the root paths"
symptom = "Task 9.29.1 attempt 1 at e5dc15a32e83 (base 153b9ea5ef) deleted activity.rs, sign.rs and the wallet vector test of services/agent/crates/layerx-wire and the four activity hash aliases of hash.rs, as do_1 and do_2 ask, and its build failed with exit 101 before any verification: the declared wire test build compiles layerx-crypto as a dev-dependency of the crate, and onboarding.rs lines 4 and 139 and disclosure.rs line 130 of that crate still import the root activity module and the root payload_hash alias. The task text predates the repair of 22.33.1522 at e8bb833488 (2026-11-07), which closed the five medium findings of audit record 22.30.92 by moving the activity envelope codec, the envelope signing preimage and the activity hash helpers into an explicitly historical module (lib.rs lines 13 to 33: pub mod historical with activity, sign and hash, and deprecated root re-exports pointing readers of archived evidence at historical::activity and submissions at layerx_crypto::evm_transaction), so a full deletion contradicts the landed repair and the finding wire_exports it closed. Outside the crate the historical path is used nowhere, and the root paths are named by twenty-two files: in layerx-crypto src/disclosure.rs and src/onboarding.rs with tests/disclosure.rs, tests/repair_22_33_1561.rs and tests/support/mod.rs; in layerx-agentd src/human_runtime.rs, src/human_runtime/native_receipt.rs, src/human_runtime/subject/tests.rs, src/approval/native_effect.rs, src/ops/program.rs, src/protocol_evidence.rs and src/protocol_evidence_native_tests.rs with tests/repair_22_31_366.rs, tests/repair_22_31_568.rs, tests/repair_22_31_575.rs, tests/repair_22_33_1550.rs and tests/support/repair_22_33_1529.rs; in layerx-sdk src/program_http.rs, src/programs/native_activity.rs and tests/sdk.rs; in layerx-intents src/canonical.rs (a pub use of activity_id and payload_hash beside the supported hash names); and in the platform authority src/human/dynamic.rs. The string-literal sweeps of boundary-check, api-gen and the attestor kernel vectors assert the absence of the root paths and are not callers. The gateway main.rs no longer decodes a signed envelope, so do_7 has nothing left to change, and no open task touches any of the twenty-two files."
fix = "Decision 3006: the historical module of layerx-wire stays as the only home of the kernel codec for reading archived evidence; 9.29.1 retires the root paths and moves every caller to the historical path in the same change, with the caller files in its touches, a build of every consumer crate and a repository grep in its verification."

[gotcha.3704]
title = "The agent fuzz crate imports the root activity module of layerx-wire through a grouped use, outside every build of the retirement task and outside the pattern of its repository grep"
symptom = "Task 9.29.1 attempt 2 at 71a71152c2e4 (base 29677b7f1b) retired the root re-exports and the root hash aliases of services/agent/crates/layerx-wire, kept the historical module, moved the twenty-two caller files, passed its build of the six consumer crates, 41 dependent checks and its verification, and its record names one remaining root import it could not change: services/agent/fuzz/tests/repair_22_33_1567.rs line 14 reads use layerx_wire with activity and encode::Encoder in one grouped list, and lines 63, 110, 112, 373 and 377 call peek_signed_activity_type, decode_signed and encode_signed through it. The fuzz crate layerx-agent-fuzz has its own manifest and lock at services/agent/fuzz, is no member of the agent workspace, is built by no public workflow, and was outside the touches of 9.29.1, so neither the consumer build of decision 3006 nor the repository grep of the verification saw it: the grep matches the root path written as layerx_wire::activity and not the grouped form. Once 9.29.1 is on main the fuzz test of 22.33.1567 no longer compiles, and its gate (cargo test on the fuzz manifest for the test repair_22_33_1567) is red until the import moves to historical::activity."
fix = "Decision 3007: a repository grep for a retired root path also matches the grouped use form, and a crate with its own manifest counts as a consumer; task 22.39.175 moves the fuzz test import to the historical path, builds the fuzz crate tests and widens the grep."

[gotcha.3705]
title = "The guarantor certificate verifier of layerx-proof already survives only as a retired stub that three proof repair tests, one hosted paxeer repair test and a compatibility path of the agent daemon still name"
symptom = "Task 9.27.4 attempt 1 at a191b6976d2f (base 29677b7f1b) deleted checkpoint.rs, settlement.rs and tests/checkpoint.rs of services/agent/crates/layerx-proof with the checkpoint evidence of evidence.rs and level.rs, added the regression test to tests/inclusion.rs, and passed its build of that one test binary; the dependents check then failed with exit 101 before the verification ran, because layerx-agentd src/cache.rs line 5 imports checkpoint::ThresholdReport for the retired compatibility constructor from_checkpoint at line 126 (uninhabited argument, no caller anywhere), and the agent-outside consumers the check does not compile fail the same way: services/platform/hosted/paxeer/tests/repair_22_33_1324.rs lines 68 and 130 build a Certificate from the archived vector and assert verify_certificate answers CheckpointError::RetiredCertificateVerifier. The task text predates the repairs of 22.31.226 (dda4cf74c4) and 22.33.1557 (884d756e24, both 2026-11-04), which left the module in place as a retired stub: verify_certificate and verify_declared_certificate return RetiredCertificateVerifier, ThresholdReport is uninhabited and settlement is a deprecated module, and their proving tests assert that retention: repair_22_33_1557.rs cases retired_settlement_items_are_deprecated_and_checkpoint_api_is_retained (line 320, lib.rs contains pub mod checkpoint and a deprecated pub mod settlement, settlement.rs declarations deprecated) and retained_checkpoint_api_refuses_historical_certificates (line 355, the stub refuses the archived certificates), and repair_22_33_1562.rs line 21 includes tests/checkpoint.rs as a module by path to check the finality labels of its three cases. repair_22_31_226.rs and the support file historical_checkpoint.rs read only layerx_types::vectors::checkpoint and layerx_types::settlement and keep compiling. Decision 928 orders the deletion and the retired-name sweep of layerx-sdk tests/sdk.rs line 383 already asserts the absence of layerx_proof::checkpoint from the SDK; the deletion is right and the consumers were simply never in the touches of the task."
fix = "Decision 3008: the deletion of decision 928 stands; 9.27.4 attempt 2 removes the compatibility constructor of the agent cache, rewrites the retention assertions of the three repair tests into absence assertions that keep every archive and vector check, builds every consumer crate and adds a repository grep, with the consumer files in its touches."

[gotcha.3706]
title = "The ai-market guest hashes every preserved state section twice per mutation, and the runtime clamps every qualification budget to the protocol maximum so a four-fold measurement cannot run"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 11 at daa08d3a6167 (base a08f6e9ee622) passed its build and the dependent checks, brought READ_HEADER to 310951 and READ_STATE_CHUNK to 346677 fuel, bounded CANCEL_TASK to 676170 to 709004 and SEAL_TASK_SET to 931030 at the maximum state, recorded all 170 maximum-state rows before and after, and failed the all-selector fuel case once more: OPEN_EPOCH at height 1408 (63175-byte state) is refused at 1000007 attempted and the 64 ADMIT_TASK rows at height 1410 (75953 to 90632 bytes) at 1000103 to 1081527 attempted, where attempted is the charge that crossed the cap and not the total. Two findings explain the remainder. First, the attempt introduced check_preserved_sections in state.rs (line 844), called from the task opening in epoch.rs line 802 and from the admission finish in tasks.rs line 794: it decodes the whole produced frame and, for every section the operation did not change, computes the in-guest SHA-256 of the old bytes and of the new bytes and compares them; at the maximum state that is two software hashes over about sixty to ninety thousand bytes on every opening and admission, whole-state work by another name, although replace_encoded_section keeps the unchanged sections byte-identical by construction. Second, the measurement with a four-fold budget that decision 3005 asked for cannot run through the public runtime interface: DeclaredBudget::new of the programs runtime rejects a CPU budget above the protocol maximum and the effective activity maximum of the executor clamps a larger executor to it, so the budgeted qualification entry measured at 1000000 and the record carries a wiring request for a diagnostic-only execution in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/execute.rs. The attempt stopped without a second fuel repair as the ruling required."
fix = "Decision 3009: a guest mutation never re-hashes the sections it leaves unchanged, and over-cap rows are measured by a journey-size sweep inside the test instead of a raised runtime budget; 22.33.223 attempt 12 removes the preserved-section hashing and measures by sweep."

[gotcha.3707]
title = "The terminal receipt test of layerx-proof and the Go conformance command still assert one case in the receipted revert vector after the corpus gained a second one"
symptom = "Task 9.27.4 attempt 2 at ec05f76886216ee795457101c6742bd51d11432c (base 3bf7dd1cc6d0bcfed840d92509da64ab55aa5d54) deleted the retired checkpoint and settlement modules of layerx-proof together with the agent cache constructor and the three repair assertions of decision 3008, passed its build and the dependents check, passed the inclusion, repair_22_31_226 and repair_22_33_1557 targets, and then failed one case of the repair_22_33_1562 target: terminal_v4::retained_positive_and_revert_receipts_verify_byte_exactly at services/agent/crates/layerx-proof/tests/terminal_v4.rs line 99 found two cases where it asserts one. The repair_22_33_1562 binary includes tests/terminal_v4.rs as a module, and that test fixes the case count of sdk/platform/conformance/fixtures/vector-v2-receipted-revert.json at one (line 96) although task 22.31.491 added the second case V2-pax-transfer-insufficient-funds on 2026-11-05 (the preexecution refusal of a PAX transfer: status zero, empty return data, no logs, result code one) and updated sdk/platform/go/conformance_vectors_test.go and the refresh script to two; the Go conformance command sdk/platform/go/cmd/conformance/main.go line 227 kept one as well, so TestConformanceCommandPassesVectorFiles of that package fails the same way, and the platform job only builds and vets the Go module. The remaining assertions of the loop hold for the second case as the fixture record rpc/repair_22_31_491.kvx states them. No gate ran the Rust test since the corpus change, and only 9.27.4 among the pending tasks touches the proof tests."
fix = "Decision 3010: a case count asserted over a conformance vector follows the fixture, the task that adds a case corrects every consumer that names the count, and a gate owner meeting a stale count corrects it with the file in its touches; 9.27.4 attempt 3 sets the terminal test to two cases, and task 22.39.176 corrects the Go conformance command."

[gotcha.3708]
title = "The Go conformance command classifies every receipted case without a ledger code as a successful execution, so the preexecution refusal case of the revert vector is refused once the count admits it"
symptom = "Task 22.39.176 attempt 1 at a09f8e4d1a94f847e305dd3b9ba3eb3569e3d67c (base b1cb0b2d80c7054e27b0aa0158abcbb82ccce431) set the revert vector count of sdk/platform/go/cmd/conformance/main.go line 227 to two, passed its build and failed TestConformanceCommandPassesVectorFiles at vectors_test.go line 65 with the message expected successful execution for V2-pax-transfer-insufficient-funds. The matcher matchVectorReceipt (main.go lines 182 to 194) knows two shapes of a receipted case: a case with lxpCode is a receipted revert (status zero and a decoded revert carrying that code) and every other case is a successful execution (status one and no revert). The case task 22.31.491 added is a third shape the SDK already verifies and asserts in sdk/platform/go/sequencer_receipt_test.go TestSequencerReceiptPreexecutionRefusal: rung receipted, status zero, receipt result code one, empty return data, no logs, no ledger code and the kernel error insufficient balance for transfer in the vmError field of the receipt view. The command follows the SDK verifier, so its matcher needs the same third shape; the attempt-1 note held the matcher unchanged and the attempt stopped correctly without a repair."
fix = "Decision 3011: the conformance command classifies a receipted case by the shape the SDK verifier establishes, with the preexecution refusal as a third shape; 22.39.176 attempt 2 adds that branch to the matcher with the count correction."

[gotcha.3709]
title = "The arbiter crate of the programs workspace still names the retired root activity paths of layerx-wire, so the host boundary build of every ai-market gate fails"
symptom = "Task 22.38.7 attempt 2 at c40704964dbd (base c2d386d18ab9) failed its build gate before the size test: the host boundary target compiles the whole programs workspace, and programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter does not compile on main since 9.29.1 retired the root activity, sign and hash::activity_id and hash::payload_hash paths of layerx-wire (decision 3006 keeps them only under layerx_wire::historical). The crate names the root paths in src/admission.rs (lines 10, 154, 156, 161, 163 and 178), src/activity_codec.rs line 1, tests/activity_codec.rs lines 3, 98 and 107, tests/authority_from_prestate.rs line 778, tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs line 597 and tests/repair_22_33_215.rs line 218. The retirement census of 9.29.1 and its verification grep covered the services directory only, while the arbiter crate depends on layerx-wire by path from programs/crates and is built by the programs workspace; the build of 22.33.223 passed because its gate builds the ai-market crate alone through its own manifest."
fix = "Decision 3012: a retirement census spans every Rust crate of the repository whichever workspace builds it; task 22.39.177 moves the arbiter callers to the historical paths and builds the programs workspace, and 22.38.7 requires it."

[gotcha.3710]
title = "Two proof crate tests read the checkpoint settlement document through the types the settlement retirement deletes"
symptom = "Task 9.26.3 attempt 1 at 7d7ba04f1018 (base 42abaa83d58e) deleted the settlement module of layerx-types with its lib.rs line, added the vectors test and passed its build; the dependents check then failed with E0432 at services/agent/crates/layerx-proof/tests/support/historical_checkpoint.rs line 8, which imports DeclaredCheckpointSettlement and CHECKPOINT_SETTLEMENT_PATH to read contracts/config/checkpoint-settlement.json for repair_22_31_226.rs (the settlement domain by name, its guarantor set and the finality policy certificate threshold), and services/agent/crates/layerx-proof/tests/repair_22_33_1557.rs line 349 parses the same document through DeclaredCheckpointSettlement for the paxeer chain id and settlement contract of each vector domain. Both tests were written by the audit repairs after the retirement task was specified, the task record of 9.26.3 names only the agent daemon, client and wire users, and its build gate builds the types crate alone, so the two consumers surfaced only in the dependents check."
fix = "Decision 3012 and gotcha 3046: attempt 2 gives the proof tests a test-local reader of the document covering the fields they read, carries the three files in its touches, builds the proof test targets in its gate and adds the repository grep to its verification."

[gotcha.3711]
title = "The qualification environment gave the launchpad delivery tests one database per variable while the public launchpad job declares the shared fixture database the test guards pin"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 1 at 655ec01cf294 (base b1cb0b2d80c7) passed its build and the chain, db and storage packages and failed five cases of the delivery and natsdriver packages: TestWebhookTargetsResumeIndependentlyPostgresTLS (webhook_test.go line 41), TestPhase3ActualRelayCrashAndConsumerRestart and TestPhase3ActualOrderedPoisonAndHundredDuplicates (driver_test.go line 302) and the two TestEpochRealPostgres cases (epoch_test.go line 198) refused the DELIVERY_TEST_DSN and BROKER_EPOCH_TEST_DSN they received. The guards pin host 127.0.0.1, port 25432 and database kindle_fixture, exactly what .github/workflows/launchpad-test.yml exports for every launchpad database variable except L07_POSTGRES_DSN; the qualification environment derived a database name from each variable name (delivery_test, broker_epoch_test) with a generic owner, so the variables named databases no guard accepts. The attempt itself is complete: the natsdriver and delivery tests skip with the variable named when it is unset, the baseline entries of the five packages are removed and the Makefile recipe reads the baseline file by its path."
fix = "Decision 3013: the qualification environment reads the database of each launchpad variable from the public launchpad job file and the guards stay; 22.39.117 attempt 2 requalifies the attempt-1 tree."

[gotcha.3712]
title = "The epoch opening, score reveal and aggregation rows of the ai-market fuel sweep stay over the cap with a slope of zero across task counts"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 12 at 013e3cee50c3 (base 4238129461d4) removed check_preserved_sections with its two calls and bounded the admission rows as decided (every ADMIT_TASK row of the 16, 32, 48 and 64 task journeys within the cap at 811216, 868640, 923084 and 980350 fuel, SealEvidence within the cap, guest 514364 bytes), and the fuel case still fails on three handlers: OPEN_EPOCH refuses at 1000006 attempted fuel from a constant 63175-byte state input at every task count (line 1408 of the record), eight RevealScore rows (line 1488) and six aggregation rows (line 1504) exceed the cap. A slope of zero across task counts means the three handlers read a quantity that does not grow with the tasks: the whole state input for the epoch opening, and per-roster inputs for the reveal and the aggregation, so the journey-size sweep of decision 3009 cannot measure them and a roster-size sweep can."
fix = "Decision 3014: the three rows are measured by a roster-size sweep at a fixed task count and their handlers read only the sections the operation touches; 22.33.223 attempt 13 applies it with one repair cycle."

[gotcha.3713]
title = "The arbiter path task names the authority test target whole, and one of its cases is qualified only by a native replay corpus the qualification environment never holds"
symptom = "Task 22.39.177 attempt 1 at 4977cff751ba (base 208444c51bfb) moved the six arbiter files to the historical activity codec paths, passed its build (the arbiter test binaries and the host boundary guest) and then failed its verification at exit 101: the activity_codec target passed, and the authority_from_prestate target failed its case canonical_native_authority_matches_authenticated_historical_facts at tests/authority_from_prestate.rs line 290, which reads LAYERX_AUTHENTICATED_REPLAY_INPUTS and LAYERX_ARBITER_ADMISSION_INPUTS and panics without them; the proof_arbiter_crate and repair_22_33_215 targets never ran. Decision 2496 classes that case as qualified by its producer inputs, and the inventory sweep repair 22.99.78 excludes it by exact name; the verification written for 22.39.177 in the previous round named the target without the exclusion, so the failure is a defect of the verification text and not of the tree."
fix = "Decision 3015: a verification that names a test target holding a producer-qualified case excludes the case by exact name, and the task requalifies at the same tree with the corrected command; 22.39.177 attempt 2 reruns the corrected verification on 4977cff751ba."

[gotcha.3714]
title = "The wallet SDK manifest gained two development dependencies that its sibling lockfile never received, and the SDK test job cannot resolve the gateway modules its tests import"
symptom = "The public Wallet tests workflow (runs 42536606312 at 6d96aafeb8 and 42536376643 at 208444c51b) and the Wallet Go tests workflow (run 42531794417) fail in every job that installs the services/wallet workspace with ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE: services/wallet/pnpm-lock.yaml is not up to date with ../sdk/wallet/package.json because react-dom ^19.0.0 and jsdom ^26.1.0 were added. Commit 5577807085 (task 22.39.145) added both to the devDependencies of sdk/wallet/package.json and refreshed sdk/wallet/pnpm-lock.yaml only, while the importer ../../sdk/wallet of services/wallet/pnpm-lock.yaml (line 229) still lists the earlier set. In the same workflow the Vitest job for sdk/wallet installs the SDK alone with --ignore-workspace (task 22.39.94) and fails with Cannot find package jose imported from services/wallet/gateway/test/support/identity.ts: sdk/wallet/test/agent.test.ts (lines 27 to 91) and test/evm-review.test.ts (lines 13 to 259) import the gateway test support and gateway sources, whose dependencies are declared in services/wallet/gateway/package.json (jose ^5.9.6 at line 33) and installed only by the services/wallet workspace install the Gateway Vitest job runs. The gate of 22.39.145 passed the same suite because it also ran the root npm install, which placed the gateway dependencies at the repository root. tests/ci/test_wallet_test_workflow.py line 38 still asserts the Run Vitest suite step as the plain vitest command while the workflow line 56 runs the matrix command since 22.39.94, so that consumer is stale as well."
fix = "Decision 3016: a wallet SDK manifest change refreshes every lockfile whose importer resolves the SDK, the SDK Vitest job installs the services/wallet workspace before it runs, a lockfile currency test guards the three wallet workspaces, and the workflow test follows the matrix command; task 22.39.178 lands all four."

[gotcha.3715]
title = "The wallet surface replay asserts a request sequence the wallet SDK read path no longer produces"
symptom = "In run 42536606312 the Vitest job for apps/wallet passes 665 cases and fails one: repair_22_33_206_unsigned_surface_fixture_replays_node_send_and_read of apps/wallet/src/surfaces/test/repair-22-33-206.test.ts expects ten requests on the fallback path at line 131 and receives eight; the pair px_getReceiptKeys and eth_getRawTransactionByHash that followed the first authenticated read of the send path is gone, while the assertions at lines 129 and 130 (the read equals the sent receipt, requireAuthenticatedReceipt accepts it, surfaceReceipt matches) still pass, so the receipt remains authenticated with one key fetch per authenticated read. The app resolves the SDK from sdk/wallet/src/index.ts through the Vitest alias (apps/wallet/vitest.config.ts line 5); the case was written on 2026-11-07 at 15:12 (commit cda4e5f2e2, task 22.39.55), and the only later change of the SDK sources is 5577807085 of 2026-11-08 (task 22.39.145: human.ts, index.ts, ladder.ts, modules/index.ts, modules/web-data.ts, types.ts)."
fix = "Decision 3017: the request sequence assertion follows the SDK read path with the producer commit named in the record; task 22.39.179 corrects the expectation after confirming the producer by running the case at the parent and at the commit."

[gotcha.3716]
title = "The 7.0.0 consensus-commit ledger holds one row while the gate from the last v6.12.0 ledger commit lists one hundred and eighty-one unlisted commits"
symptom = "docs/release/consensus-commits.md carries one row in its v7.0.0 table (12fbbeb80389) and four rows in the historical v6.12.0 table, the latest of them 68c8887a9520 of 2026-10-22. Run from the repository root at 6d57a69c0d, python3 tools/ci/consensus_commit_gate.py 68c8887a9520542d2878da3d6a44920ddd71b4b1 HEAD exits 1 and prints 181 unlisted consensus commits touching 157 node/sequencer paths, node/app.go 64 times, 43 modules/perps paths, 34 modules/layerxcustody paths, 10 precompiles/perps paths and 7 market program paths. The Release Check workflow runs the gate only on pull requests (line 55), no tag or release of v6.12.0 exists in the repository or on its releases page, and the readiness checklist line 24 remains unchecked."
fix = "Decision 3018: the ledger lists every consensus-changing commit from the latest historical ledger commit, rows are produced by a tool from history, and the gate passes at the candidate; task 22.39.181 completes the ledger and the candidate evidence task re-runs the gate."

[gotcha.3717]
title = "The release documents carry the rehearsal script gap after the tree closed it, and the readiness gaps that remain are owner inputs and after-cutover evidence"
symptom = "docs/release/7.0.0-upgrade-plan.md lists D6 as an open gap stating that tools/release/rehearse-v6120.sh still targets the v6.12.0 plan (line 268) and the timeline row T minus 16 days repeats it (line 147), while the script reads the plan from tools/release/version.json, requires --plan-info for the v7.0 plan and forwards it to the node files, as tests/ci/test_release_merge_rehearsal.py proves in four cases. The release owner waived the exported-state rehearsal for 7.0.0 (the halt and swap evidence comes from the four ordered rehearsal tests and the programme rehearsal test), the checklist lines 35 and 36 still require it, the service runbook lists the agent daemon release qualification as a repository gap (line 272) although it is evidence retained for the deployed revision after S, and the bridge manifest gap (line 271) waits for the governed signer set that only bridge governance supplies. tests/ci/test_release_docs_gap_markers.py pins the gap tables (CLOSED_IDS at line 9, the D5 and D6 rows at line 67, four checklist gap items at line 118) and must follow."
fix = "Decision 3020: the release documents state D6 as closed, record the waiver with its decision, move the agent daemon qualification to the acceptance steps after S, keep the bridge manifest gap until governance supplies the signer set, and the gap-marker test follows; task 22.39.180 lands it before the ledger and candidate tasks tick the checklist."

[gotcha.3718]
title = "The first poison envelope the ordered consumer refuses against the real broker leaves no quarantine row, so the launchpad delivery driver test fails at its first variant"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 2 at 194dca6166ee (base 208444c51bfb) ran with every launchpad database variable the qualification environment now supplies: the build passed, the chain, db, delivery and storage packages passed with their real services, and the natsdriver package failed one case, TestPhase3ActualOrderedPoisonAndHundredDuplicates at driver_test.go line 867: after one hundred network deliveries of one envelope committed exactly one effect, the first poison variant (schema version 2, class inner_schema) was refused by the store and by a restarted store, yet the query of delivery_ordered_quarantine by consumer and envelope hash returned no rows. The refusal path (store.go line 434) classes a decode failure as inner_schema and calls QuarantineAfterRollback, which inserts the row, reads it back and compares the recorded affected pools with its normalised list through reflect.DeepEqual (line 663) before it commits; a poison with no affected pools gives a nil normalised list while the text array scans back as an empty non-nil slice, so the comparison can refuse with the integrity error and the deferred rollback discards the inserted row while the caller still returns the refusal the test expects. The case never ran against a broker before this attempt (its baseline reason was the duplicates window the attempt-1 tree widened), and the delivery package tests that passed do not cover a quarantine without affected pools against the live database."
fix = "Decision 3021: a quarantine record read-back compares the affected pools by length and elements so an empty list and an absent list agree, and the quarantine of a poison envelope without affected pools commits; 22.39.117 attempt 3 confirms the site with the failing case and repairs it with a delivery package test for the empty-pool quarantine."

[gotcha.3719]
title = "The declared checkpoint settlement document is read by the historical settlement module, the proof test support, the vector generator and the image build, so deleting it fails its own retirement test at seventeen reference sites"
symptom = "Task 6.59.7 attempt 1 at 814ead680779 (base 6d57a69c0d4e) deleted contracts/config/checkpoint-settlement.json and added tests/bridge/retired/test_retired_checkpoint_settlement.py calling assert_retired on the path; the build passed and the verification failed at exit 1 because the retirement scan found live references in seventeen files: the historical settlement reader services/agent/crates/layerx-types/src/historical/settlement.rs (the constant CHECKPOINT_SETTLEMENT_PATH at line 11) and its two tests, the proof test support historical_checkpoint.rs (line 86, which reads the document as the archival producer and not as proof trust), the hosted node TLS test support (an include of the document at line 292), the vector generator tests/vectors/checkpoint/generate.py, the image compile inputs test tests/ci/test_image_compile_inputs_not_ignored.py, the layerx image Dockerfile (a copy instruction at line 18) with three ignore files, the settlement domain migration test, the qualification build makefile 104.30.2.mk, the retired-caller tests that assert its absence from retired modules, twenty-one rows of the jev ledger fixture, and a bring-up test that writes a file of the same stem under another directory. The retirement harness itself loads the document in its checkpoint_settlement helper (kernel_retirement.py line 179). Only one non-test source reads the document, the historical module, which decision 3006 keeps as the home of retired kernel facts; the trust readers of the document were deleted by 9.27.4 (the embedded copy and the certificate verifier of layerx-proof). The two hosted node tests the task touches never reference the document (the attempt changed their whitespace only)."
fix = "Decision 3022: the document stays as the archival producer of the historical settlement readers, and 6.59.7 retires its trust role instead of the file: the retirement test asserts that no source outside the historical module reads it and records the reader set; attempt 2 restores the document and rewrites the test on a reference helper of the harness."

[gotcha.3720]
title = "The launchpad whole-module gate ran without the key-value store variables and the private EVM binary the public job declares, so three modules failed for want of the environment"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 3 at 76bb1147bf8a (base 246829c496) passed its build (go vet of the shared module) and the four shared package trees of its verification (chain, db, delivery, storage, the quarantine read-back fix of decision 3021 among them), and make -C services/launchpad ci then failed in exactly three packages: shared/redis (five cases stopped at redis_test.go lines 52, 86, 127, 186 and 232 because L09_REDIS_URL is not set), shared/config/deployment and shared/config/capabilities (seventeen cases stopped at attest_test.go, revision_test.go and preflight_chain_test.go because the anvil binary is not on PATH). The public launchpad job declares L09_REDIS_URL and the other redis variables as logical databases of one server on 26379, installs the EVM toolchain through its toolchain step, and starts the owned authorization chain on 28545 with chain id 125 read through L34_ANVIL_URL; the qualification environment supplied the store only for variables named with a TEST infix and the EVM toolchain only for commands that name its binaries. Every other package of the launchpad modules passed at the attempt tree."
fix = "Decision 3023: the qualification environment of a launchpad gate mirrors the services the public job declares (the key-value store with the logical database numbers of the job file, the EVM binaries on PATH and the owned chain on 28545 exported as L34_ANVIL_URL); the attempt tree stands and 22.39.117 attempt 4 requalifies it unchanged."

[gotcha.3721]
title = "The arbiter move onto the historical activity paths broke the portable boundary leaves the proof tests decode"
symptom = "Task 22.39.177 attempt 2 at 791076fd4c6d (base 246829c496) ran the corrected verification of decision 3015 and three of its four targets passed (activity_codec, authority_from_prestate with its producer-qualified case excluded, repair_22_33_215); proof_arbiter_crate failed two cases that pass on main: runtime_producer_records_integer_steps_and_terminal_traps at tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs line 1794, where PortableBoundary::decode_untrusted of a recorded boundary leaf returns Err(Encoding), and authenticated_producer_crosses_authority_and_bounded_replay_consumers_twice at line 1538, where replay verify_step of the boundary pair 0 to 1 returns Err(Witness(Encoding)). The attempt changed seventeen lines of src/admission.rs, two of src/activity_codec.rs and six of the test beside the retirement of the layerx_wire::activity and layerx_wire::sign paths, so a boundary leaf or witness is now produced through the historical encoder where the kernel portable boundary encoding is expected; the retirement grep itself passed."
fix = "Decision 3024: the arbiter consumes the historical module of layerx-wire only for the activity codec and the signing preimage, and every boundary leaf and replay witness keeps the kernel portable boundary encoding the proof tests decode; 22.39.177 attempt 3 bisects the admission change and restores the boundary bytes."

[gotcha.3722]
title = "The roster sweep of the ai-market guest still exceeds the protocol cpu cap by three to forty fuel on four handlers, and one routed execution produced no measured fuel because the fixture submitted evidence before sealing the task set"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 13 at f3500b77dd19 (base 208444c51bfb) passed its build and the dependents check and failed three cases of tests/fuel_budget.rs after two repair cycles: roster_state_fuel_scaling at line 2828 and maximum_state_fuel_scaling at line 2777 report sweep rows where OPEN_EPOCH at height 1408 and BeginAggregation, ProcessAggregation and FinalizeAggregation at height 1504 are refused with BudgetExceeded for Cpu at attempted 1000003 to 1000040 against the limit 1000000, at the roster sizes 16, 24 and 32; and every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap at line 1873 panics with the message that every routed guest execution must produce measured fuel. The verification log shows the fixture step sealed_task_set answered through the F08 view with application error 2305 (F09_EVIDENCE_TASK_SET_UNSEALED, errors.rs line 241), so an evidence step ran before the task set was sealed, the execution was refused at admission and no fuel was measured for it. The overages are marginal and sit in the per-roster rescans of the four handlers."
fix = "Decision 3025: the sweep fixture seals the task set before any evidence step and every routed execution of the sweep is admitted, and the four epoch and aggregation handlers fit the cap with margin at every roster the sweep covers by removing their per-roster rescans; 22.33.223 attempt 14 continues with the cap, the sweep rows and the assertions unchanged."

[gotcha.3723]
title = "The release document gap-marker test asserts a decision number that the documentation rewrite removed from every release document"
symptom = "Task 22.39.180 attempt 1 at bbe08676b47c (base 246829c496) passed its build and thirty-three of its thirty-four cases; tests/ci/test_release_docs_gap_markers.py line 195 asserts that the hosted gateway section of docs/release/7.0.0-service-operator-runbook.md names decision 2521, and the section no longer does: the documentation rewrite fb22c0390a of 2026-11-07 (the producer) removed every decision number from the three release documents (the upgrade plan, the readiness checklist and the service operator runbook carry none), while the section still states the fact the decision ruled, the px_ family served at the node root of the fourteen public nodes with no router path. The test is the stale consumer."
fix = "Decision 3026: a release document test asserts the facts of a section and never the number of the decision that ruled them; 22.39.180 attempt 2 makes the hosted gateway assertion name the node-root fact and records the producer."

[gotcha.3724]
title = "The wallet workflow test asserts the named import of the lock registry that the two widget tests replaced with a namespace import"
symptom = "Task 22.39.178 attempt 1 at 6df4284976e6 (base 246829c496) passed its second build and twelve of its thirteen cases, the lockfile currency test and the shared package roots among them; tests/ci/test_wallet_test_workflow.py test_wallet_setup_provides_web_locks (lines 78 to 90) still asserts the named import of the lock registry from the Node threads module and the defineProperty and expect lines of the earlier setup, while apps/wallet/src/widgets/pns/repair-22-33-138.test.ts and apps/wallet/src/widgets/swap/repair-22-31-239.test.ts import that module as a namespace and read the registry through Reflect.get since cda4e5f2e2 (task 22.39.55, the producer). The consumer test asserts the names of a producer that changed; the two widget files are right."
fix = "Decisions 3010 and 3046 cover it: 22.39.178 attempt 2 makes test_wallet_setup_provides_web_locks assert the setup lines the two widget tests contain on main and records the producer."

[gotcha.3725]
title = "The wallet type check of the surface replay task stops at two pre-existing type errors in the server regression test"
symptom = "Task 22.39.179 attempt 1 at dfa11a0e570d (base 246829c496) failed its build gate (the frozen install and the type check of apps/wallet) with exit 2 before any verification: apps/wallet/src/server/repair-22-33-168.test.ts line 123 reports TS18047 (address is possibly null) and TS2339 (port does not exist on the union of string and AddressInfo), because the test reads server.address().port without narrowing the return of address(). The file landed with d15bd08924 (task 22.33.168) and no gate type-checked the whole application since; the task tree itself (the request-sequence expectation of decision 3017 and the record) is sound and the file is outside its touches."
fix = "Decision 2908 covers it: 22.39.179 attempt 2 narrows the address read in the server regression test with that file in its touches and records the producer; the expectation change stands."

[gotcha.3726]
title = "The retirement attempt carried whitespace changes to two hosted node test scripts outside its touches, and the image compile-inputs test still expects the settlement document as an embedded target"
symptom = "Task 6.59.7 attempt 2 at d0c441866ae8 (base fcdf55bef3ab) restored contracts/config/checkpoint-settlement.json and wrote the reader-set test of decision 3022 (sixty-one cases passed), and was refused for two reasons: the publication check found files changed outside the touches, services/platform/hosted/node/tests/signer-test.py and the sibling test script of that directory, which carry whitespace-only changes inherited from attempt 1; and tests/ci/test_image_compile_inputs_not_ignored.py test_layerx_image_includes_reachable fails at line 290, where the settlement document is asserted among the include_str targets of the image crates although 9.27.4 (the producer, 6c4902c134) deleted the embedded copy and the document now reaches the image only as a COPY input of docker/layerx/Dockerfile line 18. The second failure is pre-existing on main and exposed by the verification this task declares."
fix = "Decision 3027: the image compile-inputs test asserts the settlement document as a Dockerfile COPY input since the embedded copy was deleted; 6.59.7 attempt 3 restores the two scripts to their base content, corrects the test with that file in its touches and records the producer."

[gotcha.3727]
title = "The arbiter still decodes kernel boundary leaves as self-contained envelopes although the runtime producer has stored the record header once per record since the boundary memory commitment, so adjudication of runtime boundary leaves fails on main"
symptom = "Task 22.39.177 attempt 3 at 677da57e8c4b (base fa374671b962) completed the retirement of the layerx_wire::activity and layerx_wire::sign paths and traced the two proof_arbiter_crate failures of gotcha 3721 to the continuation base rather than to the attempt: the runtime producer of 22.31.577 (1342437ee8, 2026-11-06) introduced the record header ReplayRecordHeader, stores the immutable boundary inputs once per record, commits each raw leaf through replay_leaf_hash, decodes raw leaves only through PortableBoundary::decode_with_header with that header (replay_record.rs line 437, execute.rs line 6170), and reserves PortableBoundary::decode_untrusted for the self-contained transport envelope that ReplayRecordHeader::boundary_envelope (replay_record.rs line 275) produces under the domain of the boundary context version two. Every arbiter consumer still calls decode_untrusted on the raw leaf the proof transports: src/step.rs line 433, src/market.rs line 646, src/bisect.rs lines 66 and 616, and the proof corpus of tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs (the decode at line 1794 and Corpus::paths at line 1196), so runtime_producer_records_integer_steps_and_terminal_traps returns Err(Encoding) and authenticated_producer_crosses_authority_and_bounded_replay_consumers_twice returns Err(Witness(Encoding)) at the replay of the boundary pair 0 to 1. The proof test last passed on 2026-11-03 (22.99.78 attempt 3 at 61167fdda39f, before the producer change); the dependents check of 22.31.577 compiled the arbiter but ran none of its proof tests. The regression gotcha 3721 assumed is pre-existing, and the arbiter cannot adjudicate a boundary leaf the current runtime records."
fix = "Decision 3029 and task 22.39.183: every arbiter consumer decodes a boundary leaf through the record header the runtime producer authenticates, carried by the proof transport as the envelope the producer emits, with the path commitment kept over the raw leaf; 22.39.177 requires 22.39.183 and continues as attempt 4 once it lands."

[gotcha.3728]
title = "The launchpad redis tests fail without the namespace literal the public job pairs with the redis variable"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 4 at 0addf46863ce (base fa374671b962) passed its build (go vet of the shared module) and its verification ran every launchpad module green except sdk/launchpad/shared/redis, where TestRealRedisPrimitives (primitives_test.go line 44), TestRealRedisAbsentFloorAndEncodedBound (line 148) and TestRealPolicySnapshotOrdering (snapshot_policy_test.go line 38) failed with the message namespace required. The three cases skip when L09_REDIS_URL is unset and fail when it is set without L09_NAMESPACE; the public job (launchpad-test.yml line 111) sets L09_NAMESPACE to a fixed private prefix beside the redis variable, as it sets DELIVERY_TEST_SCHEMA, L14_POSTGRES_SCHEMA, L37_PHASE2_SCHEMA and L37_PHASE2_CANONICAL_SCHEMA beside the postgres variables. The qualification environment of decision 3023 supplied the redis logical database from the job file but not the companion literals, so the attempt-3 skip became an attempt-4 failure. The tree of the attempt is unchanged by the finding."
fix = "Decision 3030: the launchpad gate environment exports every namespace and schema literal the public job declares beside its connection variables; 22.39.117 attempt 5 requalifies the attempt-4 tree."

[gotcha.3729]
title = "The closure gate finds 2472 findings without a disposition and nine dispositions that cite no location or name a missing or self-referencing follow-up task"
symptom = "Task 22.0.1 attempt 3 at affbadc49b (base 8c5a7acd05) passed its build and its verification exited 1 with 2481 problem lines from dispositions_closure.py. 2472 are findings of spec/layerx-merge/qualification.kvx without a [disposition.<id>] block in spec/layerx-merge/dispositions: 2430 belong to done tasks, 40 to pending tasks and 2 to superseded tasks; 1914 are domain 22 findings (523 of the 22.31 series, 942 of 22.33, 203 of 22.39, 101 of 22.99, 145 of the other 22 series), 100 are domain 9 and 458 spread over domains 1 to 8, 10 to 14, 16 to 18 and 21, written after the disposition sweep of 22.92.1 to 22.92.7 closed over its lists. 123 of them carry the severity high, which the workflow does not list. The nine others: d1-3.kvx 1.12.4.1 cites grants.go and draw.go without line numbers (main: modules/layerxpayer/keeper/grants.go:14 and draw.go:19 return ErrNoPayerGrant); d17-3.kvx 17.5.1.5, 17.5.2.1 and 17.5.2.4 and d17-4.kvx 17.5.2.5 name the pending gates 17.5.1 and 17.5.2, which is right; d17-4.kvx 17.5.1.6 names 22.94.12.1, a task that does not exist, for the unused binding named level at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/agent_rpc_adapters.rs:1738 that fails the agent lint target; d22-2.kvx 22.0.1.1 names 22.0.1 itself; d22-2.kvx 22.1.9.2 names 22.1.13, which does not exist, while 9f494ac611 (2026-11-04) removed the web reference from services/platform/hosted/node/bootstrap.sh that the finding describes; d22-3.kvx 22.11.8.1 names 22.11.9, which does not exist, while modules/evm/keeper/msg_server.go:214 still copies the bare error text into the response VmError where receipt.go:300 appends the precompile error to the receipt."
fix = "Decisions 3031 to 3033: tasks 22.39.185 to 22.39.208 disposition the 2472 findings by domain file, 22.39.184 repairs the nine dispositions, 22.39.209 removes the unused binding and 22.39.210 aligns the response VmError with the receipt; 22.0.1 attempt 4 requires them and the two aggregate gates."

[gotcha.3730]
title = "The arbiter crate has not compiled on main since the kernel activity codec moved behind the historical module, and the repair task was chained behind the retirement that restores the build"
symptom = "Task 22.39.183 attempt 1 at 08733aed93 (base 466c2f53c4) failed its build with exit 101: seven errors in programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/src/admission.rs and src/activity_codec.rs, files the attempt did not change, because they import layerx_wire::activity and the activity_id and payload_hash functions of layerx_wire::hash. services/agent/crates/layerx-wire/src/lib.rs line 17 has exported the kernel activity codec only as pub mod historical since e8bb833488 (22.33.1522, 2026-11-07), so every build of the arbiter crate on main has failed since that commit, including the programs-build target of make workspace-build. The retirement task 22.39.177 moves the two arbiter consumers to the historical module; its attempt-3 tree 677da57e8c4b builds (exit 0) and fails only the two cases of tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs that 22.39.183 owns (runtime_producer_records_integer_steps_and_terminal_traps and authenticated_producer_crosses_authority_and_bounded_replay_consumers_twice, decision 3029). The previous round made 22.39.177 require 22.39.183, so neither task could land: the repair cannot compile without the retirement and the retirement waited for the repair."
fix = "Decision 3034: the retirement lands first with the two repair-owned cases excluded by exact name, 22.39.183 requires 22.39.177 and restores them, and 22.39.182 requires both."

[gotcha.3731]
title = "The wave-0 aggregate gate last ran before the retired SDK type import left the seller middleware and now waits for the arbiter build"
symptom = "Task 17.5.1 attempt 20 ran on 2026-11-01 at 855a3c3508 (base f503ea87f1): the build passed and the verification exited 1 because the platform-build-all target of make workspace-build failed in services/platform/middleware/seller/src/rpc.ts, which imported the retired SDK type MerkleProof. Commit 39f0199fb2 (8.22.8) deleted that reader after the attempt base, and the file on main no longer imports the type. The same workspace build runs programs-build, which fails on main while the arbiter crate does not compile (gotcha 3730), so a rerun today fails for a different reason; the gate test itself is unchanged and needs 22.39.177 and 22.39.183 on main first."
fix = "Decision 3034; 17.5.1 attempt 21 requalifies the unchanged gate after 22.39.177 and 22.39.183 land, with both in its requires."

[gotcha.3732]
title = "The domain-6 completion gate asserts absence for surfaces whose retirement is a height gate or whose document a later decision kept, and names one planned test by its path before a rename"
symptom = "Task 6.0.9 attempt 1 at 9afa710deb (base 8c5a7acd05) passed its build and its verification exited 1 with 12 failing subcases of TestChainModulesCompletionRetiredSurfacesAbsent out of 582. contracts/config/checkpoint-settlement.json remains: 6.59.7 (done) retired the kernel consumer and decisions 3022 and 3027 keep the document as a COPY input of docker/layerx/Dockerfile:18, while interface.6.fmt-checkpoint-settlement-json still reads status retired. The five methods of precompiles/layerxverify/abi.json and the five functions of contracts/src/precompiles/ILayerXVerify.sol remain because 6.96.2 (done) retired the 0x1012 verifier by a height gate (precompiles/layerxverify/layerxverify.go:199 calls pcommon.RetiredAt on pcommon.MergeUpgrade; precompiles/layerxverify/retire_gate_test.go and verifier_methods_retired_test.go assert the LXP_MODULE_DISABLED revert) and decision 685 requires the retired calls to decode their arguments before the gate, so the ABI keeps the methods; the interface records still say no retire gate exists. The planned path of 6.52.2, tests/bridge/retired/test_retired_emergency_exit.py, was renamed to test_retired_bridge_emergency_exit.py by 24446b7d8c (22.99.150) and the test function test_emergency_exit_is_retired is unchanged."
fix = "Decision 3035: a height-gated surface stays at its path and the completion gate checks the gate; the kept document leaves the retired inventory; 6.52.2 planned_paths and verify_cmd follow the rename; 6.0.9 attempt 2 corrects the inventory."

[gotcha.3733]
title = "The launchpad API module tests need the compiled contract artifacts, the API database variable and a message bus the public job provides and the gate environment did not"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 5 at d115388f9b (base e418f06937) passed its build and, with the job namespace literals of decision 3030 exported, every module of sdk/launchpad/shared and sdk/launchpad/protocol passed; make -C services/launchpad ci then failed in services/launchpad/api/internal/app with three cases: TestDevelopmentAuthorityAttestationCache (dev_authority_cache_test.go line 100) and TestDevelopmentReviewedInputsMatchRepository (dev_authority_test.go line 53) open contracts/launchpad/artifacts/contracts/base/BeaconProxy.sol/BeaconProxy.json, a Hardhat output that is not committed and that the public job compiles in its step named Compile launchpad contracts for API authority proofs (pnpm install with the ignored workspace and a frozen lockfile, then pnpm compile) before go test; TestDevelopmentReadsMountMarketReads (dev_market_reads_test.go line 24) requires CORE_API_TEST_POSTGRES_URL, which the job declares for the API module beside CORE_API_TEST_REDIS_URL and CORE_API_TEST_NATS_URL (a nats-server on port 24222 with JetStream). The gate environment derived its connection variables from the task paths and the command, and make -C services/launchpad names no module directory, so the API variables were never provisioned, no message bus ran and the contracts were never compiled; the contracts directory ignores node_modules and cache but not artifacts."
fix = "Decision 3036: a gate whose command runs the launchpad modules provisions every connection variable the public job declares, runs the message bus on the port the job uses, compiles the launchpad contracts as the job does and keeps the artifacts out of the index; 22.39.117 attempt 6 requalifies the unchanged tree."

[gotcha.3734]
title = "The roster sweep slopes show the ai-market epoch and aggregation handlers cost tens of thousands of fuel per roster participant, so removing rescans alone leaves them over the cap at the full roster"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 14 at c35ee22bb79c (base fa374671b962) sealed the task set in the sweep fixture (no admission refusal occurred), removed the snapshot last-entry rescans, the copied admission tables and the repeated terminal validation of the four handlers, passed its build and dependents twice and failed the same three cases twice: every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap, roster_state_fuel_scaling and maximum_state_fuel_scaling. The sweep rows of the final verification size the refusals, which the attempted fuel of a refusal (the stopping position, 1000001 to 1000063 in every row) cannot: OPEN_EPOCH at sixteen tasks costs 280519 fuel with 8 participants and 2 evaluators and 779305 with 16 and 4, about 62000 per added participant, so the implied cost is about 1.28 million at 24/6 and 1.78 million at 32/8, where it is refused; BeginAggregation costs 587315, 791622 and 997527 at 16/4, 24/6 and 32/8, about 25600 per participant and 2473 under the cap at the full roster; a ProcessAggregation chunk merges eight reports at every roster yet its first chunk costs 529378, 706846 and 879147 at the three rosters, about 21900 per added roster participant, and each later chunk of one roster costs 41000 (16/4), 50000 (24/6) and 59000 (32/8) more than the one before it, so the fourth chunk at 32/8 (implied about 1.06 million) is refused; FinalizeAggregation is admitted at 8/2 only and refused at 16/4, 24/6 and 32/8, and the attempt record states that it validates the completed reputation state after appending its history. Attempt 14 lowered OPEN_EPOCH at 16/4 from 861297 to 779305 and BeginAggregation at 16/4 from 788016 to 587315, so the rescans were a minority of the cost; the dominant cost is proportional to the roster size in handlers whose work is a fixed chunk or a single written section."
fix = "Decision 3037: the fuel of a chunked handler is independent of the roster size and the cursor, a roster-wide handler stays at or under 900000 at the full roster, and a refused row is sized by the slope of the roster sweep; 22.33.223 attempt 15 repairs the four handlers against the slopes with those targets and stops with the implied fuel recorded if a handler still exceeds the cap."

[gotcha.3735]
title = "The arbiter contract-consumer binary includes the proof producer module by path, so two registry replay cases fail on the raw-leaf decode the leaf decode repair owns once the retirement gate reaches that binary"
symptom = "Task 22.39.177 attempt 4 at 1e0231e12e70 (base a26369c7eda6) carried the attempt-3 tree with the two producer cases of 22.39.183 excluded by exact name, passed its build and the first three test binaries (activity_codec, authority_from_prestate and proof_arbiter_crate, the last with two cases filtered out), and then failed in tests/repair_22_33_215.rs, which attempt 3 never reached because cargo stops at the first failing binary: registry_authority_signature_drives_both_call_envelopes and registry_replay_signatures_reconstruct_and_verify_adjacent_steps panicked inside the producer module that binary includes with the path attribute (tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs lines 1317 and 1538) with the message that the admitted or authenticated Executor boundary pair 0 to 1 must replay, inner runtime result Witness(Encoding). That is the raw-leaf decode of gotcha 3727 and decision 3029: the arbiter consumers still decode a kernel boundary leaf with decode_untrusted where the runtime producer of 22.31.577 now emits the record header envelope, and 22.39.183 repairs it through one shared helper. No arbiter, runtime or wire commit landed between the two bases; the two cases are new to the gate, not new failures, and their binary is not in the verification of 22.39.183."
fix = "Decision 3038: a test binary that includes a producer module by path shares the qualification of that producer, so its cases that fail on the producer defect are excluded from the retirement gate by exact name and the repair gate runs that binary; 22.39.177 attempt 5 excludes the two registry cases and 22.39.183 owns them with repair_22_33_215 in its verification."

[gotcha.3736]
title = "A crate-scoped clippy gate of the agent daemon lints every path dependency that is a member of the same cargo workspace, and the types crate fails eight pedantic lints the workspace denies"
symptom = "Task 22.39.209 attempt 1 at 6c2da1a64f69 (base a26369c7eda6) removed the unused binding at agent_rpc_adapters.rs line 1738, wrote its record and passed its build; the verification then failed in cargo clippy with eight errors, none in layerx-agentd: services/agent/crates/layerx-types/src/chain.rs reports five functions returning Result whose docs lack an Errors section (lines 24, 99, 121, 160 and historical/verify.rs line 8), the unused self argument of the const method chain_id at line 86 and of rung at historical/verify.rs line 23, and the nested function take declared after statements at line 164. The workspace of services/agent denies every pedantic lint in its workspace lints, cargo clippy for one member also lints the members it depends on, and both files were last changed by the medium repair of audit record 22.30.96 on 2026-11-04 (715f8f7e66), whose gate ran tests and never the lint target. The public agent job runs the lint target (make agent-lint: clippy over the whole workspace with all targets, warnings denied) at its lint step, so that job is red on main for the same eight errors and for whatever the remaining members report after them; the two existing uses of an unused self allowance in the daemon (admin.rs line 327, tenant/isolation.rs line 280) are the workspace precedent for a public method kept for its signature."
fix = "Decision 3039: a task whose gate lints the crate it changes runs clippy with no-deps so the gate is bounded by its touches, and the agent lint target of the public job is owned by one task that brings every member under the workspace lints; 22.39.209 attempt 2 reruns with the bounded gate and 22.39.211 makes the lint target green."

[gotcha.3737]
title = "The launchpad online index test drops its private database under a three-second deadline, which the forced drop exceeds on a shared database server once the job variables let the package run"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 6 at b7b8ec69ce77 (base 47b44760f795) ran as a requalification on the attempt-5 tree with the gate environment of decisions 3023, 3030 and 3036: the launchpad contracts compiled (rc 0, 95 s, artifacts present), the message bus fixture and every connection variable of the public job were exported, and the build passed. The verification then failed in one case of sdk/launchpad/shared/db/production: TestPhase2ConcurrentIndexesAndRecovery completed its assertions (coordinator_second migration_in_progress, invalid index repaired to reconciled, lock sqlstate 55P03 after a 2.05 s lock wait) and failed in its cleanup, online_indexes_test.go line 39, private migration database cleanup failed, context deadline exceeded. The fixture of that test (line 36) drops its private database WITH FORCE under a context of three seconds, while every other deadline of the package is ten to thirty seconds and the coordinator test helper of the same package (coordinatortest.go line 334) drops its private database with no deadline and logs a drop failure instead of failing the test. The package had never run under the gate before: in attempt 5 it finished in 0.125 s because L07_POSTGRES_DSN was absent and its tests skipped, and in attempt 6 it ran for 23.7 s with the variable supplied. Every other launchpad package passed, so the environment mirroring is complete and the one remaining failure is the fixture deadline."
fix = "Decision 3040: a private test database is dropped the way the coordinator test helper of the package drops it, with FORCE, under the package deadline of thirty seconds, and a drop failure is logged; 22.39.117 attempt 7 corrects the cleanup of online_indexes_test.go with the test file already inside its touches."

[gotcha.3738]
title = "The programme golden and refusal tasks run Go tests of kernel-linked packages under the mixed profile, whose environment never builds the kernel archives"
symptom = "Task 17.1.8 attempt 1 at 9380fccc111a and task 17.2.7 attempt 1 at a7575c8f63c0 (both on base 2432a1187cc7) passed their builds and completed their programme tests (the two golden rows with test_custody_golden.py, and run_refusals with test_refusal_run.py, which attempted every refusal row once), and both verifications failed at the same place: every go test they run (modules/layerxcustody/keeper, modules/layerxexchange/keeper, precompiles/layerxanchor, precompiles/common, precompiles/layerxverify, precompiles/layerxcustody) links the kernel through modules/lxphost, and the linker found neither build/liblayerx.a nor the programs host archive. Both tasks carry the mixed profile, and decision 1709 reserves the kernel archive prebuild for the go-cgo profile, so the archives never existed in their gate shells; no golden or refusal failed on its own assertion."
fix = "Decision 3041: a programme task whose verification runs Go tests of a kernel-linked package carries the go-cgo profile; 17.1.8 and 17.2.7 continue from their attempt-1 trees under it."

[gotcha.3739]
title = "The bounded lint gate of the agent daemon reports fourteen hundred pedantic lints of the crate itself, which the lint owner task has not yet repaired"
symptom = "Task 22.39.209 attempt 2 at 50823218f0a3 (base 5dcbf4629183) kept the one-line removal of the unused binding at agent_rpc_adapters.rs and its record, passed its build, and the bounded verification of decision 3039 (cargo clippy with no-deps over the layerx-agentd library, warnings denied) failed with 1440 errors, every one inside the daemon crate under the workspace lints the agent Cargo.toml declares (clippy all and pedantic denied, unwrap, expect and float arithmetic denied): 488 functions returning Result whose docs lack an Errors section, 178 methods that could carry the must-use attribute, 66 casts the pedantic group flags, 64 arguments passed by value and not consumed, 42 documentation items without backticks, redundant closures, unnecessary semicolons and functions with more than seven arguments among the rest. The daemon crate has never been clean under the workspace lints, which is the whole-workspace repair task 22.39.211 owns; the change of 22.39.209 is complete and the lint failures belong to the crate on main."
fix = "Decision 3043: while the lint owner task is pending, a task confined to one agent crate verifies with the build and the library tests of that crate and carries no lint clause; 22.39.209 attempt 3 reruns unchanged under that gate."

[gotcha.3740]
title = "A relaunched attempt of the agent SDK Python suite task re-ran the attempt-2 tree before the ruling of its predecessor applied and repeated the known failures"
symptom = "Task 22.39.119 attempt 4 at 304025d335de (base 75ed5856c098) ran as a requalification of the attempt-2 tree 15297431f074, because it started before the attempt-4 ruling (do_4, the payment RPC producer alignment of decision 2951 and the baseline rewrite of decision 2952) was recorded for the task; it performed no work and repeated the failures the ruling already addresses: 45 failed of 702 cases, among them 34 TypeError refusals of a hosted gateway endpoint keyword that PaymentRpc never accepted, the receipt_keys attribute the payment client no longer carries, the baseline assertion of test_repair_22_33_702.py, the historical coverage case of test_repair_22_33_701.py, two deployment payload budget refusals, a payer mismatch and an unsupported network. The attempt-3 tree 51d796cb3476 carries the seventeen repaired test files, the three SDK module corrections and the forty-six retired entries, and the recorded ruling of attempt 4 names it as the starting tree."
fix = "Decision 3044: an attempt that re-ran an earlier tree without the standing ruling is a repeat; attempt 5 follows do_4 in full from the attempt-3 tree, and no further ruling is written for the repeat."

[gotcha.3741]
title = "The parity coverage check reports eighty-four stale and two hundred and twenty-nine uncovered acceptance selectors, most of them artifacts of the selector grammar and of the unapplied stale map"
symptom = "Task 17.4.5 attempt 3 (the uncovered function of parity.py with the grammar of decision 2194 and the test test_installed_spec_has_no_uncovered_acceptance) failed its gate with 84 stale selectors and 229 uncovered selectors. The 84 stale selectors (file or test name absent from the tree, every owner done) have no entry in the stale map of 22.31.438, and of the 136 entries that map carries, 102 replacement entries and all 18 retired entries are still unapplied to the acceptance entries of the spec, while 34 already agree. Of the 229 uncovered selectors (named in the tests of no task), 217 resolve to acceptance entries whose requirement is held by tasks that are all done or superseded in 214 cases, 208 are document, data or command checks rather than test selectors (go.sum, the dependency floors, the workflow directory, a Dockerfile grep gate, make and cargo invocations), 195 of those name a path that exists, 10 name a path that does not exist or are commands, 7 do not match any acceptance test string literally, and 2 belong to requirements no task holds. The report is recorded in spec/layerx-merge/programme/parity-open-selectors.txt."
fix = "Decision 3045: coverage is decided by task ownership and path existence as well as by the tests lists, the stale map is consulted and extended in a second round by task 22.39.213, and the release owner applies the map to the acceptance entries; 17.4.5 continues from its attempt-3 tree after 22.39.213 lands."

[gotcha.3742]
title = "The receipt order golden task runs two Go cases of the kernel-linked node package under the mixed profile, where the kernel archive and the programs host archive are absent"
symptom = "Task 17.1.9 attempt 1 at b484071f1a8e (base 6ad27ec1df95) added [golden.receipt-order] to the goldens data file and the test module, passed its build, and failed its verification in the one case test_receipt_order_golden_passes: the golden ran go test ./node for TestOrderCheckRefusesSeqGap and TestOrderCheckRefusesPrevSeqHashMismatch and the link step of the node package could not find the kernel archive liblayerx or the programs host archive, so the package failed to build and the golden reported false. The task carried the mixed profile, which does not prebuild the two archives; decision 3041 already moved the sibling golden tasks 17.1.8 and 17.2.7 to the kernel archive profile after the same failure (gotcha 3738), and both published under it this hour. The attempt tree is complete and its two files are exactly the touches of the task; only the profile is at fault. The two remaining programme tasks whose gates run every golden or every parity row on the candidate, 17.0.9 and 17.4.6, carry the mixed profile as well and would fail the same way."
fix = "Decision 3046: 17.1.9, 17.0.9 and 17.4.6 carry the kernel archive profile in advance of their next attempt; 17.1.9 attempt 2 continues from the attempt-1 tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3743]
title = "The Go tests of the bridge deploy packages run two Node helpers whose dependency sets nothing installs, in the public go job or in the gate"
symptom = "Task 22.39.212 attempt 1 at 57191557c5b1 (base b1fd5106ceae) aligned the nine chain configurations, the proposal records and the audit assertions with the governed signer manifest, passed its build twice and failed its verification twice at exit 1: the manifest check, the task record, the placeholder scan and the 99 Python cases passed, and go test ./services/bridge/deploy/... failed in two packages. In appenv, repair_277_test.go line 108 runs node repair_277_app.mjs, which cannot find the package viem; in proposals, repair_270_test.go line 173 runs testdata/repair_270/compile-vault.cjs, which cannot find the module solc. Both helper packages declare what they need (services/bridge/deploy/appenv/package.json pins viem 2.41.2 and @noble/curves 2.4.0 with no lockfile; services/bridge/deploy/proposals/testdata/repair_270/package.json pins solc 0.8.30 with its npm-shrinkwrap.json) and nothing installs either set: the go job of .github/workflows/bridge-test.yml installs only the Go toolchain before go test, so the public job fails on main for the same reason, and the gate shell installs the root package set only. The attempt recorded the two failures as pre-existing and stopped after its two cycles; decision 2908 gives every failure of the whole-package gate to its owner and decision 3052 treats the red public job as a defect."
fix = "Decision 3047: the go job of the bridge workflow and the build of every task whose verification runs the Go tests of services/bridge/deploy install the two helper dependency sets first; 22.39.212 attempt 2 adds the job steps, the appenv lockfile and the build steps with the workflow in its touches."

[gotcha.3744]
title = "The production database tests of the launchpad shared module create roles, schemas and tables they never drop, so the second pass of one gate run collides with the first"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 7 at c19a2e3904d3 (base b1fd5106ceae) passed its build and the first half of its verification: the direct go test of the chain, db, delivery and storage packages of sdk/launchpad/shared passed, the production package among them in 17.8 seconds. The second half, make -C services/launchpad ci, runs the test target over every module and reached the shared module again, where three cases of shared/db/production failed at once: TestPostgresRoleAndNumericBoundaries (production_test.go line 162, role l07_stats_owner already exists, SQLSTATE 42710), TestPostgresCoordinatorAndCancellation (line 275, relation l07_rollback already exists, 42P07) and TestPhase3CancellationAndAuthorization (line 371, role l07_phase3_stats_runtime already exists). The three cases create their roles, schemas and tables with plain CREATE statements (lines 153 to 164, 266 and the phase-3 setup) and register no cleanup, so the objects of the first pass survive on the shared database server and the second pass refuses them; roles are server-wide, so the fresh database of decision 2917 does not remove them either. Every other module passed."
fix = "Decision 3048: the production tests drop every role, schema and table they create before creating them and again in cleanup, so the package runs twice against one server in one gate; 22.39.117 attempt 8 corrects the three cases with the test file under its touches."

[gotcha.3745]
title = "A stale map entry of the first round points at a replacement test that a later retirement removed while the original test exists again"
symptom = "Task 22.39.213 attempt 1 at 83c457fc182d (base f473b7e0c1cb) disposed 239 selectors, passed its build and failed its verification in the validator: stale.24 names the replacement services/agent/crates/layerx-wire/tests/structures.rs::every_published_activity_and_receipt_round_trips_exactly, and that test is not in the file. The entry comes from the first round (22.31.438) and was correct when written; task 9.29.1 at 71a71152c2 retired the kernel activity envelope and its signing preimage from layerx-wire and with them the combined round-trip test, and the test the entry originally replaced, every_published_receipt_round_trips_exactly, is in structures.rs again at line 137. The validator checks every entry at every run, so a first-round entry that aged out fails the second-round task; the attempt recorded it as pre-existing and stopped."
fix = "Decision 3049: the task that runs the stale map validator corrects an aged first-round entry in the same attempt, pointing its replacement at the test that exists on main with a reason naming the retirement; 22.39.213 attempt 2 corrects stale.24 and reruns."

[gotcha.3746]
title = "The launchpad wiring test pins the baseline before retirement, so the task that retires its entries cannot pass the wiring test without changing it"
symptom = "Task 22.39.168 attempt 1 at 933ff2d7d58e (base b1fd5106ceae) passed its build and failed its verification at the wiring test before any module test ran: nine cases of tests/ci/test_launchpad_go_tests_wired.py failed because they assert the baseline as task 22.39.75 recorded it, with 261 entries (line 213: 144 against 261), the exact per-module counts of the twelve modules (line 950: gateway 12, ranking-algo 10, the stats module 23, security/control 1 against zero), the user profile and security conflict entries (lines 1001 and 1018) and the module qualification records naming the 23 analytics and stats cases (line 1050). The verification of 22.39.168 requires zero baseline entries for its modules and the wiring test green at once, which the test as written cannot satisfy; the test file is outside the touches of the task and so is the baseline file it edits. The same run shows the attempt removed two api entries of the owner 22.39.154 (TestDevelopmentTransactionStatusFromChainRPC and TestRepair_27_log_free_receipts, line 408), outside its scope, and removed its 115 entries before the module runs proved them green; the attempt record says so."
fix = "Decision 3050: the wiring test asserts the retirement state of the baseline, the retiring task updates it in the same attempt with the test and the baseline in its touches, retires only entries it owns and only after the module passed; 22.39.168 attempt 2 restores the two api entries and proceeds module by module."

[gotcha.3747]
title = "The retired caller scanner issues one git grep per 128 tracked files, so the whole-repository scan outlives the thirty-minute limit of the programme task that runs it"
symptom = "Task 17.2.8 attempt 1 at ceda589fd709 (base 97391dc9af5f) created the test module and passed its build; its one case ran python3 tools/paxeer-x/tests/retired_callers_test.py --deleted through evidence.run, the scan was still running after 26 minutes 29 seconds, and the attempt stopped it a minute before the thirty-minute limit (exit -15), so the case failed on the interrupted command and the task stayed unqualified. The scanner (scan, lines 262 to 366) lists the 77841 tracked files once and then calls git grep in batches of 128 pathspecs of the form :(top,literal)path, 609 invocations in all, each one matching its 128 pathspecs against the full index while searching the 166 symbols of the 47 components; the self-test suite drives small temporary repositories and never meets that cost, and no workflow runs the scan over the repository. The catalogue, the match rules and the output format are sound."
fix = "Decision 3051: the scanner issues a single git grep over the tracked files and filters the matches against its selected set in memory; task 22.39.214 owns the change, 17.2.8 requires it and runs with a 120-minute limit."

[gotcha.3748]
title = "The epoch opening and the aggregation finalisation of the ai-market guest keep a fuel slope per roster participant of the order of the frame size through five bounded repairs, so they still refuse at twenty-four participants"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 15 at 642ca7eae683 (base 89e829476ec2) passed its build and 21 of its 24 cases; roster_state_fuel_scaling (tests/fuel_budget.rs line 2868) and maximum_state_fuel_scaling (line 2781) failed because OPEN_EPOCH and FinalizeAggregation were refused at the cap of 1000000 cpu fuel at the rosters 24/6 and 32/8 and at every task count of the maximum-state sweep at 32/8 (attempted 1000002 to 1000195, the interruption position), and every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap (line 1877) failed on the fuel the refused rows do not report. The measured rows of the attempt: OPEN_EPOCH 283977 at 8/2 (the readiness refusal) and 775119 at 16/4, the same slope of about 61400 per added participant as attempts 11 to 14 (779305 at 16/4 before this attempt); BeginAggregation 550827, 758498 and 968527 at 16/4, 24/6 and 32/8, about 26000 per participant; the first ProcessAggregation chunk 266144, 337706 and 410918, about 9000 per participant; FinalizeAggregation 908468 at 16/4 and refused from 24/6. The slope of OPEN_EPOCH per participant is of the order of the frame size (49163 to 63175 bytes across the rosters), the attempt changed 25 source files of the crate (4062 insertions) without moving it, and its record states that the attempted fuel of a refusal is the stopping position and not the required total."
fix = "Decision 3052: before any repair, attempt 16 measures the three handlers at the fixed roster 16/4 while the frame grows through the admitted task count, so a per-participant walk of the frame is proven or excluded; a proven walk is replaced by one indexed pass, and a cost that does not track the frame stops the attempt for an owner decision on a continuation operation."

[gotcha.3749]
title = "The agent lint target reports more than a thousand diagnostics in the test targets of the base types crate once its library lints are repaired, and cargo stops at the first failing member so nine members are never linted"
symptom = "Task 22.39.211 attempt 1 at 227acaa1fe0d (base 97391dc9af5f) passed its build twice; the lint target (cargo clippy over the services/agent workspace with all targets and warnings denied under the workspace lints, which deny clippy all and pedantic, unwrap, expect and float arithmetic) exited 1 twice. At the first tree 55f3c4e36e31 it reported 108 diagnostics: the eight of gotcha 3736 in layerx-types (src/chain.rs and src/historical/verify.rs) and 100 in layerx-crypto, 56 of them uses of retained deprecated compatibility items in the onboarding, disclosure, payments and signer modules. After those repairs the target reported 1205 diagnostics at 227acaa1fe0d: 1186 in the fourteen test targets of layerx-types (477 long literals without separators, 192 cast lints, 95 double parentheses, 49 unwrap uses on Result values, 27 similar names, 17 underscore-prefixed bindings in use), 60 in layerx-crypto and 63 unexpected cfg values (opt_size, x25519, blind-keys) in the copied field and digest test support of layerx-agent-api; cargo stopped at the first failing package, so layerx-wire, layerx-proof, layerx-client, layerx-identity-binding, layerx-agent-api, layerx-agentd, layerx-agentd-host, layerx-mcp and layerx-sdk were never linted in either run, and the two repair cycles of one task cannot carry the workspace."
fix = "Decision 3053: the lint target is brought green crate by crate through tasks 22.39.215 to 22.39.229, each linting its member alone with no-deps and the agent daemon split into its library and four test groups; 22.39.211 moves to wave 5, requires them and runs the whole target last."

[gotcha.3750]
title = "The bridge app environment tests assert the record writer of the deployment scripts in the form it had before the restart-recovery repair and a record literal without the governance fields, so the deploy package fails for the whole-package gate owner"
symptom = "Task 22.39.212 attempt 2 at 4bfb39fc0f2c (base 58fc909ddd01) passed its build (the two Node helper installs, the appenv lockfile, go build), the 99 Python cases of its verification and the chainconfig and proposals packages; go test of services/bridge/deploy/appenv failed five cases that the attempt did not touch. TestEnvLinesFromEVMRecords (appenv_test.go line 238) compares LoadRecord of tests/fixtures/records/ethereum.json with a literal carrying only chain, chain id, kind and vault, while the fixture (unchanged since 2026-10-21) and the Record type carry configuration, owner, threshold 3 and five attestors, so the literal predates the fields. TestRepair_277_LegacyProducerCheckpoint (repair_277_test.go line 294) and the three TestRepairM_484 cases (repair_m484_test.go line 48) locate the record writers of deploy-solana-program.sh and deploy-evm-chain.sh by the text jq -n --arg chain up to the redirection to the record path, but the restart-recovery repairs of 2026-11-04 (ae16b636df and 6198209c5b) redirect both writers to the work directory record and publish it through the journal command, so the pattern matches nothing and the transcript digests of testdata/repair_m484 bind to writer text that no longer exists. The attempt recorded the five as pre-existing and stopped; under decision 2908 the whole-package gate owner owns them."
fix = "Decision 3054 and attempt 3 of 22.39.212: the consumer tests follow the producers as they stand (the record literal with the governance fields, the writer pattern ending at the work directory record, the transcript digests recomputed over the current writer text), with no change to the scripts or the fixture record."

[gotcha.3751]
title = "The indexer retirement task removes its baseline entries and two api entries while the launchpad wiring test still asserts the pre-retirement baseline it may not touch"
symptom = "Task 22.39.162 attempt 2 at ba731cfe3d0c (base 564eae1972e8) passed its build (foundry present, go vet of the indexer module) and repaired indexer cases in the chainreader, httpapi and processor packages; the verification failed at its pytest step with six cases of tests/ci/test_launchpad_go_tests_wired.py, so the Go tests of the module never ran. The attempt removed every indexer entry from tests/ci/data/launchpad_go_test_baseline.json (261 entries to 226) and, outside its scope, the two api entries TestRepair_27_log_free_receipts and TestDevelopmentTransactionStatusFromChainRPC of the done task 22.39.154, which the test at line 408 expects; the test at line 213 expects the pre-retirement total of 261, the cases at lines 560 and 774 expect the approved indexer failures and their refusal classes, and the two parametrised cases expect indexer entries naming 22.39.117 and 22.39.154 as wrong retiring owners. The task carries neither the wiring test nor the baseline in its touches, so the attempt stopped and asked for the scope that decision 3050 already grants the retiring task, while 22.39.168 attempt 2 holds the same two files for the other eleven modules."
fix = "Decision 3055 and attempt 3 of 22.39.162: the wiring test and the baseline join the touches, the api entries stay as main carries them, the attempt merges main after 22.39.168 lands and turns the indexer-specific cases into retirement-state assertions."

[gotcha.3752]
title = "The commit reviewer filed three hundred and forty-two issues in six days while the triage programme stopped at issue 1578, so every open issue lacks a task"
symptom = "Decision 2427 opened one triage report task per open issue for issues 1511 to 1562 and decision 2490 recorded the reports for 1563 to 1578 directly; both rounds closed on 2026-11-03 and 2026-11-05. The commit reviewer kept filing coherence issues against every landed revision at about fifty a day, so on 2026-11-09 the repository carried 343 open issues, of which 342 (1579 to 1923) had neither a report under spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues nor a task, and the one older issue 1540 waits on an owner ruling. The closure ruling needs every issue closed or ruled out with a reason, and the issue closer acts only on a report or a done 18.<N>.1 task, so the whole stream was invisible to the programme."
fix = "Decision 3056: the triage programme runs its third round as decision 2427 prescribes, one report task 22.93.k per open issue (22.93.52 to 22.93.393) over the recorded inputs, and the report tasks are reopened whenever the open set grows past the recorded inputs."

[gotcha.3753]
title = "The per-crate lint tasks skip the inventory run, repair whole crates without compiling and stall on lints whose only repair changes a public signature"
symptom = "Nine of the eleven per-crate lint tasks of decision 3053 failed their first attempt the same way (22.39.215, 217, 218, 219, 221, 222, 223, 224 and 225 at base d231853743c8). Every record states that the inventory run of do_1 was not performed because the ordered gate rules forbid running the verification command by hand, so the repairs were written from a static reading of the sources; the crates were then repaired file by file without a compile, and the two repair cycles went to compile errors the repairs themselves introduced (a closure given to an Option combinator that takes none, a removed import still in use, an extracted helper without the method its caller needs, four assertion type mismatches), so for 217, 224 and 225 the lint gate never ran and for 215, 219 and 221 the final tree no longer builds. Where the gate did run, the remaining lints were of two kinds: lints whose only repair changes a public signature (the large variant of the public ProofRecord enum in layerx-proof, a four-byte argument of a public function passed by reference in layerx-agent-api, a public method named next outside the Iterator trait in layerx-client), which decision 3053 forbids both to change and to allow at crate or module level, and lints in sources outside the touched paths: the manifest of layerx-agentd-host declares the daemon binary ../layerx-agentd/src/main.rs and four host-tests targets of the daemon crate, so the clippy run of 22.39.223 lints daemon sources that only 22.39.222 may touch. The daemon library alone inventories 1413 diagnostics, of which 374 remained after one 300-minute attempt."
fix = "Decision 3057: the inventory run is a measurement the task performs before any edit and refreshes after each repaired file, a lint whose only repair changes a public signature carries an item-level allowance with a reason on that item, large inventories proceed by tranches across attempts, and the host crate task carries the daemon binary and host-tests paths and requires the daemon library task; attempt 2 of each task continues from its record tree."

[gotcha.3754]
title = "The parity inventory on the merged revision refuses four rows at the command builder, lacks two environment prerequisites and shows five red constructs"
symptom = "Task 17.4.6 attempt 1 at 1d4c4fdef0d6 (base 016028d4d52f) wrote run_all and the test, and the run of 27 minutes failed eleven rows. Four never ran: command_for of spec/layerx-merge/programme/parity.py knows the Go, Python and Rust toolchains only, so construct.existing-kernel-replay-corpus (a C selector), construct.new-explorer-signature and construct.new-signed-receipt-logs-new-case (Elixir selectors) were refused as unsupported, and construct.existing-wallet-human-service-and-explorer was refused because its selectors mix toolchains. Two failed on the environment: TestSealBatchEqualsGigaProcessBlock of node/sequencer requires the VM built by make evmone-lib, which the node job builds before its tests and the runner did not, and the gateway rows (construct.existing-router-gateway-authority-and-indexer, construct.new-router-balances) spawn redis-server from PATH, absent in the qualification environment of a programme task. Five rows are red constructs on the merged revision: TestRevokeGrantAdvancesRevocation of modules/layerxauth/keeper sends upax, which scopeActivity (types/authorization.go line 188) refuses because the denomination has no canonical kernel asset since the mirror denominations landed; TestServiceDisputeArbiterRefusals of modules/layerxpay/keeper expects code -739 LXP_ESCROW_LINK_MISMATCH for a corrupted escrow link on open and resolve and receives another error, and TestServiceOfferPublishWithdraw finds the module store changed after a publish and withdraw and the stored offer differing from the published fields; native_request_binds_real_signed_fixture of services/agent/crates/layerx-sdk/tests/native_programs.rs line 66 expects NativeProgramCallRequest::new to refuse the legacy activity and it binds; TestProgramsGuestEventLogs and TestProgramsCallOutcomeLog of precompiles/layerxprograms fail with programs: missing canonical guest event evidence from events_call.go line 35 for receipts whose events the test fixture builds with callGuestEnvelope. The 30-minute limit of the task is below the 27-minute run plus its setup."
fix = "Decision 3058: command_for gains the C and Elixir toolchains, the mixed row is split per toolchain, run_all builds the native prerequisites once, the qualification environment provides the Redis binary to the programme gate tasks, and four repair tasks (22.39.230 to 22.39.233) bring the five red constructs green at their producers before 17.4.6 attempt 2 runs the inventory again under a 240-minute limit."

[gotcha.3755]
title = "The wave gate script refuses the task tree because the workflow bookkeeping leaves tracked files modified"
symptom = "Task 17.5.7 attempt 1 at f0619bc8c681 (base 016028d4d52f) created spec/layerx-merge/programme/tests/test_wave_6_gate.py, which calls gates.run_wave(6, root) on the task tree; the script scripts/gates/wave-6.sh goes through scripts/gates/run_gate.py, whose source identity check (git status with untracked and ignored files) refuses any tracked modification outside the evidence root and the build output directories, and the verification ended with exit 125, status source-identity-refusal, phase before. The task tree carries the bookkeeping edits the spec workflow writes at task start (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx, AGENTS.md, .cgignore, the rendered rule files) plus the backup directory of the rendered rules, so every wave gate test fails before its first command, while 17.1.7 and 17.2.7 passed because their runners call evidence.run directly."
fix = "Decision 3059: gates.run_wave runs the wave script in a detached worktree of HEAD that shares the build caches, so the gate measures the committed revision the evidence line names; 17.5.7 attempt 2 carries gates.py in its touches and runs under a 600-minute limit."

[gotcha.3756]
title = "The ranking snapshots constraint admits six categories while the ranker declares eight"
symptom = "Task 22.39.168 attempt 2 at d6875dc1123f (base d231853743c8) restored the two api entries, passed its build and the 42 wiring tests, and the runner failed in the first module: TestProductionUniverseCompletesAndPublishes of services/launchpad/ranking-algo/internal/store refused a snapshot row with the check constraint snapshots_category_check (SQLSTATE 23514), and TestNewServesAndRanks and TestRepairM_934_PublicationEveryCategoryAndRestartRecovery of internal/app reported health/ready 503 after the publication window and a vacuous trending publication. The registered migration launchpad/spec/production-system/integration/migrations/190000.sql constrains category to trending, breakout, volume, movers, unusual and new, while ranker.Categories declares eight categories including gainers and losers, so every publication that writes the two newer categories fails and readiness never arrives. The record of the attempt names the migration as outside the touched paths and stops there; the registry of migrations is append-only."
fix = "Decision 3060: the task that brings the ranking module green adds a registered migration widening the constraint to the categories the ranker declares, with the migrations directory in its touches; 22.39.168 attempt 3 continues from the attempt-2 tree."

[gotcha.3757]
title = "Three launchpad Go files are not gofmt-clean on main, so the whole-launchpad gate fails at fmt-check once its tests pass"
symptom = "Task 22.39.117 attempt 8 at 9e3d5fdcb4a4 (base 564eae1972e8) completed the database fixture cleanup, passed its build and every module test, and make ci then failed at fmt-check (services/launchpad/Makefile line 68): gofmt -l names sdk/launchpad/shared/interfaces/v2/types.gen.go, sdk/launchpad/shared/interfaces/v2/validators.gen.go and services/launchpad/trading-charts/internal/engine/candle_stream_test.go. All three were last changed by the workspace flattening commit 34d6fa0460 of 2026-10-21 and no gate reached fmt-check since, because the test stage failed first in every earlier attempt. The two generated files carry the generated-code header of tools/launchpad/production/interfaces/codegen.py, whose generator formats its output when gofmt is available."
fix = "Decision 3061: the gate owner formats the three files in place and confirms the generator check still accepts the generated pair; 22.39.117 attempt 9 carries the trading-charts test file in its touches."

[gotcha.3758]
title = "The bond operations still exceed the guest bound by 3552 bytes after the second size reduction"
symptom = "Task 22.38.7 attempt 3 at 17c9ba36e628 (base 25f2f0c1b736, after 22.39.167 and 22.39.177 landed) carried out the attempt-2 ruling (the bond module in the shared helpers and the placement book region, the bond lock in every bid setup, the batch record of the peers that did not countersign) and the build gate failed three times at the size test: the final guest measures 527736 bytes against the bound 524184, 3552 bytes over, with both repair cycles spent inside the five touched source files. The verification never ran."
fix = "Decision 2927 holds; attempt 4 continues from the attempt-3 tree and recovers the remaining bytes from the function metrics table of the bond and routing functions."

[gotcha.3759]
title = "The single git grep over the whole tracked tree does not finish the retired-caller scan within the ten-minute gate"
symptom = "Task 22.39.214 attempt 1 at 045bfdb54134 (base dc72fdfd4d65) rewrote the search loop of tools/paxeer-x/tests/retired_callers_test.py to one git grep over the tracked tree with the in-memory path filter, added the self-test case, and passed the 111 self-test cases twice; the whole-repository scan with --deleted then ended with an exit the gate refuses (neither 0 nor 1) in both verification runs, which under timeout 600 means the scan still ran at ten minutes or the scanner refused. Without pathspecs the grep walks every tracked blob, the large vendored and generated trees included, and emits every literal match for the filter to drop afterwards, so the match volume rather than the invocation count now bounds the time."
fix = "Decision 3062: the scanner issues one git grep whose pathspecs are the selected files read from standard input through --pathspec-from-file, so the tracked walk stays bounded to the selected set; attempt 2 measures the scan before the gate."

[gotcha.3760]
title = "The receipt provenance digest rename alone does not reproduce the recorded header encoding, and the historical authority lookup asks the chain fixture for a reply it never recorded"
symptom = "Task 22.39.162 attempt 3 at 316a8a12884b (base ae96a903290c) retired the 33 indexer exclusions, passed its build and the 42 wiring tests, and left three cases failing in the indexer suite after the two repair cycles. In internal/processor, TestRepairM_1000_InventoryDurableFrames fails at repair_m1000_test.go line 622 with receipt qualification rejected on the first recorded batch (block 33963716), and TestRepairM_1000_MeasurementRefusals fails at line 684 with the message source pool: identity, which no file of the indexer tree contains as a literal, so the message is composed at run time. In internal/runtimedocs, TestPaxeerRehydratedAuthorityQualifiesTradesOfEarlierMarket fails at chainfixture.go line 125 because the recorded chain-125 fixture holds no reply for the eth_getCode call that the historical emitter epoch path of internal/receipt/history.go now binds to the block hash 0xd955d693c649ee8e9a69be1e9d6d683ac05a6b846ecbb6f0d165ff1a698ceb68 for the contract 0x85fcd13735f4309833a503ee804ea32395851479. The attempt added provenanceHeaderDigest to internal/receipt/qualified.go, which renames blockAccessListHash back to balHash in the header JSON that go-ethereum 1.17.4 produces before hashing (record gotcha.7), yet the recorded receipts of the fixture still fail qualification, so the rename alone does not reproduce the encoding under which the recorded provenance digests were produced. The attempt record carries 33 repair entries and no entry for the two processor cases."
fix = "Decision 3064: a provenance digest rule is proven by re-deriving the digest of a recorded header and comparing it with the recorded digest, never by renaming a field; attempt 4 derives the established encoding from the recorded provenance of block 33963716, records the one missing fixture reply through the fixture record mode, and locates the composed source pool refusal at its producer."

[gotcha.3761]
title = "The retired-caller scanner names a git grep option the installed git does not have, so the one-pass design of decision 3062 never ran"
symptom = "Task 22.39.214 attempt 2 at the record tree of refs 22.39.214 (base 93249965659c) rebuilt scan() as decision 3062 asked: one git grep over the tracked tree with the fixed-string pattern file, the path filter applied in memory, and the path list passed through --pathspec-from-file=- with --pathspec-file-nul. git grep in the installed git 2.53.0 exposes neither option (they belong to git add, checkout, commit, reset and rm), so the command exited 129 with a usage message before any match was read, and the record tests/repair_22_39_214.kvx names the absence as an interface blocker. The attempt-1 version of the same scanner ran one unbounded git grep over the whole tree and exceeded the 600 second budget with LC_ALL=C, so neither shape has measured the scan yet."
fix = "Decision 3065: the scanner excludes the deleted trees, the test directories and the documentation files through pathspecs given on the command line (negative pathspecs with the exclude and top magic), keeps LC_ALL=C and -F, applies the in-memory path filter to every match unconditionally, runs a symbol regex only for the symbols whose literal occurs in the line, and records the git grep wall time and output size separately from the Python loop; 22.39.214 attempt 3 continues from the attempt-2 tree."

[gotcha.3762]
title = "The layerxpay integration genesis test still destructures the two-value shape of GetEscrow, so go vet of the layerxpay module fails on main"
symptom = "Task 22.39.231 attempt 1 at 3fb8fde7f50d (base 93249965659c) wrote its dispute repair and the record and failed the build: go vet ./modules/layerxpay/... reports modules/layerxpay/integration/genesis_test.go line 225, assignment mismatch, two variables but GetEscrow returns three values. The keeper view in modules/layerxpay/keeper/escrow_views.go line 42 returns the record, a presence flag and an error since 21f6e29026 (task 22.99.110), and the integration test was never updated; the file is outside the touches of the task (modules/layerxpay/keeper), so the attempt could not repair it."
fix = "Decision 2908 applies: 22.39.231 attempt 2 repairs the destructuring at line 225 (three values, the error asserted nil) with the test file in its touches, and the attempt-1 tree stands."

[gotcha.3763]
title = "The repair_m212 precompile test copies the application struct by value, which go vet refuses because the struct holds a mutex"
symptom = "Task 22.39.232 attempt 1 at fc5b1376c4e3 (base 93249965659c) wrote the events call repair and failed the build: go vet ./precompiles/layerxprograms/... reports precompiles/layerxprograms/repair_m212_test.go lines 29 and 161, assignment copies lock value to application, because the helper assigns the dereferenced EVM test application (which embeds a sync.RWMutex through node.App) to a local value before setting its LayerXHost. The file landed with ec03cd12bf (task 22.33.212) and is inside the touches of the task, and no gate of the package ran go vet over the test since."
fix = "Decision 2908 applies: 22.39.232 attempt 2 removes the struct copy in repairM212Merge, working on a pointer to the application with LayerXHost set for the call and restored afterwards, or composing the precompile keepers from the fields the merge needs; the attempt-1 tree stands."

[gotcha.3764]
title = "The fixed-roster measurement proves that opening an epoch and finalising an aggregation cost per participant, so the 32/8 roster cannot fit either operation in one call"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 16 at 011622fd5d1b (base 3520b1428059) measured the ai-market guest with the roster held at 16/4 and the task count varied over 16, 32, 48 and 64: BeginAggregation 419046, 419162, 419280 and 419396 fuel and FinalizeAggregation 804628, 804744, 804862 and 804978, about seven fuel per added task, so no per-task or per-participant frame walk hides in the chunked handlers. The roster sweep then shows the intrinsic cost: OPEN_EPOCH at 16/4 costs 747867 and is refused at 24/6 and at 32/8; FinalizeAggregation at 16/4 costs 804628 and is refused at 24/6 and at 32/8; the handler review found no per-participant frame lookup to remove. Four sweep cases failed (roster_state_fuel_scaling, maximum_state_fuel_scaling, fixed_roster_task_fuel_scaling and every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap), exit 101, log /out/logs/verify-1.log, and the attempt stopped as decision 3052 requires for an owner decision on a continuation operation."
fix = "Decision 3066: OPEN_EPOCH and FinalizeAggregation become resumable over participant chunks of eight with a cursor in the handler section, every call at or under 900000 fuel at 32/8, and the native caller repeats the call until the cursor reports completion; 22.33.223 attempt 17 continues from the attempt-16 tree."

[gotcha.3765]
title = "Ten verification commands of the fourth triage round carry doubled backslashes, so their grep and awk programs fail to parse"
symptom = "The commands of 18.1588.1, 18.1590.1, 18.1591.1, 18.1592.1, 18.1603.1, 18.1604.1, 18.1607.1, 18.1609.1, 18.1610.1 and 18.1611.1 were written with every backslash doubled, on the assumption that the task runner unescapes the kvx string before the shell reads it; it passes the string raw. 18.1592.1 attempt 1 at 6c34ffb03d2a and 18.1607.1 attempt 1 at 032667c8ca1d failed with awk syntax errors (unexpected character backslash, exit 2), and 18.1588.1, 18.1590.1, 18.1591.1, 18.1604.1, 18.1610.1 and 18.1611.1 attempt 1 failed with grep patterns that matched a literal backslash (exit 1); 18.1603.1 and 18.1609.1 passed because their patterns tolerate the doubling and stay as they are."
fix = "The eight commands that failed are rewritten with single backslashes, and the eight failed attempts requalify at their trees."

[gotcha.3766]
title = "The wave-6 completion gate counts the retired interfaces by one status word after the registry re-status wrote a second"
symptom = "Task 17.5.7 attempt 2 at 2cec5a4643d8 (base 93249965659c) ran the wave-6 script through the detached worktree of decision 3059, and the human build target failed in human_completion_retired_surfaces_absent of services/human/tools/api-gen/tests/completion_gate.rs line 216: the retired-interface inventory counted 10 where the test expects 52. The test keeps the interfaces of the thirteen wave-6 tasks whose registry status equals retire; the registry rewrote the retire rows whose file or symbol is absent at HEAD to retired (e5cb35b977 of 2026-11-03 and 88761d5290 of 2026-11-09), so forty-two of the fifty-two rows now read retired and the test no longer sees them. The test file is outside the touches of the task."
fix = "Decision 2908 applies: 17.5.7 attempt 3 makes the test count both retirement statuses of the registry with the test file in its touches, keeping the expected count of 52 when the two statuses together yield it and otherwise recording the rows by id with the registry commit that changed them."

[gotcha.3767]
title = "The layerx-mcp lint attempt broke the build with a double reference and left forty-eight lints, and the layerx-proof attempt left seven lints in test support"
symptom = "Task 22.39.224 attempt 2 at e6e1f6b3c4349f (base 93249965659c) restored the four assertion mismatches, ran the clippy inventory (48 library lints and 53 with the test targets, mostly in src/tools/wallet.rs, src/tools/web.rs, src/tools/write.rs and src/catalogue.rs: missing Errors sections, format in iterator folds, redundant closures, functions over one hundred lines, two functions with more than seven arguments, items after statements, identical match arms) and then failed its second build with E0308 at src/server.rs line 1234, where crate::hex receives a reference to a reference (hold_id is already a byte array reference). Task 22.39.218 attempt 2 at 44fccbf445bc exhausted its two cycles with seven lints left in the test targets: a 183-line function in tests/native_terminal_outcome.rs line 337, missing backticks and a field named after its struct in tests/repair_22_31_226.rs line 2, a format fold in tests/support/historical_checkpoint.rs lines 35 and 136."
fix = "Both tasks continue from their attempt-2 trees under decision 3053: 22.39.224 attempt 3 first restores the build (pass hold_id itself to hex) and then repairs the recorded inventory in file order, splitting long functions into named helpers and gathering excess arguments into a parameters struct for private functions; 22.39.218 attempt 3 repairs the seven test-target lints."

[gotcha.3768]
title = "The native program HTTP test fails at submission with a missing node read authority once the type-2 enforcement lands"
symptom = "Task 22.39.233 attempt 1 at 1f4422082db6 (base 93249965659c) made NativeProgramCallRequest::from_signed_transaction refuse empty, oversized and non-type-2 bytes before the shared decoder and brought native_request_binds_real_signed_fixture green, and program_http_decodes_signed_program_calls_as_eip1559 of tests/native_programs.rs then failed with HTTP submission: MissingNodeReadAuthority. The refusal comes from check_node_network in src/program_node.rs line 161, which requires the transport to carry the network and height-ranged receipt authority that connect_node supplies (the submission path checks it since 4e29e49379 of 2026-11-04), and the test builds its HttpProgramTransport without connecting a node; the attempt changed nothing on that path, and the whole test binary had not run under a gate since."
fix = "Decision 2908 applies: 22.39.233 attempt 2 keeps the constructor change and makes the HTTP test connect the recorded node authority of the fixture before it submits, following connect_node as the producer, with the test file inside the touches of the task."

[gotcha.3769]
title = "The native library make target builds evmone from source with cmake, which the qualification environment does not have, so the rpc gates that start with it cannot run"
symptom = "Tasks 18.1628.1 attempt 1 at f74269089bc8 and 18.1632.1 attempt 1 at b2698d0728ca (base 93249965659c) wrote their rpc changes and failed the build at make -s paxd-native-libs: chain.mk line 111 runs cmake for evmone 0.12.0 (8ea5577a87, task 22.39.165, 2026-11-08) and the shell reports cmake not found, exit 127. Eighty qualified rpc tasks gate with go build ./rpc/... and go test -count=1 ./rpc/ -run on the named cases without the native library, which the Giga executor loads at run time and no rpc test needs."
fix = "Decision 3067: an rpc gate never builds the native libraries; the two tasks gate with go build and go test and continue from their attempt-1 trees."

[gotcha.3770]
title = "The perps type check is red on main with one hundred and sixty JSX component type errors from two React type packages"
symptom = "Tasks 18.1657.1 attempt 1 at 177143db974a, 18.1663.1 attempt 1 at 5e8af1b6833c and 18.1668.1 attempt 1 at 20e8236ceca9 (base 93249965659c) wrote their perps changes and failed the shared build pnpm --dir apps/perps exec tsc --noEmit with 183 errors in files none of them touched: 160 TS2786 (a lucide icon, a next Link or a wagmi provider cannot be used as a JSX component), 17 TS2769 and 6 TS2339, the messages naming the React type declarations under services/wallet/node_modules (@types/react 18.3.31) against the perps declarations, and the perps lockfile resolving both @types/react 18.3.28 and 19.3.0. The gate last passed at ef27dfb47e85 on 2026-10-27; the manifests and lockfiles changed with 22.39.85, 22.39.10x and 22.39.113 between 2026-11-07 and 2026-11-08."
fix = "Decision 3068: task 22.39.234 brings the perps type check back to one React type resolution, and the three issue tasks require it and continue from their attempt-1 trees."

[gotcha.3771]
title = "The rpc integration test package has never been type checked under a gate and carries six unknown-typed accesses"
symptom = "Task 18.1654.1 attempt 1 at d229a7334c24 (base 93249965659c) failed its build pnpm --dir tests/integration/rpc_tests exec tsc --noEmit on files it did not touch: eth/eth_getBlockTransactionCountByNumber.spec.ts line 43 and eth/eth_getLogs.spec.ts line 50 (result is of type unknown) and utils/wasmUtils.ts lines 56 and 59 (body is of type unknown, four sites). No earlier gate ran tsc over the package."
fix = "Decision 2908 applies: 18.1654.1 attempt 2 narrows the six accesses at their sites with the three files in its touches and then implements the subscription change."

[gotcha.3772]
title = "A test-target clippy gate on the programs runtime crate lints the library too, which carries two hundred pedantic lints"
symptom = "Task 18.1635.1 attempt 1 at 9caaf3f0f83d (base 93249965659c) failed its build cargo clippy -p layerx-programs-runtime --test repair_22_33_227 --no-deps -- -D warnings with 200 errors in the library sources (complex types, functions over one hundred lines and the rest of the pedantic group the programs workspace denies), before the test target was linted; the unwrap_used lint the issue is about is denied at crate level in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/Cargo.toml line 42, and no task brings the crate under the workspace lints yet."
fix = "Decision 3069: the issue task gates with cargo build of the test target, a fixed-string check that the test file calls no unwrap, and the test run; task 22.39.235 brings the crate under the workspace lints."

[gotcha.3773]
title = "The registry artifact suite needs a live registry manifest, so its cases cannot run under pytest in the qualification environment"
symptom = "Task 18.1638.1 attempt 1 at 074ff068d28f (base 93249965659c) failed its verification: tools/bringup/tests/registry-artifacts.py is a unittest program whose setUpClass validates the manifest named by --manifest or PAXEER_X_REGISTRY_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST and prepares real bound artifacts against the registry (test_01_real_bound_artifacts_and_quota), so the pytest selection of test_22_completed_job_history_survives_cleanup_reload raised PAXEER_X_REGISTRY_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST is required without --manifest at setup. The attempt made no product change."
fix = "Decision 3070: the persistence of completed job results is proven by a module-level test under a temporary directory in tools/bringup/tests/test_registry_job_history.py, and the live case stays in the suite for the registry run; 18.1638.1 attempt 2 gates on the module-level test."

[gotcha.3774]
title = "The drift test of the UCP checkout fixture compares two file lists that hold the same entries in different orders"
symptom = "Task 18.1639.1 attempt 1 at fb2ca1f9175f (base 93249965659c) wrote the classification in sdk/platform/pipeline.kvx and the case ucp_checkout_fixture_classification_survives_check_and_write in sdk/platform/generators/tests/drift.rs, and the case failed at its OutputState equality: the two platform-conformance states carry the same files with the same digests, the regenerated one in the order the writer emits and the expected one in the order the test collected (git ls-files order against the sorted declaration order)."
fix = "18.1639.1 attempt 2 compares the states through one ordering, the sorted path order the pipeline writer uses, and keeps the assertion otherwise unchanged."

[gotcha.3775]
title = "The explorer node-fetch allow-list test is red on main because three later specification files import node-fetch without an allow-list entry"
symptom = "Task 18.1712.1 attempt 1 at e00b671ac7e4 (base 93249965659c) passed its build and failed its verification in the case nodeFetchImportsStayServerOnly of apps/explorer/repair-22-31-512.spec.ts: the case walks every file that imports node-fetch and requires each to be listed in nodeTestModules, and three files added after the list was written are not listed, nextjs/pages-tests/api/repair-22-35-10.spec.ts line 4 and ui/snippets/searchBar/repair-22-35-10.spec.tsx line 5 (22.35.10, 2026-11-06) and ui/pages/PaxeerXInference.spec.tsx line 4 (22.38.33, 2026-11-07). The failure is independent of the tree of the attempt and the allow-list file is outside its touches."
fix = "Attempt 2 adds the three test modules to nodeTestModules with the allow-list file in the touches, under decision 2908."

[gotcha.3776]
title = "The chain indicators chart specification still passes the days property the producer removed, so the explorer type check fails"
symptom = "Task 18.1720.1 attempt 1 at c4355decafc5 (base 93249965659c) removed the days property of ChainIndicatorsChart.tsx for the calendar-day window design and failed its build: apps/explorer/ui/home/indicators/ChainIndicatorsChart.spec.tsx line 53 (on main since 9a7c1d9479, 2026-10-21) still renders the component with days={ 14 }, so tsc reported TS2322 and the verification never ran. The specification file was outside the touches, so the attempt could not follow its own producer change into the consumer test (gotcha 3046)."
fix = "Attempt 2 carries the specification file in its touches and rewrites the trims-the-series case to the calendar-day window."

[gotcha.3777]
title = "The launchpad render tests fail under the receipt qualification rule the baseline already records, so the status issue task waits for the retiring task"
symptom = "Task 18.1695.1 attempt 1 at d2f97ccb678d (base 93249965659c) passed its build and failed both verification cases with receipt qualification rejected: TestRenderedProductionDocumentsBoot at render_test.go line 145 and TestIndexerStatus1695 at status_1695_test.go line 244, both through receipt.NewRPCQualification over the recorded production documents. tests/ci/data/launchpad_go_test_baseline.json records TestRenderedProductionDocumentsBoot as known failing for exactly this reason with retiring task 22.39.162 (wave 2, pending), and the new status test boots the same documents through the same rule."
fix = "18.1695.1 requires 22.39.162 and moves to wave 2; attempt 2 continues after the retiring task lands."

[gotcha.3778]
title = "The explorer backend test environment has no Redis service, so every controller test that touches the session store fails with a persistence error"
symptom = "Tasks 18.1673.1 attempt 1 at 47e42319140a and 18.1651.1 attempt 1 at d1ee7253d734 (both base 93249965659c) passed their builds and failed their verifications with BlockScoutWeb.Plug.RedisCookie.PersistenceError (18.1673.1 in confirm OTP successfully; 18.1651.1 in get watchlist id at address_controller_test.exs line 440). services/explorer/deploy/tools/mix-in-builder.sh runs mix inside the pinned Elixir builder container joined to the network namespace of one postgres:16 database container and starts nothing else; the session store of the backend endpoint (endpoint.ex line 68) writes through Redix, which services/explorer/backend/apps/explorer/lib/explorer/application.ex line 96 starts from ACCOUNT_REDIS_URL with the default redis://127.0.0.1:6379. The second verification of 18.1651.1 also showed a failure the attempt did not touch: get EIP-1967 proxy contract info (line 329) returns an empty implementations list on main."
fix = "Decision 3071 and task 22.39.236 add a Redis container beside the database container; 18.1673.1 and 18.1651.1 require it, and the verification of 18.1651.1 names its three tests while the proxy failure is recorded as a qualification finding."

[gotcha.3779]
title = "The web search receipt fixtures of the TypeScript SDK test carry a settlement operation the client refuses, and the test casts a literal the compiler rejects"
symptom = "Task 18.1713.1 attempt 1 at fca0ac74d127 (base 93249965659c) failed its first build because the script ran tsc through a package manager that is not installed for that directory, then compiled with one error, TS2352 at test/web-search.test.ts line 166 column 35 (a conversion between two object literal types with no overlap), and its verification failed twenty-nine of thirty-three cases with WebSearchError settlement-operation-mismatch thrown at services/agent/sdk/typescript/src/web-search.ts line 359, where the client requires receipt moduleId 12 and operation 2; the receipts the attempt wrote for its fixtures carry other values. The check is unchanged from main (line 358 there)."
fix = "Attempt 2 writes fixture receipts that carry the settlement module and operation of the producer and replaces the cast with a typed literal."

[gotcha.3780]
title = "Four issue task gates name a package manager the directory does not use, so the gates fail before the tests run"
symptom = "Task 18.1718.1 attempt 1 at 0daffc77f779 failed its build with ERR_PNPM_OTHER_PM_EXPECTED because apps/explorer is a yarn workspace (precedent gates of 22.33.274 use yarn). Task 18.1766.1 attempt 1 at 9402211da8e3 failed with webpack not found because services/explorer/backend/apps/block_scout_web/assets is installed with npm from its package-lock.json (precedent npm ci --ignore-scripts). Task 18.1711.1 attempt 1 at 80a88738417b failed with tsc not found because services/platform/middleware/conformance is an npm package whose build script is tsc -p tsconfig.json (precedent build of its sibling tasks). Task 18.1770.1 attempt 1 at 2a88ca65780f failed its build because apps/explorer/deploy/tools/envs-validator carries a yarn.lock and the pnpm install of its modules was refused (ERR_PNPM_OTHER_PM_EXPECTED), so vite could not resolve property-expr from the yup package (precedent gate of 22.33.499: yarn install with the frozen lock, then yarn). All four trees are complete; only the commands were wrong."
fix = "Decision 3072 fixes the rule; the four gates move to the package manager of their lock files and the attempts requalify at their revisions."

[gotcha.3781]
title = "The agent daemon proof tests start the local node, whose script builds the node binary through the chain make file, which the gate shell cannot build without cmake"
symptom = "Task 18.1743.1 attempt 1 at 37960b88eacc (base 93249965659c) passed its build and failed its verification: tests/proof_serve_errors.rs includes proof_native_reads.rs, whose cases start tools/qualification/localnode/v6120-node.sh (line 587), and the script builds paxd with make -f chain.mk install when PAXD is not executable (lines 332 to 345); that target builds evmone from source with cmake (gotcha 3769), so the node never started and the startup log was not collected. Task 21.95.1 passed the same build in its own build command (make -f chain.mk install before cargo) when the gate shell had cmake for that build."
fix = "Decision 3073: a gate whose tests start the local node builds the node binary in its build command; the gate shell provides cmake for that build, and 18.1743.1 requalifies with the build command of 21.95.1."

[gotcha.3782]
title = "The platform CLI bootstrap test passes a UUID where the trace identifier parser requires the trc_ prefix and thirty-two hexadecimal digits"
symptom = "Task 18.1747.1 attempt 1 at 492b07abcd86 (base 93249965659c) passed its build and panicked in tools/platform/cli/tests/repair_22_33_63.rs line 1648 with bootstrap peer: Malformed: the test calls TraceId::parse on 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001, and TraceId::parse (trace.rs lines 12, 13 and 38 to 46) accepts only the prefix trc_ followed by thirty-two lowercase hexadecimal digits."
fix = "Attempt 2 builds the identifier in the format of the producer."

[gotcha.3783]
title = "The px_listAssets method accepts an explicit null cursor, which the OpenRPC contract declares invalid"
symptom = "Task 18.1665.1 attempt 1 at 3dd4b2d997c5 (base 93249965659c) passed its build and failed its verification twice: px_node_root_account_test.go line 687 expects error code -32602 for a request whose cursor is JSON null and received no error, and line 589 expected eight items and received none. rpc/px_assets.go ListAssets (lines 193 to 199) validates only a non-nil cursor, so a null cursor passes as if absent."
fix = "Attempt 2 refuses a null cursor with invalid params and repairs the count case at its source."

[gotcha.3784]
title = "The subscription test fixture commits a block whose served header carries a zero state root, so the new-heads event is dropped as inconsistent"
symptom = "Task 18.1643.1 attempt 1 at efcb96016b69 (base 93249965659c) passed its build and failed rpc/subscribe_test.go line 405: the expected stateRoot 0xc216... was the zero hash in the served header, and the log recorded dropping invalid newHeads event at height 1: new head block 1 hash does not match committed event. The fixture passes a ResponseFinalizeBlock whose AppHash is the state root to notifier.OnBlockCommitted while the header the server reads for height 1 was stored without that root, so the notifier and the header disagree."
fix = "Attempt 2 wires the fixture so the committed header carries the state root the notifier announces, and asserts the value of the producer (gotcha 3046)."

[gotcha.3785]
title = "The gRPC query error test imports the auth transaction package, which imports the application through the ante handler and closes an import cycle"
symptom = "Task 18.1678.1 attempt 1 at 6b398503dc8c (base 93249965659c) failed its build: query_grpc_error_test.go imports sdk/x/auth/tx, which imports x/auth/ante, x/params/keeper and baseapp, and baseapp imports the package under test, so go reported an import cycle and nothing compiled."
fix = "Attempt 2 builds the request bytes without importing the x modules."

