[gotcha.3828]
title = "The retired-caller scan finishes in under a minute on main and reports one caller in the vendored geth four-byte signature database"
symptom = "Task 17.2.8 attempt 2 at b046adf30176 (base 9f7574fefe1a, after 22.39.214 landed) ran the scan in 47 seconds and failed in retired.owners at spec/layerx-merge/programme/retired.py line 368: no owning domain for caller core/deps/geth/signer/fourbyte/4byte.json. Line 1511 of that file is the selector entry 015bf264 for depositTokens(uint256,address,uint256), an upstream signature database of the vendored geth tree that lists every public selector ever registered, among them a retired name. core/deps holds 3006 tracked files of upstream cosmwasm and geth sources; tools/paxeer-x/tests/retired_callers_test.py excludes the catalogue, deleted and retiring trees, test directories and documentation but no vendored upstream tree, and no DOMAIN_PREFIXES entry owns core/deps."
fix = "Decision 3079: vendored upstream sources under core/deps are not callers; the scanner excludes the tree by pathspec and 17.2.8 attempt 3 carries that change with the scanner in its touches."

[gotcha.3829]
title = "The agent daemon library lint gate still reports 101 errors, all inside the crate, with the runtime module carrying most of them"
symptom = "Task 22.39.222 attempt 2 at 46e050a8fbc2 (tree cf1471ba1c8b) built and then failed cargo clippy --no-deps --lib -D warnings on layerx-agentd with 101 errors. Every error site is a file of services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src: human_runtime.rs 62 (lines 4218, 4579, 4777, 17591, 17605, 17626 among them), the agent RPC routing module source 7 (lines 322 to 335), policy/approval.rs 6 (lines 2585 to 2595), session_control.rs 6 (lines 3992 to 4226), budget/program_settlement.rs 5, approval/native_program.rs 4, approval/native_effect.rs 2, budget/execution_state.rs 2, outbox/mod.rs 2, and one each in capability/consume.rs 528, approval/call_bound.rs 549, budget/program_lifecycle_settlement.rs 319, budget/program_sources.rs 588 and read/committed.rs 665. By kind: 44 items declared after statements, 21 arguments passed by value and not consumed, 21 needless borrows, 3 let bindings returned from a block, 2 needless Ok and question mark pairs, and dead code (the Indeterminate variant, the rpc_program_discover method, unused associated items). The warnings the log also shows for layerx-crypto onboarding.rs, layerx-sdk program_http.rs and the programs crates come from compiling dependencies and are not errors of this gate."
fix = "Attempt 3 repairs the named sites; the dependency warnings belong to the crates that own them."

[gotcha.3830]
title = "The MCP crate lint gate reports 147 errors, 17 of them in files of other crates that the test targets load by path"
symptom = "Task 22.39.224 attempt 3 at d7d54522df48 (tree d3c54a79bb90) failed cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -D warnings on layerx-mcp with 147 errors. Sites inside the crate: tests/support/web_hold.rs 29, tests/repair_22_33_1551.rs 24, tests/proof_native_reads.rs 16, tests/repair_22_31_223.rs 16, tests/support/session_transport.rs 11, tests/web.rs 11, tests/repair_22_33_1556.rs 8, tests/support/node_recording.rs 6, tests/support/../approval.rs 3, tests/repair_22_31_531.rs 2, tests/support/clock.rs 2, tests/daemon_bound.rs 1 and tests/support/assert_option.rs 1. Sites outside the crate: 15 in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/proof_native_reads.rs and 2 in interop/crates/x-websearch/src/server.rs, both reached through path attributes from the MCP test targets, so their lints count against this gate while the files are outside the task touches. By kind: 46 documentation items missing backticks, 10 files loaded as a module more than once (tests/support/assert_result.rs, assert_option.rs and siblings, the duplicate_mod lint of gotcha 3826), 6 format in an iterator, 6 expect on Option, 5 expect on Result, 6 arguments passed by value, 4 needless borrows and 3 unwrap_err on Result."
