fix = "Attempt 4 splits the six functions into named helpers and replaces the five unwrap_err and expect calls with matches."

[gotcha.3832]
title = "The per-chunk participant aggregation at the 32/8 roster spends 995431 fuel against the 900000 margin cap"
symptom = "Task 22.33.223 attempt 17 at d39be6f97ce8 (tree 2b6e9694be4d) used both repair cycles and failed three of 27 cases of the repair_22_33_223 target at fuel_budget.rs line 2846: maximum_state_fuel_scaling, roster_state_fuel_scaling and every_routed_operation_fits_the_protocol_cpu_fuel_cap all panicked with each participant chunk at 32/8 must retain fuel margin: Some(995431). The participant_call_totals helper (line 2826) sums the fuel of every OPEN_EPOCH and FinalizeAggregation call at a height and requires each call at 32 participants and 8 evaluators to stay above zero and at or below 900000. The aggregation module (src/aggregation.rs line 54) fixes the chunk at eight participants; aggregate_chunk (line 257) and the chunked settlement path (line 1213) read that constant, and with the current per-participant cost eight participants exceed the cap by about ten percent. The same cap is asserted again at line 3070 for the full call."
fix = "Attempt 18 sizes the chunk so the measured fuel at 32/8 keeps the margin and records the fuel per chunk before and after."

[gotcha.3833]
title = "The cold-import RPC configuration case runs its three-by-five matrix of cold imports past the default five-second case time-out"
symptom = "Task 18.1688.1 attempt 1 at d579e1de6bf3 (tree da25e44599d8) failed at the final tree: rpcColdImportReportsInvalidOverrides timed out after 5000 ms (vitest default) while rpcColdImportPreservesValidatedSelection passed; log /out/logs/verify-2.log. The case (rpc-configuration.test.tsx lines 164 to 187) performs a fresh cold import of the rpc, wagmi and wallet modules for every pair of the three RPC variables and the invalid values, each import creating a wagmi configuration, and the registration helper at line 190 passes no time-out. The first verification at 8994fc256176 ran before the two cases were registered (one file skipped, two todo) and the tree moved afterwards, so the evidence candidate differs from the verified revision."
fix = "Attempt 2 gives the case the time-out its matrix needs, or builds the configurations once per variable, and verifies at the final revision."

[gotcha.3834]
title = "The metadata route scenario exceeds its thirty-second case time-out before any waitFor step can name itself"
symptom = "Task 18.1693.1 attempt 1 at 4d246733d224 (tree 513d4cd46733) failed metadata_routes_connect_editor_and_viewer after 32306 ms: the case is registered with timeout 30000 at route-wiring.test.tsx line 312, while its waitFor helper (line 192) polls each step against its own deadline with a labelled message. The vitest time-out fired first, so the log names no step; the scenario runs an editor upload with retry and cancel, a signed metadata commit, two chain changes, the coin route render, two viewport widths and an outage against a real HTTP server in one case."
fix = "Attempt 2 raises the case time-out above the sum of the step deadlines so a stalled step fails with its label, then repairs that step."

[gotcha.3835]
title = "The M948 native node recording was captured at the base revision while the attempt changed the producer events file"
