fix = "Attempt 2 re-records the native execution transcript from the final producer and writes the final revision into producer-revision.txt."

[gotcha.3836]
title = "The platform SDK generator refuses a handwritten agent API source file the pipeline manifest does not declare"
symptom = "Task 22.39.237 attempt 1 at bca47feb9c56 regenerated the Go, JVM and Python clients and then failed its build at services/platform/Makefile.inc line 245 with exit 2: platform-sdkgen reported an unclassified file in the generated rust root, services/agent/crates/layerx-agent-api/src/native_send.rs, and asked for it to be generated or declared under [handwritten.agent-api-rust] in sdk/platform/pipeline.kvx. The file arrived with the done task 22.39.221 (commit 2dc9fe9846); sdk/platform/pipeline.kvx lines 38 to 44 declare error.rs, identity.rs, lib.rs, read.rs, stream.rs and write.rs as handwritten and nothing else."
fix = "Attempt 2 declares native_send.rs under [handwritten.agent-api-rust] and sdk/platform/pipeline.kvx joins the touches of the task; a lint task that adds a source file to a generated root declares it in the same change."

[gotcha.3837]
title = "The vendored source fixture compiles with the control-plane TypeScript binary, which only a vendored-tree install provides"
symptom = "Task 18.1817.1 attempt 2 at 057afa0a657d passed its build (a byte-compile and a syntax check) and failed its verification with exit 1: the native source fixture support module of the vendored tests (native_source_fixture.py line 134) runs core/control-plane/node_modules/.bin/tsc, which FileNotFoundError reported absent because the build command installed nothing. the vendored tree carries pnpm-lock.yaml and the control-plane package pins typescript 7.0.2."
fix = "The build command of the task installs the vendored tree with the frozen pnpm lock before the compile checks, as decision 3075 requires; attempt 3 requalifies the attempt-2 tree."

[gotcha.3838]
title = "The client SDK public-types case enumerates the public system keys as a literal tuple, so a new public export fails the typecheck script until the tuple names it"
symptom = "Task 18.1826.1 attempt 2 at 5bb8137b2560 failed its build with exit 2 inside the typecheck script of the vendored client SDK package: the public-types case of the vendored client SDK package (test/public-types.test.ts line 610) reports TS2344, the ExpectedSystemKey type does not satisfy its constraint because the public entries now export installStatus (the install-status error constructor the issue asked for) where the tuple expected acknowledgeAppUpdate. The three public entries and the install-status case were the only files the attempt changed."
fix = "Attempt 3 adds installStatus to the expected key tuple of the public-types case at the position the public entry exports it and the case file joins the touches; a change to the public surface of the client SDK updates its public-types case in the same change."

[gotcha.3839]
title = "A lint repair of the programs runtime rewrote two test call sites to a retired seven-argument form and attributed a runtime type to the SDK crate"
symptom = "Task 22.39.235 attempt 1 at 7be3886a3b62 (base ab70c667c76c, where lxt20_tests.rs line 71 and market_tests.rs line 125 already call execute_authorized_v2_with_budget with the three-argument AuthorizedExecutionRequest form of execute.rs line 4856) failed its first build with exit 101: E0061 at both call sites, seven arguments supplied to a three-argument method, with a ResourceBudget where an AuthorizedV2Budget is expected. The repair build failed with E0432 at tests/repair_22_31_259.rs line 1052: the attempt replaced the glob import of layerx_program_sdk::arbiter (line 663 on main) with an explicit list that names MarketStepProof, a type the SDK arbiter module does not define; main imports MarketStepProof from rt::execute at line 667 and the SDK module only provides MARKET_STEP_TRANSITION."
fix = "Attempt 2 keeps the three-argument call form of main at both sites and imports MarketStepProof from the runtime execute module while the SDK import names only the arbiter constants; a lint repair of an import or a signature follows the definition site, never a remembered form."

[gotcha.3840]
title = "The launchpad indexer module keeps three red cases after the fourth round: a replay authorization deadline, an incomplete owned-explorer parity source and a pool identity in the saturation case"
symptom = "Task 22.39.162 attempt 4 at f629a39dfed2 passed its build and failed its verification with exit 1 after 42 wiring cases and every other package passed: TestPrivateReplayAuthorizationPostgres (internal/processor/replay_postgres_test.go line 263) exceeded its thirty-second context while the block processor logged closed connections and unexpected EOF retries; TestHistoricalRealRangeExplorerSuffixAndParity (internal/source/historical_integration_test.go line 374) failed ValidateParityAdmission with source owned-explorer: incomplete, the IncompleteError kind of internal/source/committed.go line 37; TestHistoricalSaturationPreservesLiveAndShutdownGenuineChain (line 655) failed with source pool: identity, the message the fourth round traced for the M1000 measurement case, which now passes."
