title = "History items at the node root carry a stability object the indexer rows did not produce"
symptom = "Task 18.1633.1 attempt 3 at 21c013003fab added tx_hash and final_basis to the history rows and failed TestPxNodeRoot_History_TransportShapesAndRestart at rpc/px_node_root_history_test.go line 275 through the schema helper of rpc/px_node_root_account_test.go line 433: result.items[0] lacks stability. services/platform/hosted/gateway/openrpc.json requires stability on px_getHistory and px_getUnifiedHistory items (lines 1664 and 2115) as an object with level (depth_stable, reversible or explorer_recorded), source (block_commit or explorer_api) and finalized_boundary (a decimal string or null)."
fix = "Attempt 4 gives every history row the stability object with the three contract fields, derived from the same classification that sets final_basis, and the transport case passes by the contract names."

[gotcha.3843]
title = "The daemon walkthrough resumed after a listener restart stays unknown with its budget still reserved"
symptom = "Task 18.1711.1 attempt 3 at 93a3f9c399d2 regenerated the daemon submission fixture and the fixture case now passes its serializer comparison; the conformance run inside test/repair-22-33-1480.test.mjs (line 141) reports one failing check, agent service: an unresolved submission resumes a committed observation after restart, with the detail resumed receipt must commit the reserved budget and the pair kind unknown, reservationState reserved. The check at services/platform/middleware/conformance/service.mjs line 745 restarts the JSON listener and runs the walkthrough with the resume reference again, expecting kind verified, reservation committed and the submission at the committed rung."
fix = "Attempt 4 repairs the resume path of the walkthrough so the second resumed run observes the committed terminal state the restarted listener serves, then regenerates the fixture at the final tree."

[gotcha.3844]
title = "The legacy explorer asset build resolves phoenix and phoenix_html from the Elixir dependency directory, which a node-only gate never fetches"
symptom = "Task 18.1766.1 attempt 3 at e92dc39d937b added terser-webpack-plugin and failed its build with exit 1: webpack reported Module not found for phoenix_html and phoenix under services/explorer/backend/apps/block_scout_web/assets/js. package.json lines 67 and 68 declare both as file:../../../deps/phoenix and file:../../../deps/phoenix_html, which exist only after mix deps.get populates services/explorer/backend/deps; the done task 22.39.97 ran mix deps.get natively under the elixir profile."
fix = "The task moves to the elixir profile and its build command runs mix deps.get in services/explorer/backend before npm ci and the webpack build; attempt 4 requalifies the attempt-3 tree."

[gotcha.3845]
title = "A pnpm directory filter with a glob and the dependency suffix matched no project, so the plugin typecheck ran without its built dependencies"
symptom = "Task 18.1772.1 attempt 2 at e220cdf708bc installed the vendored tree and then logged No projects matched the filters for the filter ./plugins/*-source-control^..., so the typecheck script of the source-control plugin ran against unbuilt dependencies and failed with exit 2: TS2307 Cannot find module for the plugin SDK package in contract.ts, app.tsx and server.ts (its exports map resolves types through bundled-types files the build produces), followed by implicit any errors downstream. The directory filter ./sdk/client^... of task 18.1826.1 at the same revision resolved its project."
fix = "The build command selects the plugin project with the brace directory form of the filter ({./plugins/*-source-control}^...), which pnpm resolves with the dependency suffix, and runs the typecheck script through the same brace selection; attempt 3 requalifies the attempt-2 tree."

[gotcha.3846]
title = "The retired-caller owner map has no domain for a README at the root of a tree several domains share"
symptom = "Task 17.2.8 attempt 3 at 24283a456abe excluded core/deps from the scan and failed test_scan_reports_no_caller with ValueError: no owning domain for caller: modules/README.md from the owners function of spec/layerx-merge/programme/retired.py (line 352 iterates DOMAIN_PREFIXES, line 18). The map assigns modules/<name> directories to domains 1 to 4 by module name and gives domain 17 only the root markdown files through DOMAIN_ROOT_FILES; a README.md directly under modules or precompiles matches nothing."
fix = "Decision 3081 assigns a README.md directly under modules, precompiles or api... to the documentation domain 17 as the root markdown files are; attempt 4 adds the rule to the owners function beside the api README rule and treats the modules README reference as the finding it is."

[gotcha.3847]
title = "The balances export retry cases compare persisted queue rows carrying database ids with in-memory rows that have none"
symptom = "Task 18.1652.1 attempt 2 at 8af3c4eafa35 compiled and failed two of ten cases of apps/indexer/test/indexer/fetcher/multichain_search_db/balances_export_queue_test.exs: the HTTP 503 retry case (line 262) and the malformed HTTP 200 retry case (line 123) assert the sorted persisted rows equal the sorted expected rows after dropping updated_at and retries_number, and the persisted side carries id 13, 14 and 15 where the expected structs carry nil. The six main export queue cases passed."
fix = "Attempt 3 drops id together with the other database-assigned fields on both sides of the two comparisons, or compares against the rows as inserted, keeping every other assertion."

[gotcha.3848]
title = "The V1 programs recorder deploys under ABI version 1, which the kernel admission policy refuses"
symptom = "Task 18.1667.1 attempt 2 at e8ec2dccfbf0 built and failed TestRecorderAllSelectedV6Executes at daemon/committed-fixture/main_test.go line 197: record vector-v1-programs-positive: V1 Programs deployment reverted with an Error(string) payload decoding to LXP_ERR_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED (code -101). The recipe at daemon/committed-fixture/vector_v1_programs.go line 69 packs deploy with uint16(1) as the ABI version; programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_interface.rs line 220 refuses an interface whose version abi_policy::admit_abi_version does not admit, so the refusal is the kernel contract and not a genesis setting; the V6 genesis preparation adds only the token code."
fix = "Attempt 3 moves the V1 programs recipe to the lowest ABI version the admission policy admits with the matching interface domain, keeps the vector name and records the admitted version and the policy site in the task record; the test stays unchanged."

[gotcha.3849]
title = "The launchpad web image build requires four production upstream arguments, not one"
symptom = "Task 18.1823.1 attempt 2 at eac60fe4def1 passed WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM to the image build and failed with exit 1 at the build stage: Error: missing production upstream: WEB_API_UPSTREAM from next build. apps/launchpad/web/src/core/next-build-config.test.ts lines 75 to 78 list the four upstreams the build configuration requires, WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM, WEB_API_UPSTREAM, WEB_SOCKETS_UPSTREAM and WEB_CHARTS_UPSTREAM; deploy/launchpad/web-build-env.sh only unsets empty build arguments."
fix = "The build command passes all four upstream build arguments with internal placeholder origins; attempt 3 requalifies the attempt-2 tree."

[gotcha.3850]
title = "The committed transaction verifier compares the Comet transaction bytes with the Ethereum raw transaction and refuses every genuine inclusion proof"
symptom = "Task 18.1833.1 attempt 3 at 31146b90f38f installed the TypeScript SDK and ran the HTTP round trip for the first time: all three sub-cases of test_typescript_settlement_metadata_round_trip failed with ValueError: transaction inclusion identity mismatch from services/agent/sdk/python/layerx_sdk/committed.py line 146, including the unchanged committed round trip, and the two altered landing references never reached the settlement-landing-mismatch refusal of x402_http.py line 672 that test_http.py line 398 expects. The proof data the fixture node returns is the Cosmos transaction envelope (a MsgEVMTransaction wrapper, hex 0ab8030ab503...), which the verifier compares byte for byte with the raw Ethereum transaction."
fix = "Decision 3082: the inclusion identity check decodes the committed transaction envelope and compares the embedded Ethereum transaction with the raw transaction; attempt 4 repairs committed.py accordingly, keeps the landing comparison, and committed.py joins the touches."

[gotcha.3851]
title = "The outage assertion of the price acceptance replay refutes every step within half a retry interval and catches a read of another table"
symptom = "Task 18.1659.1 attempt 2 at 76c78b18cb71 compiled and failed one of seven cases: replay_held_warnings_survive_database_outage at apps/explorer/test/repair/repair_22_31_490_test.exs line 328, where refute_receive on any step message of the replay process fired with a successful select returning block_hash rows, a query against a table other than the renamed backfill queue. The outage helper (line 260) renames only paxeer_x_price_acceptance_backfill, so reads of other tables keep succeeding while the queue is unavailable."
fix = "Attempt 3 narrows the refutation to steps whose query names the queue table and keeps the same-replay and durable-state assertions that prove the replay did not advance."

[gotcha.3852]
title = "The restart capture sends value to the non-payable precompile and the producer refuses with code 45"
symptom = "Task 18.1724.1 attempt 2 at 1bf96f08c220 built and failed TestCurrentReceiptRestartFixture: node/sequencer/receipt_equality_test.go line 439 reports producer refused nonzero restart capture: to 0x...101B value=25 code=45 vm_error execution reverted, revert LXP_PRECOMPILE_NON_PAYABLE, and line 441 then compares the result code 0x2d with the expected 0x0. The capture transaction carries 25 as its value while the receipt path carries the amount inside the call payload."
fix = "Attempt 3 derives the restart capture with a zero transaction value, the amount staying in the payload the producer path encodes, so the producer result code is zero and the budget state is the derived value."

[gotcha.3853]
title = "The inference availability test passes a signed voting power where the trusted validator constructor takes an unsigned one, and the build gate never compiles the test"
symptom = "Task 18.1777.1 attempt 1 at 70e0cedb2d0f built the agent daemon host binary and failed its verification with exit 101 before any case ran: E0308 at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/main.rs line 3306, expected u64 found i64 for v.voting_power passed to layerx_programs::chain_proof::validators::TrustedValidator::new (programs/crates/layerx-programs-registry/src/chain_proof/validators.rs line 18), plus an unused block closure at line 3407. The build command compiles only the binary, so a test-module error surfaces first in the verification."
fix = "Attempt 2 converts the voting power with a checked u64 conversion that refuses a negative value and removes the unused closure; a task whose cases live in a test module compiles them before the verification."

[gotcha.3854]
title = "The retargeted funding assertions paraphrase the consumer source instead of quoting it"
symptom = "Task 18.1663.1 attempt 2 at f60621bb68ae merged main after 22.39.234 landed, passed tsc, and failed two assertions of apps/perps/tests/funding-rate.test.ts: the pattern parseFundingRateHourly(t.last_funding_rate_hourly) against the quoter, whose call in the quoter module useQuoter.ts of the perps app (lines 251 to 253) breaks across three lines, and the pattern funding8h: snap?.funding_8h ?? null, against the markets rows, where apps/perps/src/widgets/markets/useMarketsRows.ts line 59 reads funding8h: snapshot?.funding_8h ?? null,."
fix = "Attempt 3 writes both patterns against the consumer text as main carries it (whitespace-tolerant for the three-line call, the identifier snapshot for the rows), the rule of gotcha 3046 that consumer tests assert the producer names."

[gotcha.3855]
title = "A pointer-to-string RPC parameter cannot distinguish an explicit null cursor from an omitted one"
symptom = "Task 18.1665.1 attempt 3 at bc7cec2a5987 built and failed TestPxNodeRoot_Assets_CursorSchema at rpc/px_node_root_account_test.go line 686: the explicit null cursor of px_listAssets was expected to answer -32602 and answered without error. rpc/px_assets.go line 212 declares ListAssets(ctx, cursor *string); the RPC decoder leaves the pointer nil both for an omitted trailing parameter and for an explicit JSON null, so the handler cannot see the difference decision 3074 requires it to refuse."
fix = "Decision 3083: an optional node-root parameter whose explicit null must be refused is declared as a raw JSON message, empty when omitted and the literal null when sent; attempt 4 changes the cursor parameter of ListAssets accordingly."

[gotcha.3856]
title = "The model endpoint refused the only turn of the signed replay authentication attempt, so no change reached the touches"
symptom = "Task 18.1750.1 attempt 1 (base 078da5472a03) ended with no revision: the model endpoint refused the turn with a content classification message after twenty-one read-only commands, no file in scope changed, and the gate recorded no change inside scope with no build and no verification run; log /out/logs/run-task.log."
fix = "Attempt 2 relaunches the task as written (decision 3044); a refused turn is not a finding against the task."

[gotcha.3857]
title = "The select control of the token transfer page scrolls its content on change, which the DOM test environment does not implement, so the rows option never applied"
symptom = "Task 18.1679.1 attempt 2 at 924f2279e9a2 (verification revision ba2c32de5246) failed tokenTransferLiveUpdatesFollowDisplayPage at apps/explorer/ui/token/TokenTransfer/TokenTransfer.spec.tsx line 121: the rows selector still read 50 after the 25 option was clicked, and vitest reported an unhandled TypeError, scrollTo is not a function, thrown by scrollContentToTop of the select machine (node_modules/@zag-js/select) inside the change action, which aborted the value update. apps/explorer/ui/snippets/footer/Footer.spec.tsx line 53 spies window.scrollTo for the same reason."
fix = "Attempt 3 gives the select content element a scrollTo function in the case (an Element.prototype.scrollTo stub installed before the page renders and removed after), so the change action completes and the rows value follows the option; the assertions stay unchanged."

[gotcha.3858]
title = "The search results route serves two general search queries for one term, one from the header input and one from the results page"
symptom = "Task 18.1717.1 attempt 2 at 46aee0f8f6f1 (verification revision 5492e8dbc53d) failed searchResultsRoutesKeepOneHeaderAndLiveSearch at apps/explorer/ui/shared/layout/LayoutSearchResults.spec.tsx line 195: the query cache held two general:search entries whose key carries the submitted term where one was expected (the multichain variant expects seven). The rendered tree carried one mobile-header and one desktop-header element, which the header assertions accepted, so the duplicate is in the search requests, not the header."
fix = "Attempt 3 prints both keys in the failure message, then removes the duplicate at its producer: the header input does not fire its own quick-search request for a term the results route already serves, and the results page query is the one the case counts."

[gotcha.3859]
title = "The native harness refuses the BeginAggregation envelope of the reward reopen case as non-canonical before execution"
symptom = "Task 18.1749.1 attempt 2 at ed01692a65d5 (verification revision 8ccc28cb224b) failed reward_reopen_preserves_recipient_balances at programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/tests/rewards_native.rs line 2691: the BeginAggregation submission returned result code -3 with a PreRuntime failure (module_version 5, parameter_version 1, encoding_version 4), the NON_CANONICAL code of the runtime (programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_interface.rs line 9) that the kernel returns from its canonical-form checks (src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c, sixty-eight LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL sites). The attempt-1 failure at line 2677 (balance -601) no longer occurs."
fix = "Attempt 3 traces the refusal to the kernel check that fires for this envelope (the activity decoder names the field) and repairs the producer of the envelope in native_reward_calls or the recipe step that builds it, recording the check and the field in the task record."

[gotcha.3860]
