[gotcha.3888]
title = "Node-root history keeps the explorer namespace in imported row ids while the OpenRPC document pins the id to a decimal pattern"
symptom = "Task 18.1632.1 attempt 3 at 62ec1d99e8b7 built and failed all four subtests of TestPxNodeRoot_History_ExplorerImportedRows with result.items[2].id fails pattern (log /out/logs/verify-2.log, lines 1001 to 1040): the regression validates every result against services/platform/hosted/gateway/openrpc.json (rpc/px_node_root_account_test.go:420 and :433) whose items.id schema for px_getHistory and px_getUnifiedHistory is the pattern ^[1-9][0-9]*$, while issue 1632 requires the explorer:<decimal> form to survive unchanged and the gateway reader (history.rs:306 to 312) already accepts both forms. The indexer change (historyID in src/modules/history/indexer.go) and the fixture page are correct."
fix = "Decision 3091: the task widens the items.id pattern of both methods in the OpenRPC document to admit the explorer namespace and keeps rejecting malformed ids; touches widened to the document."

[gotcha.3889]
title = "The token transfer live-update case matched two Next page buttons and then timed out as a whole"
symptom = "Task 18.1679.1 attempt 3 at the final revision of the attempt: cycle 1 failed with TestingLibraryElementError, found multiple elements with the role button and name Next page (the table card renders a pagination control above and below the rows; log /out/logs/verify-1.log, line 17); cycle 2, after the query was scoped to the footer pagination through within([data-footer-pagination]), the whole case timed out at 30000 ms with no failing step named (log /out/logs/verify-2.log, lines 12 to 18): the case awaits the test socket, the context socket, four notices and the socket close without a per-step bound or message, so the hanging step is invisible."
fix = "Continue: keep the scoped pagination query; give every awaited step its own waitFor timeout and message so the hanging step names itself; the component subscribes on the first display page only and unsubscribes when the page changes; the socket close is not awaited inside the timed case."

