[gotcha.3896]
title = "The inference availability case asserts an available F11 from a capture it wrote itself with the not-enabled code"
symptom = "Task 18.1777.1 attempt 2 at c4f16e6f124e built and failed inference_availability_uses_gateway_credentials at crates/layerx-agentd/src/main.rs:2885 (log /out/logs/verify-2.log, lines 2547 to 2563): the case ingests a test-local capture (mod ai_producer inside the test module of main.rs) into the indexer runtime and then asserts components.F11 == available, calling that capture the real producer; the indexer decodes the component status byte of the capture (services/platform/hosted/indexer/src/ai_market.rs availability_from: 1 available, 2 not-enabled), so the capture itself encoded F11 as not enabled. Cycle 1 at 71d91f62bd32 asserted a refusal wording the reader never produces (inference availability read refused against inference availability is not bound to the current committed program, main.rs:2791)."
fix = "Decision 3093: the capture encodes F11 with status byte 1, the comment names the fixture as the own capture of the case, and the refusal assertion uses the wording the reader produces."

