[gotcha.4014]
title = "The approved v6.12.0 manifest describes a surface runtime the chain never installed at its activation height and nothing installs it at the merge upgrade"
symptom = "Commit cf4c67eeb4 (task 18.1625.1) set the nine surface role hashes of sdk/launchpad/shared/config/deployment/current.json, SURFACE_RUNTIME_HASH of generate.py:21 and surfaceRuntimeHash of sdk/launchpad/shared/chain/client.go:1050 to 0xe67f4b12, the keccak of the guarded SurfaceRuntime at modules/launchpad/keeper/market.go:32, while keeping deploymentVersion paxeer125-v6.12.0 and activationHeight 37220320; the chain installed the unguarded runtime at that height (MigrateV6120 at keeper/migrate_v6120.go:173 calls InstallRoleSurfaces with the runtime of the binary that ran then), so the live roles hash to 0x6302ff80 as the recorded packet services/launchpad/indexer/internal/receipt/testdata/repair53-producer.json and the public attestation both show; the merge upgrade handler node/upgrades.go:471 (mergeUpgradePlan) never calls InstallRoleSurfaces (precompiles/launchpad/surface.go:39), so the guarded runtime would never reach the role addresses; every consumer comparing the network with the manifest refuses until then (gotchas 3994 and 4013)"
fix = "The v6.12.0 manifest returns to the installed hashes, the guarded hash is the staged surface runtime constant, and the merge upgrade installs it; decision 3134, tasks 22.39.295 and 22.39.296"

