title = "The private fixture receipt qualification needs a fixture chain with creation transactions, not a recorded packet"
symptom = "Task 22.39.242 attempt 6 at a6f3a58cd021: the three cases rebuilt through receipt.NewPrivateFixtureRPCQualification (services/launchpad/indexer/internal/receipt/rpc.go:572) fail with receipt qualification rejected at repair_m999_test.go:379, repair_m995_test.go:329 and repair_53_test.go:528; the entry point requires a deploymentVersion starting private-fixture-, a non-empty CreationTransactions map, an anvil_nodeInfo answer and the creation receipt of every role on the connected chain, none of which a recorded production packet carries"
fix = "Decision 3127 is withdrawn; the cases return to NewRPCQualification, which accepts the packet once the approved manifest at its activation height carries the installed hashes; decision 3135"

[gotcha.4016]
title = "The approval encoder of the Human service asserts a payload hash contract no producer uses"
symptom = "Task 18.1747.1 attempt 11 at af583cb1e6: the preflight added to native_approval_clock_units at tests/repair_22_33_63.rs:2414 shows encode_native_send_prepare_v2 (services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/native_send.rs:586) refusing with Mismatch(native_send_prepare.request) because it requires SHA256 of the raw payload bytes to equal request.payload_hash, while the producer of the hash, layerx_intents::compile at services/human/crates/layerx-intents/src/compile.rs:609, and the consumer, the daemon at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs:21556, both use the domain separated layerx_wire::hash::payload_hash_for over the registry bound payload; the encoder has no module registry and cannot recompute that hash, so every native Send approval it encodes is refused before the daemon sees it"
fix = "The encoder keeps the field checks and drops the raw SHA256 comparison; the daemon check governs; decision 3136"

